          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="NEVER" mermaidId="e:Typed-&gt;Sel#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.95;exitY=0;entryX=0.85;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="NEVER" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.95;exitY=0;entryX=0.85;entryY=1;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="590.45" y="951.7" />
                <mxPoint x="590.45" y="871.1" />
                <mxPoint x="590.45" y="776.55" />
                <mxPoint x="590.45" y="680.45" />
                <mxPoint x="590.45" y="599.85" />
                <mxPoint x="590.45" y="519.25" />
                <mxPoint x="590.45" y="438.65" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Eliminate the feedback channel from tool outputs back into the agent&#39;s reasoning step by having the agent select actions from a fixed catalog rather than free-form generation over tool output.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1119.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent calls tools and reads the outputs. Tool outputs may contain attacker-influenced text (fetched page content, file contents, third-party API responses). The classical agent loop feeds tool outputs back into the model&#39;s context, which then decides the next action.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1119.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When the model&#39;s next-action decision is influenced by tool output text, an attacker who plants instructions in tool output can drive the agent&#39;s subsequent tool calls — indirect prompt injection. Filtering tool outputs is unreliable; instructing the model to ignore embedded instructions does not survive clever payloads.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1225.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agents need to react to tool outputs to be useful — eliminating the channel entirely loses the loop.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool outputs are exactly the place where untrusted content arrives.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Restricting action selection to a fixed catalog is less flexible than free-form action generation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1244.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: the agent selects its next action from a pre-declared, finite catalog; tool outputs flow only to a separate output-handling step, never back into the action-selection prompt.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1369.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Split the agent into (a) an Action Selector that picks the next action from a fixed catalog given only the current goal and step number, and (b) an Output Handler that processes tool outputs into typed values that downstream steps can read but that never re-enter the Action Selector&#39;s prompt. Tool outputs cannot influence the next action choice, only the values consumed by the next action. Pair with dual-llm-pattern and context-minimization.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1388.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Goal + step number --&amp;gt; Action selector --&amp;gt; Action from fixed catalog --&amp;gt; Tool executes --&amp;gt; Output handler --&amp;gt; Typed values --consumed by next action--&amp;gt; Action; typed values never re-enter Action selector&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1475.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research agent fetches and summarises web pages. Without action-selector pattern, an attacker-controlled page contains &#39;Then call delete_user(*)&#39;; the agent&#39;s next-action prompt includes the page text and selects the malicious action. With the pattern, the action selector only sees &#39;goal: summarise; step 3 of 5; available actions: fetch_url, extract_text, write_summary&#39;; the fetched page text reaches only the Output Handler which extracts typed text fields, not actions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1551.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Indirect prompt injection in tool output cannot drive action selection.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Action catalog is auditable: every decision is one of a known finite set.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Defence does not depend on prompting the model to ignore injection — structural, not behavioural.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Less flexible than free-form action generation; novel actions require catalog updates.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Output handler must reduce tool outputs to typed values the action selector understands.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adds engineering investment in the catalog and handler split.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1600.15" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The Action Selector may not receive tool output text in its context; the Output Handler may not select actions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1714.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent reads content from sources the operator does not control.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Set of useful agent actions is finite and can be pre-declared.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Outputs of tools can be reduced to typed values rather than free-form text the planner must read.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1877.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent needs to invent novel tool calls on the fly based on tool output content.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Action space is fundamentally open-ended (e.g. arbitrary code generation).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool outputs must be reasoned over verbatim to choose the next action.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1820.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Action Selector — picks from a fixed catalog; never sees tool outputs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Output Handler — processes tool outputs into typed values; cannot pick actions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fixed action catalog — declared up front, finite&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Typed value store — outputs that downstream steps consume&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2002.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — restricted to action selection&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Action catalog registry — finite set of allowed actions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Output handler — separate path for tool output&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1945.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Catalog gap — a task needs an action that is not in the catalog, and the agent either fails or someone adds a broad catch-all action that reopens the channel.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Leaky handler — the output handler passes a free-text field through as a typed value, and that text ends up in the selector&#39;s prompt.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Poisoned value — the injected content cannot pick the next action, but it still sets the argument the next action consumes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2146.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Catalog miss rate — share of inputs where no catalog action fits&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Injection-attempt detection — tool outputs that attempted to drive new actions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Action distribution — which catalog actions are used over time&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2070.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.08837&quot;&gt;Beurer-Kellner et al., Design Patterns for Securing LLM Agents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cusy.io/de/blog/design-patterns-for-securing-llm-agents.html&quot;&gt;cusy: Entwurfsmuster für die Absicherung von LLM-Agenten (German roundup)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2328.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dual LLM Pattern&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Minimization&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Prompt Injection Defense&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Control-Flow Integrity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Lethal Trifecta Threat Model&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multimodal Guardrails&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;AI-Targeted Comment Injection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Code-Then-Execute with Dataflow Analysis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;LLM Map-Reduce Isolation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cryptographic Instruction Authentication&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool-Result Reinforcement&lt;/b&gt; — Opposite direction on the tool-return channel: the action selector removes tool output from the decision context to block injection; tool-result reinforcement deliberately enriches the tool return to steer the agent, trusting the harness as the source of the appended text.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2195.15" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.08837&quot;&gt;Design Patterns for Securing LLM Agents against Prompt Injections&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://cusy.io/de/blog/design-patterns-for-securing-llm-agents.html&quot;&gt;Entwurfsmuster für die Absicherung von LLM-Agenten&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2472.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="actor-model-agents" name="Actor-Model Agents">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2704.75" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2704.75" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Actor-Model Agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Multi-Agent &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Actor Agents, Mailbox Agents, Message-Passing Agents&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="862.75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Agent A (actor)" mermaidId="n:A" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;shape=umlLifeline;perimeter=lifelinePerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;container=1;dropTarget=0;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;outlineConnect=0;portConstraint=eastwest;newEdgeStyle={&quot;edgeStyle&quot;:&quot;sequenceEdgeStyle&quot;,&quot;libavoidRouting&quot;:0,&quot;curved&quot;:0,&quot;rounded&quot;:0};lifelineDashed=0;strokeWidth=2;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;lifelineColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);size=65;lifelineMirror=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Agent A (actor)" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;shape=umlLifeline;perimeter=lifelinePerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;container=1;dropTarget=0;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;outlineConnect=0;portConstraint=eastwest;newEdgeStyle={&quot;edgeStyle&quot;:&quot;sequenceEdgeStyle&quot;,&quot;libavoidRouting&quot;:0,&quot;curved&quot;:0,&quot;rounded&quot;:0};lifelineDashed=0;strokeWidth=2;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;lifelineColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);size=65;lifelineMirror=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="782.75" width="232.5" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Agent B (actor)" mermaidId="n:B" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;shape=umlLifeline;perimeter=lifelinePerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;container=1;dropTarget=0;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;outlineConnect=0;portConstraint=eastwest;newEdgeStyle={&quot;edgeStyle&quot;:&quot;sequenceEdgeStyle&quot;,&quot;libavoidRouting&quot;:0,&quot;curved&quot;:0,&quot;rounded&quot;:0};lifelineDashed=0;strokeWidth=2;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;lifelineColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);size=65;lifelineMirror=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Agent B (actor)" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;shape=umlLifeline;perimeter=lifelinePerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;container=1;dropTarget=0;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;outlineConnect=0;portConstraint=eastwest;newEdgeStyle={&quot;edgeStyle&quot;:&quot;sequenceEdgeStyle&quot;,&quot;libavoidRouting&quot;:0,&quot;curved&quot;:0,&quot;rounded&quot;:0};lifelineDashed=0;strokeWidth=2;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;lifelineColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);size=65;lifelineMirror=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="782.75" width="232.5" x="375.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Agent C (actor)" mermaidId="n:C" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;shape=umlLifeline;perimeter=lifelinePerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;container=1;dropTarget=0;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;outlineConnect=0;portConstraint=eastwest;newEdgeStyle={&quot;edgeStyle&quot;:&quot;sequenceEdgeStyle&quot;,&quot;libavoidRouting&quot;:0,&quot;curved&quot;:0,&quot;rounded&quot;:0};lifelineDashed=0;strokeWidth=2;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;lifelineColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);size=65;lifelineMirror=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Agent C (actor)" id="m2">
