        <UserObject label="yes" mermaidId="e:C-&gt;Ans3#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.58;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="yes" id="m16">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.58;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m8">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="888.05" y="1043.15" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="no" mermaidId="e:C-&gt;L#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.06;exitY=1;entryX=0.68;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="no" id="m17">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.06;exitY=1;entryX=0.68;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="680.35" y="1043.15" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Allocate inference-time compute (thinking tokens, samples, depth, model size) per query based on input difficulty, rather than using a fixed budget across all queries.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1387.3" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A reasoning agent or inference router serves queries of widely varying difficulty: simple lookups, moderate multi-step reasoning, hard novel problems. Compute per query is the dominant cost. The trivial policy — fixed budget across all queries — either wastes compute on simple ones or under-serves hard ones.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1387.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Static compute budgets force a single trade-off across all queries. With LLM inference cost dominating production economics, the slack on simple queries is large; the deficit on hard queries is real. Recent work (the 2025 arXiv survey &#39;Reasoning on a Budget&#39;, the 2026 ACM Web Conference paper on adaptive routing) shows that input-conditional allocation can reduce cost without sacrificing quality — but only if there is a reliable signal for per-query difficulty available before commitment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1493.3" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Compute is expensive; over-allocation wastes; under-allocation produces wrong answers.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-query difficulty is not always knowable upfront; some signals (self-consistency, model-uncertainty) require partial generation to read.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Routing-quality and routing-overhead trade off — a complex router can eat the savings.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1531.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: use a cheap difficulty estimator (self-consistency on a small sample, length heuristics, prior-task similarity) to pick a compute budget per query, and ramp budget on signals of low-confidence partial output.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1656.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Adopt a per-query budget pipeline: cheap difficulty estimator picks initial budget; partial-output signals (low self-consistency, low model confidence, branching mid-reasoning) trigger budget ramp; hard ceiling on budget per query prevents runaway. Variants include model routing (small model first, escalate on uncertainty), thinking-token budget control, and sample-count adaptation. Distinct from test-time-compute-scaling by being explicitly input-conditional.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1675.3" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Incoming query --&amp;gt; cheap difficulty estimator --&amp;gt; {easy -&amp;gt; small budget or fast model | moderate -&amp;gt; moderate budget -&amp;gt; confidence ok? no -&amp;gt; ramp up | hard -&amp;gt; full budget or large model} --&amp;gt; answer; per-query hard ceiling caps any ramp&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1781.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A customer-support assistant serves 10M queries/month. Profiling shows ~70% are FAQ-style (one-shot), ~25% are multi-step (need plan+execute), ~5% are genuinely novel (need extended thinking). Current setup uses a fixed extended-thinking budget on every query. The team adds a difficulty estimator: a small classifier scores prompt complexity, routes the 70% to the small fast path with no thinking tokens, the 25% to a moderate budget, the 5% to the full extended-thinking budget. Net inference cost drops 60% with no quality regression on production traffic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1838.3" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lower mean cost per query without quality regression.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hard queries get more compute when they need it; simple queries get less.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-query economic visibility — cost is now an attribute of difficulty, not a flat ledger entry.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Routing-overhead can eat savings if the difficulty estimator is itself expensive.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adversarial inputs can exploit the estimator to either burn budget or starve hard queries.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Calibration drifts as the underlying model changes — yesterday&#39;s difficulty estimator is wrong today.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1925.3" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Imposes a per-query difficulty estimation step before commitment to a compute level; constrains compute budgets to be elastic per query rather than flat across the deployment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2020.3" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Production deployments where mean-query cost dominates and query difficulty varies widely.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning agents with extended-thinking / sample-count controls available.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-model setups where smaller and larger models can be selected per query.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2221.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Workloads where queries have uniform difficulty.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Small deployments where routing overhead exceeds compute savings.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settings where the difficulty estimator&#39;s adversarial robustness has not been validated.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2126.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Difficulty estimator — small classifier or heuristic that scores per-query complexity before commitment&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Budget controller — translates difficulty score into thinking tokens, sample count, or model size&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence monitor — reads partial-output signals (self-consistency, uncertainty) to trigger budget ramp&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hard budget ceiling — caps any single query from consuming unbounded compute&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2346.3" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Prompt-complexity classifier — predicts difficulty from prompt features&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Extended-thinking / sample-count control — the budget knob the controller turns&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-consistency probe — small-N parallel samples used as a difficulty indicator&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost telemetry — per-query compute accounting feeding back into the controller&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2251.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Costly estimator — the difficulty estimator is itself a large call, and routing overhead eats the savings from cheap queries.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Starved hard query — a hard query looks simple on the surface, gets a small budget, and the confidence check never triggers a ramp.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Budget-burning input — a crafted prompt makes every query look hard and pushes all traffic to the full budget.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale calibration — the underlying model is upgraded, but the estimator keeps the old difficulty bands and misallocates budget.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2528.3" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Mean compute per query — primary cost target&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quality regression on hard subset — confirms hard queries are not under-served&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Routing accuracy — share of queries routed to the budget tier matching held-out difficulty labels&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Budget-ramp trigger rate — frequency that partial-output signals escalate budget mid-run&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Routing overhead share — fraction of total compute spent on difficulty estimation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2395.3" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3774904.3792556&quot;&gt;ACM Web Conference 2026 — Adaptive Model and Strategy Routing for Cost-Efficient LLM Services&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.02076&quot;&gt;arXiv 2507.02076 — Reasoning on a Budget survey (2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/extended-thinking&quot;&gt;Anthropic Claude — extended thinking budget controls (2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Reported Korean and Chinese-Traditional 2026 &#39;Slow AI / adaptive thinking&#39; coverage (Switas, fordige.com)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2748.3" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Test-Time Compute Scaling&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Sleep-Time Compute&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Mode-Adaptive Cadence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Model Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Process Reward Model&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Complexity-Based Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Deliberation Over Observation&lt;/b&gt; — The corrective: budget deliberation per query by difficulty instead of flat, so hard cases keep their reasoning while an interactive step that only needs a file read stops paying for a long chain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Foveated Perception Escalation&lt;/b&gt; — That allocates inference-time thinking budget per query; this allocates input-side observation fidelity, so the two budgets are spent on different axes and can be tuned separately.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Advisor Consult&lt;/b&gt; — A specific way to vary compute per task: the extra compute is a stronger model&#39;s read of the transcript, spent at points the executor selects.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2558.3" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/html/2507.02076v1&quot;&gt;Reasoning on a Budget: A Survey of Adaptive and Controllable Test-Time Compute in LLMs&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3774904.3792556&quot;&gt;Adaptive Model and Strategy Routing for Cost-Efficient LLM Services (ACM Web Conference 2026)&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.switas.com/ko/articles/the-ai-avalanche-7-agentic-llm-breakthroughs-reshaping-march-2026&quot;&gt;스위타스 — 7가지 에이전트 기반 및 LLM 혁신 기술&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2949.3" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
