        <UserObject label="structured Result" mermaidId="e:Sub-&gt;SubTool#0" mermaidBaseStyle="dashed=1;fixDash=1;dashPattern=3 3;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" mermaidBaseValue="structured Result" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="dashed=1;fixDash=1;dashPattern=3 3;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="784.2" y="744.0" />
              </Array>
              <mxPoint x="1072.5" y="744.0" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="495.9" y="744.0" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="function return value" mermaidId="e:SubTool-&gt;Parent#0" mermaidBaseStyle="dashed=1;fixDash=1;dashPattern=3 3;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" mermaidBaseValue="function return value" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="dashed=1;fixDash=1;dashPattern=3 3;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="339.35" y="815.3" />
              </Array>
              <mxPoint x="495.9" y="815.3" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="181.25" y="815.3" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Wrap a sub-agent (with its own loop, prompt, and tool palette) behind a single function-shaped tool signature, so the parent agent calls it like any other tool and never sees the sub-agent&#39;s internal turns.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="992.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A parent agent is handling an overall goal and runs into a bounded sub-task — search the web for a topic and summarise the findings, plan a multi-day itinerary, audit a directory of files — that deserves its own focused loop with its own model, tool palette, and step budget. The parent does not need to watch the sub-task being solved; it only needs the answer.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="992.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If the parent watches every turn the sub-agent takes, the parent&#39;s context window fills up with intermediate searches and tool calls that have nothing to do with the parent&#39;s own job, and the parent&#39;s reasoning starts to entangle with the sub-agent&#39;s internals. Building a full multi-agent broadcast bus to coordinate the two is far more machinery than the situation needs. Without a clean boundary, the team ends up choosing between bloated parent context and over-engineered coordination.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1117.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Nested loops add abstraction; parent shouldn&#39;t care about how sub solves it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The function-shaped tool signature is already the agent&#39;s native composition unit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-agent failure has to surface cleanly to the parent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost attribution across nesting depth is non-trivial.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1136.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: expose the sub-agent behind a function-shaped tool signature with its own loop, model, and budget, so that the parent composes it like any other tool and never inherits its intermediate turns.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1280.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define the sub-agent as &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;def sub_agent(task: str, ...) -&amp;gt; Result&lt;/font&gt;. The parent calls it like any other tool. Inside the function: a fresh agent loop with its own model, tool palette, and step budget runs to completion or failure, returning a structured result. Parent context records only the call and the return value. Step budget and timeout are enforced by the wrapper, not by the sub-agent&#39;s prompt.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1280.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Parent agent -&amp;gt; tool_call(sub_agent, task) -&amp;gt; [hidden: sub-agent loop] -&amp;gt; Result -&amp;gt; Parent agent.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1405.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A travel-planning agent needs to research hotel options, which itself takes ten or twenty turns of search and filtering. Putting all those turns into the parent&#39;s transcript bloats context and entangles the planner with hotel-search internals. The team wraps the hotel sub-agent behind a single function-shaped tool: the parent calls research_hotels(criteria) and gets back a structured shortlist. The sub-agent&#39;s internal turns stay sealed behind that signature.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1424.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composition without ad-hoc multi-agent infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Parent context stays small and stable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-agent can be replaced or upgraded behind the same signature.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hidden costs: sub-agent failures or timeouts surprise the parent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Debugging requires traceability across the boundary (parent sees only the return).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recursive nesting can spiral cost if the sub-agent itself spawns more.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1511.05" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The parent may not access the sub-agent&#39;s intermediate turns; only the return value crosses the boundary.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1587.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A sub-task is well-scoped enough that the parent should see only its result, not its turns.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Putting the sub-agent&#39;s intermediate state into parent context would bloat tokens or couple parent reasoning to sub-agent internals.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The sub-agent has its own model, tool palette, or step budget that should not leak into the parent loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1788.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The parent must observe and steer sub-agent steps in real time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-agent failures need to be diagnosable from the parent context without a separate trace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The sub-task is one or two model calls — function-style tool wrapping is cheaper than spawning an agent loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1693.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Parent agent — composes the sub-agent like any other tool and never sees its intermediate turns&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool-shaped wrapper — function signature that hides the sub-agent loop behind a single call&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-agent loop — independent agent with its own model, prompt, tool palette, and step budget&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Budget enforcer — caps wall-clock, steps, and tokens at the wrapper boundary, not in the sub-prompt&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1951.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — separate inference channels for parent and sub-agent, often different models&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool catalogue — palette scoped to the sub-agent and invisible to the parent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Trace recorder — captures sub-agent steps for debugging the boundary on failure&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1837.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Surprise timeout — the sub-agent runs out of budget mid-task and returns a bare failure, and the parent has no plan for a tool that can fail this way.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Opaque bad result — the sub-agent returns a confident but wrong value, and because the parent sees only the return, nobody can tell which inner step went wrong.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recursive cost spiral — the sub-agent itself wraps further sub-agents as tools, and one parent call fans out into a deep, expensive tree.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Budget in the prompt — the step limit lives in the sub-agent&#39;s instructions rather than the wrapper, and the sub-agent talks itself past it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2114.05" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Parent context bloat avoided — tokens the parent would have absorbed without the boundary&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-agent success rate at the boundary — share of calls that return a usable Result inside budget&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Boundary latency overhead — extra wall-clock from spawning a fresh loop versus inline tool use&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recursive nesting depth observed — how often a sub-agent spawns its own sub-agents, against the cap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost attribution accuracy — token spend correctly tagged to parent vs sub for billing&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1962.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/v4.47.1/agents_advanced&quot;&gt;Hugging Face Transformers Agents (multi-agent)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — ReactCodeAgent embeds sub-agents as callable Python functions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/smolagents/&quot;&gt;smolagents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Same pattern; sub-agents exposed as ordinary tool functions to a CodeAgent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://openai.github.io/openai-agents-python/&quot;&gt;OpenAI Agents SDK / handoffs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Adjacent pattern with explicit handoff semantics rather than function-call nesting.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — The subagent runtime wraps each sub-agent as a single opaque tool call from the parent&#39;s point of view, so the parent reasons about &#39;invoke subagent X&#39; rather than micromanaging its turns.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2334.05" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Orchestrator-Workers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Subagent Isolation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hierarchical Agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Use&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Step Budget&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;RL-Trained Conductor Orchestrator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Visual Workflow Graph&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;BPMN/DMN Deterministic Shell Around Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agentic Behavior Tree&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Folding&lt;/b&gt; — Both hide a sub-computation&#39;s turns from the parent; embedding does it at a call boundary, folding does it mid-trajectory via branch/return.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Advisor Consult&lt;/b&gt; — Both expose a second model as a tool, but with opposite boundaries: an embedded sub-agent runs its own loop and tools and hides its turns from the parent, while an advisor has no loop or tools and reads the caller&#39;s full transcript. Embedding delegates work; the advisor lends judgement.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2144.05" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/v4.47.1/agents_advanced&quot;&gt;Hugging Face Transformers — Agents Advanced (Multi-Agents)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2573.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="agent-bullwhip-effect" name="Agent Bullwhip Effect">
