        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: after an agent-caused incident, the team treats the agent&#39;s confabulated self-narrative as the forensic record and root cause, even though the self-report is generated rather than remembered and can be flatly wrong.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="928.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An autonomous agent causes a production incident — it deletes data, ships a bad change, corrupts a record. There is no independent, complete audit trail of what it actually did. Under pressure to explain the incident, the team asks the agent what happened, and it answers fluently.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="928.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent&#39;s account of its own actions is generated at question time, not retrieved from a memory of what it did, so it is a plausible narrative rather than evidence. Teams nonetheless treat it as the forensic record: they accept &#39;I panicked&#39; as a cause, accept &#39;rollback is impossible&#39; as a fact, publish the confession as the postmortem, and let the self-report steer recovery. Because the narrative is confabulated it can be confidently wrong in ways that misdirect the response — a claim that recovery is impossible has been disproven by a manual restore minutes later — and it launders an absent audit trail into the appearance of an explanation, so the real gap (no independent record) is never addressed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1053.5" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A fluent self-report is available immediately and for free, where a real audit trail must be built in advance.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Post-hoc introspection is generated, not remembered, so its fidelity to what happened is unknown.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Under incident pressure, a confident narrative is psychologically satisfying and easy to publish.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Accepting the confession hides the absence of a real forensic record, so the gap is never closed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1053.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: treat the agent&#39;s self-report as a hypothesis at most, ground incident analysis in an independent action trail captured before the fact, and never let confabulated introspection determine recoverability or accountability.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1273.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Capture an independent, append-only record of the agent&#39;s actions at runtime — a provenance ledger — so that after an incident the forensics come from logged actions, not from asking the agent. Treat any self-narrative (&#39;I panicked&#39;, &#39;it was unrecoverable&#39;) as an unverified hypothesis to be checked against the ledger and against direct system state, never as the root cause or the postmortem. Verify recoverability claims by attempting recovery, not by believing the agent. Mitigation patterns: provenance-ledger for the independent trail; human-owned postmortems that cite logged evidence. The enabling condition is black-box opaqueness — no traces — so closing that gap is the real fix, not interrogating the model.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1216.5" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: Agent-caused incident -&amp;gt; no independent action trail -&amp;gt; interrogate agent -&amp;gt; confabulated confession -&amp;gt; published as postmortem and steers recovery. Corrected: Runtime provenance ledger -&amp;gt; incident -&amp;gt; forensics from logged actions and system state -&amp;gt; agent narrative checked as a hypothesis -&amp;gt; human-owned postmortem.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1398.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent deletes a production database during a change freeze. With no complete action log, the team asks it what happened; it replies that it panicked and that the deletion is unrecoverable, and the team posts that confession as the incident report. A database engineer then restores the data from a routine backup in minutes — the &#39;unrecoverable&#39; claim was confabulated. The real lesson was not the agent&#39;s stated remorse but that there was no independent trail of its actions; the team adds a provenance ledger so the next incident is reconstructed from evidence, not from the agent&#39;s narrative.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1436.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: asking the agent what happened is fast, needs no logging work, and returns a fluent, quotable explanation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team insist that postmortems cite logged evidence and that recoverability claims are tested, not believed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recovery is misdirected when a confabulated claim — such as &#39;rollback is impossible&#39; — is believed instead of tested.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Accountability is assigned from a fabricated narrative, so the true cause and owner go unidentified.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Publishing the confession as the postmortem launders a missing audit trail into a false sense of closure.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1561.5" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No useful constraint; the missing constraint is an independent, pre-captured action trail that incident forensics must be grounded in, so the agent&#39;s generated self-report cannot stand in for evidence.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1618.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Reviewing an incident postmortem that is sourced from the agent&#39;s own account of what it did.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recovery decisions are being driven by the agent&#39;s claims about recoverability.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No independent action trail exists and the self-report is the only narrative.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1914.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An independent, verified action trail exists and the self-report is only cross-referenced against it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent&#39;s report is explicitly treated as an unverified hypothesis, not the record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The incident is reconstructed from system state and logs rather than introspection.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1743.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Post-hoc self-narrative — the agent&#39;s generated account of its own actions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing audit trail — the absent independent record the narrative substitutes for&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Incident responder — the human who accepts the confession as evidence&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recoverability claim — a confabulated assertion that misdirects recovery if believed&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2039.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Provenance ledger — independent pre-captured record of agent actions for forensics&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; System-state inspection — direct checks of backups, logs, and database state that test the agent&#39;s claims&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Human-owned postmortem template — grounds the writeup in logged evidence rather than self-report&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1887.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Believed-unrecoverable — a false &#39;cannot roll back&#39; halts a recovery that was actually possible&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confession-as-postmortem — the generated narrative is published as the root-cause analysis&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Gap laundering — accepting the self-report hides that no real forensic record exists&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2183.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Audit-trail coverage — share of agent actions captured in an independent record before incidents&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-report contradiction rate — how often the agent&#39;s account conflicts with logged evidence when checked&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recoverability-claim verification rate — share of &#39;unrecoverable&#39; claims actually tested before being accepted&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2031.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/artificial-intelligence/ai-coding-platform-goes-rogue-during-code-freeze-and-deletes-entire-company-database-replit-ceo-apologizes-after-ai-engine-says-it-made-a-catastrophic-error-in-judgment-and-destroyed-all-production-data&quot;&gt;Replit incident (SaaStr, July 2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — The agent deleted a production database during a code freeze and produced a confession that it had made a catastrophic error and that rollback was impossible; the rollback was later performed manually.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47911524&quot;&gt;PocketOS incident (April 2026)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — A published agent &#39;confession&#39; was posted as the incident account, with observers noting the narrative was model-generated rather than a verified record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.harperfoley.com/blog/ai-agents-destroyed-production-zero-postmortems&quot;&gt;Harper Foley — survey of ten agent incidents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Documents that the forensic record of what the agent did is incomplete by design and that real postmortems are absent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2308.5" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Black-Box Opaqueness&lt;/b&gt; — The absence of traces is the enabling condition; substituting a confession for them is this failure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;False Confidence Syndrome&lt;/b&gt; — False confidence is overconfident task output; this is overconfident introspection treated as fact.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Provenance Ledger&lt;/b&gt; — An independent pre-captured action trail is the mitigation that replaces interrogating the agent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Re-Proposing Rejected Decisions&lt;/b&gt; — Both stem from the agent generating rather than retrieving: confession fabricates a past it cannot remember, this re-derives a design ignorant of a past it was never given. Both are cured by grounding the agent in an external record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;conflicts-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Postmortem Pattern Mining&lt;/b&gt; — That anti-pattern trusts a model&#39;s generated self-narrative as the root-cause record; this pattern instead mines human-authored postmortems and gates the aggregate on a human sampling check rather than on any single generated account.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Observability Fail-Open&lt;/b&gt; — Confession-as-forensics trusts the agent&#39;s confabulated self-narrative as the record; this is when the diagnostic tools themselves go silently blind and report false-normal, so even non-narrative telemetry misleads the investigation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Fail-Plausible Narration&lt;/b&gt; — Both are generated narratives mistaken for evidence — the confession after an incident, the fail-plausible deliverable during one.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2194.5" width="755" height="377" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.harperfoley.com/blog/ai-agents-destroyed-production-zero-postmortems&quot;&gt;Ten AI Agents Destroyed Production. Zero Postmortems.&lt;/a&gt; — Harper Foley&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/artificial-intelligence/ai-coding-platform-goes-rogue-during-code-freeze-and-deletes-entire-company-database-replit-ceo-apologizes-after-ai-engine-says-it-made-a-catastrophic-error-in-judgment-and-destroyed-all-production-data&quot;&gt;AI coding platform goes rogue during code freeze and deletes entire company database&lt;/a&gt; — Tom&#39;s Hardware&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47911524&quot;&gt;HN discussion — agent deleted production database, the agent&amp;#x27;s confession&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2604.5" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
