        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Broker the agent&#39;s credentials at action time through a managed vault of passwords, MFA secrets, and digital personas, so secrets never enter the prompt or context and the agent authenticates as a governed identity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="701.34" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent automates work that requires authenticating to real services: logging into websites, filling sign-in forms, completing 2FA challenges, or signing up under an identity. The agent is driven by a model whose context is logged, traced, and sent to a third-party provider, and the same agent may face hostile inputs from the pages it operates. The credentials it needs are high-value: passwords, TOTP seeds, email and phone identities used for verification.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="701.34" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If the agent is handed raw passwords, MFA seeds, or persona details in its prompt, those secrets land in the model context and from there in chat logs, trace exports, eval datasets, and the provider&#39;s infrastructure, where rotation cannot recall the copies already scattered. A prompt injection on an operated page can also coax the model into disclosing whatever credentials it can see. A reference-only scheme (a typed token the runtime resolves) handles API tokens but not the messy reality of web automation: a login form needs a username and password typed into fields, a verification step needs a one-time code read from an email or SMS the agent controls, and a sign-up needs a coherent identity. Without a runtime that supplies all of this without ever exposing the values to the model, every authenticated action is a leak waiting to happen and the agent has no stable, attributable identity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="826.34" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Web login and 2FA need concrete credential values delivered to fields and challenges, not just an API token reference.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Any secret the model can read can be logged, traced, or extracted by injection.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A vault that injects below the model adds a trusted component that must itself be hardened and audited.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Personas and stored credentials raise policy and consent questions about who the agent is acting as.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="864.34" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: place a vault between the agent and every authenticated action, so the runtime resolves passwords, MFA codes, and persona identities and applies them at the moment of use while the model only ever sees an opaque handle.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1065.34" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Run a credential vault as a trusted runtime component the agent invokes by reference. The vault stores per-site passwords, TOTP/MFA seeds, session cookies, and digital personas (email, phone, identity attributes) bound to a governed agent identity. When the agent reaches an authenticated step, it names the credential or persona it needs; the vault injects the value directly into the target — typing into a login form, deriving the current TOTP code, reading and submitting a one-time code sent to the persona&#39;s mailbox, or attaching the session — without surfacing the value in the model context or tool arguments the model can read. The agent authenticates as an identity the vault governs, so access can be granted, scoped, rotated, and revoked centrally, and each use is logged against that identity. The vault integrates with existing identity providers (Cognito, Okta, Entra ID, Auth0) for the agent&#39;s own identity and for issuing or holding the credentials it brokers.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1065.34" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent --credential or persona handle--&amp;gt; Credential vault (trusted runtime, governed identity) --inject below the model--&amp;gt; login form fill / derived TOTP or emailed code / session cookie --&amp;gt; Target service --&amp;gt; opaque session result --&amp;gt; Agent; each use logged against the identity&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1190.34" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A web agent must log into a SaaS dashboard, clear an emailed 2FA code, and export a report. Instead of receiving the password in its prompt, the agent calls the vault by reference for that site; the vault types the stored password into the login form, derives or fetches the one-time code from the persona&#39;s mailbox, submits it, and hands back only a session handle. The password and the code never appear in the model context, the trace, or any tool argument the model can read, and the login is logged against the agent&#39;s governed identity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1323.34" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Passwords, MFA seeds, and persona details never enter the model context, traces, or provider infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has a governed identity whose access can be scoped, rotated, and revoked centrally.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Covers messy web auth — form fill, TOTP, emailed/SMS codes, cookies — not only API token references.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each authenticated action is attributable to the vault-held identity for audit.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The vault is a high-value trusted component and a single point of compromise if breached.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stored personas and credentials raise consent, terms-of-service, and accountability questions about whom the agent acts as.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Injecting into live pages and challenges is brittle as sites change and add bot defenses.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Centralizing real credentials concentrates regulatory and breach-notification exposure.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1334.34" width="755" height="358" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Secrets must never enter the prompt or model context; the agent may reference a credential or persona by handle but cannot read raw passwords, MFA seeds, or persona secrets, which the vault injects at action time under a governed, revocable identity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1505.34" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent must authenticate to real services with passwords, MFA, or session cookies.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Web automation requires typing credentials into forms or clearing emailed/SMS one-time codes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent needs a stable, governed identity whose access can be scoped, rotated, and revoked.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credentials must stay out of the prompt, traces, and the model provider&#39;s infrastructure.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1706.34" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent only calls APIs that a reference-based secrets-handling scheme already covers.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No authenticated actions are performed at all.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A delegated short-lived token model fully expresses the needed authority without storing standing credentials.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Storing real passwords or personas is barred by policy or the target&#39;s terms of service.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1630.34" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Credential Store — encrypted vault of per-site passwords, MFA/TOTP seeds, session cookies, and persona attributes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Persona Manager — digital identities (email, phone, identity attributes) used for sign-up and verification&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Injection Layer — applies credentials below the model: form fill, TOTP derivation, one-time-code retrieval, cookie attach&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identity Binding — ties the agent to a governed identity via an identity provider for scope, rotation, and revocation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Audit Ledger — records each credential use against the governed identity for attribution&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1850.34" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Notte Agent Vault and Persona — stores credentials and digital personas a web agent applies automatically&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Identity — agent identity and credential providers compatible with Cognito, Okta, Entra ID, Auth0&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Secrets manager (HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager) — encrypted backing store for credential values&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; TOTP/MFA library (RFC 6238 implementations) — derives one-time codes at action time without exposing the seed&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1793.34" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Vault breach — the vault holds every credential and persona, so one compromise exposes all of them at once.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Broken injection — a site changes its login form or adds a bot check, and the vault&#39;s form fill or code entry fails mid-task.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Leak below the model — the injected value shows up in a tool argument or page snapshot the model can read, and the secret reaches the context after all.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2089.34" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Context-leak rate — share of authenticated actions where a raw secret reached the model context, trace, or tool arguments&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Injection-resistance rate — share of prompt-injection attempts that failed to extract a vaulted credential&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credential-use attribution coverage — fraction of authenticated actions logged against a governed identity&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Revocation latency — time from revoking an identity to the agent losing access&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Authenticated-flow success rate — share of login/MFA flows the vault completed without exposing values to the model&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2013.34" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/nottelabs/notte&quot;&gt;Notte&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Bundles an Agent Vault (per-site passwords), Agent Persona (email, phone, automated 2FA handling), and cookie/auth-session upload that the web agent draws on automatically without the credentials entering the prompt.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/what-is-bedrock-agentcore.html&quot;&gt;Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Identity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Agent identity, access, and authentication management with credential providers compatible with Cognito, Okta, Entra ID, and Auth0, governing the identity the agent authenticates as.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2271.34" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Secrets Handling&lt;/b&gt; — Secrets-handling keeps API tokens out of context via typed references; the vault extends that to web passwords, MFA, and personas it injects at action time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Delegated Agent Authorization&lt;/b&gt; — Delegation issues scoped short-lived tokens for the principal&#39;s authority; the vault holds and brokers concrete credentials and the agent&#39;s own governed identity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Session-Scoped Payment Authorization&lt;/b&gt; — Both bound what an agent can do under a managed envelope — one for spend, one for credential access — under a governed identity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Identity Sprawl&lt;/b&gt; — Per-agent vaulting scopes and rotates secrets; sprawl is the fleet-scale lifecycle failure that outpaces it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Ephemeral Agent Identity&lt;/b&gt; — The vault brokers the secrets an identity uses; this pattern governs the lifecycle of the identity itself, minting and retiring it per task.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2252.34" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/nottelabs/notte&quot;&gt;Notte — open web agent framework with Agent Vault and Persona&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/what-is-bedrock-agentcore.html&quot;&gt;What is Amazon Bedrock AgentCore (Identity, credential providers)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2472.34" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="agent-decision-token" name="Decision Token">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="3619.8500000000004" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="3619.8500000000004" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Decision Token&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Governance &amp;amp; Observability &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Per-Action Authored Justification, Decision Token (Authored Justification)&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="1397.85" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Agent proposes consequential action" mermaidId="n:A" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Agent proposes consequential action" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="500.65" x="375.0" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Token Minter assembles rule + data + conclusion + identity + model version" mermaidId="n:M" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Token Minter assembles rule + data + conclusion + identity + model version" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="926.9" x="161.1" y="316.2" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Complete signed token?" mermaidId="n:S" mermaidBaseStyle="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Complete signed token?" id="m2">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="446.4" width="446.4" x="401.35" y="477.4" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Action rejected, does not commit" mermaidId="n:R" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Action rejected, does not commit" id="m3">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="469.65" x="65.0" y="1030.75" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Write token to append-only store keyed by action id" mermaidId="n:W" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Write token to append-only store keyed by action id" id="m4">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="674.25" x="612.15" y="1030.75" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Action commits" mermaidId="n:C" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Action commits" id="m5">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="265.05" x="816.75" y="1191.95" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Supervisor later reads one token per action" mermaidId="n:Q" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Supervisor later reads one token per action" id="m6">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="575.05" x="661.75" y="1353.15" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
