        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Pool-&gt;O#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:O-&gt;S#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: an agent fleet mints non-human identities at machine speed while scoping, rotation, ownership, and revocation stay human-speed, so over-privileged long-lived credentials accumulate, outlive their agents, and widen an ungovernable attack surface.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="987.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An organisation scales from a few agents to a fleet. Each agent, sub-agent, and tool integration needs an identity and credentials to act — a service account, an API key, an OAuth token. Provisioning these is automated and instant; governing them — scoping least privilege, rotating secrets, tracking ownership, revoking on retirement — still runs through human-speed review.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="987.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Identity creation happens at machine speed and identity governance happens at human speed, and the gap compounds. Over-broad, long-lived credentials are minted faster than anyone scopes, rotates, or retires them; tokens outlive the agents they were issued for; ownership of a given credential becomes unknown. The attack surface grows week over week because nothing reconciles created identities against active, owned, and least-privileged ones, and no human-speed approval process can keep pace with the rate of creation. The result is a population of orphaned, over-privileged non-human identities that no one is tracking and no one can confidently revoke.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1112.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agents need identities to act, and provisioning is automated, so creation is effectively unbounded.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scoping, rotation, ownership, and revocation are governance work that stays human-speed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Least-privilege scoping per agent is slower than issuing a broad credential that just works.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The creation-versus-revocation rate mismatch means the orphaned-credential population only grows.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1131.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: govern non-human identities at the rate they are created — automate least-privilege scoping, short-lived rotation, ownership tracking, and revocation on agent retirement — so the credential population stays reconciled instead of sprawling.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1313.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Make identity lifecycle keep pace with identity creation. Issue short-lived, least-privilege credentials by default rather than broad long-lived ones; bind every identity to an owning agent and a retirement trigger so it is revoked when the agent is decommissioned; continuously reconcile created identities against active, owned, scoped ones and flag orphans. The mechanism to fix is the creation-versus-revocation rate mismatch, so the controls must themselves run at machine speed. Mitigation patterns: agent-credential-vault for scoped, rotated, brokered secrets per agent; delegated-agent-authorization for narrowly scoped, time-bound grants. This is the fleet-scale lifecycle failure those per-agent patterns do not by themselves prevent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1294.4" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: Agent fleet -&amp;gt; mints identities at machine speed -&amp;gt; credential pool; scope, rotate, own, revoke at human speed -&amp;gt; orphaned over-privileged long-lived credentials -&amp;gt; growing attack surface. Corrected: Agent fleet -&amp;gt; short-lived least-privilege credentials bound to an owner and retirement trigger -&amp;gt; continuous reconciliation flags orphans -&amp;gt; revoke.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1438.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A platform team scales from a handful of agents to hundreds, each spinning up service accounts and API keys on demand. Provisioning is instant; nobody is scoping or retiring the credentials, which are broad and long-lived. A quarterly audit finds thousands of tokens, many tied to agents that no longer exist and owned by no one, any of which would grant an attacker standing access. The team moves identity issuance to short-lived least-privilege credentials bound to an owning agent and revoked on retirement, and adds continuous reconciliation — so governance finally runs at the speed identities are created.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1514.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: giving each new agent a broad, long-lived key gets it working at once and avoids waiting on an approval process.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team treat the gap between creation rate and revocation rate as the thing to fix, and automate governance at the same speed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Orphaned, over-privileged credentials accumulate and outlive the agents that needed them.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ownership of a given identity becomes unknown, so revocation is risky and often skipped.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The attack surface widens continuously, and a single leaked long-lived token grants broad standing access.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1601.4" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No useful constraint; the missing constraint is machine-speed identity governance — least-privilege scoping, rotation, ownership, and revocation that keep pace with the rate at which agents mint identities.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1715.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent fleet provisions identities and credentials faster than they are scoped, rotated, or retired.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Auditing standing access reveals orphaned or over-privileged non-human identities of unknown ownership.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identity governance runs through human-speed review while creation is automated.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1916.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Identity lifecycle is automated and reconciled at the same rate as creation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The deployment is a single agent or a small fixed set with managed credentials.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credentials are already short-lived, least-privilege, owned, and revoked on retirement.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1840.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Identity minting — automated, machine-speed provisioning of service accounts, keys, and tokens&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Governance backlog — human-speed scoping, rotation, ownership, and revocation that falls behind&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Orphaned credential — a long-lived identity that outlives its agent and its known owner&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reconciliation gap — the missing continuous check of created against active, owned, scoped identities&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2079.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Non-human identity inventory — continuously reconciles created identities against active, owned ones&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-lived credential broker — issues least-privilege, rotating secrets per agent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Revocation automation — retires credentials when their owning agent is decommissioned&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1965.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Orphan accumulation — credentials persist after their agents are gone, with no owner to revoke them&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Over-privilege drift — broad grants issued for convenience are never narrowed&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Revocation paralysis — unknown ownership makes teams afraid to revoke, so nothing is retired&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2242.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Creation-vs-revocation rate — identities minted versus retired per period&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Orphaned-identity count — credentials with no active owning agent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Least-privilege coverage — share of identities scoped to minimum needed privilege&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credential lifetime distribution — how long tokens live versus how long their agents do&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2109.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://labs.cloudsecurityalliance.org/research/csa-whitepaper-nonhuman-identity-agentic-ai-governance-v1-cs/&quot;&gt;Cloud Security Alliance — non-human identity governance whitepaper&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Names the non-human identity governance vacuum for agentic systems and the gap between machine-speed creation and human-speed governance.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unite.ai/agentic-ai-turns-nhi-sprawl-into-an-ungovernable-attack-surface/&quot;&gt;Fortra / Unite.AI analysis&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Observes that machine-speed identity creation cannot be governed by human-speed approval processes, turning NHI sprawl into an ungovernable attack surface.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2386.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Credential Vault&lt;/b&gt; — The vault scopes, rotates, and brokers secrets per agent; sprawl is the fleet-scale lifecycle failure that outpaces per-agent vaulting.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Privilege Escalation&lt;/b&gt; — Escalation is one agent gaining privilege at runtime; sprawl is the fleet accumulating over-privileged identities over time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Shadow AI&lt;/b&gt; — Shadow AI is unsanctioned use; sprawl is sanctioned agents minting governed-too-slowly identities.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Sprawl&lt;/b&gt; — Identity sprawl is the credential facet (non-human identities minted too fast to govern); agent sprawl is the operational-lifecycle facet — owning, measuring, monitoring, and retiring the agents themselves.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Static Role for a Dynamic Agent&lt;/b&gt; — Sibling non-human-identity failure: sprawl is the creation-versus-governance rate mismatch, this is the static-versus-dynamic authorization-model mismatch.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;conflicts-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Ephemeral Agent Identity&lt;/b&gt; — Sprawl is the accumulation of long-lived over-privileged agent identities; per-task minting with revocation at completion is the direct counter to it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-Speed Incident-Response Gap&lt;/b&gt; — Both are velocity mismatches between machine-speed agents and human-speed governance: sprawl is identity lifecycle out of pace, this gap is incident response out of pace.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2253.4" width="755" height="377" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.unite.ai/agentic-ai-turns-nhi-sprawl-into-an-ungovernable-attack-surface/&quot;&gt;Agentic AI Turns NHI Sprawl Into an Ungovernable Attack Surface&lt;/a&gt; — Unite.AI / Fortra&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.informationweek.com/risk-management/non-human-identity-sprawl-is-agentic-ai-s-real-risk&quot;&gt;Non-human identity sprawl is agentic AI&amp;#x27;s real risk&lt;/a&gt; — InformationWeek&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://labs.cloudsecurityalliance.org/research/csa-whitepaper-nonhuman-identity-agentic-ai-governance-v1-cs/&quot;&gt;The Non-Human Identity Governance Vacuum&lt;/a&gt; — Cloud Security Alliance&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2587.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="agent-initiated-payment" name="Agent-Initiated Payment">
