        <UserObject label="record settlement (amount, counterparty, run id)" mermaidId="e:Agent-&gt;L#0" mermaidBaseStyle="endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" mermaidBaseValue="record settlement (amount, counterparty, run id)" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m0" style="endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="678.8" y="754.85" />
              </Array>
              <mxPoint x="181.25" y="754.85" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="1174.8" y="754.85" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;The agent answers a payment-required challenge with a proof drawn from a capped wallet, then records the settlement for audit.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="892.6" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Give an agent a bounded wallet so it can settle a payment mid-request to unlock a resource — answering a payment-required challenge with a verifiable proof — instead of routing every purchase through a human.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="967.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running an agent that needs paid resources at runtime: a premium data feed, a metered API, compute or model inference, or a service offered by another agent. These resources increasingly expose a machine-payable endpoint — for example an HTTP 402 &#39;Payment Required&#39; response — that returns the data the moment a valid payment proof arrives. The team has to decide how the agent obtains and spends money for these calls without a person approving each one.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="967.6" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Pre-provisioning every possible paid resource with an account, an API key, and a billing relationship does not scale to an agent that discovers what it needs as it runs, and it leaves spend untracked across dozens of providers. Putting a human in the loop for each purchase defeats the point of an autonomous run and stalls on sub-second resource calls. But handing an agent an open-ended payment instrument invites runaway spend, fraud, and purchases no one can later reconstruct or attribute.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1092.6" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Autonomous runs cannot pause for human approval on every paid resource call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An open-ended payment instrument invites runaway spend and fraud.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Machine-payable endpoints settle in well under a second; account-and-invoice billing cannot keep that pace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Every payment must be reconstructable and attributable after the fact for audit and dispute.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resources are discovered at runtime, so pre-provisioning an account per provider does not scale.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1130.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: issue the agent a wallet scoped by hard spend caps and per-transaction limits, let it answer payment-required challenges with a verifiable proof, and write every settlement to an auditable ledger, so autonomy is bounded by budget rather than by a human in the loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1255.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Provision the agent with a constrained wallet: a balance or credit line, a per-transaction ceiling, a total budget per run, and an allow-list of payable counterparties or resource classes. When a resource returns a payment-required challenge, the agent constructs a payment (for example a signed stablecoin transfer referenced in a payment header) and retries; the resource verifies the proof and releases the data. Each settlement is recorded to a ledger with the amount, counterparty, run id, and the action that triggered it, so spend is observable and attributable. Spend caps and the counterparty allow-list are enforced outside the model, so a compromised or confused agent cannot exceed them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1312.6" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent --request--&amp;gt; resource; resource --402 + price--&amp;gt; agent; agent --check caps, sign--&amp;gt; wallet; wallet --proof--&amp;gt; agent; agent --retry + proof--&amp;gt; resource (unlocked); agent --record--&amp;gt; ledger. Caps and allow-list sit outside the model.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1380.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research agent hits a premium market-data API that responds 402 Payment Required with a price of a few cents. Instead of stopping to ask its operator, the agent — holding a wallet capped at five dollars for the run — signs a stablecoin micro-payment, attaches the proof, and retries; the API returns the data in under a second. The settlement is logged with the run id so the operator can later see exactly what was bought and why.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1513.6" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent can acquire resources discovered at runtime without pre-provisioned accounts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement happens in-band and fast enough for per-call resource access.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Spend is bounded by enforced caps rather than by human availability.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A ledger makes every machine payment attributable to a run and an action.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A wallet on an autonomous agent is a high-value target; key compromise is direct financial loss.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mispriced or adversarial resources can drain the budget up to the configured cap.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Irreversible settlement (for example on-chain) leaves little recourse for a wrong or fraudulent charge.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-provider micro-payments fragment cost reporting unless the ledger consolidates them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1524.6" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent cannot spend beyond its enforced per-transaction and per-run caps, cannot pay counterparties outside its allow-list, and may not settle a payment that is not recorded to the ledger.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1676.6" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent needs paid resources it discovers at runtime rather than a fixed pre-provisioned set.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resources expose machine-payable endpoints that settle faster than human approval allows.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Spend can be bounded by enforced per-transaction and per-run caps.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Payments must be attributable to a run and an action for audit.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1858.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The set of paid resources is small and stable enough to pre-provision with accounts and keys.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each purchase is high-value or irreversible enough to warrant a human decision.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No enforceable spend cap or counterparty allow-list can be put outside the model.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The deployment cannot tolerate the fraud and key-custody risk of an agent-held wallet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1782.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Capped wallet — holds balance or credit with per-transaction and per-run spend limits enforced outside the model&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Payment challenge handler — detects payment-required responses and constructs a valid payment proof&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Counterparty allow-list — restricts which resources or agents the wallet will pay&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement ledger — records amount, counterparty, run id, and triggering action for every payment&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement rail — the stablecoin, card, or fiat channel that clears the payment and returns a proof&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2002.6" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Machine-payable resource endpoint — API that issues a payment-required challenge and verifies proofs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wallet or key-management service — signs payments under enforced spend policy&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement rail SDK — clears stablecoin, card, or fiat transactions and emits verifiable proofs&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1926.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Wallet key theft — the agent&#39;s signing key is exposed, and an attacker spends the balance directly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Budget drain — an adversarial or mispriced resource keeps issuing payment challenges, and the agent pays up to the run cap for little value.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unrecoverable charge — an on-chain settlement goes to the wrong counterparty, and there is no way to reverse it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Untraced spend — a payment settles without a ledger entry or with a missing run id, and nobody can later say which action caused it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2222.6" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Spend-cap breach attempts — count of payments blocked for exceeding per-transaction or per-run limits&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost per resolved task — total settled spend divided by completed runs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement latency — time from a payment-required challenge to an unlocked resource&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unattributed-payment rate — share of settlements missing a run id or triggering action in the ledger&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Off-allow-list payment attempts — count of blocked payments to counterparties not on the allow-list&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2070.6" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/coinbase/x402&quot;&gt;x402 (Coinbase)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Revives HTTP 402: the agent sends a stablecoin payment proof in a payment header to unlock an API call; settles on-chain in roughly 200ms. Supported by Cloudflare and Circle.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cloud.google.com/blog/products/ai-machine-learning/announcing-agents-to-payments-ap2-protocol&quot;&gt;Agent Payments Protocol (AP2), Google + Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Gives autonomous agents a wallet, a programmable settlement rail, and auditable proofs to price, purchase, and get paid under a principal&#39;s mandate.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/blog/machine-payments-protocol&quot;&gt;Stripe + Tempo (MPP)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Multi-rail agent payments spanning stablecoin, fiat, cards, and Bitcoin Lightning behind one interface.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2442.6" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cost Gating&lt;/b&gt; — Cost-gating supplies the spend thresholds that bound what the wallet may settle without escalation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Inter-Agent Communication&lt;/b&gt; — Agent-to-agent commerce lets one agent pay another for a service over an inter-agent channel.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Session-Scoped Payment Authorization&lt;/b&gt; — Session-scoped authorization specialises agent-initiated payment by making a capped session, not a single charge, the unit of approval.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Verifiable Purchase Mandate&lt;/b&gt; — Agent-initiated payment answers a payment-required challenge with a proof of payment; the mandate is the upstream proof of user authorization that makes that charge accountable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2290.6" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/industries/x402-and-agentic-commerce-redefining-autonomous-payments-in-financial-services/&quot;&gt;x402 and Agentic Commerce: Redefining Autonomous Payments in Financial Services&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/coinbase/x402&quot;&gt;coinbase/x402&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cnblogs.com/informatics/p/19631662&quot;&gt;当 AI Agent 接管你的钱包：未来支付体系的终极演进&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Status/402&quot;&gt;HTTP 402 Payment Required (MDN)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2681.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
