        <UserObject label="error" mermaidId="e:Call-&gt;E3#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.89;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="error" id="m21">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.89;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m9">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="864.7" y="247.63" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:E3-&gt;E2#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m22">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m9" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m10">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:E2-&gt;E1#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m23">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m10" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m11">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:E1-&gt;Err#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m24">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m11" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m12">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Wrap every model call, tool call, and memory access in a composable pre/execute/post interceptor pipeline so cross-cutting concerns attach without touching agent or orchestrator code.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="311.72" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent runtime accumulates cross-cutting concerns: structured logging of every model call, rate-limit enforcement on third-party APIs, PII redaction on inputs and outputs, guardrail evaluation, latency metrics, an approval gate that may pause a call. Each concern needs to fire on the same set of touchpoints — model calls, tool calls, memory reads/writes — without each concern reimplementing the wiring.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="311.72" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If each concern is implemented as a wrapper at the agent or orchestrator layer, the runtime accretes a deep stack of decorators, the order is implicit, and adding or removing a concern requires editing agent code. Worse, concerns differ in shape — some need to see the request before the call, some need to mutate the response, some need to catch errors. Without a uniform middleware surface, each concern carries its own ad-hoc hook code and the cross-cutting layer is no longer composable or testable in isolation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="417.72" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Pre-execution interceptors (request modification, validation) need the request; post-execution interceptors (response logging, redaction) need the response; error handlers need the exception.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ordering matters — guardrails before logging, redaction before persistence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Middleware must compose at runtime so a team can add or remove a concern by configuration.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each middleware must remain testable in isolation against a synthetic call.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="474.72" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: define a single middleware contract with process_request, process_response, and process_error methods and route every model and tool call through a configurable chain, so cross-cutting concerns attach uniformly and order is explicit.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="599.72" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a BaseMiddleware with three hooks: process_request (called before the underlying call, may modify or short-circuit), process_response (called after, may mutate the response), process_error (called on exception). A MiddlewareChain runs the chain forward through process_request, invokes the underlying call, then runs the chain in reverse through process_response. Mount the chain at the runtime layer — every model call, tool call, and memory access flows through it. Cross-cutting concerns are then registered, not coded into agents.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="637.72" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Request --&amp;gt; M1.process_request --&amp;gt; M2.process_request --&amp;gt; M3.process_request --&amp;gt; Underlying call (model / tool / memory) --&amp;gt; M3.process_response --&amp;gt; M2.process_response --&amp;gt; M1.process_response --&amp;gt; Response; on exception: Underlying call --error--&amp;gt; M3 --&amp;gt; M2 --&amp;gt; M1 process_error --&amp;gt; Error&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="724.72" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent runtime mounts five middlewares in order: rate-limit, PII-redact-in, guardrail-eval, metrics, approval-gate. Every model and tool call flows through the chain forward, then through the reverse chain on response. Adding a new compliance log later is a single registration in the chain config — no agent code is touched.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="819.72" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-cutting concerns are configuration, not code, at the agent layer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Order is explicit and reviewable in one place.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each middleware is unit-testable against a synthetic call.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A long chain adds latency on every call — the chain itself is now a critical-path component.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misordered middleware (redaction after logging) silently leaks the thing it was supposed to hide.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Implicit dependencies between middlewares (one expects another&#39;s mutation) are hard to surface.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="868.72" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Cross-cutting concerns may not be coded directly into agent or orchestrator logic; they must register through the middleware contract so order is explicit and the chain is reviewable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="963.72" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple cross-cutting concerns need to fire on every model/tool/memory call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Order of operations between concerns is policy-relevant.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Teams need to add or remove concerns by configuration, not code.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1145.72" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Only one or two concerns exist and they can live as simple wrappers.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency budget cannot absorb a chain on every call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Concerns are too heterogeneous to fit a single (req, resp, err) contract.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1069.72" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; BaseMiddleware — contract with process_request, process_response, process_error.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; MiddlewareChain — orders middlewares; runs request phase forward, response phase reverse.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Runtime mount — wraps every model/tool/memory call through the chain.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1270.72" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; OpenTelemetry exporter — emits trace spans from each middleware&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Feature-flag service — toggles middlewares on or off without redeploy&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Policy-engine bridge — calls out to OPA or similar from guardrail middleware&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1194.72" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Redaction after logging — the logging middleware sits ahead of the redaction middleware, so sensitive content is written to logs before it is stripped.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hidden coupling — one middleware relies on a field another one adds, and removing or reordering the first breaks the second without any error.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Chain latency creep — each team registers one more middleware, and every model and tool call slows down because the whole chain runs on the critical path.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bypassed mount — a new tool or memory call is wired directly instead of through the runtime mount, and none of the cross-cutting concerns apply to it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1395.72" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Chain latency overhead — added ms per call&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Order incidents — bugs traced to misordered middleware&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Concern coverage — share of model/tool/memory calls touched by each registered middleware&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1319.72" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/victordibia/designing-multiagent-systems&quot;&gt;picoagents (Dibia, Designing Multi-Agent Systems)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langchain/middleware/overview&quot;&gt;LangChain Runnable middleware / LangGraph hooks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1615.72" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Input/Output Guardrails&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Decision Log&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;PII Redaction&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Rate Limiting&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Kill Switch&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Policy-as-Code Gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1444.72" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://multiagentbook.com/&quot;&gt;Designing Multi-Agent Systems&lt;/a&gt; — Victor Dibia, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/victordibia/designing-multiagent-systems&quot;&gt;victordibia/designing-multiagent-systems — picoagents middleware&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
