            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="loads" mermaidId="e:Runtime-&gt;Profile#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.51;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="loads" id="m16">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m12" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.51;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Treat agent identity as a structured profile object — persona, primary motivator, allowed actions, knowledge bindings — rather than a free-form role sentence in the system prompt.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1024.6" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A platform hosts many agent variants — customer-support persona, research-assistant persona, coding-partner persona — that share a runtime but differ in role, tone, motivator, allowed tools, and knowledge bindings. Each variant is currently defined by a free-form system prompt the team edits in markdown.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1024.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Free-form persona prompts collapse into a few failure shapes. Versioning is by git diff over prose, which is brittle. Two variants that should share a base persona accidentally diverge as engineers edit each in isolation. Knowledge bindings (which RAG corpus, which tools, which memory partition) live half in code, half in prose, with no single review surface. Swapping personas at runtime requires re-injecting the whole prompt rather than swapping a typed reference.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1130.6" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Personas need to be versionable as structured artifacts, not prose diffs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Shared persona components (motivator, tone) want to be inherited rather than copy-pasted.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Knowledge bindings (tools, RAG, memory) should be part of the persona, not adjacent code.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Runtime swap of persona must be cheap and unambiguous.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1168.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: model agent identity as a structured profile object — persona, motivator, action set, knowledge bindings — that the runtime loads as configuration, so persona is versioned, inheritable, and swappable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1293.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a Profile schema with fields: persona (role description), primary motivator (what drives this agent), action set (allowed tools), knowledge bindings (RAG sources, memory partitions, vector stores), behaviour parameters (tone, verbosity, model choice). Store profiles as configuration files. The runtime composes the active system prompt from the profile; runtime swap is by profile id. Inheritance: a base profile defines defaults; specialised profiles override fields. Distinct from [[role-prompting]] (one prose sentence) and from [[personality-variant-overlay]] (multiple voices over a single base).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1312.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Base profile --override fields--&amp;gt; Specialised profile --stored in--&amp;gt; Profile registry --load by id--&amp;gt; Inheritance resolver --&amp;gt; Prompt composer (persona, motivator, actions, knowledge bindings, behaviour params) --&amp;gt; Runtime system prompt + tool set&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1418.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A SaaS product offers three agent personas: a support-rep persona (warm, escalates to humans easily, billing-tools), a sales-rep persona (curious, asks fit questions, CRM-tools), and an internal-staff persona (terse, has admin-tools). All three inherit from a base profile defining tone defaults; each overrides motivator and action set. Switching a tenant from support-only to support+sales is a profile-id change.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1494.6" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Personas become versionable, inheritable, swappable artifacts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Knowledge bindings live in the same object as persona — one place to review.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-tenant or per-feature persona switching is a config change.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Schema rigidity can fight a persona that genuinely needs unique fields.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inheritance graphs grow tangled if not curated.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Profile fields can drift away from what the prompt actually demonstrates at runtime.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1562.6" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Agent identity must not be defined only by free-form prose in the system prompt; it is captured as a structured profile object the runtime loads as configuration.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1657.6" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple persona variants share a runtime but differ in role, tools, or knowledge.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Personas need to be versioned and inherited rather than copy-pasted.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Runtime persona swap is a product requirement.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1839.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Single persona, never changes, no inheritance need — prose prompt is fine.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Persona behaviour cannot be reduced to a schema without losing what matters.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Team will not maintain profile artifacts — they will drift from the running prompt.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1763.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Profile schema — fields for persona, motivator, action set, knowledge bindings, behaviour parameters&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Profile registry — versioned store of profile objects&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Prompt composer — builds the runtime system prompt from a profile&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inheritance resolver — applies overrides on a base profile&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1964.6" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Profile registry — versioned store of profile objects&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Prompt composer — builds the system prompt from a profile&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inheritance resolver — applies overrides on a base profile&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1888.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Profile-prompt drift — the profile file says one tone and action set, but the composed prompt or few-shot examples show another, and reviewers trust the file.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tangled inheritance — specialised profiles override overrides of a base, and nobody can tell which field value the runtime will actually load.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Schema straitjacket — a persona that needs a field the schema lacks hides it in free-text persona prose, and the single review surface is lost again.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale knowledge binding — a profile still points at a retired corpus or memory partition, and the agent answers from data the team thought was gone.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2127.6" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Profile drift rate — divergence between profile fields and observed agent behaviour&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Swap cycle time — time to switch tenants between profiles&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inheritance depth — average depth of profile inheritance graphs&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2013.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cxbxmxcx/Nexus&quot;&gt;Nexus (Lanham, AI Agents in Action) — profile/persona platform&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://help.openai.com/en/articles/8554397-creating-and-editing-gpts&quot;&gt;OpenAI Custom GPTs configuration objects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/overview&quot;&gt;Claude Skills package format&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2347.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;CAMEL Role-Playing&lt;/b&gt; — Role-prompting is the unstructured form; this is the structured form.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Personality Variant Overlay&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Skills&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Inner Committee&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Factory&lt;/b&gt; — An agent factory renders the per-instance persona/profile this pattern defines as part of one atomic template.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Simulated-User Rollout Evaluation&lt;/b&gt; — The simulated user is configured from a structured persona object — who is speaking, what they hold back, which tools they may use — rather than from a free-form role sentence.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2138.6" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.manning.com/books/ai-agents-in-action&quot;&gt;AI Agents in Action&lt;/a&gt; — Micheal Lanham, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cxbxmxcx/Nexus&quot;&gt;cxbxmxcx/Nexus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2529.6" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="agent-privilege-escalation" name="Agent Privilege Escalation">
