        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;The merchant exposes a structured feed and a checkout API; the agent discovers, compares, and buys with a scoped payment token.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="207.42" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Expose a service to agent buyers through a machine-readable product feed and an agent-initiated checkout API rather than a human click funnel, so an agent can discover, compare, and buy against a goal.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="300" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Shoppers increasingly delegate buying to agents: an agent is told to find and order something and fulfils the whole lifecycle of discovery, comparison, checkout, and payment from a goal rather than a sequence of clicks. A storefront built for humans presents this through rendered pages, search UX, and a checkout flow that assumes a person navigating a browser.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="300" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent does not browse a rendered page; it calls APIs, ingests structured feeds, and reasons across results. A catalog exposed only as human-facing HTML, with price and stock buried in scripts and a checkout that needs a person to click through, is effectively invisible to an agent, and a product the agent cannot parse is a product it never surfaces to its user. Yet maintaining a separate agent channel risks drifting out of sync with the human storefront&#39;s prices and inventory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="425" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A human storefront optimises for rendered pages and search-engine visibility; an agent consumer needs structured, queryable data and a programmatic checkout.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A goal-driven agent compares across options and transacts in one flow, so a multi-step click funnel either blocks it or forces brittle page-scraping.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A dedicated agent surface must stay consistent with the human storefront&#39;s live price and stock, or the agent transacts on stale data.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="444" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: publish a machine-readable catalog with real-time price and inventory and expose an agent-initiated checkout API that accepts a delegated, scoped payment, keeping the agent surface sourced from the same inventory and pricing as the human storefront.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="588" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Treat the agent as a first-class consumer of the service. Publish a structured product feed — titles, descriptions, images, price, stock, shipping, and policies — that an agent can ingest and reason over, kept current against the same inventory the human storefront uses. Accept agent-initiated checkout sessions through an API: the agent constructs a cart by calling the endpoint, and the buyer&#39;s authorisation arrives as a scoped payment token limited to one merchant, one amount, and a short expiry rather than raw card details. Adopting a shared protocol such as ACP or UCP lets many agents discover and transact against the surface without a bespoke integration per agent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="626" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Inventory/pricing source -&amp;gt; machine-readable product feed -&amp;gt; agent ingests and reasons -&amp;gt; agent-initiated checkout API(cart) -&amp;gt; scoped payment token -&amp;gt; order fulfilled.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="713" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An online retailer publishes a structured product feed with live prices and stock and stands up an agent checkout endpoint. When a shopper&#39;s agent is asked to find a specific espresso machine under a budget, it ingests the feed, compares options across merchants, and places the order through the API with a one-merchant payment token — a sale the retailer&#39;s human-only checkout would never have captured.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="827" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Products become discoverable to agent buyers instead of invisible, opening a channel the human click funnel cannot serve.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A shared protocol lets any conforming agent transact without a per-agent integration.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The scoped payment token keeps the merchant from handling raw card details while still completing an agent-driven sale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A second surface must be kept in sync with the human storefront, or agents buy on stale price and stock.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Exposing structured feeds and a checkout API widens the attack surface to scripted abuse and scraping at machine speed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Committing to an emerging commerce protocol couples the merchant to its evolution and to the agent platforms that speak it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="838" width="755" height="358" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent buyer cannot rely on scraping rendered pages; the merchant must publish structured, current product data and only accept agent checkout through a scoped, authenticated API, never exposing raw card details to the agent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="990" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A meaningful share of buyers delegate discovery and purchase to agents rather than browsing in person.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The catalog can be published as structured data and kept in sync with live price and stock.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A standard agentic-commerce protocol exists that the target agents already speak.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1210" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Sales depend on human browsing, merchandising, and persuasion that an agent channel cannot carry.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inventory and pricing cannot be kept current enough for an agent to transact on safely.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Regulatory or trust constraints require a human in the checkout loop for every purchase.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1115" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Product feed — structured catalog with title, description, price, stock, shipping, and policy fields&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inventory/pricing source — the single source the feed and checkout read from to stay current&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent checkout API — accepts agent-initiated cart and order sessions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scoped payment acceptor — takes a one-merchant, capped, short-lived token instead of raw card details&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Protocol adapter — conforms the surface to a shared standard (ACP, UCP) so many agents can transact&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1354" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Structured feed format (product schema / JSON) — machine-readable catalog an agent can ingest&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agentic commerce protocol (ACP, UCP) — standard discovery and checkout contract&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scoped payment token issuance — delegated, bounded payment instead of a card hand-off&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1240" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stale feed — the agent surface lags the human storefront, so the agent orders at a price or stock level that no longer holds.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Invisible catalog — products exist only as rendered HTML and never surface in an agent&#39;s results.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unbounded automation — the checkout API lacks rate and scope limits and is driven by scripts faster than a human channel ever would be.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1555" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Catalog coverage in agent results — share of products an agent can parse and surface&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Feed freshness — lag between storefront price/stock and the agent feed&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent-channel conversion versus the human storefront&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Abuse rate on the checkout API — scripted or out-of-scope sessions blocked&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1365" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.agenticcommerce.dev/&quot;&gt;Agentic Commerce Protocol (ACP)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — OpenAI and Stripe protocol behind Instant Checkout in ChatGPT; merchants expose product feeds and an agentic checkout API any compatible agent can call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/blog/google-ucp-merchant-guide-to-agentic-commerce&quot;&gt;Universal Commerce Protocol (UCP)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Google coalition protocol for agent-readable catalogs and checkout, surfacing through Search AI Mode and Gemini.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.shopify.com/blog/how-agentic-commerce-works&quot;&gt;Shopify agentic commerce (Shopify Catalog)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Shopify Catalog structures and syndicates product information across connected agent platforms in real time so shopping agents can transact.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1718" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Verifiable Purchase Mandate&lt;/b&gt; — The commerce surface accepts the charge; the purchase mandate is the signed user authorization the surface verifies before fulfilling.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Discovery&lt;/b&gt; — Tool discovery lets an agent find callable tools; the commerce surface is the provider-side mirror — designing the service so agent buyers can find and call it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Capability Manifest&lt;/b&gt; — Both publish a machine-readable description at a known location for agents to consume; the manifest advertises an agent&#39;s skills, the commerce surface advertises a merchant&#39;s catalog and checkout.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1509" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.openai.com/commerce/&quot;&gt;Agentic Commerce Protocol — OpenAI Commerce Documentation&lt;/a&gt; — OpenAI, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://commercetools.com/blog/google-ucp-merchant-guide-to-agentic-commerce&quot;&gt;Google UCP: Merchant Guide to Agentic Commerce&lt;/a&gt; — commercetools, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://gr4vy.com/posts/agentic-commerce-for-merchants-how-to-make-your-checkout-ai-agent-ready/&quot;&gt;Agentic commerce for merchants: how to make your checkout AI-agent-ready&lt;/a&gt; — GR4VY, 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1957" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="agent-resumption" name="Agent Resumption">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2445.1" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2445.1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
