        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:EXP-&gt;W#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.9;exitY=0;entryX=1;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.9;exitY=0;entryX=1;entryY=1;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="819.85" y="790.5" />
                <mxPoint x="819.85" y="695.95" />
                <mxPoint x="819.85" y="599.85" />
                <mxPoint x="819.85" y="519.25" />
                <mxPoint x="819.85" y="438.65" />
                <mxPoint x="819.85" y="358.05" />
                <mxPoint x="819.85" y="277.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:S-&gt;BEST#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.89;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.89;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="605.95" y="599.85" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Treat the agent&#39;s workflow (a graph of LLM-invoking nodes) as an artefact to search; use Monte Carlo Tree Search guided by an eval benchmark to discover the best workflow, then deploy it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="957.95" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building an agent for a repeatable task domain such as competitive coding, mathematical problem solving, or question answering, where each output can be scored automatically against a benchmark of known answers. They are choosing how to compose the agent out of named building blocks like a router, a planner, an ensembler, a reviewer, and a revise step, but no one on the team knows in advance which arrangement of these blocks will perform best on the target task.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="957.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When the workflow shape is chosen by a human designer, the choice is biased toward whatever patterns the designer has seen before, and exploring even a handful of alternatives by hand is slow and expensive. Each candidate workflow has to be implemented, run end-to-end against the benchmark, and compared, so the search space the team actually covers is a tiny fraction of the realistic compositions. The result is workflows that work but are almost certainly not the best the model and tools could deliver.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1063.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; There is a combinatorial space of workflows.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each workflow run costs money to evaluate.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Search needs a signal (benchmark scores) plus an explore/exploit policy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Workflows have to be representable as code or as a graph for search to work.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1120.95" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: treat the workflow itself as a searchable artefact and let MCTS guided by benchmark scores explore its shape, so that the deployed composition is discovered by measurement rather than by designer hunch.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1245.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Represent each candidate workflow as code or a graph of nodes (router, planner, ensemble, review, revise, executor). Use MCTS — selection by UCB-style scoring on past benchmark performance, expansion by code mutations or graph edits, simulation by running the workflow on the eval set, backpropagation of scores. After a search budget, deploy the best-scoring workflow. Use a library of operators (Ensemble, Review, Revise) to constrain the search space.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1264.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Search: workflow_graph -&amp;gt; mutate -&amp;gt; run on eval set -&amp;gt; score -&amp;gt; MCTS update -&amp;gt; repeat -&amp;gt; best_workflow -&amp;gt; deploy.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1370.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research lab has built six different agent workflows for a maths-olympiad benchmark — chain-of-thought, debate, planner-executor, and so on — and none consistently wins. Hand-tuning the next variant is slow and biased toward what the team already knows. They treat each workflow as a graph of LLM-invoking nodes and let an MCTS search explore variations, scoring each candidate against the benchmark. After a few thousand evaluations the search returns a workflow shape no one on the team had drafted, and it ships.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1427.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Discovers non-obvious workflow compositions a human designer would not try.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cheaper smaller models reach larger-model performance on some benchmarks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The search artefact is a reusable, inspectable workflow.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval set quality bounds discovered workflow quality.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compute-intensive: many workflow evaluations per search.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Risk of overfitting to the eval set; held-out eval needed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1495.95" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No workflow may be deployed that was not measured against the held-out eval set; ad-hoc human edits to a discovered workflow re-enter the search.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1609.95" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; You have a stable eval benchmark that can score full workflows end-to-end.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Designer bias toward familiar patterns is leaving real workflow improvements on the table.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compute budget for many workflow trials is available and amortised across many future runs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1772.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; No reliable eval exists to guide the search.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Workflow domain is small enough to enumerate by hand more cheaply than running MCTS.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The deployment target changes faster than search can converge on a stable workflow.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1715.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Workflow representation — code or graph encoding of router, planner, ensemble, review, revise nodes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mutation operator — proposes edits (swap node, add review, change ensemble width) to expand the search frontier&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval harness — runs a candidate workflow end-to-end against the benchmark and returns a score&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; MCTS controller — UCB selection over visited workflows, backpropagation of benchmark scores&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Held-out validator — re-scores the best workflow on an unseen split before deployment&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1897.95" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Benchmark dataset with ground-truth answers — the only signal the search trusts&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — invoked once per node per evaluation run, so the cheapest viable tier is normal&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Workflow runner / orchestrator — executes a candidate graph reproducibly inside the eval loop&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1840.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Benchmark overfit — the search finds a workflow that scores well on the eval set by exploiting its quirks, and it does worse on real traffic.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Weak eval ceiling — the eval set misses the cases users care about, so the search optimises hard for the wrong target.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Budget burn — every expansion runs a full workflow over the benchmark, and the search spends its compute before it leaves the familiar region.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hand-edited deploy — an engineer tweaks the discovered workflow before shipping and skips the held-out check, so the deployed graph was never measured.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2098.95" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Best-workflow benchmark score vs hand-designed baseline — the headline lift the search has to justify&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Held-out vs search-set score gap — flags overfitting of the discovered workflow to the search benchmark&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evaluations consumed per point of score lift — search efficiency under a fixed compute budget&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Operator library coverage in the surviving workflow — which mutations actually contributed to wins&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost per inference of the deployed workflow — the bill the discovered shape will run at in production&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1965.95" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/FoundationAgents/AFlow&quot;&gt;AFlow (DeepWisdom + HKUST(GZ))&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — MCTS over code-represented workflows; outperforms hand-designed baselines by 5.7% average.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2318.95" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Eval Harness&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Eval as Contract&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Language Agent Tree Search&lt;/b&gt; — LATS searches reasoning trees; AFlow searches workflow graphs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Spec-First Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Best-of-N Sampling&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2185.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.10762&quot;&gt;AFlow: Automating Agentic Workflow Generation&lt;/a&gt; — Zhang et al., 2024&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2424.95" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
