        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Biz-&gt;VDB#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.9;entryX=0;entryY=0.51;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.9;entryX=0;entryY=0.51;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="950.05" y="398.35" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Biz-&gt;Cache#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.67;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.51;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.67;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.51;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="950.05" y="579.7" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Split an LLM application into a CPU-bound business microservice (retrieval, prompt assembly, orchestration) and a GPU-bound LLM microservice (only model.generate behind REST), so each tier scales on its own hardware budget.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="675.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A production LLM application bundles retrieval, prompt assembly, post-processing, business logic, and the LLM inference call into a single service. The service autoscales as a unit. The LLM call needs GPU; the rest does not. The unified deployment pays GPU prices to autoscale the CPU-only parts.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="675.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Bundled deployments waste expensive hardware. As traffic grows, the autoscaler adds whole GPU pods to handle CPU-bound spikes in prompt assembly and retrieval, while genuine GPU-bound spikes drag the entire service. Maintenance is coupled: bumping the model means redeploying the business logic; bumping the retrieval code means restarting GPU pods. The single service is a strict generalisation that loses on cost, scaling, and deploy velocity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="800.85" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM inference needs GPU; retrieval and prompt assembly do not.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Independent scaling axes (RPS, token throughput) have different load shapes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Coupled deploys slow both teams; decoupled deploys let model and business iterate independently.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; REST boundary adds one network hop per request — a measurable latency cost.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="800.85" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: split the application into a CPU business service (retrieval, prompt assembly, orchestration) and a GPU LLM service exposing only model.generate over REST, so each tier scales on its own hardware budget and is deployed on its own cadence.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="963.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define the LLM microservice&#39;s contract as a single REST endpoint: generate(prompt, params) → completion. Run it on GPU autoscaling on token-throughput metrics. Run everything else — retrieval, prompt templating, business logic, orchestration, output post-processing — in the CPU business service that calls the LLM service over REST. Bound the LLM service&#39;s tail latency with batching, queueing, and admission control. The business service can use multiple LLM service instances (different models, different providers) behind the same contract.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="944.85" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;User request -&amp;gt; CPU business service (retrieval via vector DB/cache, prompt assembly, orchestration) --REST generate(prompt, params)--&amp;gt; GPU LLM service (batching, queueing, admission control; scales on token throughput) --completion--&amp;gt; business service (post-processing) -&amp;gt; response&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1088.85" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A RAG support platform deploys a CPU FastAPI business service handling retrieval (Qdrant), prompt assembly, and tenant routing, plus a separate GPU LLM service hosting a fine-tuned model behind TGI. Traffic spike: CPU pods scale 5x for retrieval load, GPU pods scale 2x for inference load. A model swap (Llama-3-8B to Llama-3-70B) is a deploy in the LLM service only; the business service is unchanged.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1126.85" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; GPU pods size to GPU-bound load only; CPU pods to CPU-bound load only.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Model swaps and business-logic changes deploy independently.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple LLM providers can sit behind one contract without business-service changes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; One extra network hop per LLM call — latency cost.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Two services to operate, deploy, monitor.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-service tracing required to make end-to-end latency visible.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1232.85" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An LLM application must not bundle GPU inference with CPU business logic in one service when scaling and deploy cadence diverge; the LLM call lives behind its own service contract.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1270.85" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM inference and business logic have diverging scaling profiles.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Model swaps should not force business-logic redeploys.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple LLM providers may sit behind one contract.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1509.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Very low traffic — one service is simpler and within budget.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency budget cannot absorb one network hop.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Team has no capacity to operate two services and cross-service tracing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1376.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Business service — CPU-bound retrieval, prompt assembly, orchestration&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM service — GPU-bound model.generate behind REST&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; REST contract — generate(prompt, params) -&amp;gt; completion&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-service tracing — propagates request IDs for end-to-end visibility&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1634.85" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM serving runtime (TGI, vLLM, SageMaker)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; REST framework for business service (FastAPI, Express)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; OpenTelemetry — cross-service tracing&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1501.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Leaky contract — business logic such as prompt templating creeps into the GPU service, and a retrieval change once again forces a GPU redeploy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hop latency pile-up — an orchestration step calls the LLM service many times in sequence, and the extra network hop per call adds up to a slow response.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Blind spot between services — without cross-service tracing, a slow request cannot be pinned on retrieval, queueing or generation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unbounded queue — the LLM service has no admission control, a traffic spike fills its queue, and tail latency climbs for every caller.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1778.85" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; GPU utilisation — share of GPU pod time on real inference&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-service tail latency — added ms from the network hop&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Deploy decoupling — independent deploy frequency per service&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1626.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.packtpub.com/en-us/product/llm-engineers-handbook-9781836200079&quot;&gt;LLM Engineer&amp;#x27;s Handbook (Iusztin, Labonne, Packt 2024) — Twin business/inference services&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://huggingface.co/docs/text-generation-inference/en/index&quot;&gt;Hugging Face TGI / vLLM / SageMaker deployments as standalone LLM services&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/overview&quot;&gt;Most production LLM platforms (Anthropic, OpenAI) — model inference behind API&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1998.85" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;FTI LLM Pipeline Split&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Adapter&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Augmented LLM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Prompt Caching&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Rate Limiting&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Channel-Decoupled Agent Core&lt;/b&gt; — Both split an agent system along a boundary so each side evolves on its own: that pattern splits CPU business logic from GPU inference, this splits the channel-agnostic core from per-channel adapters.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1751.85" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.packtpub.com/en-us/product/llm-engineers-handbook-9781836200079&quot;&gt;LLM Engineer&amp;#x27;s Handbook&lt;/a&gt; — Paul Iusztin, Maxime Labonne, 2024&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.decodingai.com/p/architect-scalable-and-cost-effective&quot;&gt;Architect scalable and cost-effective LLM &amp;amp; RAG inference pipelines&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2180.85" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="camel-role-playing" name="CAMEL Role-Playing">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2417.05" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2417.05" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CAMEL Role-Playing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Multi-Agent &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; experimental &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Inception Prompting, AI-User AI-Assistant&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
