        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Every identifier is resolved against authoritative master data before it enters an action; the model supplies intent, the resolver supplies the identifier of record.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1140.6" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Require the agent to resolve every business identifier it uses — SKU, account, supplier, customer — through an authoritative lookup against the system of record, rather than emitting the identifier from the model&#39;s parametric memory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1215.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent acts over enterprise systems whose entities are identified by exact codes — general-ledger accounts, stock-keeping units, supplier numbers, customer ids, project codes — that carry no meaning the model could infer and that must match a record exactly to be valid. The model is fluent enough to produce strings that look like these codes, and a code that is plausible but wrong points at the wrong account or the wrong part. The authoritative values live in master data the model was never trained on and that changes after training.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1215.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Asked for an identifier it does not have, a model will supply one from parametric memory that is well-formed and confidently wrong — a close-enough part number, an account code from a similar company, a supplier id that no longer exists. In an enterprise system there is no credit for close: a transaction posted to a plausible-but-wrong GL account is a real error, not an approximation. Because the fabricated identifier is syntactically valid, downstream format validation often accepts it, and the mistake surfaces only later as a misposting or a failed integration.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1340.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The model is good at mapping a vague reference such as &#39;the Berlin office supplier&#39; to intent, but bad at producing the exact code that intent corresponds to.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Master data is authoritative and current; the model&#39;s parametric knowledge of identifiers is neither.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A fabricated identifier is often well-formed, so format validation passes and the error escapes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Calling a lookup on every identifier costs latency and tool calls; skipping it risks silent corruption of a system of record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identifiers change after the model is trained, so even a once-correct memorised code drifts out of date.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1397.6" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: treat any identifier the model produces as an unresolved reference until it is confirmed against the authoritative store, and require the agent to call a lookup tool that returns the canonical id — or no match — before that identifier is used in an action, so a write to the system of record can only ever name an entity that exists.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1522.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Give the agent a resolver tool over master data that takes a description or a candidate identifier and returns the canonical id with a confidence, or an explicit no-match. Require every identifier that will enter an action — especially a write — to pass through this resolver first; the model proposes intent (&#39;post to the marketing-travel account for the Munich entity&#39;) and the resolver returns the exact code, rather than the model emitting the code directly. Treat the resolver&#39;s output, not the model&#39;s text, as the identifier of record. On a no-match or a low-confidence result the agent asks for clarification or halts rather than guessing. Once an identifier is resolved, the rest of the operation runs against that canonical id deterministically. Where volume is high, the resolver can present a fetched candidate set the model selects among, so the model chooses among real entities rather than inventing one.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1636.6" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Model --(reference: description or candidate id)--&amp;gt; resolver tool --(query)--&amp;gt; master data. Resolver --&amp;gt; {canonical_id + confidence | no-match}. On match: action uses canonical_id. On no-match / low confidence: clarify or halt. Model never supplies the identifier of record directly.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1666.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent processes supplier invoices into an ERP. A scanned invoice reads &#39;Müller Bürobedarf, Munich&#39;, and the agent&#39;s first instinct is to fill in a supplier number that looks right from similar vendors. Instead it calls a master-data resolver with the name and address; the resolver returns the one canonical supplier id on file, or reports no confident match. When a new vendor has no record, the agent stops and flags it for onboarding rather than posting to a guessed account. Only resolved, real identifiers ever reach the posting step.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1894.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Writes to the system of record can only name entities that exist, removing a whole class of confident-but-wrong errors.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The boundary between fuzzy intent (the model) and exact identity (master data) is explicit and testable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resolution against current master data tolerates identifiers that changed after the model was trained.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A no-match becomes a visible clarification or halt instead of a silent misposting found weeks later.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A lookup on every identifier adds latency and tool calls, which matters in high-volume batch work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The resolver itself can return the wrong entity when the description is ambiguous or master data is dirty.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Building and maintaining a resolver over messy master data is real integration work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Over-eager resolution can mask a genuine data-entry problem a human should have seen.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1810.6" width="755" height="396" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent must not use a self-generated identifier in an action against the system of record: every GL account, SKU, supplier, or customer id must be confirmed by the resolver tool first, and on a no-match or low-confidence result the agent must not guess but must clarify or halt.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2076.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent writes to or acts on a system whose entities are identified by exact codes that must match a record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong-but-well-formed identifiers would pass format validation and corrupt downstream data.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Authoritative master data exists and can be queried at action time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identifiers change after the model&#39;s training cut-off.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2220.6" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The task is free-form generation with no identifiers that must match a record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is no authoritative store to resolve against, so a lookup cannot confirm anything.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The identifiers are already supplied verbatim by a trusted upstream system and never authored by the model.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2201.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Master-data resolver — tool that maps a description or candidate id to the canonical id or a no-match&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Candidate set — the real entities the resolver returns for the model to select among when volume is high&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence threshold — the line below which the agent clarifies or halts instead of using a result&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No-match handler — routes unresolved references to clarification, onboarding, or a halt&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2383.6" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Master-data lookup API — authoritative query over GL accounts, SKUs, suppliers, and customers&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fuzzy matcher / entity-resolution service — maps free-text references to candidate canonical records&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; System-of-record write API — accepts only resolved canonical identifiers&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2345.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;GUARDRAILS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Write-path resolver enforcement — no identifier reaches a system-of-record write without passing the resolver&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Low-confidence halt — results below threshold force clarification instead of action&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2565.6" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Resolver skipped — the model writes an account code from memory into a write call, format checks pass, and the posting lands on the wrong ledger.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ambiguous match accepted — the description fits two suppliers, the resolver returns one with moderate confidence, and the agent proceeds instead of asking.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Dirty master data — duplicate or retired records in the system of record make the resolver return a stale id.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Masked data problem — the resolver quietly maps a bad input to some valid entity, hiding an upstream data-entry error a human should have fixed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2489.6" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Fabricated-identifier rate — action identifiers not produced by the resolver; the target is zero&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No-match handling rate — share of no-match results that led to a clarify/halt rather than a guess&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misposting rate — entries posted to a wrong-but-valid identifier, caught in reconciliation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resolution latency — added time per identifier, watched in high-volume batch runs&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2690.6" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/grounding-an-agent-with-data/learn-the-basics-of-grounding&quot;&gt;Salesforce Agentforce — Grounding&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Agents are grounded in CRM records so entity references resolve against data rather than model memory.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.starburst.io/blog/agent-grounding-the-missing-discipline-in-enterprise-ai/&quot;&gt;Starburst&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Frames entity resolution and verified identifier grounding as a prerequisite discipline for enterprise agents.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.rudderstack.com/blog/why-ai-agent-hallucinates-on-your-data&quot;&gt;RudderStack&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Describes grounding agents on governed enterprise data so they resolve identifiers instead of hallucinating them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2709.6" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agentic RAG&lt;/b&gt; — RAG retrieves relevant documents; canonical-entity grounding resolves exact identifiers. Retrieval finds context, resolution pins identity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;CRAG&lt;/b&gt; — Corrective RAG checks retrieved evidence quality; this checks that an identifier corresponds to a real master-data record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Chain of Verification&lt;/b&gt; — Chain-of-verification re-checks claims; here the identifier is verified against the authoritative store before use.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;JSON-Only Action Schema&lt;/b&gt; — A strict action schema validates an identifier&#39;s shape; resolution validates that the entity actually exists.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Citation Attribution&lt;/b&gt; — Citation attribution grounds prose in sources; this grounds identifiers in master data — the same discipline applied to exact codes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tenant-Scoped Tool Binding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Risk-Tiered Action Autonomy&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Affordance Grounding Before Action&lt;/b&gt; — Both ground a proposed action against an authority before acting; canonical-entity-grounding resolves business identifiers, the affordance gate resolves physical feasibility against the scene.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Verify-Before-Cite Resolution Gate&lt;/b&gt; — Entity grounding resolves identifiers the agent uses in actions against a system of record; this gate resolves authorities the model cites in output against an external index.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Table-Augmented Generation&lt;/b&gt; — Grounding resolves the identifiers a TAG query filters and joins on, so synthesis builds plans over authoritative ids rather than model-emitted ones.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Semantic-Layer Query Guardrail&lt;/b&gt; — Grounding replaces model-emitted identifiers with authoritative lookups; this pattern replaces model-authored metric definitions and SQL with vetted ones, so the two together bound both the entities and the measures an agent&#39;s data query may reference.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2834.6" width="755" height="491" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s19" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.starburst.io/blog/agent-grounding-the-missing-discipline-in-enterprise-ai/&quot;&gt;Agent Grounding: The Missing Discipline in Enterprise AI&lt;/a&gt; — Starburst, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.06002&quot;&gt;Deterministic Legal Agents: A Canonical Primitive API for Auditable Reasoning over Temporal Knowledge Graphs&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://trailhead.salesforce.com/content/learn/modules/grounding-an-agent-with-data/learn-the-basics-of-grounding&quot;&gt;Ground an Agent with Data — Salesforce Trailhead&lt;/a&gt; — Salesforce, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.rudderstack.com/blog/why-ai-agent-hallucinates-on-your-data&quot;&gt;Why Your AI Agent Hallucinates on Your Data&lt;/a&gt; — RudderStack, 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2948.6" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="cascading-agent-failures" name="Cascading Agent Failures">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2793.4" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2793.4" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cascading Agent Failures&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Anti-Patterns &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; deprecated &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Kaskadierende Ausfälle, ASI08, Multi-Agent Cascade&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="1084.4" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Agent A emits bad output → Agent B treats as fact" mermaidId="n:Trigger" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#fee;strokeColor=#c33;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Agent A emits bad output → Agent B treats as fact" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#fee;strokeColor=#c33;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="654.1" x="80.5" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Recognise as anti-pattern?" mermaidId="n:Bad" mermaidBaseStyle="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Recognise as anti-pattern?" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="491.35" width="491.35" x="161.1" y="316.2" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Harm propagates" mermaidId="n:Harm" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#fee;strokeColor=#c33;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Harm propagates" id="m2">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=#fee;strokeColor=#c33;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="282.1" x="65.0" y="914.5" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Apply mitigation pattern" mermaidId="n:Mitigate" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Apply mitigation pattern" id="m3">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="367.35" x="424.6" y="914.5" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Risk bounded" mermaidId="n:Safe" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Risk bounded" id="m4">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="240.25" x="488.15" y="1075.7" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Trigger-&gt;Bad#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m5">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m0" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="no" mermaidId="e:Bad-&gt;Harm#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.16;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="no" id="m6">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.16;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m2">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="206.05" y="860.25" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="yes" mermaidId="e:Bad-&gt;Mitigate#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.84;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="yes" id="m7">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.84;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="609.05" y="860.25" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Mitigate-&gt;Safe#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m8">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: build a multi-agent system where one agent&#39;s failure or hallucination propagates as input to peers, until the whole system has drifted.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1204.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A multi-agent system has agents that consume each other&#39;s outputs — a researcher feeds a writer, a writer feeds an editor, a critic feeds a planner. Each agent treats its inbound messages as if they were trustworthy peer outputs. There is no circuit-breaker between agents.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1204.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A localised failure — a hallucinated fact, a corrupted memory write, a tool error misinterpreted as success — propagates through the message graph. Each downstream agent integrates the failure into its own reasoning and emits a confidently-wrong output that the next agent in turn treats as input. The system fails as a unit, not as individual agents; classical per-agent retries do not help because the inputs are themselves poisoned.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1310.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-agent systems gain throughput by delegating; eliminating inter-agent trust eliminates the gain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Failures in one agent are silent at the message layer — bad outputs look syntactically valid.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Synchronous fan-out amplifies single failures into multi-agent failures within one trace.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1329.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: introduce circuit-breakers, output validation, and confidence signalling at agent boundaries; cap propagation depth; fall back to single-agent or human paths when a downstream check fails.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1473.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Don&#39;t. Apply per-edge validation between agents — type checks, schema validation, confidence thresholds. Use external-critic or agent-as-judge on intermediate messages, not just final output. Cap retry-fan-out so one root failure cannot recursively spawn more agents. See unbounded-subagent-spawn and unbounded-loop for related shapes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1473.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: agent A fails or hallucinates -&amp;gt; message to agent B -&amp;gt; B integrates and emits wrong output -&amp;gt; agent C -&amp;gt; whole system drifts. Corrected: agent A -&amp;gt; per-edge validation (schema, type, confidence, critic) -&amp;gt; agent B -&amp;gt; capped retry fan-out.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1579.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research-pipeline of researcher → drafter → editor agents produces a customer-facing report. The researcher hallucinates a citation. The drafter integrates it with confident phrasing. The editor polishes the prose and adds three more references that &#39;support&#39; the hallucinated one. The report ships. Postmortem: no inter-agent validation; the editor&#39;s job was prose, but the failure was factual, and no edge in the graph was responsible for catching it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1617.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: passing messages straight between agents is simple and makes the multi-agent system fast to build.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team place validation on every edge, not only on the final output.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A single bad upstream output corrupts every downstream agent that touches it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-agent uptime is irrelevant; system uptime is the product of trust hops.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Forensics requires walking the message graph, not reading a single agent&#39;s logs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1723.4" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No useful constraint; the missing constraint is per-edge validation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1780.4" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Never. Cite when reviewing multi-agent topology.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Add per-edge validation, confidence thresholds, and circuit-breakers between agents.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bound retry depth so root failures cannot recursively expand the agent graph.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2000.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Any multi-agent system where outputs are consumed by other agents without validation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Systems where downstream agents have side effects that depend on upstream correctness.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Long-running pipelines where one bad message can pollute downstream memory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1872.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent message graph — defines who-feeds-whom in the multi-agent system&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inter-agent message channel — carries outputs from one agent&#39;s tool surface to the next agent&#39;s input&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-agent retry layer — local resilience that does not see cross-agent corruption&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing edge validator — would check message validity at each agent-to-agent boundary&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2125.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-agent orchestrator — runs the agent graph (AutoGen, CrewAI, LangGraph)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Edge validator — the missing pre-handoff check on each inter-agent message&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence signal — the missing metadata that would let downstream agents discount low-confidence input&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1997.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Confident relay — one agent hallucinates a fact, and each downstream agent builds on it and passes on a more confident wrong answer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Error read as success — a tool error is taken as success by one agent, and peers act on a result that never existed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Retry fan-out — retries on poisoned input spawn more agents, which spread the same bad input further through the system.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2288.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Cascade depth — number of agents that integrated a single root failure before any catch&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Edge-validation coverage — fraction of inter-agent edges that run a structural or semantic check&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mean blast radius per upstream failure — average count of corrupted downstream messages&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-agent vs system uptime gap — how much worse the system MTBF is than per-agent MTBF&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2141.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://genai.owasp.org/resource/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-applications-for-2026/&quot;&gt;OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications 2026 — ASI08&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Reported AutoGen / CrewAI multi-agent runs where a hallucinated researcher claim propagates to a polished, confidently-wrong final report&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2470.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Unbounded Subagent Spawn&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Unbounded Loop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-as-a-Judge&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Subagent Isolation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Memory Poisoning&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Insecure Inter-Agent Channel&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Bullwhip Effect&lt;/b&gt; — Cascading failures propagate one agent&#39;s error to peers; the bullwhip amplifies a legitimate demand signal through the agents&#39; own ordering policy, not an error.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Ghost Delegation&lt;/b&gt; — Cascading failures propagate an error across agents; ghost delegation fires no error at all, the handoff disappears so nothing triggers recovery.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hidden Distributed Monolith (Multi-Agent)&lt;/b&gt; — No failure isolation means one agent&#39;s failure is not contained — a direct consequence of the hidden coupling this anti-pattern names.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2285.4" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://neuraltrust.ai/blog/owasp-top-10-for-agentic-applications-2026&quot;&gt;OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications 2026 — ASI08&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.heise.de/hintergrund/KI-Sicherheitsrisiken-OWASP-Top-10-for-Agentic-AI-Applications-11280779.html&quot;&gt;heise online — Kaskadierende Ausfälle in agentischen Systemen&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2614.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="cdc-vector-sync" name="CDC-Driven Vector Sync">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1946" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="1946" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CDC-Driven Vector Sync&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Retrieval &amp;amp; RAG &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; mature &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Change-Data-Capture RAG Sync, Event-Driven Vector Index Update&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Source-of-truth store" mermaidId="n:Src" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=10;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Source-of-truth store" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;shape=cylinder3;boundedLbl=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=10;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
