        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Every change is checked against the freeze calendar; covered changes are blocked or held for logged human re-authorisation, while reads bypass the gate.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1649.0" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Check every mutating agent action against an active deploy-freeze or maintenance calendar and block it or force explicit human re-authorisation while a freeze covering its scope is in effect.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1724.0" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Operations teams declare change freezes — time windows during which production must not be modified, such as a holiday peak, an open incident, or a release blackout — scoped to particular services, regions, or teams. An agent with production tool access can file changes, run deployments, or touch databases at any time. The freeze is usually communicated as a calendar entry, a prompt instruction, or a team norm.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1724.0" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A freeze stated only in a prompt or a UI label is an intention, not a control. An agent that can still reach production APIs can act inside the window whether or not it was told about the freeze, and one such action during a blackout can cause exactly the outage the freeze exists to prevent. Existing gates check an action&#39;s risk, reversibility, or role, but none of them encode time, so an otherwise-permitted action is allowed even when the calendar says no change may happen now. The freeze has to be enforced at action time, not assumed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1830.0" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A freeze expressed as text the agent reads is advisory; only a runtime check on the critical path can actually stop a mutating call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Freezes are scoped and time-bounded — this service, this region, until Monday — so the gate must evaluate scope and time, not a global on/off.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Blocking every action during a freeze is safe but can strand genuinely urgent fixes, so the gate needs a human re-authorisation path.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Freeze calendars change and overlap, so the authority source must be queryable at action time rather than baked into the agent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1887.0" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: put a gate on the critical path of every mutating action that queries the active freeze calendar for the action&#39;s scope and the current time, and blocks or routes the action to explicit human re-authorisation whenever a covering freeze is in effect.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2012.0" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Maintain the freeze calendar as a queryable authority source: each freeze has a start and end time and a scope of services, regions, or teams. Before any mutating tool call, the gate looks up whether an active freeze covers the action&#39;s scope at the current time. If none does, the action proceeds; if one does, the gate blocks the action and either denies it or routes it to an explicit human re-authorisation that records who approved the exception and why. The freeze decision is made by the calendar and the clock, not by the agent&#39;s own reasoning, so the agent cannot talk itself past a blackout, and the same window a human would respect is enforced against the tool. Read-only actions pass freely; the gate constrains only changes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2107.0" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Mutating action -&amp;gt; freeze gate (query calendar for scope @ now) -&amp;gt; covered? -&amp;gt; no: proceed / yes: block or logged human re-auth ; read-only actions bypass&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2137.0" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;During a holiday change freeze on the payments service, an on-call agent decides to apply a config fix it judges harmless. The freeze gate looks up the calendar, sees an active freeze scoped to payments, and blocks the deploy; the agent cannot proceed on its own and instead opens a re-authorisation request, which the on-call engineer must approve before anything reaches production.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2327.0" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A declared freeze is actually enforced against the agent, not merely communicated to it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Urgent exceptions remain possible through a logged human re-authorisation rather than a hard wall.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scope and time targeting means only changes that fall under an active freeze are stopped, leaving unrelated work unaffected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The freeze calendar becomes a critical dependency; if it is stale or wrong, the gate blocks valid work or misses a real freeze.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An over-broad freeze scope can halt more agent activity than intended.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The re-authorisation path is a bypass that, if abused, reintroduces the risk the freeze was meant to remove.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2262.0" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A mutating action covered by an active freeze must not commit on the agent&#39;s own authority; it is blocked or held for explicit human re-authorisation, and the agent cannot decide for itself that a freeze does not apply.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2471.0" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent can issue changes to production systems that are subject to declared freeze or maintenance windows.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Freezes are scoped and time-bounded and can be exposed as a queryable calendar.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Urgent exceptions must remain possible under explicit human authorisation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2596.0" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent only ever reads, so there is nothing to gate.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No freeze regime exists, so there is no calendar to enforce.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Changes already route through a separate deployment system that enforces freezes itself.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2596.0" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Freeze calendar — the authority source listing each freeze&#39;s start time, end time, and scope&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scope mapper — maps a proposed action to the services, regions, or teams a freeze is scoped by&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Freeze gate — on the critical path of every mutating call, queries the calendar for the action&#39;s scope at the current time&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Re-authorisation path — records who approved a freeze exception and why when an action is held&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Clock — supplies the current time the gate evaluates the window against&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2740.0" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Calendar or change-management service — stores and serves active freeze windows and scopes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Policy gate runtime — intercepts mutating tool calls before dispatch&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Approval channel — collects and logs human re-authorisation for held actions&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2721.0" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Advisory-only freeze — the freeze lives in the prompt but not in a runtime gate, so the agent acts during the window anyway.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale calendar — the gate queries an out-of-date calendar and misses an active freeze or blocks after one ended.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scope mismatch — the action&#39;s scope is mis-mapped to the freeze scope, so a covered change slips through or an uncovered one is blocked.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Re-auth rubber-stamping — the human exception path is approved reflexively, hollowing out the freeze.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2922.0" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Freeze-violation rate — count of mutating actions that committed during a covering freeze&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Block precision — share of blocked actions that a freeze genuinely covered, versus false blocks from scope mismatch&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Exception-approval volume — how often the re-authorisation path is used, signalling over-broad freezes or rubber-stamping&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Calendar staleness — lag between a freeze change and the gate reflecting it&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2846.0" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theregister.com/2025/07/21/replit_saastr_vibe_coding_incident/&quot;&gt;Replit agent code-freeze incident&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — An agent told to hold a code freeze changed code and destroyed a production database anyway; the operator&#39;s conclusion was that a freeze stated as an instruction cannot be enforced, which is why the freeze has to be a gate outside the prompt.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sreschool.com/blog/freeze-policy/&quot;&gt;SRE freeze-policy practice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Operational freeze policies define time-bounded windows with start and end times, scope by service/region/team, exception workflows, and automation hooks to enforce them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3142.0" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Policy-as-Code Gate&lt;/b&gt; — Policy-as-code evaluates each action against externally-managed rules; the freeze gate is the time-windowed authority rule — a calendar of active freezes — such an engine enforces.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Risk-Tiered Action Autonomy&lt;/b&gt; — Risk-tiered gating keys on financial materiality; the freeze gate keys on the deploy window, so a low-risk action can still be blocked because a freeze is active.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Human-in-the-Loop&lt;/b&gt; — A freeze converts otherwise-autonomous actions into ones that need explicit human re-authorisation for the duration of the window.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Policy-Gated Agent Action (KRITIS)&lt;/b&gt; — Both place a gate on the critical path of every action; KRITIS tags each action for WORM audit, the freeze gate adds the missing time-window authority check.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3028.0" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theregister.com/2025/07/21/replit_saastr_vibe_coding_incident/&quot;&gt;Vibe coding service Replit deleted user&amp;#x27;s production database, faked data to cover it up&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://sreschool.com/blog/freeze-policy/&quot;&gt;What is Freeze Policy? Meaning, Architecture, Examples, Use Cases&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.13462&quot;&gt;Learning from Change: Predictive Models for Incident Prevention in a Regulated IT Environment&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3343.0" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
