        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:P3-&gt;Out#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Decompose a long, multi-disciplinary task into ordered phases; within each phase, run a paired-role chat between two agents until the phase artefact is signed off; pass the artefact to the next phase.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1339.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is using agents to carry out a long task — build a small program, prepare a regulatory brief, produce a multi-section report — that naturally breaks into several disciplines that have to happen in order: requirements, design, implementation, testing, documentation. The whole task is too long to fit in one agent&#39;s loop, and each discipline benefits from focused two-agent dialogue rather than a solo monologue.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1339.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A single agent loop loses focus halfway through, forgetting the early requirements by the time it is writing tests. A broadcast multi-agent chat where every agent sees every message tangles design discussion with code review and blows up context windows. Flat prompt-chaining — one prompt feeds the next — cannot host the multi-turn back-and-forth a discipline like design review needs. The team needs structure across the disciplines but flexibility inside each one.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1445.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Each discipline benefits from focused two-agent dialogue.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Context windows blow up if every agent sees every chat.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phase-to-phase hand-off needs a clean artefact contract.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Termination of a phase has to be explicit, not vibes-based.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1502.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: arrange the work as an ordered chain of phases where each phase is a paired-role chat with a completion predicate and a typed artefact handoff, so that micro-flexibility inside a phase coexists with macro-discipline across phases.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1608.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define an ordered chain of phases. Each phase has (a) a defined input artefact, (b) two role-paired agents (e.g. designer + coder, coder + tester), (c) a phase-specific completion predicate, (d) a defined output artefact. Within a phase, the two agents converse multi-turn; the completion predicate ends the phase; the artefact moves to the next phase. The chain is the macro-control; the chat is the micro-control.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1646.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Phase_1 (Role_A &amp;lt;-&amp;gt; Role_B) -&amp;gt; artefact_1 -&amp;gt; Phase_2 (Role_B &amp;lt;-&amp;gt; Role_C) -&amp;gt; artefact_2 -&amp;gt; ... -&amp;gt; final_artefact.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1733.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is using an agent system to ship a small internal tool. A single agent loop forgets the requirements by the time it&#39;s writing tests, and a free-for-all multi-agent chat tangles design discussions with code review. They structure the work as a Chat-Chain: phase 1 is two agents pairing on requirements until a spec is signed off, phase 2 is two agents pairing on design against that spec, phase 3 is implementation, and so on. Each phase&#39;s signed-off artefact becomes the only context that crosses into the next.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1809.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Clear macro-progression with chat-level flexibility inside each phase.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Keeps each phase&#39;s context tight; only the artefact crosses the boundary.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Auditable artefact trail per phase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Designing the chain (phases + completion predicates) is the architecture problem.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sequential by construction; parallelism inside a phase requires extra design.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong phase decomposition forces agents into awkward role pairings.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1839.25" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Agents may not skip phases or address agents outside the current phase; phase output must satisfy the completion predicate before transition.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1991.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The work decomposes naturally into ordered phases, each with a paired role and an artefact.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phase-specific completion predicates can be expressed clearly enough to gate handoff.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A single agent loop loses focus and broadcast multi-agent chat tangles context.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2116.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The task does not split into phases with clean artefact handoffs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Completion predicates are too vague to gate phase transitions reliably.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Two-role conversations would just slow down a competent single-agent solution.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2097.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Phase controller — sequences phases and gates each transition on the completion predicate&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Role-paired agents — two specialists (e.g. designer-coder, coder-tester) inside a single phase&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phase artefact — typed handoff document that crosses the boundary to the next phase&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Completion predicate — phase-specific stop hook that signs the artefact off&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Artefact registry — auditable trail of all signed artefacts across phases&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2241.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — invoked for every turn inside each paired-role chat&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; ChatDev framework — provides phase definitions, role pairings, and artefact contracts&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Artefact store — versioned storage for each phase output&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Predicate evaluator — checks artefact conformance before allowing phase transition&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2222.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Weak completion predicate — a phase signs off an artefact that only looks finished, and the next phase builds on a broken base.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong phase split — the chain pairs roles that do not fit the work, so agents in a phase argue about things they cannot decide.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phase skipping — an agent jumps ahead to code while still in design, and the artefact trail no longer matches what was done.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lost early requirement — a detail from phase one is not written into the artefact, so later phases never see it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2404.25" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Phase-completion rate — share of phases that satisfy the predicate without manual override&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Turns per phase — distribution of dialogue length inside each paired-role chat&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Artefact rejection rate — handoffs blocked by predicate for schema or content failure&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; End-to-end success vs single-agent baseline — does the chained structure beat one big prompt&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-phase rework rate — later phases that have to send the artefact back upstream&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2366.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/OpenBMB/ChatDev&quot;&gt;ChatDev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Software-development chain: design → coding → testing → documentation, each as a paired-role chat.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2624.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
