          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="no inter-clone communication" mermaidId="e:C1-&gt;C2#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.68;exitY=1;entryX=0.32;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="no inter-clone communication" id="m22">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.68;exitY=1;entryX=0.32;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="303.7" y="806.0" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;N identical full-capability agents run in isolation; aggregation is a single one-shot pass at the end.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1511.05" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Spawn 100 or more identical, full-capability agent instances in parallel — each a complete general agent rather than a role-specialised worker — and aggregate their independent outputs into a single answer.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1586.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team needs an agent to do a wide-coverage job — compare a long list of candidate libraries, scan a hundred different sources for the same kind of information, or sample many independent strategies for the same problem. Each individual unit of work is too large for a stripped-down worker prompt but small enough that a full general agent can finish it on its own. The infrastructure can hand each instance its own isolated environment, such as a sandbox virtual machine or a separate working copy of the codebase.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1586.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The usual orchestrator-workers pattern assumes specialisation: the orchestrator decomposes the job by role and hands each piece to a worker with a different skill. Many wide-coverage jobs are not role-decomposable at all — every unit needs the same full agent capability, just over a different slice of input. Inventing fake roles wastes the orchestrator&#39;s effort and produces inconsistent worker quality. Spawning hundreds of clones without isolation or an aggregation strategy collapses into the unbounded-subagent-spawn anti-pattern.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1711.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Wide coverage demands high parallelism, but parallel agents collide if they share state.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each unit of work needs full agent capability, not a stripped-down worker.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregation must reconcile many independent outputs without an O(N²) comparison.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Spawn cost and per-agent isolation cost grow linearly with N.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1768.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: spawn N identical full-capability agent clones into isolated sandboxes, give each the same prompt template parametrised by a different input slice, and pipe their structured outputs into a single aggregation pass so wide-coverage jobs scale by replication rather than by role decomposition.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1893.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A driver computes the input partition (one slice per clone), allocates N isolated sandboxes (e.g. VMs or worktrees) so the clones cannot interfere with one another, and launches N instances of the same agent with the same system prompt and tools — only the input slice differs. Each clone runs to completion independently and writes a structured result to a shared collection bucket. A separate aggregator pass (LLM or deterministic) consolidates results — voting, ranking, deduplication, or synthesis. The clones never communicate; aggregation is one-shot at the end. N is bounded by a declared budget and the available sandbox pool, not by the agent&#39;s own discretion.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1912.05" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Driver -&amp;gt; partition -&amp;gt; {Clone_1 ... Clone_N in isolated sandboxes} -&amp;gt; structured outputs -&amp;gt; Aggregator -&amp;gt; single answer.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2037.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A user asks an agent to compare 200 candidate libraries against five evaluation criteria. The driver partitions the list into 200 slices and spawns 200 identical agents, each in its own sandbox VM, each tasked with evaluating one library and emitting a structured row. After all clones finish, an aggregator pass ranks the rows and synthesises a shortlist. None of the clones talked to each other; the fan-out is bounded by the declared N=200.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2113.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wide-coverage jobs scale linearly with sandbox count.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identical clones simplify reasoning about per-agent quality.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No inter-clone coordination means no message-passing failure modes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Isolation prevents one clone&#39;s failure from poisoning others.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost scales linearly with N; budgets must be explicit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregation quality caps overall quality; a weak aggregator wastes the fan-out.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identical clones cannot specialise to harder slices.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Without strict spawn bounds this collapses into Unbounded Subagent Spawn.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2162.05" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The driver must declare N up front; the agent itself cannot decide to spawn more clones recursively; clones must run in isolated sandboxes with no shared mutable state; results must be aggregated in a single declared pass, not by inter-clone chatter.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2276.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The job naturally partitions into many independent units that each need full agent capability.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Isolated sandboxes are available so clones cannot interfere.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An aggregator (vote, rank, dedup, or synthesis) can produce one answer from N structured outputs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2477.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The subtasks are role-differentiated; use orchestrator-workers instead.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No aggregation strategy exists; raw N outputs are not a deliverable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-clone cost makes N infeasible at the needed coverage.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2401.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Driver — partitions the input and declares the fan-out bound N&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Identical agent clones — N full-capability instances seeded with the same system prompt&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Isolated sandboxes — one per clone, preventing shared mutable state&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Structured result bucket — collects per-clone outputs in a canonical schema&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregator — single one-shot vote, rank, dedup, or synthesis pass over the bucket&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2602.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Sandbox provisioner — VMs or worktrees that give each clone an isolated runtime&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — invoked independently by every clone for its slice&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Job scheduler — bounds concurrency and enforces the declared N&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Result store — shared collection bucket the aggregator reads from&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2526.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Weak aggregator — hundreds of good clone results feed one poor consolidation pass, and the final answer is no better than a single run.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Spawn creep — the agent is allowed to start more clones on its own, and the run turns into unbounded subagent spawning.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Shared-state leak — clones share a sandbox or a mutable store, and one clone&#39;s writes corrupt another&#39;s slice.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Uneven slices — every clone gets the same capability, so the hard slices get the same effort as the easy ones and come back thin.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2765.05" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Coverage of the input partition — fraction of slices that produced a usable structured result&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-clone failure rate — fraction of sandboxes whose run errored or timed out&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregator quality vs single-agent baseline — quality lift from the fan-out after consolidation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost per useful result — total spend divided by accepted aggregated outputs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Spawn discipline — observed N versus declared N, catches unbounded recursion&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2670.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/1934558071381812623&quot;&gt;Manus Wide Research (Monica / Manus AI)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Wide Research mode spawns 100+ identical full-capability agent instances in parallel VMs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://manus.im/blog/introducing-wide-research&quot;&gt;Manus Wide Research — official announcement (Manus blog)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Coverage of the architecture and parallelism model.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.oschina.net/news/363554/manus-wide-research&quot;&gt;Manus Wide Research announcement (OSCHINA)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Product-level introduction of the Wide Research feature.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2985.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Orchestrator-Workers&lt;/b&gt; — Orchestrator-workers decomposes by role; clone fan-out replicates the same role.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Parallelization&lt;/b&gt; — A specific shape of sectioning where every section gets the same full agent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Subagent Isolation&lt;/b&gt; — Each clone runs in its own isolated sandbox.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;conflicts-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Unbounded Subagent Spawn&lt;/b&gt; — This pattern is the bounded, aggregated counterpart of that anti-pattern.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Lead Researcher&lt;/b&gt; — Lead-researcher uses a small number of specialised subagents; clone fan-out uses many identical ones.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Role-Typed Subagents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Query-Decomposition Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Epistemic Fault-Domain Quorum&lt;/b&gt; — Identical workers fanned out over one corpus multiply reports without multiplying evidence roots, which is the case this pattern is designed to price correctly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Forkable Agent Sandbox&lt;/b&gt; — Fan-out over identical workers assumes the starting environment is cheap to reproduce; forking one snapshot supplies that starting state when provisioning from scratch is expensive.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2833.05" width="755" height="377" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/1934558071381812623&quot;&gt;Manus大升级，100多个智能体并发给你做任务&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://manus.im/blog/introducing-wide-research&quot;&gt;Introducing Wide Research (Manus official blog)&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.oschina.net/news/363554/manus-wide-research&quot;&gt;Manus推出Wide Research功能&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3167.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
