        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Cluster by stem tokens, cap by count, keep most-recent by mtime, archive the rest with timestamp.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1232.05" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Cap the number of insights per stem-token cluster and archive the oldest variants by mtime so the long-term store keeps the active research edge instead of accumulating near-duplicates.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1307.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running a long-lived agent that writes small insight notes to disk over weeks and months as it reflects on its work. The store is append-only by default and grows continuously. Whenever the agent thinks about a recurring topic, it tends to produce slightly different versions of the same insight rather than locating and updating the old one, so a topic the agent revisits often ends up with a cluster of near-duplicate files.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1307.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;With no structural ceiling on per-topic clusters, the insight store accumulates twelve or fifteen variations on the same theme, and retrieval increasingly surfaces older drafts of the agent&#39;s own thinking instead of the current view. Asking a language model to merge each cluster into a single canonical insight is expensive to run on every consolidation pass and risks quietly losing the nuance that distinguishes the variants. The team is forced to choose between unbounded growth and a slow, opaque, model-driven cleanup.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1413.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Pure age-based eviction loses durable insights.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Pure popularity loses fresh edges.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM-driven merge is expensive and unauditable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archived versions must remain available for forensics.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1470.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: cluster insight files mechanically by the first two stem tokens of their id, cap each cluster at a small N (default three) keeping the most-recently-touched by mtime, and move overflow to a timestamped archive directory, so that the active edge stays visible without losing the older variants.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1595.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A periodic job (runs each consolidation pass) scans the insight directory, groups files by the first two stem tokens of the id (for example &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;affect-substrate-&lt;i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;completion-narration-&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/font&gt;), and for any cluster above MAX_PER_CLUSTER keeps the N newest by mtime. Older files move to &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;archive/insights-dedup-&amp;lt;timestamp&amp;gt;/&lt;/font&gt; with original names preserved. No model call, no merge. The archive is read-only after the move; provenance is preserved.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1614.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Consolidation pass --&amp;gt; Scan insight directory --&amp;gt; Group by first two stem tokens --&amp;gt; per cluster: count &amp;lt;= MAX -&amp;gt; keep all | count &amp;gt; MAX -&amp;gt; sort by mtime desc -&amp;gt; newest N stay in active store, older move to archive/insights-dedup-&amp;lt;ts&amp;gt;/ (read-only, names kept)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1739.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent has been writing insights for six months. An audit shows twelve files starting with &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;affect-&lt;/font&gt;, ten with &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;completion-narration-&lt;/font&gt;, three with &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;concept-rotation-&lt;/font&gt;. The agent reads stale variants instead of the current one. The team adds a Cluster-Capped Insight Store: the consolidation pass groups files by first two stem tokens, caps each cluster at three keeping the most-recently-touched by mtime, and moves overflow to a timestamped archive. The active store shrinks from over two hundred files to under eighty and retrieval improves immediately.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1777.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Active store keeps the current research edge, not a graveyard of variants.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mechanical clustering has no model cost and is fully auditable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive preserves older variants for forensics.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stem-token clustering will sometimes split related insights or merge unrelated ones.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The cap is opinionated and bad clusters lose useful older work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Storage continues to grow because archive is preserved.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1883.05" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Insight files in the active store are capped per stem-token cluster; an insight cannot survive in the active store if it falls outside the most-recent N of its cluster — archive promotion is mechanical, not model-judged.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1959.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Insights are written to disk continuously and near-duplicates accumulate.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An LLM-merge approach is too expensive or too opaque for the use case.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stem-token clustering is a reasonable proxy for topical similarity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2160.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Insights are small in number or grow slowly enough that dedup is unnecessary.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stem-token clustering would lose critical distinctions (highly polysemous topics).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive preservation is not feasible because of storage constraints.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2084.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Insight Store — append-mostly directory of insight files keyed by stem-id&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stem-Token Clusterer — groups files by the first two stem tokens of the id&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mtime Sorter — orders each cluster by most-recently-touched&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive Mover — relocates overflow into a timestamped archive directory&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Consolidation Scheduler — invokes the dedup pass on each consolidation cycle&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2285.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Frontmatter store — flat filesystem directory holding insight files with mtime preserved&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Filesystem rename — atomic move of overflow files into the timestamped archive&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2209.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong cluster — two unrelated insights share the first two stem tokens, and one archives the other&#39;s newest work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Split theme — related insights use different id prefixes, so near-duplicates survive in separate clusters and the cap never trims them.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lost foundation — an older insight that newer variants build on is archived by mtime alone, and retrieval no longer finds it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Touched-file revival — an unrelated process updates an old file&#39;s mtime, and it jumps back into the newest N while a current insight is archived.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2448.05" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Active-store file count — total surviving files after a dedup pass&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cluster-cap breach rate — clusters that exceeded MAX_PER_CLUSTER before pruning&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Retrieval-on-current-version rate — share of reads that hit the newest file in a cluster, not an old draft&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive growth per cycle — files moved per consolidation pass as a load signal&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2315.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2668.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dream Consolidation Cycle&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Summaries&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agentic Context Engineering Playbook&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Corpus Vocabulary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Adaptive Memory Decay&lt;/b&gt; — A hard size cap evicts by ceiling; adaptive decay forgets by a continuous score.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2478.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.buildingasecondbrain.com/book&quot;&gt;Building a Second Brain (chapter on knowledge fragment hygiene)&lt;/a&gt; — Tiago Forte, 2022&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2774.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
