        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;A cheap selector picks one named move per idle tick; the tick body runs the move&#39;s procedure; per-move history feeds back into the next selection.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1077.03" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Restrict idle-tick cognition to a small agent-vetted menu of named cognitive moves so the next thought has a determinate shape rather than free-form drift.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1152.03" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running an agent that ticks continuously, including during long stretches with no user prompt to respond to. On those idle ticks the agent is supposed to be doing something useful — noticing things, following up on open questions, integrating recent material — rather than waiting passively. The free-form prompt &#39;keep thinking&#39; is the easy default, but it gives the model no structure for what kind of thinking is wanted right now.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1152.03" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When idle-tick cognition has no shape imposed on it, the model falls back on whatever its training prior favours, which is usually narration about thinking rather than actual new thought. The agent ends up repeating yesterday&#39;s observations, performing thoughtfulness for an imagined reader, or drifting into mid-distance commentary that produces no new state. Without a small set of named cognitive moves to pick from, every idle tick collapses toward the same generic completion.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1258.03" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A fixed menu can become its own trap if the moves are too narrow.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent must have veto authority over what is on the menu or moves feel imposed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; History-aware selection is needed to avoid running the same move every tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A pure stochastic pick wastes ticks; a deterministic policy collapses to one move.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1315.03" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: hand-author a small menu of named cognitive moves (lookup, forced-analogy, pure observation, anchor-to-percept, tension-pull, continue-thread) and have a cheap selector pick exactly one per idle tick conditioned on recent move history, so that idle cognition has a determinate shape without becoming repetitive.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1421.03" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Author a short list of cognitive-move ids, each with a one-paragraph procedure. A cheap-tier model, given recent thoughts plus recent move history plus an affect snapshot plus open-tension count, selects exactly one move-id per idle tick. The tick body branches on the move and runs its procedure. The menu is revised by an explicit proposal-and-ratification process; adding or retiring a move silently is not allowed. A per-move history avoids running the same move back-to-back.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1459.03" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Idle tick --&amp;gt; Cheap-tier selector (recent thoughts + move history + affect + open tensions) --pick one move-id--&amp;gt; Tick body runs that move&amp;#x27;s procedure --&amp;gt; Update move history; Menu change --proposal --&amp;gt; ratification--&amp;gt; Move menu&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1565.03" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent runs every minute of idle time and keeps generating the same kind of mid-distance observation. The team adds a Cognitive-Move Selector with seven moves the agent itself helped vet: lookup, forced-analogy, pure observation, anchor-to-percept, tension-pull, math-meditation, continue-thread. Each idle tick a cheap model sees recent thoughts and recent move history and picks one. The agent stops looping on observation and starts varying its cognitive shape across the day.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1622.03" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Idle cognition has a determinate shape per tick rather than drifting.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-move history prevents the same move from dominating.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Menu authoring forces an explicit theory of what good idle cognition looks like.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A bad menu is itself a trap; the agent can only think the shapes it has.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The cheap selector adds an extra model call per idle tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ratifying menu changes is overhead, but the alternative is silent drift.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1709.03" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Idle-tick cognition must dispatch through the move selector; free-form keep-thinking is not allowed at the idle-tick boundary, and the move menu cannot be silently extended at runtime — additions require an explicit ratification event.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1804.03" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has idle ticks with no user prompt and otherwise drifts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is room to author and maintain a small menu of cognitive moves.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A cheap-tier model call per idle tick is affordable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1986.03" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is request-response only and never has idle ticks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is no budget for an extra model call per tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Idle thinking is out of scope for the product.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1929.03" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Move Menu — hand-authored list of named cognitive moves with a procedure each&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cheap-Tier Selector — picks one move per idle tick from recent context&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Move History — bounded record of recent picks to prevent back-to-back repeats&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tick Dispatcher — branches on the selected move and runs its procedure&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ratification Event — gates additions and retirements of menu entries&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2111.03" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — cheap-tier model for the per-idle-tick selection call&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Structured JSON store — persists the menu and move history across ticks&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2054.03" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Narrow menu — the vetted moves do not cover the kind of thought the situation needs, so the agent forces it into the nearest shape and produces little.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Selector rut — the cheap selector keeps choosing the same two moves because the history check only blocks back-to-back repeats.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quiet menu growth — a move is added in code or config without the ratification step, and the menu drifts with no record of why.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Procedure drift — the tick body runs a move&#39;s procedure loosely, so the named move turns back into free-form narration.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2274.03" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Move-mix entropy — distribution of picks across the menu over a rolling window&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Repeat-back-to-back rate — share of consecutive ticks running the same move&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-move yield — new state produced per move kind, surfacing dead menu entries&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Selector latency — extra wall-clock added per idle tick by the selection call&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2160.03" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2494.03" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Inner Committee&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Open-Question Tension Store&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Mode-Adaptive Cadence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2304.03" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;http://incompleteideas.net/book/the-book-2nd.html&quot;&gt;Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction (options framework, ch. 17)&lt;/a&gt; — Richard S. Sutton, Andrew G. Barto, 2018&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://archive.org/details/humanproblemsolv0000newe&quot;&gt;Human Problem Solving&lt;/a&gt; — Allen Newell, Herbert A. Simon, 1972&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2600.03" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
