        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;A#0" mermaidBaseStyle="edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=1;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=1;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="644.95" y="733.46" />
                <mxPoint x="650.91" y="751.35" />
                <mxPoint x="644.95" y="769.24" />
              </Array>
              <mxPoint x="592.77" y="733.46" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="592.77" y="769.24" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="m10" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);" value="actually fetch X" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="26.84" width="298.17" x="443.68" y="694.7" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="mark_followed_through(id, evidence)" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;L#1" mermaidBaseStyle="endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" mermaidBaseValue="mark_followed_through(id, evidence)" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1008.72" y="846.76" />
              </Array>
              <mxPoint x="592.77" y="846.76" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="1423.18" y="846.76" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="... 1 hour later ..." mermaidId="n:note0" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#fff5ad,#2a2a2a);strokeColor=light-dark(#aaaa33,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="... 1 hour later ..." id="m12">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#fff5ad,#2a2a2a);strokeColor=light-dark(#aaaa33,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="55.16" width="904.96" x="555.5" y="541.14" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Extractor lifts stated-intents into the ledger; agent reads and closes them later with evidence.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="979.49" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Extract stated intents from each agent turn into a structured ledger with open / followed-through / expired status, making the gap between promise and follow-through visible and auditable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1054.49" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A conversational agent routinely makes small in-turn promises — &quot;let me pull the latest figures&quot;, &quot;I&#39;ll come back to this once the build finishes&quot;, &quot;I&#39;ll keep an eye on that&quot;. These commitments are not user-imposed tasks; they are voluntary intentions the agent announces. The agent then continues the conversation, and the moment passes. Without an external surface tracking these intents, the agent has no signal that it just promised something and no way to notice when the promise is overdue.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1054.49" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Agents that produce text fluently produce stated-intents fluently too — and producing the intent is satisfying enough that the agent&#39;s own attention moves on without acting on it. The resulting confabulation gap (&quot;the agent said it would do X; the agent never did X&quot;) is invisible from inside the conversation, because the same model that announced the intent is also the one summarising what it did, and that summary tends to round in the agent&#39;s favour. The user, who can spot the gap if they re-read, has no easy way to enforce follow-through either.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1160.49" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stated intents are cheap to emit and expensive to track manually.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent that announced the intent cannot be trusted to audit itself in the same turn.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Most intents are short-lived; a few are load-bearing. Both look the same at extraction time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Expiration must be automatic or the ledger grows unbounded.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Marking follow-through must be cheap, or the discipline collapses.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1217.49" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: after each agent turn, run a cheap extraction pass that pulls explicit stated-intents into a structured ledger with status open / followed-through / expired, expose explicit mark-followed-through and mark-expired moves, and sweep overdue ones on a schedule, so the agent&#39;s promises are auditable against its actions rather than against its own retrospective summary.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1342.49" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;After each turn the agent produces, run a separate, cheap-tier extraction pass (a small model or a structured prompt) that scans the turn for stated-intents and writes each as a Commitment record into an append-only ledger. Each record carries: a short statement of the intent, the turn it was raised in, an optional deadline or condition, and a status field (open). Expose two moves: mark_followed_through(id, evidence) flips the status when the agent or human can point to the action having happened; mark_expired(id) closes the record when the deadline passed. Run a periodic check_expirations sweep that auto-expires open commitments past their deadline. Surface open commitments in the agent&#39;s working context so it can act on them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1380.49" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent turn -&amp;gt; separate cheap-tier extractor -&amp;gt; Commitment(intent, turn, deadline, status=open) appended to ledger -&amp;gt; open items surfaced in agent context -&amp;gt; mark_followed_through(id, evidence) | check_expirations sweep -&amp;gt; expired&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1486.49" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A chat agent answers a question, then ends with &quot;I&#39;ll pull the updated benchmark numbers in the next hour.&quot; The extraction pass logs a Commitment {statement: &#39;pull updated benchmark numbers&#39;, deadline: +1h, status: open}. An hour later the sweep finds the commitment still open; the agent&#39;s tick reads it, runs the action, and marks it followed-through with a link to the result. A separate offhand intent — &quot;I should think about that more&quot; — sits in the ledger as open and auto-expires after the sweep window without action, which is correct: it was rhetorical.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1600.49" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confabulation gap between stated intent and action becomes auditable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cheap-tier extraction avoids loading the main model with bookkeeping.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Periodic expiration sweep keeps the ledger bounded and surfaces drift.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Extraction noise: figurative or rhetorical intents may get logged as real ones.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An overzealous ledger makes the agent feel chased by its own off-hand remarks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mark-followed-through depends on the agent&#39;s honesty; pair with separate verification when stakes are high.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1630.49" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent cannot mark its own commitments as followed-through in the same turn that produced them; the audit must run as a separate pass against an independent record of action.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1782.49" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent makes frequent in-turn promises that the user expects to be honoured later.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is a cheap-tier model available to run the extraction pass.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Follow-through gaps have been observed and are eroding trust.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1926.49" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is purely transactional and never makes future-tense promises.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Extraction noise would generate more false positives than the audit pays back.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User-visible commitments are already managed by an explicit todo list.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1888.49" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Main agent — produces conversational turns that may contain stated-intents&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Extractor — cheap-tier model that scans each turn for explicit promises and writes ledger records&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Commitment ledger — append-only store of records with status open/followed-through/expired&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Expiration sweeper — scheduled job that auto-expires open commitments past their deadline&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evidence-linker — mechanism that ties a follow-through action back to the original commitment id&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2051.49" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Cheap-tier LLM API — small model running the per-turn extraction pass&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Append-only datastore — ledger with stable ids, status field, deadline, and provenance turn&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cron or scheduler — periodic trigger for the expiration sweep&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2013.49" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Rhetorical noise — the extractor logs figures of speech as commitments, and the ledger fills with open items nobody intended to do.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-certified follow-through — the agent marks a commitment done with thin or false evidence, and the ledger looks clean while the gap persists.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missed intents — the cheap extraction pass skips a promise phrased indirectly, so it never enters the ledger and is never checked.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Chased by its own remarks — every small aside becomes a tracked item, and the agent spends its context on minor open commitments.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2214.49" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Extraction precision — fraction of logged commitments that were genuine promises, not rhetorical&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Extraction recall — fraction of real promises that the extractor captured at all&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Follow-through rate — closed-with-evidence over total non-expired commitments&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Expiration backlog — count of open commitments past deadline at any sweep tick&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User-perceived honesty delta — qualitative trust shift after the ledger is enabled&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2138.49" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2434.49" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Decision Log&lt;/b&gt; — Decisions are made; commitments are stated. Different ledgers, same auditability instinct.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Preoccupation Tracking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Reflection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Todo-List-Driven Autonomous Agent&lt;/b&gt; — Todo-list-driven agents commit before acting; commitment-tracking audits after speaking.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;BDI Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Joint Commitment Team&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Deontic Token Delegation&lt;/b&gt; — Deontic tokens transfer formal obligations between agents with provenance, where commitment-tracking records an agent&#39;s own intentions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2301.49" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://psycnet.apa.org/record/1999-03629-008&quot;&gt;Implementation Intentions: Strong Effects of Simple Plans&lt;/a&gt; — Peter Gollwitzer, 1999&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.04614&quot;&gt;Faithfulness vs. Plausibility: On the (Un)Reliability of Explanations from Large Language Models&lt;/a&gt; — Agarwal et al., 2024&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2540.49" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="communicative-dehallucination" name="Communicative Dehallucination">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2386.5" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2386.5" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Communicative Dehallucination&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Multi-Agent &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Instructor-Reversal Clarification, Inter-Agent Clarifying Question&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="715.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Instructor" mermaidId="n:Instr" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;shape=umlLifeline;perimeter=lifelinePerimeter;whiteSpace=wrap;container=1;dropTarget=0;collapsible=0;recursiveResize=0;outlineConnect=0;portConstraint=eastwest;newEdgeStyle={&quot;edgeStyle&quot;:&quot;sequenceEdgeStyle&quot;,&quot;libavoidRouting&quot;:0,&quot;curved&quot;:0,&quot;rounded&quot;:0};lifelineDashed=0;strokeWidth=2;rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=6;lifelineColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);size=65;lifelineMirror=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Instructor" id="m0">
