        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;M1#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.25;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.25;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="171.91" y="585.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;M2#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.75;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.75;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="456.06" y="585.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;M3#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.83;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.83;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="745.84" y="585.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="false" mermaidId="e:Q-&gt;Step#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.54;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="false" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.54;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1032.81" y="426.49" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="true" mermaidId="e:Q-&gt;Stop#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.98;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="true" id="m16">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.98;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m8">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1377.45" y="426.49" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Express agent stop criteria as small single-purpose conditions composed with AND/OR into one explicit termination contract instead of ad-hoc loop guards.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="741.58" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent or orchestrator loops over model calls, tool invocations, and message exchanges until something tells it to stop. The realistic stop criteria are heterogeneous: a max number of messages, a token budget, a phrase the model emitted, a particular tool call (e.g. submit_final), a handoff to another agent, a timeout, an external operator signal, or a user cancellation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="741.58" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Inlining these stop conditions as ad-hoc &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;if&lt;/font&gt; statements in the orchestrator loop scatters the termination logic, makes its precedence implicit, and prevents reuse across loops. Adding a new condition requires editing the loop. Combining conditions (stop on max_messages OR external signal AND a specific tool call) becomes an unreadable nest. Operators reading a trace cannot tell why a run ended without re-reading the loop code.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="847.58" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Different agents need different combinations of the same primitive conditions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Conditions must compose with AND/OR while preserving short-circuit semantics.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The trace must record which condition tripped, for postmortem.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External signals (operator cancellation, kill-switch) must be expressible as a condition like any other.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="885.58" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: model each stop criterion as a typed termination condition and compose them with AND/OR into a single decision the loop consults each iteration, so termination is one explicit contract whose trip cause is recorded.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1010.58" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a small set of primitive termination conditions: MaxMessages, TokenBudget, TextMention, FunctionCall, Handoff, Timeout, ExternalSignal, Cancellation. Each implements a single method &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;is_terminated(state) -&amp;gt; bool, reason&lt;/font&gt;. Define a Composite that combines conditions with &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;any&lt;/font&gt; (OR) or &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;all&lt;/font&gt; (AND) semantics. The orchestrator loop consults the composite once per step. The trip cause (which leaf condition fired) is logged with the termination event.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1048.58" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Orchestrator loop --each step--&amp;gt; Composite.is_terminated(state) [any / all over MaxMessages, TokenBudget, Timeout, ExternalSignal, ...] --false--&amp;gt; next step | --true--&amp;gt; Stop + log trip cause&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1135.58" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research-agent loop is configured with &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;MaxMessages(50) | TokenBudget(200_000) | TextMention(&#39;final_answer&#39;) | ExternalSignal(cancel_token)&lt;/font&gt;. Each step the orchestrator asks the composite whether to stop. When the cancel token flips, the loop ends and the trace records &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;terminated_by=ExternalSignal&lt;/font&gt;; when the model emits &#39;final_answer&#39; first, the trace records that instead.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1211.58" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stop criteria are testable in isolation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; AND/OR composition reads as a single contract per loop.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External operator signals are expressible as conditions, unifying termination paths.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Trip cause is structured for postmortem.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An expressive DSL invites complex compositions that surprise on edge cases.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Polling-based conditions (timeout, external signal) need a clock the loop trusts.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1260.58" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Termination criteria must not be inlined as ad-hoc loop guards; they must be expressed as named conditions and composed with AND/OR into a single termination contract per loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1355.58" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent loop must combine multiple heterogeneous stop criteria.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Operators need structured trip-cause for postmortem.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External signals (cancellation, kill-switch) need to share termination semantics with intrinsic stops.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1537.58" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Only a fixed max-steps budget is needed — a single primitive is fine.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The orchestrator is a one-shot non-looping call.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1461.58" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; TerminationCondition base — is_terminated(state) -&amp;gt; (bool, reason).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Primitives — MaxMessages, TokenBudget, TextMention, FunctionCall, Handoff, Timeout, ExternalSignal, Cancellation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composite — any/all combinator preserving short-circuit semantics.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1681.58" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Token-usage tracker — feeds TokenBudget&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External signal channel — feeds ExternalSignal (kill-switch, cancel)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wall-clock — feeds Timeout&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1567.58" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Surprising composite — an AND nested inside an OR stops the run too early or never, and the edge case only shows up in production.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Untrusted clock — a timeout or external-signal condition polls a clock the loop does not control, so the stop fires late or not at all.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lost trip cause — the composite returns true but the firing leaf is not logged, and operators again cannot tell why the run ended.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1825.58" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Trip-cause distribution — share of runs ended by each leaf condition&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Premature termination rate — runs flagged as ended too early&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unbounded runs — share that ran to wall-clock instead of any meaningful condition&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1692.58" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/&quot;&gt;AutoGen TerminationCondition + handoff/text/maxmessages set&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/victordibia/designing-multiagent-systems&quot;&gt;picoagents (Dibia, Designing Multi-Agent Systems) — full termination package&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2007.58" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Kill Switch&lt;/b&gt; — ExternalSignal condition is the in-loop side of the kill-switch.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Step Budget&lt;/b&gt; — MaxMessages / TokenBudget are conditions of the budget family.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cost Gating&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Degenerate-Output Detection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Interruptible Agent Execution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Unbounded Loop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Symptom-Remediation Thrashing&lt;/b&gt; — An explicit escalate-after-N-attempts termination is the corrective; thrashing lacks any stop-or-escalate condition on repeated remediation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Ghost Delegation&lt;/b&gt; — An explicit timeout and completion contract on each delegated subtask is part of the corrective; ghost delegation is what happens when a subtask can wait forever with no stop condition.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1817.58" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://multiagentbook.com/&quot;&gt;Designing Multi-Agent Systems&lt;/a&gt; — Victor Dibia, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/stable/user-guide/agentchat-user-guide/quickstart.html&quot;&gt;AutoGen TerminationCondition&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2151.58" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
