        <UserObject label="load_relevant" mermaidId="e:UserMemoryStore-&gt;Session#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.55078125;exitY=1;entryX=0.6150442477876106;entryY=0;curved=1;exitX=0.55;exitY=1;entryX=0.62;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="load_relevant" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m0" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.55;exitY=1;entryX=0.62;entryY=0;" target="m9">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <mxPoint as="offset" />
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="371.9" y="621.55" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="add / forget" mermaidId="e:Session-&gt;UserMemoryStore#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.38495575221238937;exitY=0;entryX=0.44921875;entryY=1;curved=1;exitX=0.38;exitY=0;entryX=0.45;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="add / forget" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m9" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.38;exitY=0;entryX=0.45;entryY=1;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <mxPoint as="offset" />
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="189.0" y="621.55" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Persist user-specific facts, preferences, and prior context across all sessions, threads, and devices.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="984.3" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building a user-facing assistant where the user expects continuity between visits. The user mentioned a preference last Tuesday, named a project two weeks ago, and told the assistant their pet&#39;s name a month ago. Today they expect the assistant to remember those facts without being re-told.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="984.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Per-thread memory loses everything between sessions: every new conversation starts from a blank slate, the user has to repeat themselves about basic facts, and the assistant feels amnesic and impersonal. The team needs a mechanism that captures the right kind of information at the right time, stores it durably across sessions, and surfaces it back into context when relevant — without leaking private details, blurring sessions together, or storing every passing remark as if it were load-bearing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1090.3" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; What to remember vs forget; user agency.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Privacy, deletion, portability requirements.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost of always-on memory loading per turn.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1128.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: distil per-user facts into a separate store loaded per session with explicit forget controls, so that the agent remembers across threads without holding the user hostage to its memory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1253.3" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Maintain a per-user store of distilled facts (preferences, prior context, names, projects). Load relevant slices into each session&#39;s context. Provide explicit add/forget tools. Audit and surface memory entries to the user. Deletion controls and a user-visible memory inspector (delete / disable / export) satisfy regulatory and trust requirements.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1253.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Session start --load_relevant(user)--&amp;gt; User memory store --&amp;gt; Session context; Session --add / forget tools--&amp;gt; User memory store; User --memory inspector (view / delete / disable / export)--&amp;gt; User memory store&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1359.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A user uses their personal assistant on the laptop in the morning, the phone at lunch, and a smart speaker in the evening. Without persistent memory, each device feels like a stranger — the user repeats their dietary restrictions three times in one day. The team adds Cross-Session Memory: stable user-specific facts (allergies, preferred name, default timezone) are stored centrally and loaded into every new session on every device. The assistant stops feeling amnesic and the user stops repeating themselves.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1397.3" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Continuity across sessions and devices.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compounding usefulness over time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Privacy obligations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memory hallucinations are stickier than chat hallucinations.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1484.3" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Memory entries must be added through declared tools; the model cannot silently mutate persistent user state.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1579.3" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Per-thread memory loses important user-specific facts between sessions and the assistant feels amnesic.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A per-user store of distilled facts can be maintained with audit, deletion, and forget controls.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Loaded memory slices meaningfully improve responses across sessions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1723.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Sessions are deliberately stateless for privacy or compliance reasons.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No reliable distillation step exists and the store would fill with noise.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Users expect a fresh agent per session and persistent memory would surprise them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1685.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Per-user memory store — durable store keyed by user identity, holding distilled facts across sessions and devices&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Distillation step — turns finished sessions into stable key-value facts, narrative summaries, or embedded chunks&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Add/forget tool — declared interface the model uses to mutate the store; silent writes are forbidden&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Session loader — selects the relevant slice for each new session and injects it into the prompt&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User-visible memory inspector — surface where the user can view, delete, disable, or export stored entries&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1867.3" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Document or key-value store — Postgres, DynamoDB, or Letta-style memory blocks for distilled facts&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Embedding model + vector index — used by the embedded-session-retrieval variant for similarity recall&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Summarisation LLM — runs at session close to produce the narrative or fact-extraction summary&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Deletion/export tooling — GDPR-shaped endpoints that satisfy forget-me and data-portability requirements&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1810.3" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Sticky false memory — the model stores a wrong fact about the user and repeats it in every later session.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Over-capture — passing remarks are saved as lasting preferences, and the assistant acts on them long after they stopped being true.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-user bleed — a slice loaded for one user includes facts from another user&#39;s store.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unhonoured forget — the user deletes an entry in the inspector, but a cached copy keeps showing up in context.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2106.3" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Repeat-question rate — how often users restate facts the system was supposed to remember&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memory precision — fraction of stored facts that human review confirms as correct and worth keeping&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Forget compliance latency — time from user delete request to verified removal from all retrieval paths&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memory hallucination rate — sampled cases where the agent acts on a fact never said by the user&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-session memory load cost — tokens added to each session prompt by injected memory slices&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1992.3" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;ChatGPT Memory&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Claude Projects + memory&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.letta.com/&quot;&gt;Letta&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Lindy memory&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
