        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="bounded; eviction keeps diverse stepping-stones" mermaidId="e:ARCH-&gt;ARCH#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.31;exitY=1;entryX=0.69;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="bounded; eviction keeps diverse stepping-stones" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m0" style="dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);curved=0;rounded=1;arcSize=20;exitX=0.311;exitY=1;entryX=0.692;entryY=1;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <mxPoint y="164.3" as="offset" />
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="789.47" y="305.58" />
                <mxPoint x="944.47" y="305.58" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Mutation parents are sampled for diversity, not best score, so low-scoring novel variants can seed future high-scoring ones.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1715.65" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent rewrites its own source code, archives every successful variant, and samples mutation parents from the archive rather than the latest version, using archive diversity as stepping-stones to escape local optima.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1790.65" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research team builds an agent that can read and rewrite parts of its own implementation, such as its system prompt, its tool definitions, the scaffolding around its main loop, or the code that implements it. The team has a clear way to measure whether one version of the agent is better than another: a benchmark, a task suite, or an automated self-evaluation that returns a score per variant. The point of the project is to let the agent improve itself over many generations without human-in-the-loop edits.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1790.65" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When the agent always mutates the latest accepted version (greedy self-rewrite), it climbs whatever local hill it started on and stops. The move that would unlock a higher ridge is several mutations away from anything that currently scores well, so a strictly score-maximising selection rule will never reach it. Throwing away the variants that scored worse destroys the very diversity that would have been the bridge to a better region of the search space. The agent gets stuck in a local optimum, and without some way of preserving and revisiting worse-scoring stepping-stones it has no path out short of a manual reset.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1915.65" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Greedy ascent from the latest variant converges to local optima quickly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Useful stepping-stone variants often score worse short-term than the current best.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Throwing away history makes those stepping-stones permanently unreachable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-modification needs a safety gate so each variant is at least viable before it enters the archive.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive growth must be bounded or sampling becomes diffuse and useless.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1972.65" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: keep an archive of every variant that passes a viability gate, sample the parent for the next mutation from the archive (weighted by diversity, not by score), and let the archive&#39;s diversity supply evolutionary stepping-stones so self-rewrite can escape local optima without an outside reset.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2116.65" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent maintains a versioned archive of self-modifications. Each generation: (1) sample a parent variant from the archive using a diversity-aware policy (not strictly the current best); (2) propose a code or prompt mutation; (3) run the mutated variant through a viability gate (compiles, passes safety checks, runs end-to-end on a smoke test); (4) score it on the objective; (5) if viable, add it to the archive with its score and lineage. Selection from the archive is the key move — it lets a low-scoring but novel variant become the parent of a future high-scoring variant. The archive is bounded by a retention policy that favours diversity over raw score so stepping-stones are preserved.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2154.65" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Archive (variants with score + lineage) -&amp;gt; sample parent (diversity-weighted) -&amp;gt; propose mutation -&amp;gt; viability gate -&amp;gt; score on objective -&amp;gt; if viable, add to archive. Outer loop iterates; archive is the memory of evolution, not just the leaderboard.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2260.65" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research agent rewrites its own coding scaffolding to maximise a benchmark score. The greedy version stalls at a plateau after twenty generations. Switching to an archive-sampled scheme, a worse-scoring variant from generation six becomes the parent for generation twenty-two; its odd tool-handling structure happens to combine well with a mutation that the greedy line never reached, and the score jumps. The archive stored that stepping-stone for sixteen generations before it paid off.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2355.65" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Escapes local optima that greedy self-rewrite cannot.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive preserves lineage and makes regressions debuggable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diversity-weighted sampling reuses old branches as starting points for new exploration.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Viability gate keeps the archive populated with runnable variants only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive storage and bookkeeping grows with generations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diversity metric is a design choice and a bad one biases the search the wrong way.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Viability gate is a single point of failure — a bug there lets broken variants in.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-modifying agents are inherently harder to audit and to safety-check than fixed ones.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2404.65" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Each proposed variant must pass the viability gate (compiles, safety-checks, smoke test) before entering the archive; the agent must not mutate or sample outside the archive; the archive must keep score and lineage for every variant and must not be silently pruned by score alone.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2518.65" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent can rewrite its own implementation (code, prompt, scaffolding) safely.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A clear objective score is available per variant.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Greedy self-rewrite has empirically plateaued.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2719.65" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Self-modification is out of scope or unsafe in the deployment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Storage and compute cannot support an archive plus repeated viability gating.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Objective score is too noisy for variant-to-variant comparison to mean anything.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2643.65" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Variant archive — bounded store of variants with score, lineage, and diversity tags&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diversity-weighted sampler — picks the parent variant for the next mutation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mutation proposer — generates code or prompt edits against the sampled parent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Viability gate — compile/safety/smoke-test check that admits a variant to the archive&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Objective scorer — evaluates each viable variant on the benchmark or task suite&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2844.65" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Code-execution sandbox — runs each variant for the viability gate and the smoke test&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Benchmark or task-suite harness — produces the objective score per variant&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Versioned archive store — persists variants with score, lineage, and eviction metadata&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — proposes the code or prompt mutations on each generation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2768.65" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Leaky viability gate — a bug in the gate lets a broken or unsafe variant into the archive, and later generations inherit it as a parent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bad diversity metric — the measure of novelty rewards irrelevant differences, so sampling wastes generations on variants that lead nowhere.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Score-only pruning — under storage pressure someone trims the archive by score, and the low-scoring stepping-stones the search needed are deleted.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Audit gap — after many generations of self-rewrite, nobody can explain why the current code behaves as it does, and safety review falls behind.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3007.65" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Generations to escape plateau — how many archive samples it takes to beat the prior best&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stepping-stone payoff rate — fraction of high-scoring variants descended from below-best parents&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive diversity index — coverage of the variant space, not just top-N score&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Viability-gate false-pass rate — broken variants that slip through and pollute the archive&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Objective score lift over greedy self-rewrite baseline — net gain from archive sampling&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2912.65" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sakana.ai/dgm-jp/&quot;&gt;Sakana AI Darwin-Gödel Machine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Self-improving agent that rewrites its own code, archives variants, and samples from the archive as evolutionary stepping-stones.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — The Soft-Norm Approach Ledger variant: behavioral norms (rules, moves, motivations, hypotheses) are versioned in an append-only ledger; confidence updates asymmetrically from agent-reported outcomes; sampling exposes named modes (greedy / diverse / historical / aged) as caller verbs rather than as a fixed selection policy.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3227.65" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Refine&lt;/b&gt; — Self-refine rewrites once from the latest version; DGM samples from the archive instead.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Reflexion&lt;/b&gt; — Reflexion writes verbal lessons; DGM rewrites the agent itself and archives the rewrites.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Modification Diff Gate&lt;/b&gt; — Inner-critic / self-modification diff gate can serve as the viability gate at the front of the archive.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Evaluator-Optimizer&lt;/b&gt; — Evaluator-optimizer scores variants; DGM adds an archive plus diversity-weighted sampling on top.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Edit Critic Gate&lt;/b&gt; — The self-edit critic gate is the viability gate that reviews each self-rewrite before it lands.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3075.65" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://sakana.ai/dgm-jp/&quot;&gt;Darwin-Gödel Machine (Sakana AI)&lt;/a&gt; — Sakana AI, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://sakana.ai/dgm/&quot;&gt;Darwin-Gödel Machine: AI agents that learn by rewriting their own code&lt;/a&gt; — Sakana AI, 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3409.65" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
