        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Gated-&gt;Safe#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: ship a demo-validated agent straight into production without a frozen eval, cost ceiling, loop-detector, or named oncall, then act surprised when accuracy drops and cost runs away.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1539.2" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent has been built and demoed successfully against a curated set of inputs in a clean environment. Stakeholders are convinced; the model &#39;works&#39;. The team now wants to ship it to production traffic — variable input distributions, real concurrency, real rate limits, real cost meters, real adversarial inputs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1539.2" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Demo conditions hide most of what kills agents in production. Latency at low concurrency does not predict p99 under load. A 95% pass rate on a hand-picked eval does not predict accuracy on the long tail. Token spend on a few demo turns does not predict the cost of an undetected recursive multi-agent conversation running overnight. Industry surveys (88% of agents never reach production; 70–95% failure rate among those that do) consistently attribute the gap to missing evaluation infrastructure, monitoring, dedicated ownership — not to model quality. The t3n analysis names this directly: it is not the model that fails, it is the architecture around it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1645.2" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Demos reward speed-to-impressive-output; production rewards stability under load that the demo never sees.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-query cost is invisible until traffic scales; recursive loops between agents can drain a budget in days without tripping any classical alert.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval suites that worked in development are rarely re-run as the model, tools, or prompt drift; what looked safe at v1 is unmeasured at v17.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ownership of agent operations sits between the ML, platform, and product teams; without a named owner, monitoring and cost gating fall through the gap.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1683.2" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: before shipping, instrument the agent with per-run cost telemetry, loop-detection, a frozen eval that gates deploys, rate-limit-aware retries, and a named oncall — and stage at production-scale traffic, not demo-scale.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1846.2" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Treat the demo as the beginning of evaluation, not its conclusion. Stand up an eval harness with a frozen rubric before production traffic; gate deploys on it. Add cost-observability per agent-run and a hard budget ceiling per session. Add loop-detection (typed-tool-loop-detector or step-budget) to catch recursive multi-agent chatter. Replay production traffic in a shadow-canary before promotion. Name an oncall for the agent system the same way as for any other production service.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1903.2" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: demo on curated inputs -&amp;gt; ship to production -&amp;gt; loops, cost, latency, long-tail accuracy drop unseen. Corrected: demo -&amp;gt; frozen eval gate + cost ceiling per session + loop detector + shadow canary + named oncall -&amp;gt; production.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1971.2" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A four-agent research assistant nails its demo: clean queries, three-agent rounds, ~$0.40 per answer, 8-second latency. It ships. Two weeks later, finance flags a $47k spend over 11 days. Investigation finds one of the agent pairs has been in a self-perpetuating clarification loop on a class of malformed inputs that never appeared in the demo set; no step-budget, no cost-observability dashboard, no oncall. Postmortem conclusion: the model worked; the architecture around it had no production-readiness gates.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2066.2" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: a good demo builds momentum, and shipping it as-is skips weeks of eval and monitoring work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team list the readiness gates that must exist before live traffic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Undetected recursive loops between agents drain budget — single documented case: $47k over 11 days from one runaway multi-agent dialogue.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; p99 latency in production is unrelated to the demo&#39;s mean latency; rate-limit-induced backoff cascades through tool calls.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Accuracy on long-tail production inputs is materially worse than on the curated demo set; without a frozen eval the regression is invisible.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Industry-wide pilot-to-production failure rate sits around 88%; the dominant root causes are operational, not algorithmic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2115.2" width="755" height="358" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No useful constraint; the missing constraint is mandatory production-readiness gating (frozen eval, cost ceiling, loop-detector, named oncall) before any agent ships to live traffic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2248.2" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Never. Cite this anti-pattern when reviewing the deploy plan of any agent that has only been validated against a curated demo set.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Demand a frozen eval, cost ceiling, loop-detector, and named oncall before sign-off.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stage at production-scale shadow traffic, not demo-scale.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2487.2" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Any agent that has impressed in a stakeholder demo but has no production-scale evaluation harness.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Any multi-agent system without explicit step-budgets or loop-detection on the inter-agent message channel.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Any deployment where no single team holds oncall for the agent&#39;s operational metrics.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2354.2" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Demo eval — small curated set that proved the agent worked&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing frozen eval — production-representative suite that should gate deploys but does not exist&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing cost telemetry — per-run cost ledger that should fire on budget overrun but does not exist&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing loop-detector — should catch recursive multi-agent conversations but does not exist&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing oncall — named owner of the agent&#39;s operational metrics; nobody holds the pager&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2631.2" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Production traffic mirror — replays real query distribution into a staging copy of the agent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost dashboard — per-run, per-session, per-agent token and dollar accounting&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Loop-detector — typed-tool-loop-detector or step-budget enforcement on the inter-agent channel&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frozen-rubric eval harness — eval-as-contract that gates promotion&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2498.2" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Overnight loop — two agents keep talking to each other with no loop detector, and spend runs up for days before anyone sees it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Load surprise — tail latency under real concurrency and rate limits is far worse than the demo, and backoff spreads through tool calls.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Invisible regression — accuracy on long-tail inputs drops, and with no frozen eval nobody can show it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Nobody on call — the agent fails at night, and no named owner is there to respond.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2794.2" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Pilot-to-production survival rate — share of demoed agents that survive 30 days of production traffic without an incident&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Time-to-detect-cost-anomaly — minutes between an anomalous cost spike and an oncall page&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval-gate coverage — share of production deploys that ran a frozen eval before promotion&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Loop-detection coverage — share of multi-agent paths that have step-budget or loop-detector instrumentation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Production-vs-demo accuracy delta — measured regression between the demo set and the long-tail production sample&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2642.2" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://t3n.de/news/ki-agenten-scheitern-nicht-am-modell-sondern-an-diesen-fuenf-architekturfehlern-1730278/&quot;&gt;t3n.de — German trade-press post-mortem of five recurring production-failure patterns, naming the architecture-not-model framing explicitly&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://habr.com/ru/articles/1031114/&quot;&gt;Habr — Russian post-mortem with the same five-modes structure (&amp;#x27;And none are about the model&amp;#x27;)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.atlantatech.news/artificial-intelligence/88-of-ai-agents-fail-before-production-the-reason-isnt-technical-consultants-must-wake-up/&quot;&gt;Atlanta Tech News / DigitalApplied / Fiddler AI — English-language industry analyses citing 88% pilot-to-production failure rate, attributing it to evaluation/monitoring gaps&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2995.2" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Perma-Beta&lt;/b&gt; — perma-beta is the cultural after-effect — the cliff hits, no one fixes it, the system stays in &#39;beta&#39; forever&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Unbounded Loop&lt;/b&gt; — one of the canonical failure shapes hidden by demo conditions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cost Observability&lt;/b&gt; — the missing capability&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Eval as Contract&lt;/b&gt; — the missing gate&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Shadow Canary&lt;/b&gt; — the missing staging step&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Errors Swept Under the Rug&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Step Budget&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Automating a Broken Process&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agentic Debt&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Demo-Production Cliff (Multi-Agent)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;evaluation-driven-development&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Silent Pilot-to-Production Promotion&lt;/b&gt; — Both are go-live failures, but inverted: the cliff ships a demo-validated agent into production with no readiness gate and watches metrics collapse; silent promotion never declares production at all, so the gate is dodged rather than skipped at a known launch.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Mirrored Tool Environment&lt;/b&gt; — Shipping on a mirror-only score, with no holdout against the live service, is one route onto that cliff.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2862.2" width="755" height="396" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://t3n.de/news/ki-agenten-scheitern-nicht-am-modell-sondern-an-diesen-fuenf-architekturfehlern-1730278/&quot;&gt;KI-Agenten scheitern nicht am Modell – sondern an diesen fünf Architekturfehlern&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://habr.com/ru/articles/1031114/&quot;&gt;Пять способов как ИИ-агенты падают в проде. И ни один не про модель&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.atlantatech.news/artificial-intelligence/88-of-ai-agents-fail-before-production-the-reason-isnt-technical-consultants-must-wake-up/&quot;&gt;88% of AI Agents Fail Before Production. The Reason Isn&amp;#x27;t Technical.&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fiddler.ai/blog/ai-agent-failure-rate&quot;&gt;AI Agent Failure Rate: Why 70-95% Fail in Production&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3234.2" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
