        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Ticking-&gt;root_end#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.84;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.84;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="446.3" y="370.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Run a deeper, slower reflection pass distinct from per-tick reflection — reading hours of recent thoughts, promoting themes, releasing affective residue, and clearing working memory — so the agent does not accumulate residue indefinitely.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="530.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running a long-lived agent that already has two reflection cadences in place: a quick reflection pass that runs after every tick to keep the immediate conversation coherent, and a much slower insight extraction that runs perhaps once a week to promote durable patterns into a long-term store. Between those two cadences there is a gap of several hours during which the agent accumulates thoughts, mood, and partly-finished threads without any consolidation step.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="530.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Per-tick reflection is too shallow to notice that a theme has been recurring all afternoon, and the weekly insight pass is too coarse to release the affective residue from yesterday&#39;s tense exchange before today begins. Without an intermediate sleep-like pass that runs every few hours, the agent keeps ruminating on stale items, its affect scalars never get a chance to decay back toward baseline between sessions, and working memory stays cluttered with threads it should have either consolidated or let go.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="655.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A deeper pass costs more (stronger model, longer context) and cannot run every tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Triggering only on a clock misses affect-driven events that warrant a pass.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Letting the dream pass write to charter or rules turns it into uncontrolled self-edit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resetting working memory is helpful, but resetting too much loses continuity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="693.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: schedule a slower, stronger reflection pass that distils themes, decays affect, and writes to a dedicated journal without editing rules, so that residue is cleared periodically without giving the deep pass unbounded self-edit rights.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="837.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;On a slow timer (every few hours, or when an affect scalar crosses a threshold), pause normal ticking. Load the last few hours of thoughts and affect history. Run a stronger model with a dream-pass prompt that distils themes into journal entries, applies decay to all affect scalars, optionally clears workspace focus, and appends the dream summary to a dedicated dream-journal surface. Persistent learning (rules, charter, insights) is not edited here; the dream pass produces proposals that a subsequent reflection pass can ratify.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="837.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Normal ticking --timer or affect threshold--&amp;gt; Pause ticking --&amp;gt; Load hours of thoughts and affect history --&amp;gt; Stronger model dream pass --&amp;gt; {themes -&amp;gt; dream journal, decay all affect scalars, optional focus clear, proposals} --&amp;gt; Resume ticking; proposals --&amp;gt; later reflection pass --ratify--&amp;gt; persistent learning&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="962.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent has been talking with its user daily for three months. Per-tick reflection keeps it coherent within a session; weekly insight extraction is too coarse. Affective residue from a tense conversation last Tuesday still colours its tone today. The team adds a Dream Consolidation Cycle: once a night the agent reads its last twenty-four hours of thoughts, promotes recurring themes into long-term memory, and writes off the affective residue, clearing working memory before the next day. The agent stops ruminating on stale items.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1019.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affective residue gets a release path that does not depend on weekly cycles.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Themes consolidate at a granularity between per-tick and per-week.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Working memory resets without losing the long-term store.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stronger-model passes are expensive; cadence has to be tuned.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quality of the dream summary depends heavily on the prompt.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; If proposals are not ratified by a follow-up pass, the dream pass becomes journaling without learning.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1125.15" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A dream pass cannot edit charter, rules, or insights directly — its only writes are to the dream-journal surface and to affect-state decay; persistent learning requires a follow-up reflection pass to ratify dream proposals.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1201.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent runs continuously enough to accumulate hours of recent thoughts that need consolidation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affective residue or working-memory clutter measurably degrades reasoning over time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is a separate dream-journal write surface distinct from charter/rules/insights.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1421.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is request-response and never accumulates residue.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is no idle window long enough to run the deeper pass without disturbing user-facing latency.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-tick reflection is already sufficient.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1326.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Per-Tick Reflection — shallow pass that runs after every tick&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Dream Pass — stronger-model pass over hours of recent thoughts and affect&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Dream Journal — dedicated write surface that receives the dream summary&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affect Substrate — receives decay updates from the dream pass&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Trigger — slow timer or affect-threshold event that initiates the pass&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1546.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — stronger model with a long-context dream-pass prompt&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frontmatter store — dream-journal directory keyed by date&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affect-state file — bounded scalars that the dream pass decays&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1451.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Journaling without learning — the dream pass writes proposals, but no follow-up reflection pass ratifies them, so nothing changes in rules or insights.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bad cadence — the pass runs so often that cost climbs, or so rarely that affect residue piles up between passes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Over-clearing — the pass wipes workspace focus while a live task still needs it, and the agent resumes with no thread.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Prompt-shaped themes — a weak dream prompt promotes surface repetition as a theme and misses what actually recurred.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1709.15" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Affect-residue half-life — wall-clock until baseline affect is restored after a stressful exchange&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Theme-promotion rate — recurring themes the dream pass surfaces per cycle&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ratification share — dream proposals that a subsequent reflection pass actually promotes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost per dream pass — tokens and latency spent per cycle&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1576.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot (author&amp;#x27;s long-running personal agent; single private deployment)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Periodic deeper passes consolidate short and mid-term thoughts into long-term insights and clear working state; framed publicly as &#39;System 2 sleep&#39;. Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1929.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Summaries&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Frozen Rubric Reflection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Emotional State Persistence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Axis Promotion Scoring&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cluster-Capped Insight Store&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Meditation Mode&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Sleep-Time Compute&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Fragment Juxtaposition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Corpus Vocabulary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Rogue Agent Drift&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Procedural Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Adaptive Memory Decay&lt;/b&gt; — Idle-time consolidation pairs with continuous reinforcement-modulated decay.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1720.15" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stanford.edu/~jlmcc/papers/McCMcNaughtonOReilly95.pdf&quot;&gt;Why there are complementary learning systems in the hippocampus and neocortex: insights from the successes and failures of connectionist models of learning and memory&lt;/a&gt; — McClelland, McNaughton, O&#39;Reilly, 1995&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20046194/&quot;&gt;The memory function of sleep&lt;/a&gt; — Susanne Diekelmann, Jan Born, 2010&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11691983/&quot;&gt;Sleep, learning, and dreams: off-line memory reprocessing&lt;/a&gt; — Robert Stickgold, J. Allan Hobson, Roar Fosse, Magdalena Fosse, 2001&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2073.15" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="dry-run-harness" name="Dry-Run Harness">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2489.95" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2489.95" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dry-Run Harness&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Safety &amp;amp; Control &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Action Preview Harness, Side-Effect Diff Preview&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
