        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Obs-&gt;Adj#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.16;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.16;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="237.05" y="1142.35" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="yes" mermaidId="e:Adj-&gt;Rec#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.84;exitY=0;entryX=0.72;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="yes" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.84;exitY=0;entryX=0.72;entryY=1;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="1142.35" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="1061.75" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="981.15" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="900.55" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="806.0" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="709.9" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="629.3" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="534.75" />
                <mxPoint x="463.35" y="438.65" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="no" mermaidId="e:Adj-&gt;Done#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="no" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Generate the agent team — role descriptions and instances — at run time based on the specific task, then adjust team composition between iterations based on evaluation feedback.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1672.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A multi-agent platform accepts a wide range of tasks through one entry point — drafting a regulatory filing, refactoring a Python module, planning a marketing campaign — and the right team of specialists varies sharply from one task to the next. The platform cannot know the task type in advance and cannot afford to keep one large fixed crew always running.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1672.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A hard-coded role list is brittle: the team that suits a legal filing is not the team that suits a code refactor, and the writer-reviewer-editor lineup that helped the first request is dead weight for the second. Over-provisioning a large fixed pool wastes tokens and creates noise. Under-provisioning misses the specialist the task actually needed. Without a way to assemble the team at run time, every workflow either drags around unnecessary roles or quietly skips work that should have happened.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1778.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Pre-specified roles are stable but mis-fit;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Run-time generation costs an extra LLM call before any work begins;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adaptive composition risks instability: the team that solves step 1 may not solve step 5.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1816.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: let a recruiter agent generate the role descriptions and instantiate the team for the specific goal, and adjust composition between iterations on evaluator feedback, so that the team matches the task instead of the task being squeezed into a fixed team.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1941.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Add a recruiter agent (or a meta-agent committee: planner + agent observer + plan observer). Stage 1 — Drafting: recruiter receives the goal, generates role descriptions matched to that goal, instantiates the team and an execution plan. Stage 2 — Execution: the team works. Stage 3 — Evaluation: a reviewer scores progress; if unsatisfactory, the recruiter adjusts the team (add, remove, replace roles) and the next iteration runs. The recruiter is the only meta-agent that mutates team composition.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1941.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;goal -&amp;gt; Recruiter -&amp;gt; [role descriptions] -&amp;gt; instantiated agents -&amp;gt; joint execution -&amp;gt; Evaluator -&amp;gt; feedback -&amp;gt; Recruiter (adjust team) -&amp;gt; ...&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2066.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A multi-agent platform runs both &#39;draft a regulatory filing&#39; and &#39;refactor this Python module&#39; through the same hard-coded team of writer, reviewer, and editor. The reviewer is fine for prose but useless on code. They switch to Dynamic Expert Recruitment: a meta-agent reads the task and instantiates appropriate roles — for the filing, a compliance expert and a legal editor; for the refactor, a senior engineer and a unit-test author. After the first iteration&#39;s evaluation, the team composition is adjusted between rounds.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2104.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Team matches the task instead of the task being squeezed into a fixed team.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adaptive composition closes the gap as the task evolves.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recruiter prompt is the only place the meta-policy lives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recruiter quality is the bottleneck; a bad recruiter produces bad teams.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Run-time team generation is non-deterministic; reproducibility suffers.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adjustment between iterations can churn (replace too aggressively).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2191.5" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No role may be instantiated outside the recruiter; agents may not unilaterally co-opt or invent peers.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2286.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Hard-coded role lists are brittle because the right team varies wildly across tasks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A recruiter agent can generate role descriptions and instantiate the team based on the goal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evaluation feedback can drive team composition adjustments between iterations.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2468.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tasks are homogeneous enough that one fixed team handles them all.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recruiter latency or cost outweighs the benefit of dynamic team composition.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stable, certified roles are required for compliance reasons.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2392.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Recruiter agent — reads the goal and generates role descriptions matched to that goal&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Generated specialist team — instantiated agents whose roles came from the recruiter, not a fixed list&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Plan observer — meta-agent that scores progress against the original goal&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent observer — meta-agent that scores team composition and flags missing or unused roles&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composition mutator — recruiter step that adds, removes, or replaces team members between iterations&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2593.5" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — recruiter and observers each cost a call before and between work iterations&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent registry — runtime catalogue where freshly instantiated roles are registered and addressable&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; AgentVerse or AutoAgents framework — supplies the recruiter scaffolding and observer harness&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2517.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Bad recruiter, bad team — the recruiter misreads the goal and generates roles that do not fit it, and every later iteration inherits that mistake.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Team churn — the recruiter replaces roles after every weak evaluation, and no team runs long enough to show whether it works.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unreproducible runs — the same goal produces a different team each time, so a good result cannot be repeated or debugged.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-recruiting agents — a team member invents a new peer on its own, outside the recruiter, and the team grows without control.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2794.5" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Team-fit score — observer-rated match between generated roles and task needs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composition churn — roles added or replaced per iteration, against an over-churn threshold&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; End-to-end success vs fixed-team baseline — does dynamic recruitment beat a hard-coded crew&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recruiter latency overhead — extra wall-clock spent generating and adjusting the team&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reproducibility variance — outcome spread across repeated runs with the same goal&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2642.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/OpenBMB/AgentVerse&quot;&gt;AgentVerse&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Recruiter agent generates expert descriptions per goal; team composition adjusted across iterations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Link-AGI/AutoAgents&quot;&gt;AutoAgents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Drafting stage with three meta-agents (Planner, Agent Observer, Plan Observer) synthesises the team.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3014.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Supervisor&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Role Assignment&lt;/b&gt; — Role assignment is the design-time special case.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Mixture of Experts Routing&lt;/b&gt; — MoE routes to a fixed expert pool; this constructs the experts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Orchestrator-Workers&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Evaluator-Optimizer&lt;/b&gt; — Evaluation step drives team adjustment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tacit-Knowledge Elicitation Agent&lt;/b&gt; — Expert recruitment spins up synthetic agent personas at run time; elicitation extracts real human experts&#39; tacit knowledge into a reusable base ahead of time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Consensus-Averaging Over Expertise&lt;/b&gt; — Recruitment names the expert for the task; consensus-averaging is the failure to use that expert because the team compromises toward the average.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2805.5" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.10848&quot;&gt;AgentVerse: Facilitating Multi-Agent Collaboration and Exploring Emergent Behaviors&lt;/a&gt; — Chen et al., 2023&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.17288&quot;&gt;AutoAgents: A Framework for Automatic Agent Generation&lt;/a&gt; — Chen et al., 2023&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3158.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="dynamic-scaffolding" name="Dynamic Scaffolding">
