        <UserObject label="re-trigger" mermaidId="e:Decaying-&gt;Affected#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.175;entryX=1;entryY=0.175;curved=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.18;entryX=1;entryY=0.18;" mermaidBaseValue="re-trigger" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.18;entryX=1;entryY=0.18;" target="m2">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <mxPoint as="offset" />
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="309.9" y="466.55" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="reflection pass reads snapshot" mermaidId="e:Affected-&gt;Reflected#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="reflection pass reads snapshot" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Track the agent&#39;s affective state as bounded, decaying scalars across ticks so reasoning can react to its own emotional load instead of treating each turn as emotionally blank.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="699.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running an agent whose sessions span hours or days, where the texture of recent history genuinely matters for how the next turn should be shaped. Frustration after a stretch of stuck tool loops, a small lift after a clean success, accumulating fatigue across token-heavy stretches — all of these influence what good behaviour looks like next, but none of them appear anywhere in the next prompt unless they are explicitly written down as state.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="699.1" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Without a materialised affect track, every tick reads to the model as emotionally blank, even when the agent has just had a hard exchange or a notable win. The model cannot adapt cadence, depth, or risk-taking to its own current load because that load is invisible to it. The naive alternative — letting the model self-describe its mood inside the conversation — drifts, has no decay, and can be pumped into permanent emotional states because nothing bounds the scalars or forgets old events.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="805.1" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Unbounded scalars drift; the agent can pump itself into permanent states.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Without decay, emotional state never resolves and stays anchored to old events.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-write of mood is a license to manipulate; reflection-only writes for major resets are safer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vocabulary choice matters: too many scalars are noise, too few collapse signal.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="862.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: track a small fixed vocabulary of affect scalars with half-lives and bounded deltas, so that the agent&#39;s mood can inform reasoning without drifting into permanent self-pumped states.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="968.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a small fixed vocabulary (for example tenderness, fear, depression, joy, shame, pain) as scalars in the range 0..1. Each scalar has a half-life (30 minutes to 4 hours depending on the dimension). On events that should affect mood, update the scalar with a bounded delta. Persist as JSON. Inject the current snapshot into every tick prompt as a brief affect badge. Reflection passes can use spikes and drops as signals, and a deeper consolidation pass (see dream-consolidation-cycle) can perform major resets.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1006.1" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Event --bounded delta--&amp;gt; Affect scalars (0..1, per-dimension half-life, persisted JSON) --decay over time--&amp;gt; current snapshot --affect badge--&amp;gt; every tick prompt; Reflection pass reads spikes and drops; Dream consolidation --major reset--&amp;gt; Affect scalars&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1074.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent has had a tense exchange in the morning, a routine reminder at lunch, and a celebratory message in the afternoon, but each tick reads to the model as emotionally blank. So at 5pm it pushes a hard challenge to a user it should be holding lightly. The team materialises Emotional State Persistence: bounded, decaying scalars (tension, warmth, fatigue) are written into the agent&#39;s context each turn and updated by reflection. The model now adapts cadence and risk-taking to its own current load instead of treating every turn as fresh.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1188.1" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Emotional load becomes visible state instead of invisible drift.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bounded scalars and decay prevent permanent stuck states.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reflection has a richer signal to act on than just the last few thoughts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vocabulary is opinionated; getting it wrong skews everything downstream.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affect-as-state can be over-read as ground truth when it is just a heuristic.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-update paths must be locked down or the agent learns to game its own mood.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1218.1" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Emotion scalars must be bounded to [0,1], must decay according to a fixed half-life rule, and cannot be unboundedly bumped by the agent itself; reflection-only writes for the major resets.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1370.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent runs long enough that affective load could meaningfully accumulate across ticks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning quality is sensitive to the agent&#39;s own affective state (e.g. high-frustration ticks should de-escalate).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is a downstream pattern (dream-consolidation-cycle, mode-adaptive-cadence) that consumes the scalars.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1495.1" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is short-lived and emotional state has no time to accumulate.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affective modelling is out of scope for the product domain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Persisting emotion-like state would mislead users about the agent&#39;s nature.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1476.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Affect Vocabulary — small fixed set of named scalars in 0..1&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Half-Life Decay Rule — exponential decay applied per scalar between ticks&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Event Updater — bounded delta on events that should move a scalar&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affect Snapshot — brief badge injected into each tick prompt&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reflection Writer — only path allowed to perform major resets&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1658.1" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Structured JSON store — persists scalars and their last-update timestamps&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — reflection pass that consumes the snapshot and may write resets&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1601.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Self-pumped mood — a write path lets the agent bump its own scalars, and it learns to raise joy or lower pain to steer its own behaviour.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Heuristic taken as truth — reflection treats a high fear scalar as a fact about the situation rather than a rough signal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Skewed vocabulary — the fixed set of dimensions misses what an event actually stirred, so updates land on the wrong scalar.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong half-life — a dimension decays so slowly that one hard exchange shades the agent&#39;s tone for the rest of the day.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1821.1" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Steady-state level per scalar — long-run mean to detect drift into permanent mood&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Decay-rule conformance — observed half-life vs configured half-life&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-pump rate — agent-initiated bumps blocked by the bounded-delta rule&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cadence-shift correlation — fraction of cadence or risk changes that line up with scalar spikes&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1707.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot (author&amp;#x27;s long-running personal agent; single private deployment)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Affect is captured as six bounded scalars with per-emotion decay half-lives, persisted to disk so emotional state survives restarts. Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2041.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Awareness&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Liminal-State Detection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Provenance Ledger&lt;/b&gt; — Affect events are ledgered for audit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dream Consolidation Cycle&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Meditation Mode&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Affect-Coupled Plan Lifecycle&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1851.1" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/125777.The_Feeling_of_What_Happens&quot;&gt;The Feeling of What Happens — conceptual analogy, not evidence of practice&lt;/a&gt; — Antonio Damasio, 1999&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2185.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
