          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="regressed" mermaidId="e:Run-&gt;Block#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.02;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="regressed" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.02;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1291.18" y="186.8" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="holds" mermaidId="e:Run-&gt;Ship#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.98;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="holds" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.98;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1291.18" y="309.3" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Forbid building the LLM application before its evaluation harness exists; freeze the eval set first and let those metrics drive model selection, prompting, and every subsequent change.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="386.11" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team starts an LLM application — RAG over policy documents, an agent that fills CRM fields, a chatbot for a narrow workflow. The first instinct is to prototype the prompt, see if it &#39;feels right&#39;, then circle back to evaluation when stakeholders ask for numbers.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="386.11" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Eval-after-build collapses for three reasons. The team converges on prompts that look good on hand-picked demos; the evaluation written later is shaped by what the prompt already does well rather than by the user need. Model swaps, prompt refactors, and tool changes have no comparator — every commit is a vibe check. When a stakeholder finally demands quality numbers, building the harness retroactively requires re-running every prior change, which never happens. The application ships with no defensible quality story.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="492.11" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Building eval first feels slower than prototyping but is faster once the first regression appears.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval sets must be frozen before changes start, or every change moves the bar.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval sets shaped after the prompt encode the prompt&#39;s biases.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Without eval, model swaps and prompt edits have no comparator.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="511.11" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: build the evaluation harness and a frozen eval set before the first prompt commit, so every subsequent change is judged against a stable target rather than against author taste.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="674.11" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Before authoring the first prompt, write the eval. Define what &#39;good&#39; means as a checkable rubric (an expected-output set, a judge prompt against a frozen rubric, a deterministic checker, or a mix). Build the eval set from real user inputs or synthetic inputs that span the named dimensions of the task. Pin the rubric and the set as a versioned artifact. Run every prompt change, model swap, and tool edit through that harness; any drop is a blocker.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="655.11" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team building a contract-clause-summarisation agent freezes a 200-item eval set drawn from real contracts the legal team flagged. The judge rubric scores three named properties (faithfulness, named-entity coverage, length). The first prompt scores 71%. Every prompt edit, every model upgrade from one Sonnet generation to the next, every retrieval tweak runs through the harness; any drop is a blocker. Three months in the team has comparable numbers for nine prompt variants and three models.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="780.11" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Model swaps, prompt edits, and tool changes have a single comparator.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Surfaces regressions early; every commit is a measurement.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Forces explicit articulation of &#39;what good looks like&#39; before development begins.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Front-loaded eval work delays first shippable prototype.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval sets drift away from production traffic if not periodically refreshed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frozen rubric can become a goal in itself, gameable by overfitting prompts.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="818.11" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The application must not be developed before its evaluation harness exists; the frozen rubric and eval set are authored first and changes are gated on them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="943.11" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Starting an LLM application that will change prompts, models, or tools over its lifetime.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple engineers will work on the same prompt and need a comparator.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quality regressions are user-visible and must be caught before deployment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1095.11" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Throwaway prototype with a one-week lifespan.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No agreed definition of &#39;good&#39; is reachable in the project&#39;s timeframe.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The application has no notion of correct answer (purely creative outputs with no rubric).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1049.11" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;AI Engineering (Huyen) — Evaluation-Driven Development chapter&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;i&gt;Available&lt;/i&gt; — &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/ai-engineering/9781098166298/&quot;&gt;https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/ai-engineering/9781098166298/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Production LLM teams running rubric-judged eval gates on every prompt commit&lt;/b&gt; — &lt;i&gt;Available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1220.11" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; → [eval-harness](eval-harness.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; → [frozen-rubric-reflection](frozen-rubric-reflection.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; → [llm-as-judge](llm-as-judge.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; → [shadow-canary](shadow-canary.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; → [dimensional-synthetic-eval-set](dimensional-synthetic-eval-set.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; → [demo-to-production-cliff](demo-to-production-cliff.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; → [bayesian-bandit-experimentation](bayesian-bandit-experimentation.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; → [sampled-prompt-trace-eval](sampled-prompt-trace-eval.md)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; → [prompt-variant-evaluation](prompt-variant-evaluation.md)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1174.11" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; (book) &lt;i&gt;AI Engineering&lt;/i&gt;, Chip Huyen, 2024, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/ai-engineering/9781098166298/&quot;&gt;https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/ai-engineering/9781098166298/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; evaluation, process, governance&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1345.11" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
