        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Surface-&gt;L#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m19">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m7" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m8">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Catch and react to predictable failure modes (tool errors, rate limits, validation failures) with structured recovery paths.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1266.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team runs a production agent that calls many tools in a loop: search APIs, internal databases, third-party services, model endpoints. In real traffic those tools fail in predictable, repeating ways — the API is briefly down, the caller hit a rate limit, the response came back malformed, the credential was rejected, the request timed out. Each of those failure modes wants a different response from the agent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1266.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If the tool layer returns errors as opaque strings stuffed back into the conversation, the agent treats them as text and reacts with whatever the model invents — sometimes a retry, sometimes a confident hallucinated explanation to the user, sometimes a stall. The agent has no way to branch deterministically on a rate-limit versus a validation error, so it cannot back off correctly on the first or replan on the second. Without typed errors and named recovery branches, the team is forced to choose between blanket retries that mask real bugs and giving up on partial-failure handling altogether.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1372.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Recovery logic must not mask bugs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Some errors are user-visible; others should be silent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Retry storms on transient errors.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1429.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: catalogue each predictable failure as a typed error with a defined recovery branch (retry, fall back, surface, replan), so that the agent reacts deterministically instead of hallucinating an explanation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1554.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Catalogue failure modes. For each, define: detect (typed error), respond (retry / fall back / surface to user / replan), and log. The agent receives a structured error message and can react with a typed branch in its loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1554.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent step --error?--&amp;gt; Typed error --&amp;gt; Recovery branch: transient -&amp;gt; retry with backoff | rate limit -&amp;gt; wait + retry | validation -&amp;gt; fall back / replan | unknown -&amp;gt; surface to user; every branch --&amp;gt; structured log&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1679.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research agent calls a search tool that returns a rate-limit error. Without typed handling the error string flows back into the conversation as an opaque blob; the agent invents a plausible-sounding explanation and stalls. The team adds Exception Recovery: each tool wraps known failure modes (rate-limit, auth, validation, timeout) into typed error envelopes, and the agent&#39;s prompt has explicit recovery branches — back off and retry on rate-limit, switch tool on validation, escalate on auth. Failures stop becoming silent confusion.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1679.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Failure modes become first-class.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reliability under partial failures rises.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Exception-handling code is its own surface to maintain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hidden retries can mask deeper issues.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1823.4" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Errors must arrive at the agent as typed events from the catalogue; untyped errors are escalated to the operator.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1861.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tool errors, rate limits, or validation failures occur often enough that random retries waste effort.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Failure modes can be catalogued with typed errors and structured recovery responses.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent loop can branch on typed error messages.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2062.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Failures are rare enough that a single generic retry handles them.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Failure modes change faster than the catalogue can be maintained.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has no loop to react in (single-shot pipelines).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1967.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Failure-mode catalogue — enumerated typed errors the system knows how to react to&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool wrapper — translator from raw tool exceptions into typed error envelopes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recovery branch table — mapping from error type to retry, fallback, replan, or surface&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Structured error log — record of typed events for later debugging and trend analysis&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2206.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Exponential-backoff utility — paces retries on transient and rate-limit errors&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Structured logging library — emits typed error events to the central log&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2092.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Masking retry — a silent retry loop keeps succeeding on the third attempt, and a degrading dependency goes unnoticed until it fails for good.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Uncatalogued error — a new failure arrives that maps to no typed branch, falls into &#39;unknown&#39;, and the agent treats a recoverable case as fatal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong branch — a validation error is classed as transient, so the agent retries the same bad input with backoff instead of replanning.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2350.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Recovery-success rate by error type — share of typed errors the right branch resolved&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Untyped-error escape rate — failures that bypassed the catalogue and surfaced raw&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Retry-storm incidents — back-off violations that overran a downstream quota&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mean steps to recovery — loop iterations between first failure and stable progress&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2198.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Production agent platforms&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Gulli Exception Handling pattern&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Tool errors and plan-step failures are typed; each type has a deterministic recovery path (retry-once, abort-step, escalate-to-human) rather than a generic try/except wrapper.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2532.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Fallback Chain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Circuit Breaker&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Replan on Failure&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Graceful Degradation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Missing Idempotency on Agent Calls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Machine-Checkable Tool Contract&lt;/b&gt; — Recovery presupposes the failure is detectable; typed failure fields are what make it detectable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2342.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/237795815&quot;&gt;Agentic Design Patterns (Gulli)&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2695.4" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
