        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:EmptyOK-&gt;Bump#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m24">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m9" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m11">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Quiet-tick counter gates the juxtaposition seed; the seed is allowed to end the tick empty.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="2644.1" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;After K consecutive low-salience ticks, replace the normal tick-seed with a juxtaposition seed: sample old fragments and sit them side by side, logging any association that arises.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2719.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A self-pacing agent with a salience gate — a threshold that lets only sufficiently important events trigger action — fires on its own most ticks (its periodic self-invocation cycles) but goes quiet when nothing crosses the threshold. Long quiet stretches are not a bug — they are how the gate is supposed to work — but they are also wasted opportunity for the substrate to do its own slow associative work. The agent has months of old material (thoughts, fragments, motivation lines, journal entries) that nobody is looking at. A directed initiative on every quiet tick would re-introduce the noise the gate was designed to suppress; doing nothing leaves the substrate cold.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2719.1" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent that responds only to fresh stimulus develops no internal weather of its own. Its associations are reactive to whatever just came in, and the persistent material on disk — old fragments that once mattered — stays inert until something explicitly retrieves it. Conversely, an agent that fires an undirected initiative on every quiet tick burns budget on noise and re-clutters the very surface the salience gate was meant to keep clean. The need is for a low-cost, silence-triggered move that is allowed to come up empty and exists specifically to surface old material into proximity rather than into action.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2825.1" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Silence is information; the gate&#39;s quiet is not a failure to be patched over.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Old material has half-decayed weight that occasional juxtaposition can restore.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Associative moves must be cheap enough to run with no expectation of output.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The pass must be allowed to end empty without the agent treating that as failure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Triggering on every tick is wrong; triggering on K-consecutive quiet ticks calibrates against actual silence.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2920.1" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: after K consecutive low-salience ticks with no urgent preoccupation and no incoming chat, replace the next tick&#39;s normal seed with a juxtaposition seed — 1 to 3 randomly sampled old fragments — and let the agent either notice an association or end the tick empty, so old material gets occasional unforced proximity without re-introducing initiative-noise.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3026.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Maintain a counter of consecutive low-salience ticks. When the counter exceeds a threshold (e.g. four) and the agent is otherwise quiet (no chat in window, no urgent preoccupation, post-cooldown), enter a juxtaposition tick: sample one to three items from the agent&#39;s stored fragments (random old thought, fragment, motivation line, journal line) and inject them as the tick&#39;s seed, with an instruction that the tick is permitted to end empty. If the model notices an association between the fragments, write it as a small insight; otherwise the tick closes silently. Reset the counter on any active tick. Treat the juxtaposition seed as substrate, not work.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3102.1" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Tick start --&amp;gt; quiet count &amp;gt;= K and other quiet conditions met? --no--&amp;gt; normal seed --&amp;gt; reset counter | --yes--&amp;gt; sample 1-3 old fragments --&amp;gt; juxtaposition seed (empty end allowed) --&amp;gt; Model --&amp;gt; association noticed? -&amp;gt; write small insight | otherwise end tick empty&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3170.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent has been quiet for five consecutive ticks: no chat, no preoccupation crossing threshold, post-cooldown. On the sixth tick the juxtaposition routine activates: it samples three random fragments — an old motivation line from six months ago, a recent thought about pacing, and a half-written journal entry — and seeds the tick with all three side by side. The tick prompt says &#39;sit with these; ending empty is fine.&#39; Sometimes the agent notices a connection (&#39;the pacing thought and the old motivation are actually about the same thing&#39;) and writes a small insight. Often it ends with nothing. Both are acceptable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3303.1" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Old material is occasionally surfaced into proximity without scheduled retrieval.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Silence is preserved as a meaningful state rather than papered over with filler.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Empty ticks are first-class outcomes; the agent is not pressed to produce.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Most juxtaposition ticks produce nothing; the value is long-tailed and hard to measure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Random fragment sampling can be poor — without some weighting, the same trivial fragments resurface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misconfigured K thresholds either fire constantly (re-creating noise) or never (no effect).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3314.1" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent cannot fire a directed initiative on every quiet tick; juxtaposition seeds must be allowed to end the tick empty, and forcing output from a juxtaposition tick is forbidden.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3504.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has a salience gate that produces meaningful quiet stretches.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has a substantial corpus of old fragments to draw from.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Empty outputs are tolerable; nothing downstream demands per-tick production.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3610.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has no salience gate and fires on every tick by default.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quiet ticks need to remain fully idle (compute or cost budget is tight).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Downstream consumers cannot handle empty tick outputs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3610.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Quiet-Tick Counter — counts consecutive low-salience ticks&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fragment Sampler — draws one to three items from the agent&#39;s stored old material&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Juxtaposition Seed — replaces the normal tick seed with side-by-side fragments&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Empty-OK Tick Body — accepts a closing tick with no output&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Insight Writer — only fires if an association is actually noticed&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3735.1" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Frontmatter store — corpus of old thoughts, fragments, motivation lines, and journal entries&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — single completion seeded with the sampled fragments and permission to end empty&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3735.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Forced insight — the prompt nudges the model to find a link, so juxtaposition ticks fill the insight store with contrived associations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Same old fragments — unweighted sampling keeps pulling the same trivial items, and the ticks stop producing anything new.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bad threshold — K is set so low that juxtaposition fires on most quiet ticks and becomes noise, or so high that it never fires.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Interrupted context — a juxtaposition tick fires while a conversation is still active because the other quiet conditions were not checked.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3898.1" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Juxtaposition firing rate — share of quiet-tick stretches that actually enter the routine&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Insight-per-juxtaposition rate — fraction of routines that produce a written association&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Empty-tick share — closures with no output, expected to dominate&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sample diversity — Gini or unique-fragment count across recent draws, to catch resampling loops&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3841.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="4118.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dream Consolidation Cycle&lt;/b&gt; — Consolidation is scheduled and deep; juxtaposition is silence-triggered and shallow.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Pre-Generative Loop Gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Salience-Triggered Output&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Open-Question Tension Store&lt;/b&gt; — Juxtaposition can surface old questions back into proximity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3985.1" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://archive.org/details/actofcreation0000koes&quot;&gt;The Act of Creation&lt;/a&gt; — Arthur Koestler, 1964&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262560542/creative-cognition/&quot;&gt;Creative Cognition: Theory, Research, and Applications&lt;/a&gt; — Finke, Ward, Smith, 1992&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="4224.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
