        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Desk-&gt;FS#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.27;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.27;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="673.87" y="435.0" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Desk-&gt;PW#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.73;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.73;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1004.06" y="435.0" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="bounded by" mermaidId="e:Desk-&gt;SB#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.85;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="bounded by" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.85;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1365.94" y="435.0" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Give the agent a complete containerized OS desktop with native apps, a persistent filesystem, and desktop credential stores, so it can finish multi-application workflows a browser-only surface cannot.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="621.32" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team needs an agent to complete real end-user workflows that cross several native applications: download an invoice in a mail client, edit it in a spreadsheet app, sign into a vendor portal through a password manager, then file the result in a local folder. The applications have no shared API, some live only on the desktop, and steps depend on files and logins that must survive from one step to the next.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="621.32" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A browser-only agent reaches web pages but cannot drive native desktop applications, install tools it needs mid-task, or hold a working filesystem across steps. A single-app or pixel-only Computer Use surface drives one screen at a time but provides no durable storage and no credential store, so logins, downloaded artifacts, and installed tooling evaporate between turns. Workflows that span a mail client, an editor, a terminal, and an authenticated portal stall because no single narrow surface covers all of them and nothing carries state across the application boundaries.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="727.32" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Full-OS scope covers native apps a browser surface cannot reach.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A persistent filesystem and installed tooling must survive across steps.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Desktop credential stores enable logins and 2FA but widen the blast radius.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A whole OS is heavier and slower to provision than a single browser tab.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="784.32" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: run the agent inside a containerized OS desktop with native applications, a persistent filesystem, and a configured password manager, so that it completes multi-application workflows end-to-end while staying inside an isolation boundary.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="909.32" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Provision a containerized desktop OS (for example Ubuntu with a lightweight window manager) preloaded with a browser, mail client, editor, and terminal. The agent observes the screen and emits mouse and keyboard actions over the whole desktop, not one app. A mounted persistent filesystem retains downloads, installed packages, and intermediate artifacts across steps. A desktop password manager extension supplies credentials and handles two-factor prompts. The entire desktop is the sandbox: the agent has full scope inside it and none outside it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="928.32" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent --mouse / keyboard--&amp;gt; Containerized OS desktop --screenshot--&amp;gt; Agent; Desktop contains native apps (mail / editor / terminal / browser) + persistent filesystem + password manager with 2FA, all bounded by the sandbox isolation boundary&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1034.32" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An operations agent must pull a PDF invoice from a mail client, reconcile it in a desktop spreadsheet, log into a supplier portal that requires two-factor authentication, and save a receipt locally. A browser-only agent cannot open the mail client or the spreadsheet app and loses the downloaded file between steps. Placed on a full containerized desktop with a persistent home directory and a configured password manager, the agent opens each native app in turn, keeps the invoice on disk across steps, and clears the 2FA prompt from the password manager extension.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1110.32" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Completes workflows that span native desktop applications, not just web pages.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Persistent filesystem and installed tooling carry state across steps and sessions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Desktop credential stores let the agent clear logins and 2FA without hardcoded secrets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A whole OS is slower and costlier to provision and snapshot than a single browser tab.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stored credentials and a persistent disk widen the blast radius if the agent is compromised or prompt-injected.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Maintaining a desktop image (apps, drivers, window manager) is ongoing engineering.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1178.32" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent must operate inside the containerized desktop boundary only; it cannot reach the host OS or any resource outside the provisioned image.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1292.32" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The task spans several native desktop applications with no shared API.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; State (downloads, installed tools, logins) must persist across steps or sessions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent needs authenticated access through a desktop password manager, including 2FA.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1474.32" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The whole task lives in the browser and a Browser Agent surface suffices.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A clean API covers the workflow and is cheaper and more reliable than driving a desktop.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The deployment cannot afford the provisioning cost or the blast radius of a persistent credentialed OS.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1398.32" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Containerized Desktop OS — provisioned image (e.g. Ubuntu plus a window manager) the agent operates as a whole&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Native Application Set — preinstalled mail client, editor, terminal, and browser the agent drives directly&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Persistent Filesystem — mounted home/working directory that retains downloads, artifacts, and installed packages across steps&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credential Store — desktop password-manager extension that supplies logins and clears two-factor prompts&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Screenshot/Action Loop — feeds screen frames in and applies mouse and keyboard actions across the whole desktop&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1599.32" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Container runtime (Docker or equivalent) — hosts the desktop image and enforces the isolation boundary&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Desktop automation library (xdotool, PyAutoGUI, or platform equivalent) — applies the emitted mouse and keyboard actions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Password manager (1Password, Bitwarden) — stores credentials and handles 2FA inside the desktop&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1542.32" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Credential exposure — a prompt-injected page drives the agent to open the password manager, and stored logins are used for the wrong site.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Persistent contamination — a malicious download stays on the persistent disk, and later steps run it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Image rot — an app or driver in the desktop image falls out of date, and workflows break on a dialog the agent has never seen.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Slow provisioning — booting and snapshotting a whole OS per task makes short jobs costly and slow.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1857.32" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-app workflow success rate — fraction of cross-application tasks completed end-to-end&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; State-persistence integrity — share of runs where files and logins survive correctly across steps&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Authenticated-step success rate — fraction of login and 2FA steps cleared without manual help&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Desktop provisioning latency — cold-start time to a ready credentialed desktop&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Containment incidents — confirmed reaches outside the desktop boundary per million runs&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1705.32" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/bytebot-ai/bytebot&quot;&gt;Bytebot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Self-hosted agent running a containerized Ubuntu desktop (XFCE) with Firefox, an editor, and a mail client; persistent filesystem, and password-manager extensions for logins and 2FA.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/news/3-5-models-and-computer-use&quot;&gt;Anthropic Computer Use reference desktop image&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Ships a containerized desktop (browser plus utilities) the model drives end-to-end, used as the canonical full-desktop reference environment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2058.32" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Computer Use&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Sandbox Isolation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Browser Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1868.32" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/bytebot-ai/bytebot&quot;&gt;bytebot-ai/bytebot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.bytebot.ai&quot;&gt;Bytebot Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/news/3-5-models-and-computer-use&quot;&gt;Introducing computer use, a new Claude 3.5 Sonnet, and Claude 3.5 Haiku&lt;/a&gt; — Anthropic, 2024&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2240.32" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="generate-and-test-strategy" name="Generate-and-Test Strategy">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2565.95" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2565.95" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
