        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;A handoff vanishes with no acknowledgement or error, so the parent closes over an orphaned subtask and nothing triggers recovery.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="889.5" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: in a multi-agent hierarchy a task handoff silently vanishes — the delegated work waits forever and the parent closes while its subtask is orphaned, and because no error fires nothing restarts it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="964.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A multi-agent system decomposes work hierarchically: a parent or orchestrator agent delegates subtasks to other agents and waits for their results to assemble a final answer. Delegation happens through messages, queues, or tool calls between agents. The parent expects each delegated subtask to come back, and composes its result once the children report in.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="964.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Sometimes a handoff just disappears: the delegated subtask is never picked up, or it enters a wait that never resolves, while the parent — having no signal that anything went wrong — eventually closes or moves on, leaving the subtask orphaned. Because nothing raised an error, no retry, timeout, or recovery path triggers; the work is simply gone, and the final result is silently incomplete. In production multi-agent systems this lost-handoff failure is a large share of observed breakdowns, and it is hard to spot precisely because there is no error to find.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1089.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Delegation across agents is asynchronous, so a dropped or never-acknowledged handoff produces silence rather than an exception.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A parent that composes results when children report cannot distinguish a slow child from one that will never return without an explicit timeout.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No error means no automatic retry or recovery fires, so a lost subtask stays lost.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adding acknowledgements, timeouts, and orphan detection to every handoff is overhead a happy-path design skips.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1108.5" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: do not treat a delegated subtask as fire-and-forget; require acknowledgement of every handoff, put a timeout and explicit completion contract on each subtask, and detect orphaned or never-returning work so it is restarted or escalated instead of silently lost.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1271.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Make every delegation accountable end to end. Require the receiving agent to acknowledge a handoff, so an unpicked-up subtask is detectable rather than silent, and put a timeout and an explicit completion contract on each delegated subtask so a never-resolving wait surfaces as a failure the system can act on. Track outstanding subtasks against their parent so the parent cannot close while a child is still owed, and detect orphaned work to retry or escalate it. Treat a missing result as an error condition, not as nothing — the absence of a report is itself the signal. The control is acknowledgement plus timeouts plus orphan detection, so a lost handoff becomes a recoverable event rather than a silent gap.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1309.5" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Parent delegates subtask -&amp;gt; handoff dropped or waits forever (no ack, no error) -&amp;gt; parent closes, subtask orphaned -&amp;gt; no recovery fires -&amp;gt; result silently incomplete (BROKEN) ; Corrected: ack + timeout + completion contract + orphan detection -&amp;gt; retry/escalate&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1396.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An orchestrator agent delegates a data-fetch subtask to a worker and moves on to assemble the report. The worker never acknowledges the handoff — a queue hiccup dropped it — so it never runs, and nothing errors. The orchestrator, seeing no failure, finishes and returns a report missing that data. No log shows a problem; the only sign is the silently absent section, discovered later by a user.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1529.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: fire-and-forget handoffs are simple to build and need no acknowledgement or tracking code.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team require acknowledgements, timeouts, and completion contracts, and treat a missing result as an error.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Final results are silently incomplete because a delegated subtask vanished with no error to flag it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Orphaned subtasks consume resources or hang indefinitely while the parent reports done.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Debugging is hard: there is no exception, log line, or failure to trace back to the lost handoff.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The failure scales with hierarchy depth, since every delegation boundary is another place a handoff can disappear.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1540.5" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A delegated subtask must not be treated as fire-and-forget; every handoff is acknowledged, each subtask carries a timeout and completion contract, and a parent cannot close while a delegated child is still outstanding — a missing result is handled as a failure rather than ignored.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1673.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Recognising this failure when a multi-agent system returns silently incomplete results with no error to trace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reviewing a delegation design where handoffs are fire-and-forget with no acknowledgement or timeout.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diagnosing orphaned subtasks or parents that close while children are still outstanding.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1893.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Every handoff is acknowledged, each subtask has a timeout and completion contract, and orphaned work is detected and recovered.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is no inter-agent delegation, so no handoff can be lost.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Delegation is synchronous and a dropped subtask raises an immediate error.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1798.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Parent or orchestrator agent — delegates subtasks and composes their results&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Delegated subtask — the unit of work handed to a child agent that can silently vanish&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Handoff channel — the message, queue, or call across which delegation can be dropped&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing acknowledgement and timeout — the absent contract that would make a lost handoff detectable&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing orphan detection — the absent tracking that would catch a never-returning subtask&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2056.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-agent orchestrator — runs the delegation this anti-pattern leaves unacknowledged&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Handoff acknowledgement and timeout — the corrective contract on each delegated subtask&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Outstanding-task tracker — the corrective that detects orphaned work for retry or escalation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1942.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Lost handoff — a delegated subtask is never acknowledged or picked up and simply disappears.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Infinite wait — the subtask enters a state that never resolves, with no timeout to end it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Orphaned subtask — the parent closes while a child it delegated is still outstanding.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No recovery trigger — because nothing errored, no retry or escalation path ever fires.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2238.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Lost-handoff rate — fraction of delegated subtasks that never returned and were not detected&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Silent-incompletion rate — share of final results missing a subtask with no error raised&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Orphan-detection latency — time from a dropped handoff to it being caught&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recovery coverage — fraction of lost subtasks retried or escalated rather than abandoned&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2067.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://shalomeir.substack.com/p/multi-agent-orchestration-problems&quot;&gt;Multi-agent orchestration post-mortem (Ghost Delegation)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Production write-up attributing a large share of failures to delegation that should have happened entering infinite wait, with handoffs vanishing mid-process and subtasks left orphaned.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://azguards.com/technical/the-delegation-ping-pong-breaking-infinite-handoff-loops-in-crewai-hierarchical-topologies/&quot;&gt;CrewAI delegation ping-pong&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Hierarchical CrewAI topologies hit infinite handoff loops that saturate the context window and crash, a related lost-control-of-delegation failure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.13657&quot;&gt;MAST multi-agent failure taxonomy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Empirical taxonomy whose premature-termination, information-withholding, and task-derailment modes formalise a handoff ending before objectives are met, clustered under inter-agent misalignment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2382.5" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Phantom Action Completion&lt;/b&gt; — Phantom completion narrates a task as done that never ran; ghost delegation makes no claim — a handoff just vanishes, leaving an orphaned subtask and no error.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cascading Agent Failures&lt;/b&gt; — Cascading failures propagate an error across agents; ghost delegation fires no error at all, the handoff disappears so nothing triggers recovery.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Agent on Sequential Workloads&lt;/b&gt; — Sequential degradation loses accuracy splitting a sequential task; ghost delegation loses the subtask entirely when a handoff is dropped.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Composable Termination Conditions&lt;/b&gt; — An explicit timeout and completion contract on each delegated subtask is part of the corrective; ghost delegation is what happens when a subtask can wait forever with no stop condition.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2211.5" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://shalomeir.substack.com/p/multi-agent-orchestration-problems&quot;&gt;Why Multi-Agent Orchestration Goes Wrong&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://azguards.com/technical/the-delegation-ping-pong-breaking-infinite-handoff-loops-in-crewai-hierarchical-topologies/&quot;&gt;The Delegation Ping-Pong: Breaking Infinite Handoff Loops in CrewAI Hierarchical Topologies&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.13657&quot;&gt;Why Do Multi-Agent LLM Systems Fail?&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2659.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
