                <mxPoint x="1250.75" y="1106.7" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When a dependency fails, downgrade the user-facing experience to a working subset rather than failing entirely.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1274.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A user-facing agent product combines several optional capabilities — a retrieval-augmented-generation backend that produces citations, a vision model that reads screenshots, a sandbox that runs user code, a payment integration. Each of these dependencies can have its own bad day independently of the others. The product is more than the sum of any single capability and can produce something useful even when one piece is missing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1274.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If the product treats every dependency as load-bearing and fails the whole request when any one of them is down, an isolated vendor outage becomes a complete product outage from the user&#39;s point of view. If it silently drops the failing capability and ships whatever it can produce without disclosure, the user gets a worse answer than expected without knowing why and loses trust the next time it happens. Without a defined per-feature fallback, neither outcome is acceptable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1380.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Degradation paths multiply test surface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User-visible degradation messaging is its own UX problem.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Some failures must hard-fail (PII path, payment).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1437.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: define per-feature downgrades and disclose them to the user when triggered, so that a dependency outage reduces the experience instead of killing it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1543.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define per-feature fallback behaviour. On dependency failure, downgrade (text-only when vision fails, no citations when retrieval fails, simple summary when code execution fails) and disclose to the user that degraded mode is active. Feature flags double as degradation switches.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1562.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Request --&amp;gt; Health check per dependency --healthy--&amp;gt; Full feature path --&amp;gt; Response | --dependency down--&amp;gt; Per-feature fallback (text-only | no citations | simple summary) --&amp;gt; Disclosure notice --&amp;gt; Response; hard-fail features --&amp;gt; explicit error&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1649.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A multimodal customer-support bot relies on a vision model to read screenshots, a vector store for citations, and a code sandbox for repro. During an outage of the vision provider, every screenshot upload returns a 503 and the whole conversation errors out. The team adds graceful degradation: when vision fails the bot falls back to asking the user to describe the screenshot in words and tells them so plainly; when retrieval is down it answers from the model&#39;s own knowledge with a visible &#39;no sources today&#39; badge. Outages now feel like reduced service rather than total failure.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1687.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Product resilience under partial outages.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User trust via transparent degradation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Test matrix grows with feature count.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Degraded modes can themselves have bugs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1793.15" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;On failure, the agent must produce a degraded response with disclosure rather than a generic error.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1869.15" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A dependency outage would otherwise fail the user request entirely.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-feature fallback behaviour can be defined (text when vision fails, no citations when retrieval fails).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The user can be told that degraded mode is active without breaking trust.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2032.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; There is no meaningful subset of working features to degrade to.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Silent degradation would mislead the user and explicit failure is more honest.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Feature flags do not exist and per-feature fallback cannot be wired without a major refactor.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1961.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Health check — per-dependency probe that decides whether the full path is available&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-feature fallback handlers — text-only, no-citations, simple-summary paths defined ahead of time&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Feature-flag store — runtime switch to force a feature into degraded mode without redeploy&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Disclosure layer — composes the user-visible notice that degraded mode is active&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hard-fail allowlist — features (payment, PII) that refuse to degrade and surface an explicit error&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2176.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Feature-flag platform — LaunchDarkly, Unleash, OpenFeature, or an in-house store&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Dependency health probes — synthetic checks against vision, retrieval, sandbox endpoints&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Observability stack — metrics and traces tagging each response with its degradation mode&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2086.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Undisclosed downgrade — the degraded path ships its answer without the notice, and the user takes a citation-free reply as the full result.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Untested fallback — a degraded mode that rarely runs has its own bug, and it fails on the day the dependency actually goes down.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Degrading what must hard-fail — a payment or PII feature drops into a reduced mode instead of returning a clear error.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale degradation switch — a feature flag forced into degraded mode during an incident is never reset, and users get the reduced path long after recovery.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2358.15" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Per-feature degraded-mode firing rate — how often each downgrade path is taken&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User-visible disclosure completeness — share of degraded responses that carried the notice&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Conversion or task-completion delta under degraded vs full mode — value preserved by the downgrade&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hard-fail rate on allowlisted features — degradation correctly refused for PII or payment paths&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Time-to-recovery — how quickly each feature flips back to full mode after the dependency heals&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2211.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.perplexity.ai/&quot;&gt;Perplexity (citations missing under retrieval issues)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://chat.openai.com/&quot;&gt;ChatGPT (vision unavailable falls back to text)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — When a dependency fails (provider down, MCP server unreachable, voice channel offline), the dispatcher downgrades to a working feature subset rather than refusing the whole tick.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2578.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Fallback Chain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Circuit Breaker&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Exception Handling and Recovery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Infrastructure Burst Bottleneck (Agent Scale-Out)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Silent External-Source Rot&lt;/b&gt; — Graceful degradation is the corrective stance: route a failed source-health check to a degraded-mode fallback instead of feeding the empty payload forward.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Fail-Plausible Narration&lt;/b&gt; — The remedy shape: on partial failure, degrade explicitly and disclose the gap instead of letting the model fabricate over it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Control-Loop-Mapped Agent Chain&lt;/b&gt; — A missing or invalid proposal degrades the loop to its base regulatory controller instead of stalling the sample, which is what makes a per-sample model call safe to depend on.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Feasibility-Negotiated Intent Contract&lt;/b&gt; — There degradation happens after a dependency has already failed and is disclosed to the user; here the degradation is proposed before actuation as a counter-offer the caller agrees to in advance.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2374.15" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://pragprog.com/titles/mnee2/release-it-second-edition/&quot;&gt;Release It! (Michael Nygard, ch. 4)&lt;/a&gt; — 2007&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2741.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
