        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Anc-&gt;Ans#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.19;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m17">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m7" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.19;" target="m9">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="734.6" y="846.3" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:MR-&gt;Ans#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.19;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m18">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m8" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.19;" target="m9">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1266.25" y="846.3" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Build an LLM-extracted entity-and-relation knowledge graph plus hierarchical community summaries, then answer global queries via map-reduce over those summaries.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1174.95" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is using a retrieval-augmented system over a large corpus and starts receiving questions about the corpus as a whole rather than individual facts in it: &#39;what are the main themes in these reports?&#39;, &#39;how does this position evolve across the documents?&#39;, &#39;which entities are central to the discussion?&#39; These are corpus-level sensemaking queries, not local lookup queries, and they arrive alongside the easier fact-style questions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1174.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Naive retrieval pulls the top-k chunks for each query, which is fine for local lookup but cannot answer questions about the whole corpus. The answer to &#39;what are the main themes?&#39; does not live in any single chunk; it requires seeing how chunks connect, what entities recur across them, and how communities of related content cluster. Without a representation that captures corpus-level structure — entities, relations, communities — chunk-level retrieval is mismatched to corpus-level questions, and the system returns confidently wrong, partial summaries that the user has no easy way to spot.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1280.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Indexing cost is high (LLM calls per entity, relation, community).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Graph quality depends on extraction prompts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Local-search vs global-search modes serve different query types and must be routed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1337.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: index documents into an LLM-extracted knowledge graph with hierarchical community summaries and route queries by scope, so that global questions get global answers and local questions stay local.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1462.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Index time: extract entities and relations from chunks; build a knowledge graph; cluster into hierarchical communities; summarise each community. Query time: classify query as local (entity-specific) or global (corpus-wide). Local queries use entity-anchored retrieval; global queries map-reduce over community summaries.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1462.95" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Index: Chunks --&amp;gt; Extract entities + relations --&amp;gt; Knowledge graph --&amp;gt; Cluster into hierarchical communities --&amp;gt; Summarise each community. Query: Query --&amp;gt; Local or global? --local--&amp;gt; Entity-anchored retrieval --&amp;gt; Answer | --global--&amp;gt; Map over community summaries --&amp;gt; Reduce --&amp;gt; Answer&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1587.95" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An analyst pointed at a 4000-page deal-room corpus asks &#39;what are the recurring risk themes across these contracts?&#39; Naive RAG returns five chunks and an answer that misses two themes entirely because no single chunk carries them. The team switches to GraphRAG: at index time the LLM extracts parties, obligations, and clauses into a knowledge graph, clusters the graph into communities, and writes a summary of each. The corpus-wide question now map-reduces over community summaries and surfaces the recurring themes the chunk-level retriever could not see.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1606.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Answers corpus-level sensemaking questions naive RAG cannot.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Communities are inspectable artefacts of the corpus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; High indexing cost (orders of magnitude more LLM calls).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Entity extraction errors cascade through the graph.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1731.95" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Global queries operate only on community summaries, not raw chunks; local queries operate only on entity-anchored neighbourhoods.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1788.95" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Users ask global, corpus-wide questions that local chunk retrieval cannot answer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The corpus has clear entities and relations worth extracting into a graph.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Index-time cost can be paid up front to enable hierarchical community summaries.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1970.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Queries are narrowly local and naive RAG already serves them well.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The corpus is small or volatile enough that graph extraction will not pay off.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Entity and relation extraction quality is too low to trust the resulting graph.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1894.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Entity-and-relation extractor — LLM-driven pass over chunks that builds the typed graph&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Community detector — clusters the knowledge graph into hierarchical communities&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Community summariser — emits a natural-language summary per community&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Query router — classifies a query as local or global and dispatches accordingly&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Map-reduce answerer — for global queries, maps the question over community summaries and reduces to a single answer&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2095.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — heavy index-time use for extraction and community summarisation, plus inference-time generation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Knowledge graph store — persists entities, relations, and community hierarchy (Neo4j, in-memory, or columnar)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Graph clustering library — Leiden or similar for hierarchical community detection&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2019.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Extraction error cascade — the extractor splits one entity into two or links unrelated ones, and every community and summary built on top inherits the error.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Local-global misroute — an entity-specific question is classified global, and the answer comes back as a vague theme summary instead of the specific fact.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale summaries — the corpus changes, the costly index is not rebuilt, and global answers describe themes that no longer hold.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lossy map-reduce — community summaries drop a minor but important thread, and the reduced answer reads complete while missing it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2277.95" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Win rate on global sensemaking benchmarks — head-to-head against naive RAG on corpus-wide questions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Entity-extraction F1 — quality of the graph the rest of the pipeline rests on&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Local-vs-global router accuracy — share of queries dispatched to the right mode&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Index-time LLM cost per million corpus tokens — the high capex this pattern incurs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Community-summary groundedness — fraction of summary claims traceable to the chunks they cover&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2182.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/microsoft/graphrag&quot;&gt;Microsoft GraphRAG (open source)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2497.95" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Naive RAG&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;MapReduce for Agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Knowledge Graph Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;HippoRAG&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hierarchical Retrieval&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;World-Model Graph Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Vectorless Reasoning-Based Retrieval&lt;/b&gt; — Both impose explicit structure at index time; vectorless retrieval reuses the document&#39;s own table-of-contents tree instead of an extracted entity graph.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Repo Map&lt;/b&gt; — GraphRAG builds an entity-relation graph over prose; a repo map builds a symbol-dependency graph over code.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tacit-Knowledge Elicitation Agent&lt;/b&gt; — GraphRAG indexes documented knowledge into an entity-relation graph; elicitation front-loads the undocumented criteria so there is expert knowledge for that graph to capture in the first place.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2364.95" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16130&quot;&gt;From Local to Global: A Graph RAG Approach to Query-Focused Summarization&lt;/a&gt; — Edge, Trinh, Cheng, Bradley, Chao, Mody, Truitt, Metropolitansky, Ness, Larson, 2024&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2589.95" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
