          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Lift archived memory items back into short-term tiers when something re-attends to them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1643.05" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running agent has archived a piece of information into cold storage — a previous insight, a prior thought, an observation from days ago. Retrieving items from cold storage is slow and out-of-band; it happens only when the agent explicitly searches for them. Today, the current context has drifted close to a topic where that archived item is relevant again, but the agent has no reason to go looking and so it never realises the item is there.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1643.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Archived items might as well not exist if the agent never thinks about them again, even when the current context makes them relevant. The bottleneck is not the storage itself — the item is on disk and addressable — but the absence of any mechanism that periodically pulls archived items back into the agent&#39;s active attention, the way the hippocampus rehearses memories during sleep. Without rehearsal, the agent has perfect recall in principle and amnesia in practice.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1735.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Re-attention triggers must be cheap to evaluate.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lifting too aggressively floods the working tier.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The lifted item is now a duplicate of the archive copy.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1806.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: when salience matches an archived item, copy it back into short-term memory for a few cycles while leaving the archive intact, so that re-attention re-grounds without losing the original record.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1898.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When salience scoring matches against archived items (embedding similarity, keyword match, explicit reference), the matched item is reactivated into short-term memory for one or more cycles. The original archive copy stays untouched.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1931.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;New input / cue --&amp;gt; Salience scoring --embedding / keyword / reference match--&amp;gt; Archive item --reactivate--&amp;gt; Short-term memory (one or more cycles); archive copy stays untouched; no match --&amp;gt; no-op&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2023.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent archives anything older than seven days into cold storage. When the user mentions &#39;the dentist thing&#39; six weeks later, the agent has no idea what they mean. The team adds hippocampal-rehearsal: the salience scorer also runs against archived items, and when the embedding similarity for &#39;dentist&#39; clears the threshold, the original archived note (&#39;molar crown, scheduled Nov 14&#39;) is reactivated into short-term memory for the next several cycles. The agent picks up the thread without the user explaining anything.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2056.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Long-tail relevance does not require the agent to remember to remember.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mimics the rehearsal step of biological memory consolidation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; False rehearsals waste working-memory slots.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Operationally complex; requires content-addressable storage.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2148.05" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Archived items become readable only after rehearsal lifts them; direct cold reads are not part of the agent&#39;s primary path.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2238.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Archived memory items become relevant again and must re-enter short-term context.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A salience scorer can match current context against the archive reliably.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reactivation can be bounded so short-term memory does not flood.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2387.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Memory is small enough that nothing needs to be archived in the first place.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Salience scoring is unreliable and would surface noise rather than relevance.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term context cannot afford the additional reactivated tokens.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2344.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Re-attention trigger — cheap salience check on every cue that decides whether to query the archive at all&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive matcher — runs embedding similarity or keyword match against cold storage to find candidate items&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reactivator — copies the matched item into short-term memory for a bounded number of cycles&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cycle-budget controller — caps how many items can be lifted at once so the working tier does not flood&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cold archive — content-addressable store where the original copy stays untouched after rehearsal&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2512.05" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Content-addressable cold store — S3/GCS or a file-backed archive with stable IDs the rehearser can resolve&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vector index over archived items — Chroma/FAISS that lets cheap similarity match drive the rehearsal trigger&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Embedding model — used to score current context against archived items&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2469.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; False reactivation — a loose keyword match lifts an unrelated archived item, and it takes a short-term slot from something useful.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rehearsal storm — one broad cue matches many archived items at once and floods short-term memory.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Never-cued item — an important archived fact shares no words or embedding neighbours with current input, so it is never lifted.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Archive mutation — the reactivation step edits or moves the archive copy, so the original is lost.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2732.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Rehearsal precision — fraction of reactivated items the agent actually used in the next few cycles&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; False-rehearsal rate — how often reactivation displaced more relevant working-set content&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cue-to-lift latency — milliseconds from new input arriving to the matched item being available in short-term&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Long-tail recall lift — answer-quality delta on questions about content older than the short-term horizon&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Working-tier flood incidents — counts of cycles where the rehearsal cap was breached&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2632.05" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2914.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Five-Tier Memory Cascade&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2833.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5847173/&quot;&gt;The Role of Hippocampal Replay in Memory and Planning&lt;/a&gt; — Ólafsdóttir, Bush, Barry, 2018&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4648295/&quot;&gt;Hippocampal sharp wave-ripple: A cognitive biomarker for episodic memory and planning&lt;/a&gt; — György Buzsáki, 2015&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16474382/&quot;&gt;Reverse replay of behavioural sequences in hippocampal place cells during the awake state&lt;/a&gt; — David J. Foster, Matthew A. Wilson, 2006&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3020.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
