        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:abandoned-&gt;root_end#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.43;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m16">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.43;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1083.35" y="568.85" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Hypothesis lifecycle: commit at active, transition once a next-test fires or another hypothesis subsumes.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="649.25" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Persist the agent&#39;s candidate provisional answers as a typed ledger of records carrying summary, confidence, status, and next-test, so guesses survive sessions and stay distinguishable from open questions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="724.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running agent maintains an open-question ledger (unresolved pulls of curiosity) and observes patterns of evidence that point toward provisional answers. As the agent commits enough weight to a guess to act on it, that guess stops being a question and becomes a hypothesis — something it would defend until disconfirmed. Without a place to put hypotheses they live only in the current prompt window and dissolve at the end of the turn.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="724.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent that holds candidate answers only implicitly is forced to re-derive them each time the topic resurfaces, with no continuity of confidence: a guess held with strength one session evaporates by the next, and a guess that was once disconfirmed quietly re-emerges as if it were new. Storing hypotheses under the same surface as open questions is no better — the ledger conflates &#39;still wondering&#39; with &#39;tentatively believes&#39;, and the agent loses the move that actually matters for inquiry: comparing yesterday&#39;s provisional answer against today&#39;s new evidence.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="849.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Hypotheses are different from questions: questions pull, hypotheses commit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence must be a graded scalar, not a binary, because the agent revises rather than flipping.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each hypothesis needs a falsifiable next-test or it rots into untestable belief.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hypothesis state must survive across sessions, because evidence accumulates over weeks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Status transitions (active → confirmed | disconfirmed | superseded | abandoned) must be cheap and visible.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="887.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: store each candidate provisional answer as its own typed record with summary, confidence, status, a next-test field, and a small evidence list, separate from the open-question store, so the agent can carry provisional answers across sessions and revise them against incoming evidence rather than re-derive them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1031.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Maintain a hypothesis store keyed by short id. Each record has: a one-line summary; a numeric confidence (0..1); a status drawn from {active, confirmed, disconfirmed, superseded, abandoned}; a next-test sentence stating what observation would move the confidence; and an evidence list of short notes with sources. When the agent commits a guess, write a new record at active. When evidence arrives, append it and adjust confidence; if the next-test fires, transition to confirmed or disconfirmed; if a better hypothesis subsumes it, transition to superseded. Render the active records into the agent&#39;s daily working context so it sees what it currently believes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1069.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent commits guess --&amp;gt; Hypothesis record (id, summary, confidence, status=active, next-test, evidence) --evidence arrives--&amp;gt; append and adjust confidence --&amp;gt; {next-test positive -&amp;gt; confirmed | negative -&amp;gt; disconfirmed | subsumed -&amp;gt; superseded | untested sweep -&amp;gt; abandoned}; active records --&amp;gt; daily working context&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1175.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent maintains a small store of open questions (&quot;why does request latency spike between 02:00 and 04:00 UTC?&quot;). After a week of incidents, the agent commits to a guess: &quot;the spike is correlated with a vendor&#39;s scheduled embedding-index rebuild.&quot; It opens a hypothesis with confidence 0.6, status active, next-test &quot;observe whether the next spike correlates with the vendor&#39;s announced rebuild window.&quot; Two weeks later the test fires positive; the hypothesis transitions to confirmed and the question is closed. A separate guess about GC pauses, which had reached confidence 0.4, transitions to superseded.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1270.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provisional answers survive across sessions with a continuity of confidence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Disconfirmed hypotheses leave a paper trail rather than being silently re-spawned.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Next-test fields keep hypotheses falsifiable rather than free-floating belief.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Two-store discipline (questions vs hypotheses) is harder than one undifferentiated note pile.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence numbers are seductive; the temperature is the agent&#39;s, not the world&#39;s.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hypothesis stores grow if abandonment is not periodically swept.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1338.25" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent cannot store provisional answers in the same surface as open questions; conflating the two ledgers is forbidden because the moves they support — pulling for inquiry vs revising belief — are different.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1471.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent runs over weeks and accumulates partial evidence about persistent questions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provisional answers need to be defensible and revisable, not just remembered.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An existing open-question store already separates pulls of curiosity from commitments.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1615.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is short-lived and never re-encounters the same question.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The product has no surface for the agent to render its own belief state.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence numbers will be read as authoritative by downstream consumers without context.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1596.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Hypothesis Ledger — typed records with summary, confidence, status, next-test, evidence&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evidence Appender — adds short notes with sources and adjusts confidence&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Next-Test Field — falsifiable observation that drives a status transition&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Status Machine — active to confirmed, disconfirmed, superseded, or abandoned&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Open-Question Store — separate surface that pulls of curiosity live in, not commitments&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1740.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Structured JSON store — keyed by short id with confidence and status fields&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — drafts new hypotheses, evidence summaries, and next-test sentences&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1721.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Merged ledgers — hypotheses are written into the open-questions store, and the agent cannot tell what it is wondering about from what it already believes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; False precision — a confidence of 0.8 is read as a measured probability instead of the agent&#39;s own temperature on a guess.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Zombie hypotheses — active records are never swept, so untested guesses pile up and crowd the daily working context.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Revived disconfirmed guess — a later session ignores the disconfirmed status and commits the same hypothesis again as if it were new.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1903.25" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Hypothesis-revision rate — confidence shifts per active record over a window&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confirm/disconfirm ratio — closures by next-test outcome rather than by abandonment&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Untested-active count — active records past their natural sweep window, flagging belief rot&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence calibration — predicted vs observed outcomes on confirmed and disconfirmed records&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1827.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2123.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Open-Question Tension Store&lt;/b&gt; — Questions pull; hypotheses commit. Same agent typically runs both.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Confidence Reporting&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Chain of Verification&lt;/b&gt; — Next-test fields parallel CoVe&#39;s question-then-verify shape, applied to the agent&#39;s own guesses.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Archaeology&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;BDI Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1971.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.routledge.com/The-Logic-of-Scientific-Discovery/Popper/p/book/9780415278447&quot;&gt;Logik der Forschung (The Logic of Scientific Discovery)&lt;/a&gt; — Karl Popper, 1934&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.05660&quot;&gt;Hypothesis Search: Inductive Reasoning with Language Models&lt;/a&gt; — Wang et al., 2024&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2229.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="incident-response-runbook" name="Incident Response Runbook">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2635.3500000000004" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2635.3500000000004" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Incident Response Runbook&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Governance &amp;amp; Observability &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; mature &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: IR Runbook, Agent Failure Playbook, Agent Incident Procedure&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="1377.35" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Alert: kill-switch / sandbox-escape / cost spike" mermaidId="n:Alert" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Alert: kill-switch / sandbox-escape / cost spike" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="620.0" x="65.0" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Severity" mermaidId="n:Sev" mermaidBaseStyle="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Severity" id="m1">
