        <UserObject label="explicit switch" mermaidId="e:Interrupted-&gt;Switched#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.73;exitY=1;entryX=0.51;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="explicit switch" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.73;exitY=1;entryX=0.51;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="460.25" y="568.85" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Switched-&gt;root_end#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.51;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.07;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.51;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.07;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="460.25" y="737.8" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Preserve multi-step reasoning across interrupts by supporting paused-and-resumed thought frames so a new message handles cleanly without clobbering in-flight work.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="897.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running an agent whose individual reasoning chains take longer than a single turn — a six-step synthesis, a multi-stage debugging walkthrough, a careful comparison across documents. While the chain is mid-flight, new external messages can arrive: a user follow-up, a system notification, a scheduled note from earlier. The agent has no built-in concept of a paused thought, so every incoming message lands on whatever the model was about to say next.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="897.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Without explicit continuation support, the agent has only two bad options when an interrupt arrives mid-chain. It can ignore the new message and look rude, finishing the previous thought as if nothing happened. Or it can answer the interrupt and quietly lose the in-flight reasoning, restarting from scratch later if at all. There is no notion of &#39;hold this thread, handle that one, then come back to where I was,&#39; so any reasoning that takes longer than one turn fragments into shards every time the user speaks.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1003.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Latency: humans expect quick acknowledgement of new input.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Context capacity: holding a paused thought costs tokens.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resume reliability: returning to a paused thought without distortion is hard.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Priority: not every interrupt deserves to suspend work; some are themselves interruptable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1060.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: push a named thought-frame onto a bounded stack at the start of a multi-step chain and require any interrupt to acknowledge, handle, and pop-then-resume the top frame, so that incoming messages neither clobber in-flight reasoning nor disappear into it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1185.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Introduce an explicit thought-frame: when starting a multi-step chain, push a frame onto a stack with the goal, the steps completed, and the next step. On interrupt: acknowledge briefly (&#39;hold on — finishing X first&#39; or &#39;switching: Y&#39;), handle the interrupt, then look at the top frame and explicitly resume (&#39;back to X — I was at step 3 / 6&#39;). Cap stack depth to prevent infinite suspension. Frames older than a configurable window expire (the agent admits the resume would be reconstruction, not continuation).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1204.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Start multi-step chain --push frame (goal, steps done, next step)--&amp;gt; Working --new message--&amp;gt; brief acknowledgement --&amp;gt; handle interrupt --&amp;gt; read top frame --&amp;gt; announce and resume at step k | frame too old -&amp;gt; admit reconstruction or abandon explicitly&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1310.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research agent is on step 4 of a 7-step literature synthesis when the user fires off &#39;oh, also, what was that paper from Tuesday?&#39;. The current agent either ignores the interrupt and looks rude, or starts answering it and loses the synthesis state. The team adds interrupt-resumable-thought: the synthesis pushes a thought-frame onto a stack, the agent acknowledges the interrupt with &#39;one sec — finishing the synthesis section, then I&#39;ll grab Tuesday&#39;s paper&#39;, completes the step, then pops the frame and resumes. Long thinking survives mid-flight questions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1386.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Coherent long-form work survives interruptions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Human gets quick acknowledgement without losing depth.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Failure mode (forgetting to resume) is observable as a stack with un-popped frames.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stack management adds complexity to the agent loop.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token cost of holding paused frames in context.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resume distortion over long pauses is a real failure.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1454.5" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Interrupts cannot silently discard in-flight multi-step reasoning; all paused chains must be visibly tracked, named in the next reply, and either resumed or explicitly abandoned.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1568.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent supports incoming interrupts (new user messages) while it is mid-reasoning.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-step reasoning chains are common enough that losing one is a meaningful regression.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The transport allows the agent to expose paused chains to subsequent turns.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1731.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is strictly request-response with no interruptible loops.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning chains are short enough that restarting them is cheaper than paging them out.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The user expects every new message to fully reset the agent&#39;s working state.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1674.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Thought Frame — named record with goal, steps completed, and next step&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frame Stack — bounded LIFO stack of paused chains&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Interrupt Handler — acknowledges, handles, then pops and resumes the top frame&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frame Expiry — clock-bounded window after which resume becomes reconstruction&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resume Announcer — visibly names the frame being resumed in the reply&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1856.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Structured JSON store — durable frame stack across process restarts&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — generation that emits the acknowledge, handle, and resume turns&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1799.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Resume distortion — the agent comes back to a frame after a long pause and continues from a step whose premises no longer hold.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stack pile-up — repeated interrupts push frames faster than they resolve, and the depth cap starts dropping work without telling the user.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Silent drop — the agent handles the interrupt and never names the paused chain, so the frame expires unseen.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong frame resumed — with several frames paused, the agent resumes the top one when the user meant an older thread.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2019.5" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Resume-completion rate — share of pushed frames that are popped and finished, not abandoned&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Un-popped frame count — leaked frames sitting on the stack past their expiry window&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resume distortion — semantic drift between the paused frame&#39;s next step and the actual resume&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Acknowledge latency — wall-clock from interrupt arrival to brief acknowledgement&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1905.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Self-observed in long-running cognitive agents&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — In-flight plans are preserved across user interrupts (chat arrives mid-tick) so the agent can resume the prior thread on a later tick rather than losing the train of thought.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2239.5" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Resumption&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Conversation Handoff to Human&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Decision Log&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Append-Only Thought Stream&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Short-Term Thread Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Interruptible Agent Execution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2049.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://langchain-ai.github.io/langgraph/concepts/human_in_the_loop/&quot;&gt;LangGraph — interrupts and human-in-the-loop&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2383.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="interruptible-agent-execution" name="Interruptible Agent Execution">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2537.25" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2537.25" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Interruptible Agent Execution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Safety &amp;amp; Control &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Pause/Resume/Cancel Control Surface, User-Interruptible Agent&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="847.25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="n:root_start" mermaidBaseStyle="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="21.7" width="21.7" x="227.75" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
