        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="persisted note" mermaidId="n:note0" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#fff5ad,#2a2a2a);strokeColor=light-dark(#aaaa33,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="persisted note" id="m9">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#fff5ad,#2a2a2a);strokeColor=light-dark(#aaaa33,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="57.35" width="300.7" x="650.9" y="342.55" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Let an agent drop a note for its own future self at a specified time so present decisions can hand off context to a later run without external infrastructure.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="908.35" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running an agent that ticks continuously across many sessions and frequently has the thought &#39;I should come back to this tomorrow&#39; or &#39;check whether X resolved by Friday afternoon.&#39; The present-self has context the future-self will need, but the natural prompt window only carries a handful of recent turns, so by tomorrow that intention has fallen out of context entirely.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="908.35" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Without some way to drop a note for its own future self, the agent has only two unsatisfying options. It can act on the thought right now — pinging the user at 9am about something that should have waited until 4pm — or it can hope to remember on its own, which it will not. External scheduling systems like cron or a queue can fire on time but live outside the agent&#39;s working memory, so when they do fire the agent has no idea why the reminder is showing up or what its past-self intended.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1014.35" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent needs to commit to future action without acting now.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External cron is brittle, opaque, and lives outside the agent&#39;s prompt.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Forgetting is a real failure mode in multi-turn / multi-day work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The future-self should treat the past-note as a SYSTEM message, not as an unprompted user input.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1052.35" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: give the agent a tool to drop a note for its own future self into a persistent queue that drains as SYSTEM messages at fire time, so that present thoughts can commit to future action without spamming now or being forgotten by then.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1177.35" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Provide a tool &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;schedule_future_thought(when, content, intent)&lt;/font&gt; that appends to a persistent scheduled-thoughts queue. At each tick or turn, drain due entries and prepend them into the next prompt as &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;[SYSTEM: scheduled note from past-self (set &amp;lt;ts&amp;gt;, fires &amp;lt;when&amp;gt;): &amp;lt;content&amp;gt;]&lt;/font&gt;. Mark fired so they only run once. Accept ISO timestamps and relative offsets (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;+1h&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;+2d&lt;/font&gt;).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1196.35" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent (now) --schedule_future_thought(when, content, intent)--&amp;gt; Scheduled-thoughts queue (persisted) --&amp;gt; each tick: drain due entries --&amp;gt; prepend &amp;#x27;[SYSTEM: scheduled note from past-self]&amp;#x27; to prompt --&amp;gt; mark fired --&amp;gt; Agent (later)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1302.35" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent decides at 09:00 that it should remind the user about a tax deadline at 16:00, but the only options it has are tell them now (annoying) or hope it remembers (it won&#39;t). The team adds intra-agent-memo-scheduling: the agent calls schedule_future_thought(when=&#39;16:00&#39;, content=&#39;nudge user re Form 1040 deadline&#39;, intent=&#39;time-sensitive reminder&#39;), which appends to a persistent scheduled-thoughts queue. At 16:00 the next tick prepends &#39;[SYSTEM: scheduled note from past-self ...]&#39; into the prompt and the agent acts. No external cron required.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1340.35" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent can defer action without forgetting.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Past-self can leave context for future-self across long gaps.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provides &#39;check back on this&#39; semantics native to the agent.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Without expiry or dismissal, scheduled notes accumulate and waste prompt tokens; obsolete future-self commitments can pollute attention long after they&#39;ve stopped being relevant.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Drift between schedule time and actual tick time depending on tick cadence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Risk of accumulating stale promises that pollute the agent&#39;s sense of obligation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1446.35" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Future thoughts must surface at or after their fire time; failures to drain are observable bugs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1522.35" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent runs across many ticks or sessions and present-self has context the future-self will need.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External schedulers (cron, queues, durable workflows) are unavailable or overkill.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Future-fire memos are a small enough volume to keep in the agent&#39;s own store.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1742.35" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A real workflow engine (LangGraph durable execution, Temporal) is already integrated and reliable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memos must survive the agent process being deleted; intra-agent storage is too fragile.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memo volume is high enough that an external scheduler is required for performance.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1614.35" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Schedule Tool — appends a future-fire entry to the queue with when, content, intent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scheduled-Thoughts Queue — persistent store keyed or sorted by fire time&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Drain Step — runs each tick, pops due entries, marks them fired&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; System-Prefix Injector — prepends matured notes as SYSTEM lines into the next prompt&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fire-Once Marker — prevents the same memo from re-firing on subsequent ticks&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1886.35" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Structured JSON store — persistent queue surviving process restarts&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tick scheduler — drains due entries at the agent&#39;s loop cadence&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1739.35" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stale promises — notes outlive their purpose, keep firing or piling up, and the agent acts on commitments that no longer matter.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Late delivery — a slow tick cadence means a note set for 9:00 surfaces long after, and the moment it was meant for has passed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Double fire — the mark-fired write fails after the note is prepended, so the same note surfaces again on the next tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Undrained queue — a bug in the drain step leaves due notes in the queue, and the agent never sees them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2049.35" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Fire-time drift — gap between scheduled fire time and actual injection time&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale-memo backlog — unfired entries past a reasonable age, surfacing forgotten cron entries&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Double-fire count — memos that fired more than once, which must stay zero&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memo-to-action conversion — share of fired memos that produced a downstream move rather than being ignored&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1845.35" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/tintinweb/pi-schedule-prompt&quot;&gt;pi-schedule-prompt (Pi Heartbeat)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Schedules a prompt to be re-sent to the agent after a relative delay (+5m/+1h/+2d) or at an ISO time, optionally waking the parent agent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2269.35" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Scheduled Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Append-Only Thought Stream&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Decision Log&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Salience-Triggered Output&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2008.35" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/durable-execution&quot;&gt;LangGraph — durable execution and scheduled tasks&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442&quot;&gt;Generative Agents: Interactive Simulacra of Human Behavior&lt;/a&gt; — Park et al., 2023&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2432.35" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
