          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Lift the agent loop into a search tree with a learned value function and backtracking.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1119.15" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team gives an agent a problem where several reasoning paths are plausible at the start — a coding bug with multiple possible root causes, a puzzle with several candidate frames, an investigation that could go in three directions. The first plausible path is often not the best one, and committing to it produces confidently wrong answers when it dead-ends. The team has at least some signal (test suite, verifier, heuristic scorer) that can rate a partial trajectory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1119.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Single-chain agent loops like ReAct (the reason-act-observe loop) and Plan-and-Execute commit to one chain of thought from the first step. When that chain enters a wrong frame they cannot backtrack cheaply; they either thrash inside the wrong frame or restart from scratch. Self-consistency (sample many answers and vote) helps for one-shot tasks but does not help an agent that needs to interleave tool calls with reasoning. The team needs a way to explore alternative trajectories while still spending most of the compute on the branches that are paying off.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1211.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Search is expensive; the value function must be cheap.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Branch ranking determines whether search beats greedy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memory of failed branches must not leak into successful ones.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1282.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: lift the agent loop into an MCTS-style tree of partial trajectories scored by a value function, so that the agent can backtrack from failing branches instead of committing to the first plausible chain.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1393.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Apply Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS) to the agent loop. Each node is a partial trajectory. Expansion samples next thoughts/actions. Backpropagation updates a value estimate. Selection chooses the next node by UCT. The agent can backtrack from a failing branch instead of committing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1407.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Root partial trajectory --&amp;gt; UCT selection --&amp;gt; Expansion (sample next thoughts/actions from LLM) --&amp;gt; Simulate --&amp;gt; Value estimate --&amp;gt; Backpropagate to ancestors --&amp;gt; UCT selection (failing branch: backtrack to another node)&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1518.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A coding agent given an ambiguous bug report tries the first plausible fix, finds it wrong on the test suite, then thrashes because its single chain-of-thought has already committed to that frame. The team rebuilds the loop as LATS: each partial trajectory is a node, expansion samples alternative next actions, the test suite acts as the value signal, and UCT selects the next node to explore. When a branch fails its tests the agent backtracks instead of digging in. Hard bugs that previously needed a human now resolve autonomously.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1532.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Higher answer quality on hard / ambiguous tasks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Explicit exploration / exploitation trade-off.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token cost can be 5-10x ReAct.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The value function is hard to train without supervision signals.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1662.15" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Each node may be expanded only by sampling actions consistent with the parent state.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1714.15" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Single-chain agent loops commit too early on ambiguous problems.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A learned or heuristic value function can score partial trajectories.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Backtracking from failing branches is worth the search overhead.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1901.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; ReAct or Plan-and-Execute already solves the task without search.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No useful value function or step-level signal exists.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency and token cost cannot absorb tree expansion and rollouts.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1806.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Trajectory tree — nodes are partial agent traces (thought/action/observation prefixes)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; UCT selector — picks the next node to expand by upper-confidence bound&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Expansion policy — samples next thoughts and actions from the LLM&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Value function — scores partial trajectories, learned or heuristic&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Backpropagator — updates ancestor value estimates after a rollout&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2026.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — used both as expansion policy and (optionally) as self-evaluator&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool catalogue — actions the agent can take inside a rollout&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Test harness or external verifier — provides reward signal when available&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tree state store — persists nodes, visit counts, and value estimates&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1931.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Token overrun — the tree search runs many rollouts, and one task costs several times a plain ReAct run without a matching gain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misleading value estimate — an untrained or heuristic value function scores a wrong partial trajectory high, and selection keeps expanding it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inconsistent expansion — an expansion samples an action that does not follow from the parent state, and the branch describes steps that never happened.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Shallow backtracking — the search backs out of a failing branch only after spending most of the budget inside it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2189.15" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Pass rate vs single-chain ReAct — quality lift from search&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token cost multiple over ReAct — overhead the tree expansion pays&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Backtrack rate — fraction of runs that abandon a failing branch versus committing&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Value-function calibration — correlation between predicted value and final reward&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Branch-memory bleed — incidents of failed-branch context leaking into successful ones&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2075.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/lapisrocks/LanguageAgentTreeSearch&quot;&gt;LanguageAgentTreeSearch (reference implementation)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Original code release by the LATS paper authors (Zhou et al.).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph&quot;&gt;LangGraph LATS example&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — LangGraph ships an LATS notebook in its examples.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2409.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;ReAct&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Consistency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tree of Thoughts&lt;/b&gt; — LATS adds learned value function and MCTS-style search.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Exploration vs Exploitation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Test-Time Compute Scaling&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Graph of Thoughts&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Process Reward Model&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Automatic Workflow Search&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Adaptive Branching Tree Search&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;World Model as Tool&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Path Plan Generator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Forkable Agent Sandbox&lt;/b&gt; — Tree search with backtracking assumes the environment can be reset at each node; snapshot-and-fork is what makes that reset cheap enough to search deeply.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2238.15" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.04406&quot;&gt;Language Agent Tree Search Unifies Reasoning, Acting, and Planning in Language Models&lt;/a&gt; — Zhou, Yan, Shlapentokh-Rothman, Wang, Wang, 2023&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2553.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
