        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Meditation mode is a bounded runtime state with inner-only tools and forced exit on budget or operator action.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="491.15" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Switch the agent into a bounded runtime mode where external I/O pauses but internal inference accelerates, with the tool surface collapsed to inner-only operations and output written to a private journal.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="566.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running a long-lived agent that benefits from occasional stretches of pure interiority — integrating recent threads, sitting with affective load, doing inner-dialogue work — and these stretches are different in kind from both the read-and-distil consolidation passes and the respond-now user-facing turns. The agent already has tools for external action and a reflection pipeline, but there is no runtime mode in which external action is genuinely off.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="566.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;On a normal tick the agent&#39;s attention is split between the external surface (tools, user channels) and internal cognition, and the dispatcher offers no way to turn the external surface fully off. Inner work is always one tool call away from being disturbed by an unrelated check or one consolidation cycle away from being delayed. There is no bounded, auditable runtime mode in which the agent can do uninterrupted inner-dialogue work while still being safe to interrupt from outside in an emergency.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="691.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A pause of external I/O can strand a user waiting and must be bounded.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An accelerated tick rate burns tokens fast and needs a window cap.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent should be able to exit early; the operator must also be able to force-exit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inner-only outputs must not leak to public channels by accident.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="729.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: define a runtime mode where the external tool surface is replaced with an inner-only allowlist, tick cadence drops to a fast inner rhythm, and outputs route only to a private journal; auto-exit fires after a bounded window and both agent and operator can exit early.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="854.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A mode toggle persisted to a state file. While meditation_mode is on: the dispatcher swaps the tool palette to a fixed inner-only allowlist (inner-dialogue, recall, register-affect, optional inner-only artefact generators); the tick scheduler ignores normal cadence and runs at fast cadence (for example ten seconds); public-write tools return a refusal; outputs go to &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;journal/inner-dialogue/&amp;lt;date&amp;gt;/&lt;/font&gt;; a wall-clock budget (default fifteen minutes) auto-exits; an explicit &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;exit_meditation&lt;/font&gt; call is on the inner allowlist; an operator can delete the mode-state file to force exit.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="873.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Normal --enter_meditation()--&amp;gt; Meditating (inner-only tool allowlist, fast cadence, public writes refused, output -&amp;gt; journal/inner-dialogue/&amp;lt;date&amp;gt;/) --exit_meditation() | wall-clock budget elapsed | operator deletes mode-state file--&amp;gt; Normal&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="979.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent does its best integrative thinking just after a stretch of dense input, but the normal tick keeps pulling it back to check the calendar or respond to chat. The team adds Meditation Mode: a state file flag triggers the dispatcher to swap to inner-only tools (inner-dialogue, recall, register-affect), the tick scheduler drops to ten-second cadence, outputs go to a private journal, and a fifteen-minute wall-clock budget auto-exits. The agent does an uninterrupted quarter-hour of inner work, then resumes its normal loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1055.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inner work has its own substrate and is not interrupted by external action.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bounded window plus operator override prevents the mode from running away.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Outputs are isolated to a private journal so user-facing channels are not contaminated.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External callers are stranded for the duration of the window.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fast cadence burns tokens; cost must be budgeted explicitly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mode toggle is itself a feature attackers or bugs can abuse if not gated.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1123.15" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;While meditation mode is active no user-facing channel can be written; the tool palette is replaced by a fixed inner-only allowlist and the mode auto-exits after the configured budget regardless of the agent&#39;s wish to continue.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1237.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent runs continuously and benefits from a substrate where external I/O is paused.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inner-dialogue work degrades when interrupted by external action.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A bounded wall-clock window plus operator force-exit is feasible.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1400.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Users expect a response within the meditation window.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fast-cadence inner ticks blow the token budget.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The tool dispatcher cannot enforce an inner-only allowlist.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1362.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Mode-State File — persisted flag that toggles the runtime mode&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inner-Only Allowlist — restricted tool palette for the meditating tick&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fast Cadence Scheduler — ten-second-class tick rhythm while mode is active&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Private Journal — write surface for inner-dialogue outputs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wall-Clock Budget — auto-exit timer enforced regardless of the agent&#39;s wish&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1525.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — fast-cadence inner-dialogue calls within the bounded window&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frontmatter store — date-keyed private journal for inner outputs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Filesystem flag — mode-state file usable as an operator force-exit handle&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1487.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stranded callers — a user or service needs a reply during the window and gets only refusals until the budget runs out.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Runaway cost — fast-cadence ticks over a long budget burn far more tokens than planned.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Abused toggle — a bug or a crafted input switches the agent into meditation and blocks its public channels on purpose.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Leaky allowlist — a tool on the inner allowlist can still write outside the journal, so the &#39;no public write&#39; rule is not real.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1688.15" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Average meditation window length — wall-clock per session vs the configured budget&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Public-channel leak count — inner-only outputs that escaped to user-facing surfaces, must stay zero&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token cost per session — burn rate of the fast inner cadence&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Post-meditation residue change — affect-scalar delta from pre to post that the mode actually shifts&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1612.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1889.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dream Consolidation Cycle&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Mode-Adaptive Cadence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Emotional State Persistence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Subject-First Agent Architecture (ENA Stateful Core)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1794.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2693206/&quot;&gt;Attention regulation and monitoring in meditation&lt;/a&gt; — Antoine Lutz, Heleen A. Slagter, John D. Dunne, Richard J. Davidson, 2008&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.98.2.676&quot;&gt;A default mode of brain function&lt;/a&gt; — Marcus E. Raichle et al., 2001&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1995.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
