          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="no" mermaidId="e:val-&gt;discard#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.12;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="no" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.12;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="196.75" y="1305.1" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="yes" mermaidId="e:val-&gt;reg#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.89;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="yes" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.89;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="537.75" y="1305.1" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:reg-&gt;call#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.07;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.07;" target="m2">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="537.75" y="1480.25" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;When no tool fits, a creator role writes and validates a new tool, which the user role then calls.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1608.7" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When no available tool fits a subtask, have the agent write, validate, and register a new tool on the spot, separating the tool-creating role from the tool-using role.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1683.7" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent faces an open-ended task space, but its toolset is fixed at deployment. Sooner or later a subtask needs a capability no available tool provides — parse an unusual format, call an API with no wrapper, or run a computation the tools cannot express. The agent either gives up, fakes the result, or contorts existing tools into something brittle.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1683.7" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A fixed toolset cannot cover an open task space, yet shipping every conceivable tool is impossible and bloats tool selection. When the agent hits a capability gap mid-task it has no clean way forward: hallucinating a tool fails, and forcing the wrong tool produces wrong results. The agent needs a way to manufacture the missing capability as a proper, callable tool, and to do so without blindly trusting code it just wrote.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1789.7" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A fixed toolset cannot cover an open task space, but shipping every possible tool bloats discovery and selection.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Letting the agent author and run its own code adds an untrusted-code surface that needs validation and sandboxing.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A tool created for one subtask is wasted effort unless it is registered for reuse, yet over-eager tool creation clutters the registry.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1827.7" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: when no tool matches, have one role synthesize a new tool (code plus an interface spec), validate it against a test, and register it, so a separate tool-using role can call it like any other.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1952.7" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Split the work into a tool-creator and a tool-user. When the user role finds no tool fits the subtask, it hands the specification to the creator role, which writes the tool&#39;s code and interface, generates or runs a test to confirm it behaves, and registers it in the tool registry. The user role then calls the new tool exactly as it would a built-in one, and the tool persists for later reuse. Execution of synthesized code runs in a sandbox, and a tool that fails its validation check is discarded rather than registered.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2009.7" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;tool-user (no tool fits) -&amp;gt; tool-creator writes code + spec -&amp;gt; validate (test) -&amp;gt; pass: register; fail: discard -&amp;gt; tool-user calls registered tool&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2058.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent answering data questions is asked to compute a Gini coefficient, but it has only a generic SQL tool and a calculator. No tool fits, so the creator role writes a small gini(values) function, runs it against a known example to confirm the output, and registers it. The user role then calls gini on the query result, and the tool stays available for the next inequality question.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2191.7" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent closes capability gaps mid-task instead of failing or faking a result.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A small, fixed toolset can cover an open task space, since missing tools are made on demand.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Validated tools accumulate, so the same gap is not re-synthesized next time.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Generated, executable tools are an untrusted-code surface that must be sandboxed and reviewed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Validation is only as good as the test the agent writes for its own tool.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unchecked synthesis clutters the registry with near-duplicate or single-use tools.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2183.7" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A synthesized tool may not be called until it has passed a validation check; untested generated code is never registered or invoked, and its execution is confined to a sandbox.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2335.7" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The task space is open-ended and a fixed toolset will inevitably hit capability gaps.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent can run code in a sandbox and write a check that validates a new tool before use.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Synthesized tools are worth keeping because similar gaps recur.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2460.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A small, stable toolset already covers the domain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Running agent-authored code cannot be safely sandboxed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each gap is unique, so synthesized tools never get reused and only add risk.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2441.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tool-user — the role that selects and calls tools to make task progress&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool-creator — the role that writes a new tool&#39;s code and interface when no tool fits&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Validator — runs a test against the synthesized tool before it may be registered&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sandbox — confines execution of generated tool code&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool registry — stores validated tools so the user role and later runs can call them&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2585.7" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Code sandbox — executes synthesized and validated tool code in isolation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool registry and dispatcher — registers new tools and routes calls to them&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Test runner — checks a freshly synthesized tool against an expected result&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2566.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Self-validating blind spot — the agent writes a test that its own buggy tool passes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sandbox escape — synthesized code reaches resources it should not touch.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Registry sprawl — many one-off tools accumulate and degrade later tool selection.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2748.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Capability-gap resolution rate — fraction of no-tool-fits subtasks the agent closes by synthesis&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Synthesized-tool validation pass rate — how often generated tools survive their own check&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool reuse rate — how often a synthesized tool is called again rather than re-created&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sandbox-violation count — attempts by generated code to exceed its confinement&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2691.7" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17126&quot;&gt;LATM (LLMs as Tool Makers)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;pure-future&lt;/i&gt; — Decouples a tool-maker role from a tool-user role: the maker writes a reusable tool, the user calls it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14318&quot;&gt;CREATOR&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;pure-future&lt;/i&gt; — Transforms an abstract problem into a concrete Python tool, separating tool creation from decision making.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.22862&quot;&gt;Evolution of Tool Use in LLM Agents (survey)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Treats &#39;Autonomous Tool Expansion&#39; (LATM, CREATOR, ToolMaker, RestGPT) as a distinct branch of the tool-use literature.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.11705&quot;&gt;ToolMaker&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Agentic framework that autonomously transforms papers-with-code repositories into LLM-compatible tools, installing dependencies and using a closed-loop self-correction mechanism with unit tests before the tool is exposed for use.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.17428&quot;&gt;CRAFT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Creates a toolset of diverse, reusable, validated code-snippet tools and retrieves from it at inference, separating tool creation from tool use.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/MineDojo/Voyager&quot;&gt;Voyager&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Maintains an ever-growing skill library of executable code synthesized on demand as tools.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/KatherLab/ToolMaker&quot;&gt;ToolMaker (KatherLab/ToolMaker)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Shipping implementation that autonomously generates and self-corrects executable tool code from a task description and repo URL.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2873.7" width="755" height="377" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Skill Library&lt;/b&gt; — Skill Library accumulates critic-gated skills over runs for long-term reuse; On-Demand Tool Synthesis fabricates a tool just-in-time to close a capability gap in the current task, with an explicit creator/user role split.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Code-as-Action Agent&lt;/b&gt; — Code-as-Action runs code as the answer; here the code is packaged and registered as a reusable, callable tool.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Discovery&lt;/b&gt; — Discovery finds existing tools; synthesis creates one when discovery finds nothing that fits.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2835.7" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17126&quot;&gt;Large Language Models as Tool Makers&lt;/a&gt; — 2023&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14318&quot;&gt;CREATOR: Tool Creation for Disentangling Abstract and Concrete Reasoning of Large Language Models&lt;/a&gt; — 2023&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.22862&quot;&gt;The Evolution of Tool Use in LLM Agents&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.11705&quot;&gt;LLM Agents Making Agent Tools (ToolMaker)&lt;/a&gt; — Georg Wölflein, Dyke Ferber, Daniel Truhn, Ognjen Arandjelović, Jakob Nikolas Kather, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.17428&quot;&gt;CRAFT: Customizing LLMs by Creating and Retrieving from Specialized Toolsets&lt;/a&gt; — Lifan Yuan, Yangyi Chen, Xingyao Wang, Yi R. Fung, Hao Peng, Heng Ji, 2023&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3264.7" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="one-tool-one-agent" name="One Tool, One Agent">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2029.6352395672334" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2029.6352395672334" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;One Tool, One Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Multi-Agent &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Specialist-Per-Tool Design, Microservices-Style Agent Decomposition&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="377.64" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="User request" mermaidId="n:User" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="User request" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="61.34" width="171.54" x="696.62" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
