        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Tensions enter the ledger, rank by curiosity times intrusiveness, drive the next idle move, and close via a new append rather than edit.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="990.25" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Persist the agent&#39;s unresolved questions as a typed ledger so they drive its next inquiry instead of dissolving when the prompt ends.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1065.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running a long-lived agent that is meant to initiate inquiry on its own — to ask follow-up questions, look things up between turns, return to half-understood references — rather than only responding when prompted. In every conversation the agent notices things it does not fully understand: a name it has not heard before, an inconsistency in what the user just said, a thread the user dropped that seems worth picking back up later.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1065.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;By default these unresolved pulls vanish at the end of the turn that produced them. There is no surface to record what was noticed-but-not-followed-up, so the next idle moment starts as if from scratch and the agent&#39;s curiosity decays into amnesia between sessions. Even if the agent jots open questions into its general thought stream, nothing ranks them or surfaces the most worthwhile one when there is finally time to chase it, so they pile up undifferentiated and unactioned.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1171.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An inbox grows without bound if every passing thought becomes a tension.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A score is needed to rank which question to pull now — pure recency rewards trivia.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-write of tensions can be gamed: the agent invents tensions to look thoughtful.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tensions that never resolve still need to expire or the store becomes a graveyard.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1228.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: record each unresolved pull as a typed entry with curiosity, intrusiveness, and expiry, so that the next idle moment can choose between ask-now, store-for-later, and let-lapse rather than treating every open question alike.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1334.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Maintain an append-only ledger of tensions. Each entry carries id, opened-at, topic, source, curiosity (0..1), intrusiveness (0..1), and expiry. On each idle tick the agent reads the top entries by curiosity times intrusiveness as candidates for the next move. Intrusiveness gates ask-the-user-now versus store-quietly. Entries below a curiosity floor expire after a TTL. Resolution writes a closing event into the same ledger; the original entry is never edited.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1372.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Thought or observation --notices unresolved pull--&amp;gt; append tension (id, topic, source, curiosity, intrusiveness, expiry) --&amp;gt; Tension ledger (append-only) --top by curiosity x intrusiveness--&amp;gt; idle-tick candidate --&amp;gt; cognitive move --close event--&amp;gt; ledger; low curiosity past TTL or cap overflow --&amp;gt; expired&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1459.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent notices in passing that the user mentioned a half-read book by an author the agent has never encountered. Without somewhere to put that, the moment passes and the agent never returns to it. The team adds an Open-Question Tension Store: the agent appends a tension with topic &#39;who is this author&#39;, curiosity 0.6, intrusiveness 0.2, expiry seven days. Three idle ticks later the move-selector picks the tension, the agent does a targeted lookup, writes a small note, and closes the tension — instead of having forgotten the moment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1535.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Open questions survive across turns and across sessions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Curiosity and intrusiveness scores make the next move defensible instead of stochastic.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Expiry plus a cap stops the store from becoming a graveyard.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Score weights are opinionated and a bad calibration suppresses real curiosity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-write of tensions invites gaming unless the agent&#39;s training discourages it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ledger growth is real even with expiry; archive paths must be planned.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1603.25" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The tension store is append-only; tensions cannot be silently rewritten or back-dated, and the agent cannot exceed a configured cap on net-open tensions — overflow is auto-expired by lowest curiosity times intrusiveness.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1717.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent should initiate inquiry on idle ticks, not only respond.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unresolved questions otherwise vanish at turn end and never return.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is an idle-tick body that can read top-ranked tensions and act on one.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1880.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is request-response only and never has idle ticks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is no mechanism for the agent to act on its own initiative.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Persisting open-question state across sessions creates privacy or alignment risks.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1842.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tension Ledger — append-only entries with curiosity, intrusiveness, expiry&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ranking Function — curiosity times intrusiveness picks the next candidate&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Idle-Tick Reader — pulls top entries on quiet ticks to drive the next move&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Expiry Sweep — drops entries below a curiosity floor past their TTL&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Close-Event Writer — resolution writes a new append rather than editing the entry&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2005.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Structured JSON store — append-only ledger of tension entries&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — drafts tension entries and resolution notes&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1967.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Muted curiosity — weights are miscalibrated, so real open questions sit below the curiosity floor and expire unread.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Pushy intrusiveness — high intrusiveness scores send too many questions straight to the user instead of storing them quietly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Gamed tensions — the agent writes inflated tensions to pull its own idle ticks toward favourite topics.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ledger sprawl — expiry and the open cap still leave a growing tail, and no archive path was planned.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2168.25" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Net-open tension count — open vs closed tensions over time, against the configured cap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mean time to close — wall-clock from open to close per tension&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-write rate — tensions opened by the agent vs by observation events, surfacing gaming&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resolution-quality sample — auditor-rated share of closures that named an actual resolution&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2073.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot (author&amp;#x27;s long-running personal agent; single private deployment)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Unresolved questions (&#39;tensions&#39;) are kept as a typed ledger separate from thoughts and from hypotheses; they drive what the next idle tick attends to instead of dissolving when the prompt ends. Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2388.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Preoccupation Tracking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cognitive-Move Selector&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Append-Only Thought Stream&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Fragment Juxtaposition&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hypothesis Tracking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Socratic Questioning Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2217.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sup.org/books/title/?id=3850&quot;&gt;A Theory of Cognitive Dissonance&lt;/a&gt; — Leon Festinger, 1957&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://people.idsia.ch/~juergen/ieeecreative.pdf&quot;&gt;Formal Theory of Creativity, Fun, and Intrinsic Motivation&lt;/a&gt; — Jürgen Schmidhuber, 2010&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2532.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
