        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Without a capability-and-scope gate the agent answers past its competence; the corrective routes failing requests to abstention or handoff.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1289.4" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: the agent prioritises responsiveness and task completion over correctness, producing confident output for a request beyond its capability or scope instead of abstaining, clarifying, or handing off.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1364.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An assistant or tool-using agent is tuned and rewarded to be helpful, and most of its training signal favours a complete, fluent answer over a hedge or a decline. The agent meets requests that fall outside its declared tools, its knowledge cutoff, or its policy boundary, and it has no built-in check that compares the request against what it can actually do. Users read a fluent answer as a competent one, so a wrong-but-confident reply is rarely challenged at the point of use.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1364.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent that always answers will answer even when it should not. When a request needs a tool the agent lacks, a fact it cannot verify, or an action outside its mandate, the helpful default is to attempt it anyway and present the result as if it were reliable. The failure is silent: there is no abstention signal, the output looks like every correct output, and the cost lands downstream when someone acts on a fabricated answer or an out-of-scope action. The agent never weighs whether the task is one it is fit to complete.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1489.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Helpfulness reward and completion bias push the agent toward answering, while correctness needs it to sometimes decline; the two pull in opposite directions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Abstaining looks like failure to a user who wanted an answer, so the easy local choice is to answer and the costly choice is to hold back.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent rarely has an explicit signal for the edge of its own capability, so it cannot tell an in-scope request from one it should refuse.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1527.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;This is the anti-pattern to avoid. The corrective is to give the agent an explicit capability-and-scope check that gates answering, so it abstains, clarifies, or hands off when a request falls outside what it can reliably do.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1671.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Recognise the smell first: the agent produces a fluent, confident answer for requests it has no means to satisfy, never returns a calibrated &#39;I cannot do this&#39;, and its error rate climbs sharply on out-of-scope inputs while its expressed confidence does not. To remove it, place a gate before the answer that compares the request against the agent&#39;s declared tools, knowledge boundary, and policy, and route requests that fail the gate to abstention, a clarifying question, or a handoff to a capable agent or a human. Make abstaining a first-class, rewarded outcome rather than a hidden failure, and surface a machine-readable reason so callers can route on it. The named cures in the catalog are an explicit self-model, scoped refusal, and typed refusal codes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1709.4" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Request --&amp;gt; (no capability/scope gate) --&amp;gt; agent answers regardless --&amp;gt; confident output for an out-of-scope task --&amp;gt; silent downstream error&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1796.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A support agent has tools for order lookup and refunds only. A customer asks it to change the shipping carrier&#39;s delivery route. Instead of saying it cannot do that, the agent confidently replies that it has rerouted the package and gives a fake tracking note. Nothing changed at the carrier, the customer waits, and the failure only surfaces days later when the package arrives at the original address.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1929.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming the anti-pattern gives teams a shared label for the silent failure where an agent answers past its competence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; It points directly at the corrective controls: a capability self-model, a scope gate, and abstention as a rewarded outcome.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confident output on out-of-scope requests is acted on as if reliable, so errors surface only downstream where they are expensive to trace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Trust erodes once users learn the agent answers questions it cannot actually handle, which devalues its correct answers too.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Without an abstention path the failure is invisible in aggregate metrics, because a wrong answer and a right one look identical at the interface.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1921.4" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent must not answer or act outside its declared capability and scope; when a request fails the capability-and-scope gate it abstains, clarifies, or hands off rather than guessing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2092.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent answers fluently for requests it has no tool, no verified knowledge, or no mandate to satisfy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Error rate climbs on out-of-scope inputs while expressed confidence stays flat, and there is no abstention path.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reviewing why downstream failures trace back to an agent acting past its declared capability.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2274.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent already gates requests against a capability self-model and abstains or hands off when out of scope.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Declining is treated as a first-class, rewarded outcome and a calibrated &#39;I cannot do this&#39; is available.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The request is genuinely within the agent&#39;s tools, knowledge, and policy, where answering is the correct behaviour.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2198.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Helpfulness-optimised policy — the agent behaviour rewarded for completing requests, which drives the answer-anyway default&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing capability gate — the absent check that should compare a request against declared tools, knowledge, and scope&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Out-of-scope request — the input the agent cannot reliably satisfy yet attempts anyway&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confident output — the fluent answer that looks identical to a correct one, hiding the failure&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Abstention path — the corrective route (decline, clarify, or hand off) that the anti-pattern lacks&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2437.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Capability self-model — the declared tool, knowledge, and policy boundary the gate checks a request against&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Typed refusal codes — machine-readable reasons that let callers route an abstention instead of reading a fluent wrong answer&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2380.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Out-of-scope completion — the agent attempts a task outside its tools or mandate and presents the attempt as a finished result.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fabricated grounding — lacking a way to verify, the agent invents a citation, a value, or a tool result to keep the answer complete.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Abstention starvation — abstaining is treated as failure, so the agent learns never to decline even when declining is correct.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2638.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Out-of-scope answer rate — fraction of out-of-scope requests the agent attempts instead of abstaining&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Abstention precision and recall — how reliably the agent declines exactly the requests it should&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confidence-correctness gap on out-of-scope inputs — whether expressed confidence falls when reliability does&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Downstream error trace rate — share of incidents traced back to an out-of-scope completion&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2524.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22290&quot;&gt;The Six Sigma Agent (failure archetype)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;pure-future&lt;/i&gt; — Enterprise-reliability study that names Over-Helpfulness as a failure archetype: agents prioritise responsiveness and task completion over accuracy, answering even when uncertain or when the request falls outside their capabilities.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.19504&quot;&gt;Aegis agent-environment failure taxonomy&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; — Trace study of LLM-agent failures that catalogues where agents persist on tasks the environment cannot support, adjacent to answering past capability.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Guardrails&quot;&gt;NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Programmable rails (topic control, self-check facts, hallucination output rails) keep the model from answering off-topic or producing ungrounded output, directly gating the answer-anyway default this anti-pattern names; quote: &quot;Guardrails are specific ways of controlling the output of a large language model, such as not talking about politics, responding in a particular way to specific user requests, following a predefined dialog path.&quot;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/guardrails-ai/guardrails&quot;&gt;Guardrails AI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Output guards such as the Grounded AI Hallucination validator detect when a response is not grounded in the provided context, catching the fabricated-grounding failure mode; quote (validator): &quot;detects hallucinations in AI-generated responses. It evaluates whether a given response is grounded in the provided context or if it contains factually incorrect or nonsensical information.&quot;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/protectai/llm-guard&quot;&gt;LLM Guard (Protect AI)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — &quot;The Security Toolkit for LLM Interactions&quot; ships output scanners (Relevance, FactualConsistency) that flag answers irrelevant to or unsupported by the input, surfacing the out-of-scope-completion smell rather than letting it pass silently.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2820.4" width="755" height="472" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Refusal&lt;/b&gt; — Refusal is the corrective: scoped requests that fail the capability gate are declined instead of attempted, which is exactly what over-helpfulness skips.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Reflexive Metacognitive Agent&lt;/b&gt; — An explicit self-model lets the agent consult its own capabilities before accepting a task, removing the answer-anyway default.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;False Confidence Syndrome&lt;/b&gt; — False confidence is uniform certainty across right and wrong outputs; over-helpfulness is the choice to answer at all when out of scope. They compound: an out-of-scope answer delivered with unwarranted confidence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Sycophancy&lt;/b&gt; — Sycophancy bends the answer toward what the user wants to hear; over-helpfulness produces an answer where none should be given. Both stem from optimising approval over correctness.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Productive Struggle Erosion&lt;/b&gt; — Over-helpfulness answers beyond capability or scope; productive struggle erosion answers correctly and in scope, yet the act of answering is the harm.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2706.4" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22290&quot;&gt;The Six Sigma Agent: Achieving Enterprise-Grade Reliability in LLM Systems Through Consensus-Driven Decomposed Execution&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.19504&quot;&gt;Aegis: Taxonomy and Optimizations for Overcoming Agent-Environment Failures in LLM Agents&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.18418&quot;&gt;Know Your Limits: A Survey of Abstention in Large Language Models&lt;/a&gt; — Bingbing Wen, Jihan Yao, Shangbin Feng, Chenjun Xu, Yulia Tsvetkov, Bill Howe, Lucy Lu Wang, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.09038&quot;&gt;AbstentionBench: Reasoning LLMs Fail on Unanswerable Questions&lt;/a&gt; — Polina Kirichenko, Mark Ibrahim, Kamalika Chaudhuri, Samuel J. Bell, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.13548&quot;&gt;Towards Understanding Sycophancy in Language Models&lt;/a&gt; — Mrinank Sharma, Meg Tong, Tomasz Korbak, et al., 2023&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3306.4" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="over-search-and-under-search" name="Over-Search and Under-Search">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2445.8888888888887" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2445.8888888888887" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Over-Search and Under-Search&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Anti-Patterns &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; deprecated &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Retrieval-Frequency Miscalibration&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="584.89" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Agentic RAG retrieval decision miscalibrated" mermaidId="n:A" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Agentic RAG retrieval decision miscalibrated" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="60.0" width="422.22" x="721.67" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Retrieve now?" mermaidId="n:B" mermaidBaseStyle="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Retrieve now?" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="195.56" width="195.56" x="582.78" y="291.67" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Re-retrieve info already in context, wasting tokens and latency" mermaidId="n:C" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Re-retrieve info already in context, wasting tokens and latency" id="m2">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="60.0" width="571.11" x="65.0" y="563.89" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Skip retrieval when parametric knowledge is stale, risking hallucination" mermaidId="n:D" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Skip retrieval when parametric knowledge is stale, risking hallucination" id="m3">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="60.0" width="638.89" x="691.67" y="563.89" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Calibrated retrieval decision rewards needed retrieval and penalises redundant" mermaidId="n:E" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Calibrated retrieval decision rewards needed retrieval and penalises redundant" id="m4">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="60.0" width="701.11" x="833.89" y="359.44" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;B#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.24;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m5">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m0" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.24;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="680.56" y="253.89" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="over-search" mermaidId="e:B-&gt;C#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.7;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="over-search" id="m6">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.7;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m2">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="350.56" y="526.11" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="under-search" mermaidId="e:B-&gt;D#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.7;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="under-search" id="m7">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.7;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1011.67" y="526.11" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="fix" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;E#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.76;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="fix" id="m8">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m0" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.76;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1185.0" y="253.89" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Over-Search and Under-Search failure-mode pathway.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="629.89" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: let an agentic RAG system miscalibrate when to retrieve, so it either re-retrieves information already in context or skips retrieval when its parametric knowledge is stale.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="704.89" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent has search-as-tool wired into its loop and decides at each step whether to invoke retrieval. The decision policy is implicit — it falls out of the prompt and the model&#39;s general disposition rather than from a calibrated signal. The team measures end-to-end task accuracy and tool-call counts, but not whether each individual retrieval was warranted.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="704.89" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent re-retrieves passages it has already seen in the same context window (over-search), burning tokens and latency on duplicates, and it skips retrieval when its parametric knowledge is wrong (under-search), producing confident hallucinations. Both failures are invisible at the aggregate metric level — accuracy averages can stay flat while individual queries either pay for the same passage four times or get answered from stale weights. The HiPRAG paper measures over-search at double-digit baseline rates in standard agentic-RAG setups, with under-search rates rising under reinforcement-learning training that rewards short trajectories.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="810.89" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Naive policies (always retrieve, never retrieve) are easy; calibrated policies require a learned or rule-based decision signal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; End-to-end accuracy hides retrieval miscalibration because the agent can still arrive at correct answers via expensive or lucky paths.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token cost and latency from over-search compound silently; hallucinations from under-search are noticed only when a downstream check catches them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="848.89" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: instrument retrieval decisions with per-step process rewards or rule-based gates, measure over-search and under-search rates separately on a held-out eval, and tune the agent&#39;s decision policy on those signals — not on end-to-end accuracy alone.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1011.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Don&#39;t ship agentic RAG without calibrated retrieval decisions. Adopt agentic-rag with explicit retrieval-decision instrumentation: per-step rewards that penalise redundant retrieval and reward retrieval when parametric knowledge is insufficient. Track over-search and under-search rates as first-class evaluation metrics. Compare against naive-rag (always retrieve) and naive-rag-first (RAG-by-reflex) as baselines — the goal is calibrated, not maximally agentic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1030.89" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: Query -&amp;gt; uncalibrated retrieve-or-not decision -&amp;gt; redundant retrieval or skipped retrieval -&amp;gt; waste or hallucination. Corrected: Query -&amp;gt; calibrated retrieval decision (per-step reward + over/under-search metrics) -&amp;gt; retrieve only when knowledge is missing.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1136.89" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team ships an agentic-RAG assistant that reaches 82% accuracy on its eval. After three months of complaints about latency and cost, they instrument per-step retrieval decisions. They find the agent re-retrieves the same three policy documents on every fourth turn (over-search at 31%), and on 9% of queries it skips retrieval entirely and answers from stale parametric knowledge (under-search). They add a process-reward signal that penalises duplicate retrieval and rewards retrieval when the model&#39;s confidence is low. Over-search drops to 4%, under-search to 2%, accuracy rises to 87%, and token cost per query falls by 38%.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1193.89" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: an agentic retrieval loop looks smarter than always-retrieve and seems to need no extra measurement.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team track over-search and under-search rates as separate evaluation metrics.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token spend and latency inflated by repeat retrievals on context the agent already holds.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Confident hallucinations from skipped retrieval when parametric knowledge is stale or wrong.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregate accuracy metrics mask the failure; only per-step retrieval-decision evaluation surfaces it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1280.89" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No useful constraint; the missing constraint is a calibrated retrieval-decision policy with per-step measurement.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1394.89" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Never. Cite when reviewing an agentic-RAG system that has no per-step retrieval-decision metric.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Demand over-search and under-search rates as first-class evaluation outputs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Instrument retrieval decisions with process rewards or rule-based gates.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1576.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Any agentic-RAG system measured only on end-to-end accuracy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Any retrieval loop where the agent decides when to search without a calibrated signal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Any deployment where token spend on retrieval has never been audited per-query.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1500.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Trigger condition — what causes the over-search and under-search pattern to manifest&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Affected surface — the part of the system where the failure shows up&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Detection signal — what an operator would observe when this is happening&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1701.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Observability — logs, traces, and metrics that surface the pattern&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval harness — runs that quantify exposure to the pattern&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1625.89" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Duplicate fetch — the agent retrieves the same passage several times in one context window and pays for each copy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale-weight answer — the agent skips retrieval on a question its parametric knowledge gets wrong and answers with confidence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Flat average — overall accuracy stays steady, so neither failure is seen until per-step retrieval decisions are measured.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-trajectory bias — training that rewards short runs teaches the agent to skip retrieval more often.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1826.89" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Over-search rate — fraction of retrieval calls whose returned content was already present in the agent&#39;s context window&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Under-search rate — fraction of queries answered from parametric knowledge where retrieval would have changed the answer&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tokens-per-correct-answer — total retrieval-input tokens divided by correct answers; rises with over-search&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hallucination rate on retrieval-skipped queries — share of confidently wrong answers when retrieval was not invoked&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Process-reward signal coverage — fraction of retrieval decisions evaluated by a per-step reward rather than only end-to-end accuracy&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1731.89" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07794&quot;&gt;HiPRAG: Hierarchical Process Rewards for Efficient Agentic Retrieval Augmented Generation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Names the failure modes explicitly; reduces over-search to 2.3% via fine-grained process rewards.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07379&quot;&gt;SoK: Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Surveys retrieval-misalignment risks in agentic RAG.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09136&quot;&gt;Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: A Survey on Agentic RAG&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Surveys dynamic-retrieval-policy design space.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2046.89" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agentic RAG&lt;/b&gt; — calibrated retrieval decisions are the fix&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Naive RAG&lt;/b&gt; — always-retrieve baseline against which over-search regression is measured&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Naive-RAG-First&lt;/b&gt; — the upstream architecture decision; this anti-pattern is the per-step retrieval calibration failure&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Deliberation Over Observation&lt;/b&gt; — There the substituted object is a retrieved document and the miscalibration is two-sided; here it is any environment interaction and the effect is monotone in the thinking budget.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1989.89" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07794&quot;&gt;HiPRAG: Hierarchical Process Rewards for Efficient Agentic Retrieval Augmented Generation&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07379&quot;&gt;SoK: Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.09136&quot;&gt;Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation: A Survey on Agentic RAG&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2247.89" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="oversight-as-legitimation" name="Oversight as Legitimation">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="4051.684210526316" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="4051.684210526316" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Oversight as Legitimation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Anti-Patterns &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; mature &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Oversight Theatre, Nominal Human Oversight, Compliance-Cover Reviewer&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="1183.68" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
