        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:B-&gt;Agg#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:C-&gt;Agg#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.07;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.07;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="612.15" y="599.85" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Agg-&gt;R#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Run independent LLM calls concurrently and combine results.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="928.5" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A task either splits cleanly into independent subtasks that can run side by side — for example reviewing a pull request for security, style, and test coverage — or benefits from running the same prompt several times and combining the results, which is the basis of self-consistency style voting in mathematical reasoning. In both cases the agent is making more than one LLM call where none of the calls depend on each other&#39;s output. The provider&#39;s rate limits and the team&#39;s budget can absorb running these calls in parallel.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="928.5" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If independent subtasks run one after another, the user waits for the sum of every call even though nothing forces the order. If the model produces only one attempt at a hard reasoning problem, an unlucky sample can be wrong with no chance of catching it because there is nothing to compare against. Sequential single-attempt execution leaves both latency and quality on the table whenever the work is genuinely parallelisable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1020.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Concurrency limits and rate limits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregation logic for voting (majority? best? union?).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost multiplies linearly with parallel branches.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1110.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: fan independent work or repeated attempts out into concurrent LLM calls and join them at a single aggregator, so that latency drops on sectioning and outliers surface on voting.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1183.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Two flavours. Sectioning: split a task into independent subtasks, run them concurrently, concatenate results. Voting: run the same task multiple times, aggregate by majority or judge.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1235.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Task --&amp;gt; Splitter (sectioning) or Replicator (voting) --&amp;gt; Call A | Call B | Call C (no shared state) --&amp;gt; Aggregator (concatenate / majority / judge) --&amp;gt; Result&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1289.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A code-review agent runs three independent checks on each PR — security scan, style review, and test-coverage analysis. Running them in series adds up to thirty seconds per PR. The team applies parallelization in its sectioning flavour: the three checks run as concurrent LLM calls and the results concatenate into one review. For high-stakes PRs they also use the voting flavour: the security check runs three times and an aggregator emits the majority verdict, catching the occasional outlier hit.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1341.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wall-clock latency drops; quality rises (voting).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Independent failures isolate cleanly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost scales with branch count.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregation logic is its own correctness problem.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1414.5" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Branches cannot share state during execution; aggregation is the only join point.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1504.5" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Independent subtasks can run concurrently to cut wall-clock time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Voting across multiple attempts catches outliers a single run would miss.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregation by concatenation, majority, or judge is feasible.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1653.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Subtasks have hard dependencies that force sequential execution.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The cost of running multiple attempts outweighs the quality gain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No reliable aggregation step is available for the votes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1596.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Splitter or replicator — fans the task into sectioning subtasks or repeated voting branches&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Parallel branches — independent LLM calls that share no state during execution&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregator — majority vote, judge model, union, or concatenation depending on flavour&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Concurrency controller — bounds the fan-out width against rate limits and budget&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Failure-isolation wrapper — per-branch error handling that does not poison the join&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1778.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Async LLM client (LangChain &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;RunnableParallel&lt;/font&gt;, asyncio gather, Promise.all) — drives the fan-out&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple LLM API keys or load-balanced endpoints — sustain the parallel request rate&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregation library — voting helpers, judge prompts, or merge utilities&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1721.5" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; False independence — sectioned subtasks actually depend on each other, and the concatenated result contradicts itself at the seams.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Correlated votes — every branch makes the same mistake from the same prompt, so the majority vote confirms the wrong answer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Poisoned join — one branch fails or times out, and the aggregator drops the whole result or merges an error into it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fan-out cost — branch count is raised for quality, and the spend grows linearly while the gain flattens.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1941.5" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Wall-clock latency vs sequential baseline (sectioning) — the speedup the fan-out delivers&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quality lift over single-attempt baseline (voting) — accuracy gain from majority or judge&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Branch agreement rate (voting) — how often branches converge, which calibrates n&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost multiplier per resolved request — branch count times unit cost&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Aggregation-step error rate — judge or vote miscalls measured on a labelled set&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1846.5" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Anthropic Building Effective Agents (Workflow #3)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Self-consistency in mathematical reasoning&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2161.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Consistency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;MapReduce for Agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Best-of-N Sampling&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;LLMCompiler&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Parallel Tool Calls&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Prompt Chaining&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Lead Researcher&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Clone Fan-Out Research&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Iteration Node&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Race Conditions on Shared Tool Resources&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Parallel Fan-Out / Gather&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Agent on Sequential Workloads&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;generalises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Scatter-Gather Plus Saga&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2009.5" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/research/building-effective-agents&quot;&gt;Anthropic: Building Effective Agents&lt;/a&gt; — 2024&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2267.5" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="partial-global-planning" name="Partial Global Planning">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1943.986970684039" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="1943.986970684039" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Partial Global Planning&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Planning &amp;amp; Control Flow &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; experimental &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: PGP, Durfee-Lesser Planning&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
