                <mxPoint x="1308.04" y="265.13" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Each agent maintains a partial view of others&#39; plans and incrementally merges local plans into a shared partial global plan, interleaving coordination with execution.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="335.99" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A multi-agent system coordinates on a problem where a complete global plan is impractical to compute — the problem is too large, the world is non-stationary, or agents only learn what they need to coordinate as they go. Waiting for a global plan to complete before any agent acts is unworkable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="335.99" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Centralised global planning hits scaling limits and is fragile to change. Fully local planning produces inconsistent action choices that violate global constraints. Without an intermediate — a plan that is partial in coverage and global in scope, refined incrementally as agents share what they know — the team either pauses for impossible centralisation or acts inconsistently in isolation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="441.99" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Complete global plans are often infeasible to compute or maintain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Local plans alone produce inconsistent global behaviour.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agents have incentives to share plan fragments only when coordination benefits exceed cost.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Plan revision must propagate without thrashing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="460.99" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: maintain a partial global plan that each agent holds a fragment of and refines incrementally as it shares with neighbours, so coordination interleaves with action and the system stays responsive without waiting for a complete plan.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="585.99" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Each agent runs a planner that produces both local actions and partial-global-plan fragments. Agents periodically exchange fragments with neighbours; merging produces consistent shared plan structure for the parts agents care about. When new observations or revisions arrive, the affected fragment is updated and shared again. The team never holds a complete global plan; it holds a sufficient partial one. Execution and planning interleave.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="604.99" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Each agent: Local planner --&amp;gt; local actions + partial-global-plan fragment --exchange with neighbours--&amp;gt; Fragment merger --&amp;gt; updated shared view --&amp;gt; execute local actions --new observations--&amp;gt; revise fragment --&amp;gt; exchange again&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="710.99" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A fleet of research agents investigates a sprawling open question. Each holds a partial plan over its sub-area plus the fragments it has received about adjacent sub-areas. When agent A discovers its sub-area&#39;s evidence reframes the global picture, it revises its fragment and shares with the agents whose fragments referenced it. The team never produces a single global research plan; it produces overlapping partial plans that stay consistent enough.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="767.99" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Coordinated behaviour without the cost of a complete global plan.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Resilient to non-stationary worlds — revisions are local fragments.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scales beyond what a single planner could handle.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fragment merging is non-trivial; conflicting fragments need a resolution rule.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Some coordination cases require global structure the fragments don&#39;t capture.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Thrashing on rapid revisions can degrade into pure local planning.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="854.99" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Multi-agent coordination must not wait for a complete global plan; agents exchange and merge partial-global-plan fragments while continuing to act.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="930.99" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-agent problem too large for a single global planner.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; World is non-stationary; plans must keep revising.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Coordination benefits exceed fragment-exchange cost.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1131.99" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Problem is small enough for one global planner.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fragment merging cannot be defined for the domain.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agents have no incentive to share plan fragments honestly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1036.99" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Local planner — produces per-agent action plans&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Partial global plan fragment — overlapping subset of structure shared with neighbours&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fragment exchanger — propagates updates&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fragment merger — produces consistent local view from received fragments&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1256.99" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Plan-fragment schema — shared format across agents&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Message bus — carries fragments&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Local planner runtime — re-runs when fragments change&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1161.99" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Fragment conflict — two agents send incompatible plan fragments, and with no resolution rule each keeps its own version.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Revision thrash — fragments change faster than they can be merged, and agents fall back to acting on local plans only.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing global structure — a constraint spans agents that never exchange fragments, so the partial plan cannot see it and the joint action breaks it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale fragment — an agent acts on a neighbour&#39;s fragment that was already revised, and their actions collide.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1400.99" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Coordination gap — distance between local plans and the implied global plan&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fragment-exchange volume — operational cost of coordination&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Revision-thrash rate — frequency of contradictory updates&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1286.99" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cse-robotics.engr.tamu.edu/dshell/cs631/papers/durfee87using.pdf&quot;&gt;Durfee &amp;amp; Lesser — Partial Global Planning (1987)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262731317/multiagent-systems/&quot;&gt;Multiagent Systems (Weiss) — Distributed planning chapter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1620.99" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
