        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Three role-isolated agents talk only through structured artefacts on disk; the evaluator never sees the generator&#39;s trace.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1734.25" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Decompose a long-running job into three role-isolated agents — a Planner emitting a feature list, a Generator working one chunk per fresh context, and an Evaluator grading against a rubric without seeing the Generator&#39;s trace.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1809.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team runs a coding-agent harness on multi-day creative work — building a new feature across a large application, conducting a large refactor, drafting a long design document. The job is too big to fit into a single model context window, so it has to be split across many runs. There is a clear external artefact (code, document, design) that can be evaluated on its own merits without inspecting how it was produced.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1809.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A single agent trying to do all of this in one head hits context limits within a few hours and conflates planning, generation, and self-grading; its own scratch reasoning leaks into how it judges its work. A two-role loop where one agent generates and the other critiques lets the generator read the critic&#39;s notes as hints and game them. Generic orchestrator-worker decomposition does not name a grader role with hard isolation, so quality drifts run by run and there is no fixed place to enforce the acceptance bar. The team needs a three-way split where each role&#39;s context stays small, the grader cannot be socially engineered by the generator, and the plan survives across runs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1934.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Each role&#39;s context must stay small enough to fit, yet the overall job spans days.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The evaluator must judge the artefact, not the process, but the generator naturally wants to argue.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Plans must be machine-checkable so the generator can pick up the next chunk without re-reading the user&#39;s prompt.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Role isolation costs orchestration complexity and inter-role hand-off latency.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1972.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: split the harness into three agents with disjoint contexts — Planner produces a structured feature list, Generator works one chunk at a time from a fresh context seeded only by the plan plus prior artefact, and Evaluator scores the artefact against a fixed rubric without access to the Generator&#39;s reasoning trace — so each role optimises one objective and cannot collude with the others.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2135.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The Planner runs once (or rarely) and emits a structured feature-list artefact: ordered chunks, acceptance criteria, dependencies. The Generator is invoked per-chunk in a fresh context that includes only (a) the feature-list, (b) the current artefact state, and (c) the chunk to build; it produces a new artefact revision and exits. The Evaluator is invoked in its own fresh context with only the artefact and the fixed rubric; it returns pass/fail plus structured findings, and never sees the Generator&#39;s chain of thought or scratch notes. A small driver loop routes between the three: failed evaluation re-invokes the Generator with the findings as input (not the full Evaluator transcript). The fixed rubric makes Evaluator behaviour reproducible across runs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2154.25" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Driver --&amp;gt; {Planner | Generator | Evaluator}. Planner reads user prompt, writes feature-list.json. Generator reads feature-list.json + artefact, writes artefact&amp;#x27;. Evaluator reads artefact&amp;#x27; + rubric, writes findings.json. Driver dispatches based on findings.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2279.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A coding agent is asked to add OAuth support across a large web app. The Planner reads the prompt and writes feature-list.json: ten ordered chunks with acceptance criteria. The Generator boots a fresh context per chunk, edits files, exits. The Evaluator boots its own fresh context, reads only the diff and the rubric (&quot;does it compile, do the new tests pass, are there no plaintext secrets&quot;), and returns findings. Chunk 4 fails; the driver re-invokes the Generator with the findings but not the Evaluator&#39;s reasoning trace. Across two days the artefact converges without any one context exceeding its limit.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2374.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each role&#39;s context stays small and bounded.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evaluator isolation makes scores harder to game from inside the generator.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fresh-context generation per chunk avoids long-trace attention rot.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Plans are durable artefacts that survive crashes and resumption.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Three-agent orchestration adds significant harness complexity over single-agent loops.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inter-role hand-offs through files add latency.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A weak or mis-specified rubric makes the Evaluator useless or actively harmful.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Planner errors propagate through the whole run because the Generator trusts the plan.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2423.25" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The Evaluator must never receive the Generator&#39;s reasoning trace or scratch context, only the artefact and the rubric; the Generator must not re-plan (any plan change goes back to the Planner); the Planner must not generate the artefact directly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2575.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A single agent run cannot fit the job into one context window.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; There is a clear external artefact that can be evaluated without inspecting how it was produced.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A stable rubric exists or can be authored.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2738.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The job is short enough for a single agent with extended thinking.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No meaningful rubric can be written; the evaluator will degrade to noise.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency matters more than quality; the inter-role hand-offs are too expensive.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2700.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Planner — runs once and emits a structured feature-list artefact&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Generator — fresh-context worker invoked per chunk, edits the artefact&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evaluator — fresh-context grader that sees artefact plus rubric only&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Driver loop — routes between the three roles based on evaluator findings&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fixed rubric — durable acceptance criteria the evaluator scores against&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2863.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — three role-isolated invocations, contexts never overlap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Artefact store on disk — feature-list, current artefact, and findings files&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rubric file — version-controlled, fixed across runs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Test harness or compiler — verifies the artefact for the evaluator&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2825.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Trace leak — the evaluator is given the generator&#39;s scratch notes, and it grades the reasoning it was shown rather than the artefact.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bad rubric — the fixed rubric checks the wrong things, and the evaluator passes broken chunks run after run.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Trusted bad plan — the planner lists a wrong or missing feature, and the generator builds every chunk on top of it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Generator re-planning — the generator changes the feature list to make a chunk easier, and the plan and artefact drift apart.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3026.25" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Context-window pressure per role — peak tokens any single role uses&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evaluator gaming rate — incidents of generator influencing evaluator outcomes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Chunk-acceptance rate — fraction of generator chunks that pass evaluation first try&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-run rubric stability — variance in evaluator scores on the same artefact&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Total wall-clock per accepted chunk — including evaluator retries&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2969.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/harness-design-long-running-apps&quot;&gt;Anthropic harness for Claude Code long-running tasks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Three-agent harness described in Anthropic engineering posts on long-running application development.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents&quot;&gt;Anthropic effective-harnesses guidance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Codifies role isolation and fresh-context generation as harness primitives.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3246.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Evaluator-Optimizer&lt;/b&gt; — Adds a separate Planner role and enforces evaluator isolation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Planner-Executor-Observer&lt;/b&gt; — POE&#39;s observer is a monitor; here the evaluator is a peer grader with veto power.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Orchestrator-Workers&lt;/b&gt; — Fixes three named roles instead of dynamic worker decomposition.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Spec-First Agent&lt;/b&gt; — The Planner output is a machine-readable spec.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Frozen Rubric Reflection&lt;/b&gt; — Evaluator runs against a fixed rubric.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="3132.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/harness-design-long-running-apps&quot;&gt;Harness design for long-running application development&lt;/a&gt; — Anthropic Engineering, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-harnesses-for-long-running-agents&quot;&gt;Effective harnesses for long-running agents&lt;/a&gt; — Anthropic Engineering, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.infoq.com/news/2026/04/anthropic-three-agent-harness-ai/&quot;&gt;Anthropic Details Three-Agent Harness for Long-Running Coding Agents&lt;/a&gt; — InfoQ, 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3428.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
