          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Represent a family of related entities in a single core schema with type-specific extensions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="798.3" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is designing a data model for a family of related entities that share most of their fields but differ in a few. A textile catalogue has yarn, fabric, and trim records, each with a common core (a stock-keeping unit, a supplier, a lead time) plus a handful of type-specific fields (yarn weight, fabric weave, trim attachment). A user-content system has projects, queues, and favourites that share an owner and a timestamp but diverge in their payloads. The team has to decide how to represent the shared core and the divergent extensions in a single schema that clients of different ages can still read.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="798.3" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Two naive choices both go wrong. One schema per sub-type duplicates the common fields and forces every client to know about every sub-type; when a new sub-type appears, old clients break or have to be updated in lockstep. A single flat schema that contains every possible field for every sub-type is bloated, hard to validate, and silently allows nonsensical combinations such as a fabric record carrying a yarn weight. The team needs a representation that keeps the common parts common, isolates the per-sub-type fields, and lets old clients survive the addition of a new sub-type.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="890.3" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Common fields must stay common; new sub-types must not break old ones.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Type-specific fields need a clean place to live.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Validation must be per-sub-type, not just per-record.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="999.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: factor the family into a core schema with a discriminator plus namespaced extension blocks, so that common fields stay common and sub-types extend without breaking older clients.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1072.3" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a core schema with the common fields and a discriminator (e.g. &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;material_type&lt;/font&gt;). Sub-type fields live in a namespaced extension block (e.g. &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;yarn: {...}&lt;/font&gt; for yarn-specific). Clients that do not understand a sub-type still read the core fields and round-trip the rest without data loss.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1124.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Record core (id, discriminator e.g. material_type, common fields) + namespaced extension per sub-type (yarn: {...} | fabric: {...}) -&amp;gt; client reads core -&amp;gt; known sub-type: validate and use extension; unknown sub-type: keep and round-trip extension untouched&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1178.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A textile-trading platform has yarn, fabric, and trim records, each with shared fields (sku, supplier, lead-time) plus type-specific ones (yarn count, fabric weave, trim attachment). Three separate schemas duplicate code; one bloated &#39;material&#39; schema with every field is unenforceable. The team adopts a polymorphic-record: a core schema with the shared fields and a &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;material_type&lt;/font&gt; discriminator, plus namespaced extension blocks (yarn:{}, fabric:{}, trim:{}). Clients that don&#39;t understand a sub-type still read the core fields and round-trip the rest losslessly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1249.3" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Forward-compatible: new sub-types don&#39;t break old clients.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; One core schema; many specialisations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Validation logic per sub-type adds complexity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Discriminator-driven code paths can be hard to debug.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1322.3" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Sub-type fields must live under their namespaced extension; they cannot pollute the core.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1431.3" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A family of related entities shares a core schema with type-specific extensions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Clients should round-trip unknown sub-types without losing data.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A discriminator field can flag the sub-type cleanly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1561.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-types share so few fields that separate schemas are clearer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; All clients understand all sub-types and a flat schema is simpler.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-type extension blocks would proliferate unboundedly without governance.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1523.3" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Core schema — common fields shared by every sub-type, readable by clients that do not know any sub-type&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Discriminator field — names the sub-type (e.g. material_type) and drives per-sub-type validation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Namespaced extension block — holds the sub-type-specific fields under a key (e.g. yarn: {...}) so they cannot pollute the core&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-sub-type validator — checks that the extension block matches the discriminator value&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Round-trip preserver — keeps unknown extension blocks intact when a client reads and rewrites a record&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1686.3" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; JSON Schema with oneOf + discriminator — standard mechanism for declaring polymorphic records&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; OpenAPI discriminator — language-neutral way to expose the pattern in an API contract&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tagged-union type (Pydantic discriminated union, TypeScript discriminated union, Rust enum) — language-level enforcement of the pattern in code&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1648.3" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Core pollution — a sub-type field is added at the top level for convenience, and other sub-types start carrying a meaningless value for it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lossy round-trip — an old client reads a record with an unknown sub-type, drops the extension block on save, and the type-specific data is gone.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Discriminator mismatch — &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;material_type&lt;/font&gt; says one sub-type while the extension block belongs to another, and per-type validation does not catch it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Branch sprawl — code switches on the discriminator in many places, and a new sub-type is handled in some branches but missed in others.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1906.3" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Per-sub-type validation pass rate — how often records actually conform to their declared discriminator&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Forward-compatibility round-trip rate — fraction of unknown-sub-type records that old clients read and write back without data loss&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Discriminator mismatch rate — records whose extension block does not match the declared sub-type&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Core-field pollution count — sub-type-specific fields that leaked into the core schema and need to be moved&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sub-type proliferation rate — new sub-types added per release; flags governance drift&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1792.3" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Weft&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Material with material_type=yarn / fabric / thread / etc.; Pattern across knitting / crochet / weaving / etc.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;FHIR resource polymorphism&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Stripe API discriminated objects&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;JSON-LD @type&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;OpenAPI discriminator/oneOf&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/api/payment_methods/object&quot;&gt;Stripe API (PaymentMethod object)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — A single PaymentMethod record carries a type field plus a matching nested hash with type-specific fields.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;[HL7 FHIR (choice[x] elements)](https://build.fhir.org/formats.html)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Polymorphic elements named nnn[x] where [x] is replaced by the title-cased name of the type actually used.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2126.3" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Schema Extensibility&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Translation Layer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2012.3" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://dataintensive.net/&quot;&gt;Designing Data-Intensive Applications&lt;/a&gt; — Martin Kleppmann, 2017&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2384.3" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
