        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Append-&gt;Store#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.28;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m17">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.28;" target="m8">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="264.95" y="1142.35" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Mark-&gt;Store#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m18">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m7" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m8">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Store-&gt;R#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.07;entryX=0.68;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m19">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m8" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.07;entryX=0.68;entryY=1;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="1142.35" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="1061.75" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="967.2" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="871.1" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="790.5" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="709.9" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="629.3" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="548.7" />
                <mxPoint x="982.6" y="454.15" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Maintain a third agent memory type alongside episodic (past events) and semantic (facts): procedural memory captures &lt;i&gt;learned how-to&lt;/i&gt; — reusable skills, workflows, and self-rewritten system instructions that map situations directly to actions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1329.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent operates across many sessions and accumulates experience. Some of that experience is best stored as facts (semantic), some as event records (episodic). A third category — how to do something — does not fit either: it&#39;s the agent&#39;s accumulated playbook, recipes, and shortcuts. Without a dedicated store, this knowledge either lives in a static system prompt (no learning) or gets re-derived from episodic memory each time (slow, wasteful).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1329.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Episodic memory stores &#39;on 2026-03-12 I did X&#39;; semantic memory stores &#39;X is true&#39;. Neither stores &#39;when situation S arises, the right action sequence is A1, A2, A3&#39;. Without a procedural store, the agent re-derives skills from raw episodes on every invocation, or relies on a frozen system prompt that cannot improve. LangChain&#39;s LangMem SDK explicitly names this gap and provides three memory types; the arXiv ProcMEM paper shows learned procedural memory outperforms episodic-only retrieval on reusable-skill tasks.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1454.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Episodic memory recalls past events but does not generalise to reusable shortcuts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Static system prompts cannot improve from experience.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Procedural memory must be safely updatable — the agent rewriting its own instructions is itself a risk surface (see rogue-agent-drift).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Skills must be retrievable by situation, not by keyword — requires structured indexing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1492.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: maintain a procedural store keyed by situation pattern; allow the agent to read, append, and revise entries; gate updates with provenance and review; retrieve at decision-time by matching current situation against stored patterns.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1636.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Implement a procedural-memory store as a first-class memory type alongside episodic and semantic. Entries are (situation pattern, action sequence, success record). The agent reads at planning time and appends after successful workflows. Updates are gated — naïvely letting the agent overwrite its own playbook risks rogue-drift, so add provenance and review. Common implementations: LangChain&#39;s LangMem &#39;procedural&#39; channel, Claude Agent Skills (manually authored), ProcMEM-style learned skill libraries.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1655.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Current situation --retrieve by situation pattern--&amp;gt; Procedural store --match--&amp;gt; Stored procedure (A1 -&amp;gt; A2 -&amp;gt; A3) | --no match--&amp;gt; Plan from scratch; --&amp;gt; Execute --&amp;gt; Outcome --success + novel--&amp;gt; gated append | --failure--&amp;gt; mark procedure for review&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1761.95" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A software-engineering agent works across hundreds of pull-request reviews. Initially, it re-derives the right review approach (run tests, check coverage, look for security smells) from its general training each time. After adopting procedural memory, the agent stores &#39;on PRs touching auth code, the right procedure is: 1) load OWASP cheatsheet, 2) check auth-test coverage, 3) flag any new secrets to security review&#39;. On future auth PRs, the procedural retrieval surfaces this playbook, saving derivation cost and producing more consistent reviews. Updates to the procedure require a successful application before they overwrite the prior version.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1818.95" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent learns reusable skills across sessions without re-deriving from raw episodes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Skills compose: complex procedures built from learned sub-procedures.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inference cost drops on recurring tasks — retrieved procedures replace re-planning.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Procedural memory updates by the agent itself create rogue-drift risk.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Retrieval by situation requires structured indexing — keyword search is insufficient.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale procedures persist after the environment changes; needs invalidation discipline.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1905.95" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Imposes a third memory type with structured situation→action indexing and update governance; constrains the agent to retrieve procedures by situation match rather than by free-text query.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2019.95" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agents that operate across many sessions and encounter recurring task shapes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Workflows where the cost of re-deriving the right action sequence is high.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Long-running agents that benefit from accumulated playbooks.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2182.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Single-session agents with no recurring task structure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Deployments where rogue-drift risk outweighs skill-reuse benefit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settings where situation-pattern indexing infrastructure is unavailable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2125.95" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Procedural store — keyed by situation pattern, stores (situation, action sequence, success record)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Situation matcher — retrieves stored procedures whose pattern matches the current situation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Update gate — controls when and how the agent can append or revise procedures&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provenance tracker — records who/what authored each procedure (manual, learned, imported)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2307.95" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LangMem-style procedural channel — production library implementation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Skill registry — manually-authored procedures (Anthropic Agent Skills)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Situation embedding index — vector store keyed by situation features for retrieval&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Procedure success ledger — tracks outcomes so failed procedures get demoted&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2250.95" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Rogue drift — the agent rewrites its own playbook after a lucky success, and a bad procedure spreads to every later task.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale procedure — the environment changes, but the stored action sequence still matches the situation and is run as if nothing changed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong situation match — loose indexing retrieves a procedure for a situation that only looks similar, and the steps fail midway.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ungated append — every successful run is saved as a new procedure, and near-duplicates crowd the store.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2451.95" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Procedure hit rate — share of decisions where a stored procedure matches the current situation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Skill-reuse cost saving — inference cost saved by retrieving vs re-planning&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Procedure success rate — fraction of stored procedures that produce successful outcomes when retrieved&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Update-governance violation rate — frequency of unsupervised self-rewrites of the procedural store&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Procedure staleness — share of stored procedures that fail validation against current environment&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2394.95" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://langchain-ai.github.io/langmem/&quot;&gt;LangChain LangMem SDK — procedural memory channel (2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/equipping-agents-for-the-real-world-with-agent-skills&quot;&gt;Anthropic Claude Agent Skills — manually-authored procedural surface (2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.01869&quot;&gt;ProcMEM — learned procedural memory via non-parametric PPO (arXiv 2026)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://techsy.io/en/blog/ai-agent-memory-guide&quot;&gt;techsy.io Italian memory taxonomy — names procedural memory as one of the seven memory types&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2671.95" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Summaries&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Knowledge Graph Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Archaeology&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dream Consolidation Cycle&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;conflicts-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Rogue Agent Drift&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Semantic Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Memory-Type Storage Specialization&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Three Layers of Agentic AI Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-to-Rule Distillation&lt;/b&gt; — Procedural memory keeps learned how-to inside the agent&#39;s memory; distillation externalises the learned path so the model is no longer consulted at all for that case.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2576.95" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.langchain.com/blog/langmem-sdk-launch&quot;&gt;LangChain — LangMem SDK for Agent Long-Term Memory&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.01869&quot;&gt;ProcMEM: Learning Reusable Procedural Memory from Experience&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://techsy.io/it/blog/guida-memoria-agenti-ia&quot;&gt;techsy.io — Memoria degli Agenti IA&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2891.95" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
