          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Runtime templates standardise both the model&#39;s input and its output.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="948.4" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;At runtime, transform user inputs and model outputs into standardised, template-aligned prompts and responses against predefined constraints, so the agent and its downstream consumers see consistent shapes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1023.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running an agent that sits between free-form human input on one side and a chain of downstream consumers on the other — other agents, tool calls, and user-interface components that each expect a particular shape. Users write whatever they want, in whatever phrasing they want, and downstream code expects predictable structure. The team needs a place to standardise both ends without asking either side to change its habits.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1023.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If user prompts go straight to the model and the model&#39;s free-form output goes straight to consumers, two things drift in parallel. The model&#39;s behaviour changes with every small wording variation in how users phrase the same intent, and each downstream consumer ends up writing its own ad-hoc parser to extract what it needs from prose, with parsers that disagree on edge cases. Over time the agent&#39;s behaviour becomes hard to reproduce and downstream integrations become brittle, because there is no single contract that both the model and the consumers are held to.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1148.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Standardisation: consistent shape across prompts and responses helps reliability.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Goal alignment: optimisation must serve the user&#39;s actual goal, not just template compliance.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Interoperability: other tools/agents need predictable shapes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adaptability: templates must accommodate different domains and constraints.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1186.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: insert a runtime component that refines prompts on the way in and responses on the way out using a registry of templates with constraints, so that what the model sees and what consumers see are standardised against the same contract.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1330.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A prompt/response optimiser sits between the user-facing surface and the foundation model. On input, it loads a template for the current task (few-shot examples, format constraints, goal restatement) and rewrites the user&#39;s prompt to match. On output, it post-processes the model&#39;s response into the consumer&#39;s expected shape. The template registry can be evolved independently of the agent logic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1330.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;User input → Prompt optimiser (template registry) → Foundation model → Response optimiser → Consumer.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1455.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An onboarding agent accepts any free-form question from a new employee. A prompt/response optimiser wraps every user message in a template that restates the company policy context, the employee&#39;s department, and the required output format (a JSON object with answer + citation). The model never sees raw user wording without that frame, and the downstream UI always renders a predictable shape.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1474.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Standardisation across prompts and responses without changing user behaviour.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Goal alignment: refined prompts re-state the underlying goal explicitly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Interoperability: downstream agents/tools consume predictable shapes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adaptability: domain-specific templates without re-training the model.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Underspecification: the optimiser may strip context the user meant to convey.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Maintenance overhead: templates need to evolve as goals and consumers change.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Drift if templates aren&#39;t versioned alongside the agent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1561.4" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Both the model and the downstream consumers see only template-conformant shapes; raw user wording does not propagate.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1618.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple downstream consumers depend on the agent&#39;s response shape.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Domain-specific prompt scaffolding must be reused across many requests.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Templates can be evolved separately from agent logic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1857.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A single inline prompt suffices and no consumer chain exists.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Templates would over-constrain user expression in ways that hurt goal alignment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1724.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Prompt optimiser — rewrites raw user input against the loaded template before it reaches the model&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Response optimiser — post-processes model output into the shape the consumer expects&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Template registry — versioned store of templates, format constraints, and few-shot exemplars per task&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Foundation model — sees only template-conformant input, never raw user wording&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Downstream consumer — agent, tool, or UI that depends on the standardised response shape&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1982.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Prompt-template runtime (LangChain PromptTemplate, Bedrock Prompt Management, Dialogflow Generators) — loads and applies templates at request time&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Template versioning system — tracks template changes alongside agent code so behaviour is reproducible&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Output post-processor (regex, JSON parser, schema validator) — coerces model output into the consumer&#39;s shape&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1830.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stripped intent — the rewrite into the template drops a detail the user meant, and the model answers a cleaner but different question.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Template lag — goals or consumers change while the templates stay the same, so rewritten prompts and shaped responses no longer fit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unversioned registry — templates change without being versioned with the agent, and behaviour shifts with no record of why.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bypass path — one consumer reads raw model output instead of the optimised response, and the ad-hoc parsing the pattern removed comes back.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2164.4" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Template-conformance rate on inputs — fraction of optimised prompts that match the declared template structure&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Response-shape conformance rate — fraction of post-processed outputs the consumer accepts without further parsing&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Goal-alignment regression — sample-audited rate at which template rewriting strips context the user meant to convey&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Inter-template behaviour drift — variance in agent behaviour across template versions for the same intent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Consumer-side parser complexity — lines of ad-hoc parsing each consumer still needs; should trend to zero&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2012.4" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://api.python.langchain.com/en/latest/prompts/langchain_core.prompts.prompt.PromptTemplate.html&quot;&gt;LangChain prompt templates&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Practitioners author and reuse prompt templates as a runtime construct.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/prompt-management.html&quot;&gt;Amazon Bedrock prompt management&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Bedrock Prompt management lets users create reusable prompt templates with variables, alternative variants, and versioning.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cloud.google.com/dialogflow&quot;&gt;Google Dialogflow&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Generators allow users to specify agent behaviours and responses at runtime.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2384.4" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Prompt Versioning&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dynamic Scaffolding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Structured Output&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;DSPy Signatures&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Passive Goal Creator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Proactive Goal Creator&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2270.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jss.2024.112278&quot;&gt;Agent design pattern catalogue: A collection of architectural patterns for foundation model based agents&lt;/a&gt; — Yue Liu, Sin Kit Lo, Qinghua Lu, Liming Zhu, Dehai Zhao, Xiwei Xu, Stefan Harrer, Jon Whittle, 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2604.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
