        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;API1#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.49;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m18">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.49;entryY=0;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:B-&gt;API2#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m19">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m8">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:C-&gt;API3#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.49;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m20">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.49;entryY=0;" target="m9">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:D-&gt;API4#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m21">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m10">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:E-&gt;APIn#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m22">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m11">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Select the model and provider for a request through a single namespaced string (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt;) backed by env-var credentials, so the caller specifies what to run with one parameter rather than a typed provider object.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="761.48" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building an application that needs to talk to several language-model providers and many model variants — OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI, OpenRouter, and others — possibly choosing between them on a per-request basis for cost lanes, experiments, or tenant-specific routing. The application is otherwise model-agnostic; it does not need to depend on the typed object hierarchy of any one provider&#39;s software development kit. The team controls the call sites where each model invocation happens.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="761.48" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;When the call site is written as a typed provider object such as &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;OpenAI(...)&lt;/font&gt; or &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anthropic(...)&lt;/font&gt;, the provider becomes part of the application&#39;s source code and switching between them requires conditional construction at every call site. Per-request, per-tenant, or per-experiment routing across providers turns into a tangle of imports and adapter classes, and adding a new provider means another typed branch wherever models are invoked. The application ends up coupled to provider SDK shapes that have no business in its core logic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="886.48" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string is the cheapest possible call-site signature for cross-provider routing.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Env-var-driven credentials let the deployment pick keys without code changes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability differences across providers (tool calls, structured output, vision, max-context) must still be discoverable at runtime.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-call provider selection lets experiments, A/B routing, and cost lanes share a single call site.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; String-typed identifiers lose compile-time checking of valid combinations.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="943.48" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: take a single &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string at the call site, resolve credentials from environment, and dispatch through a provider-agnostic interface, so that swapping providers is a string change rather than a typed-object change.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1068.48" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a unified language-model interface and a registry of providers keyed by short prefix (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;openai/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;anthropic/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;google/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;xai/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;openrouter/...&lt;/font&gt;). Each provider implementation knows how to read its credentials from environment variables. The call site takes a single string (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;&#39;anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6&#39;&lt;/font&gt;) and the runtime resolves provider, credentials, and capability flags. Pair with provider-fallback (chain strings for resilience), multi-model-routing (pick a string by quality/cost), and vendor-lock-in (this is its mirror — the un-locked version).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1144.48" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Call site → `generate(model=&amp;#x27;provider/model&amp;#x27;, ...)` → ProviderRegistry → ProviderAdapter → upstream API.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1193.48" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team builds an agent that should route easy tasks to a cheap small model, hard tasks to a frontier model, and a long-context task to a third provider entirely. With a typed provider object hierarchy, each lane needs its own client construction and credential plumbing. The team switches to provider-string routing: the agent receives a &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;model&lt;/font&gt; string (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;&#39;openai/gpt-5-mini&#39;&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;&#39;anthropic/claude-opus-4-7&#39;&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;&#39;google/gemini-2.5-pro&#39;&lt;/font&gt;) and the registry handles credentials and capability discovery. Adding a new provider for one experiment is a string change plus an env-var.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1326.48" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Switching provider is a string change.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-call experiments and A/B routing share a single call site.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Configuration moves out of code into environment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composable with provider-fallback and multi-model-routing without further abstraction.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; String typing loses compile-time checking of valid provider/model combinations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-provider capability gaps must be discoverable at runtime, not at type-check time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misspelled identifiers fail at runtime rather than at edit time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credential rotation depends on the env-var convention being consistent across providers.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1299.48" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Application code is not allowed to import provider-specific SDK classes at call sites; all model invocations must go through the &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string interface and the central registry.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1508.48" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The application targets multiple providers and may change the mix over time.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-call routing (experiments, A/B, cost lanes) shares a single call site.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credentials are managed by environment, not by application code.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A central capability registry is acceptable to track which providers support which features.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1614.48" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The application is single-provider with no realistic switch in the planning horizon.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compile-time guarantees on valid model identifiers are essential and a typed enum is preferred.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The provider exposes features that the unified spec cannot represent and the team accepts the lock-in for them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1614.48" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Provider registry — keyed by short prefix (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;openai/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;anthropic/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;google/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;xai/&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;openrouter/&lt;/font&gt;)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider adapter — per-provider class that translates the unified call into the upstream API&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credential resolver — reads provider-specific env vars at adapter instantiation time&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability flags — runtime descriptor (tool calls, structured output, vision, context window) per model&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unified call site — single &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;generate(model=&#39;provider/model&#39;, ...)&lt;/font&gt; entry point all code must use&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1758.48" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Mastra, Vercel AI SDK, or LiteLLM — existing implementations of the unified model interface&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Environment configuration store — dotenv, AWS Secrets Manager, or HashiCorp Vault holding provider keys&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability catalog — JSON or YAML file mapping model strings to supported features&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1758.48" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Runtime typo — a misspelled &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string passes code review and fails only when that path is first called in production.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability mismatch — a string is switched to a model that lacks tool calls or structured output, and the call site breaks because nothing checked capability flags first.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credential convention gap — one provider reads a differently named env var, so a rotated key is picked up by some adapters and not others.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; SDK leak — a call site imports a provider SDK class directly for a special feature, and the single routing interface stops being the only path.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1940.48" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Provider-switch effort — lines changed to move a workload from one provider to another (target: a string)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Call-site SDK-import count — direct imports of provider SDKs that bypass the registry (target zero)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misspelled-identifier failure rate at runtime — gap left by losing compile-time checking&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability-mismatch incidents — production errors where a model was called for a feature it does not support&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider mix in production — share of traffic per provider as evidence the abstraction is exercised&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1902.48" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastra.ai/models&quot;&gt;Mastra (provider/model string across 4000+ models)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Mastra exposes a single &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string for selection across 120+ providers; credentials and capability flags resolve at the registry level.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/foundations/providers-and-models&quot;&gt;Vercel AI SDK&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Standardised language-model specification abstracts provider differences so the same call site addresses any provider.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.litellm.ai/&quot;&gt;LiteLLM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — OpenAI-shaped proxy over 100+ providers, addressed by &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; style strings.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2160.48" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Model Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Provider Fallback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Vendor Lock-In&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Translation Layer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Unified Voice Interface&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Complexity-Based Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Serving-Stack Attestation&lt;/b&gt; — The provider/model string is the claim this pattern tests; routing by string makes the claim easy to write and makes verifying it necessary.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
