          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Require multiple consecutive ticks (or runs) to agree before a mutation to durable state lands.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="996.7" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team runs a long-running agent that is allowed to propose changes to its own durable state — its persistent rules, its memory entries, its operating preferences. Over time the agent revises these to fit how the user actually behaves. Some of those proposed changes come from a single frustrated moment in a single conversation, and the agent has no built-in way to tell a passing reaction apart from a genuine long-term preference.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="996.7" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If a proposed mutation lands on a single tick&#39;s say-so, then a momentary misreading — a user vented once, the agent overinterpreted a single sentence, a transient confusion in context — becomes a permanent rule that degrades the agent for weeks. If the team simply disables self-mutation to avoid this, the agent stops learning from real signals and the operator has to hand-edit every rule change. Without a way to require multiple consecutive endorsements before a mutation lands, single-tick confusion gets baked into durable state.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1088.7" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; More ticks = slower change; legitimate improvements are delayed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Coordination across ticks needs a proposal / approval state machine.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User override should always be available for legitimate fast paths.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1159.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: hold each proposed mutation in escrow until K consecutive ticks re-endorse it against fresh context, so that single-tick confusion cannot land as durable state.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1270.7" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Mutation proposals are written to a holding area. A subsequent tick must confirm the proposal (still endorses it given fresh context). After K consecutive confirms, the mutation lands. Explicit user approval bypasses the wait.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1284.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Propose mutation --&amp;gt; Holding area --tick confirms (fresh context)--&amp;gt; ... --K consecutive confirms--&amp;gt; Write to durable state; any tick disagrees --&amp;gt; Dropped; explicit user approval --&amp;gt; Write immediately&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1376.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent reads a frustrated user message and proposes a new persistent rule: &#39;never offer suggestions before being asked.&#39; Under single-tick mutation the rule would land immediately and degrade the agent for weeks. Instead the proposal goes to a holding area; the next tick re-reads the rule against fresh context and the user&#39;s later message (&#39;actually keep proposing, I just hated that one&#39;) and declines to confirm. The mutation expires unwritten. Only rules that survive K consecutive endorsements join the durable charter.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1409.7" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reduces transient-confusion mutations.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Surfaces hesitation: K-1 confirms then a withdrawal is itself signal.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency on legitimate changes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Implementation complexity in the agent&#39;s state machine.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1501.7" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A mutation cannot land on a single tick&#39;s say-so; it requires K consecutive endorsements.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1591.7" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Durable state changes must not capture single-tick confusion.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mutation proposals can be held until subsequent ticks confirm them.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Explicit user approval is available as a bypass for urgent edits.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1740.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Mutations are cheap to revert and the quorum delay just slows learning.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has no durable state worth protecting.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Single-tick edits with diff review already meet the safety bar.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1683.7" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Mutation proposer — agent path that drafts a change to durable state&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Holding area — escrow store for proposals awaiting subsequent-tick endorsement&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quorum state machine — tracker that advances proposals through K confirmation states&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Endorsement check — re-reads each proposal against fresh context on later ticks&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User-override path — explicit fast-path bypassing the wait for urgent edits&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1865.7" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Durable proposal store — keyed by proposal id with confirmation counter and expiry&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tick scheduler — runs the re-endorsement step at defined cadence&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1808.7" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Slow legitimate change — a real preference waits K ticks to land, and the agent keeps the old behaviour the user already corrected.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Echo confirmation — each later tick reads the pending proposal and endorses it from the same stale context, so the quorum adds no independent check.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lost proposal — a state-machine bug drops pending proposals on restart, and neither the mutation nor its rejection is recorded.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2028.7" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Transient-mutation rejection rate — share of single-tick proposals dropped before landing&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quorum-induced latency on legitimate changes — extra ticks before landing an improvement&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hesitation signal frequency — K-1 confirms followed by a withdrawal, useful as its own data&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Durable-state-degradation incidents avoided — rules that would have landed under single-tick&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1914.7" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.safe.global/advanced/smart-account-overview&quot;&gt;Safe (Safe Smart Account multisig)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Requires signatures from at least a threshold of owners before a transaction (mutation) executes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/aetos53t/agent-multisig-api&quot;&gt;Quorum (multi-agent wallet coordination; hosted service retired)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;deprecated&lt;/i&gt; — Threshold approval (2-of-2, 2-of-3, 3-of-5) of agent signatures before an action executes. The hosted service (quorumclaw.com) no longer resolves; the source repository remains the citable record.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2210.7" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Constitutional Charter&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Modification Diff Gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;World-Model Separation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Race Conditions on Shared Tool Resources&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Edit Critic Gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Epistemic Fault-Domain Quorum&lt;/b&gt; — Sets how many endorsements a mutation needs before it lands; this pattern asks how many distinct upstream roots those endorsements descend from.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2058.7" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://lamport.azurewebsites.net/pubs/byz.pdf&quot;&gt;The Byzantine Generals Problem&lt;/a&gt; — Lamport, Shostak, Pease, 1982&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2430.7" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
