        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="drop all reasoning_content" mermaidId="e:Reply-&gt;NextUserTurn#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="drop all reasoning_content" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=#E8E8E88D;fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:NextUserTurn-&gt;root_end#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=classic;endSize=9;fillColor=none;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;For reasoning models that emit a separate reasoning trace, preserve that trace in context across the same logical task episode (across tool-call/result turns) but drop it at user-turn boundaries.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="967.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is using a reasoning-capable model (for example one of the OpenAI o-series, Claude with extended thinking, or DeepSeek-R1) that returns the model&#39;s chain-of-thought in a separate reasoning_content field, distinct from the user-visible content. The agent runs in a tool-use loop with multi-turn history: the model reasons, calls a tool, sees the result, reasons again, possibly answers, and then a new user message starts the next turn.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="967.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Two failure modes pull in opposite directions. If the reasoning trace is dropped between a tool call and its result, the model loses the thread of why it called the tool in the first place, and the next reasoning step starts from a degraded context. If the reasoning trace is instead preserved across user-turn boundaries, conversation history bloats with stale reasoning from earlier tasks and the next user message inherits irrelevant prior thinking that pollutes its own reasoning. Neither &#39;always carry forward&#39; nor &#39;always drop&#39; is correct; the team needs a rule keyed to where in the loop the trace appears.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1073.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning trace is the bridge between tool-call intent and post-tool-result interpretation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning trace is private intermediate state, not conversational record.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tokens are expensive; preserving traces forever costs money.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale reasoning leaks bias into the next task.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1130.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: preserve assistant reasoning_content across tool turns within a single user-to-user episode and drop it at the next user boundary, so that tool calls and their interpretations stay coherent without leaking stale reasoning into the next task.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1274.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define an episode as: from one user turn to the next user turn (inclusive of all intervening tool calls and tool results). Within an episode, preserve assistant reasoning_content as part of the context concatenation across all turns. At the next user turn boundary, drop reasoning_content from prior episodes (the API silently ignores it when passed across boundaries). The user-visible content remains in history; only the reasoning trace is episode-scoped.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1274.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;User -&amp;gt; [reasoning + tool_call] -&amp;gt; tool_result -&amp;gt; [reasoning + tool_call] -&amp;gt; tool_result -&amp;gt; [reasoning + final_content] -&amp;gt; User. Within episode: preserve reasoning. Across episodes: drop reasoning, keep content.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1399.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent built on a reasoning model debugs flaky CI by calling a log-fetch tool. Without trace carry-forward, the model emits its hidden reasoning, calls the tool, then on the result turn the reasoning is dropped and it forgets why it asked for those logs and re-derives from scratch, sometimes incorrectly. The team scopes an episode from one user turn to the next and preserves reasoning_content across all intervening tool calls, dropping it only at the next user turn. Tool-result interpretations stop drifting and token usage stays bounded.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1437.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool-using episodes get the benefit of CoT continuity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-turn dialogues do not accumulate stale reasoning.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cheaper than naive reasoning-trace preservation forever.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Episode boundary detection has to be encoded in the agent loop, not the model.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; If the model expects its own past reasoning at a later turn, dropping it breaks that.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider-specific (DeepSeek-style reasoning_content); needs adaptation per API.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1524.25" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Internal reasoning content may not cross user-task boundaries; only user-visible content persists in conversation history.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1619.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The model is a reasoning model that emits a separate reasoning trace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Within an episode (one user turn through tool calls and results), reasoning context must persist.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning traces should be dropped at user-turn boundaries to avoid stale carryover.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1801.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The model does not produce a separable reasoning trace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The provider already manages reasoning persistence across turns automatically.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stateless single-turn use cases that do not span tool-call cycles.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1725.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning-capable model — emits user-visible content and a separable reasoning_content field per assistant turn&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Episode boundary detector — agent-loop rule that marks each user turn as the start of a new episode&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Context concatenator — assembles the next call&#39;s history, including or excluding reasoning_content per the episode rule&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning store (in-memory) — holds episode-local reasoning_content until the next user-turn boundary drops it&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider adapter — translates the rule to the specific API (DeepSeek reasoning_content, Anthropic thinking blocks, o-series)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1926.25" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning-model API — DeepSeek thinking mode, Anthropic extended thinking, or OpenAI o-series with reasoning surfaces&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tokeniser — used to budget the additional cost of carrying reasoning across tool turns&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1850.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Misplaced boundary — the loop treats a tool result as a new user turn, drops the reasoning, and the next step forgets why the tool was called.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Boundary leak — prior-episode reasoning is passed along at a user turn, and the new task inherits stale thinking.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Expected reasoning gone — a later turn refers back to a past decision whose reasoning was dropped, and the model reconstructs it wrongly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider mismatch — the carry-forward rule is ported to another API that handles the reasoning field differently, and traces are lost or rejected.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2184.25" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tool-result interpretation accuracy — correctness of the post-tool reasoning step with vs without carry-forward&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-episode contamination rate — sampled cases where prior-episode reasoning leaked into a new user task&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning-token cost per episode — additional tokens consumed by carrying reasoning across tool turns&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Boundary-detection precision — fraction of user-turn boundaries the loop correctly identifies for the drop step&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider portability — pass rate of the same agent loop across reasoning APIs from different vendors&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1975.25" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/thinking_mode&quot;&gt;DeepSeek API (thinking mode)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Documented behaviour: pass reasoning_content back across tool-call turns; drop it across user turns.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2404.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Extended Thinking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Window Packing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Short-Term Thread Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Prompt Caching&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Trajectory-Summary Test-Time Scaling&lt;/b&gt; — Carry-forward keeps a single trace within an episode; this carries a summary of a whole rollout across attempts for sequential scaling.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2233.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
