        <UserObject label="peer better" mermaidId="e:Reason-&gt;Hand#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.75;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="peer better" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.75;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="787.3" y="644.8" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="refreshes" mermaidId="e:Eval-&gt;Self#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.8;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="refreshes" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.8;entryY=0;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="613.7" y="292.95" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Agent maintains an explicit self-model of its own capabilities, confidence and limitations, and reasons over that model when accepting / refusing / handing off tasks.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="826.2" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team has an agent. The default agent accepts whatever task it is given and proceeds. There is no explicit self-model — the agent does not represent &#39;what I am good at&#39; or &#39;what I should refuse&#39;.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="826.2" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Without an explicit self-model, the agent has no principled way to refuse tasks outside its competence or hand off to a more suitable peer. Refusals are ad-hoc, based on prompt-level instructions that are inconsistent across calls. Differs from confidence-reporting (which is per-output) by making the self-model an &lt;i&gt;input&lt;/i&gt; to decision-making, not just an output.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="932.2" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Maintaining an explicit self-model requires upfront capability characterization.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model drift — the agent&#39;s actual capabilities change with model updates.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning over a self-model adds a step to every decision.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="932.2" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: the agent carries an explicit, structured self-model (capabilities, confidence calibrations, declared limitations); decision logic reasons over the self-model before accepting a task — accept, refuse, or hand off.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1076.2" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Self-model is a structured artifact: {capabilities: [...], confidence-by-task-class: {...}, declared-limitations: [...]}. At task acceptance, agent reasons over self-model: does this task fall in my capabilities? what&#39;s my confidence for this class? are any declared limitations triggered? Output: accept / refuse-with-reason / handoff-to-peer-with-capability-X. Self-model refreshed periodically against eval-suite results. Pair with confidence-reporting, decentralized-swarm-handoff, refusal, typed-refusal-codes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1057.2" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Incoming task --&amp;gt; Self-model {capabilities, confidence by task class, declared limitations} --&amp;gt; reason: in capability? confidence? limitation triggered? --&amp;gt; {accept | refuse with reason | hand off to peer with capability X}; Eval suite -.periodic refresh.-&amp;gt; Self-model&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1201.2" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research agent&#39;s self-model: {capabilities: [literature-search, summarization], confidence: {medical-research: 0.6, legal-research: 0.3}, limitations: [no-citation-verification]}. Asked a legal-research question, the agent consults self-model, sees 0.3 confidence, refuses-with-reason and hands off to a legal-specialist peer. Without self-model, the agent would have attempted and produced low-quality output.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1239.2" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Principled refusals and handoffs based on declared self-model.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model as a versionable artifact, not implicit prompt behavior.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval-driven self-model updates — agent&#39;s known capabilities track measured reality.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Upfront capability characterization is work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model drift if not refreshed against evals.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning over self-model adds a step to every task-acceptance.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1345.2" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent does not accept tasks without consulting its self-model; the self-model is an explicit artifact, not implicit prompt behavior.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1402.2" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent operates in a domain where competence boundaries are clear.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Handoff to peer agents is feasible.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval suite can refresh self-model periodically.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1622.2" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Single general-purpose agent with no peers to hand off to.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability boundaries are not characterizable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No eval suite to refresh self-model.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1508.2" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model artifact — structured capability/confidence/limitation record&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model reasoner — decides accept/refuse/handoff&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Refusal-with-reason emitter — structured refusal output&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Handoff mechanism — to peer with matching capability&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model refresher — eval-driven updates&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1747.2" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model artifact (capability/confidence/limitation registry)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model reasoner&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Refusal/handoff emitter&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1633.2" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stale self-model — the model behind the agent is upgraded, but the self-model is not refreshed against evals, so the agent refuses tasks it can now handle.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Overconfident class — confidence for a task class is set from a narrow eval, and the agent accepts work it will fail.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bypassed check — a fast path accepts tasks without consulting the self-model, and refusals become ad-hoc again.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Handoff to nowhere — the agent hands off to a peer with capability X that does not exist or is not reachable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1910.2" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Refusal rate — out-of-scope task detection&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Handoff success rate to capable peer&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-model accuracy — eval-measured vs declared capability&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1758.2" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.joakimvivas.com/tech/17-patrones-arquitecturas-agenticas-ia/&quot;&gt;Joakim Vivas: 17 Patrones de Arquitecturas Agénticas de IA (Reflexive Metacognitive)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2130.2" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Confidence Reporting&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Decentralized Swarm Handoff&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Refusal&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Typed Refusal Codes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Awareness&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Subject-First Agent Architecture (ENA Stateful Core)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;False Confidence Syndrome&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Confidence-Checking Workflow&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Over-Helpfulness&lt;/b&gt; — An explicit self-model lets the agent consult its own capabilities before accepting a task, removing the answer-anyway default.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Advisor Consult&lt;/b&gt; — The advisor&#39;s value depends on the executor knowing when it is out of its depth; an explicit self-model of competence gives it a better trigger than a nudge.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1883.2" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.joakimvivas.com/tech/17-patrones-arquitecturas-agenticas-ia/&quot;&gt;17 Patrones de Arquitecturas Agénticas de IA&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2236.2" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
