        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:J-&gt;W#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.2;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.2;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1326.95" y="621.08" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Rigor Relocation flow.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="698.85" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Relocate verification rigor from the model loop to surrounding scaffolding (evals, judges, decision logs, policy gates) so failures are caught by the wrapper rather than the agent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="773.85" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team has handed real code-writing work to coding agents. The keystrokes that used to carry the engineer&#39;s discipline — careful naming, defensive checks, hand-written tests — are now produced at a different speed and by a different author. Senior engineers worry that quality is collapsing; the productivity numbers say the opposite. Both can be true if nobody asks where the rigor went.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="773.85" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Treating agentic coding as if rigor itself were optional produces drift: undocumented conventions the agent re-invents each session, invariants that exist only in code review folklore, and verification that runs by hand when somebody remembers. The opposite mistake — preserving every prior practice unchanged — applies rigor at the wrong layer, so reviewers grade tokens the agent wrote on autopilot while the load-bearing decisions go unexamined. The team is forced to choose between performative discipline at the old layer and accepting that discipline has quietly left the building.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="879.85" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Engineering rigor does not vanish when a constraint is removed; it relocates to whichever surface still binds behaviour.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agents read context files, configs, and tests far more reliably than they read human folklore.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Verification cost falls as compute gets cheap, so &#39;check it every time&#39; becomes affordable where &#39;check it once at review&#39; used to be the cap.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="917.85" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: name the new surfaces — agent context files, machine-enforced invariants, continuous evaluation — and move each prior rigor practice deliberately to whichever of those surfaces now binds the agent&#39;s behaviour, so discipline migrates up the stack instead of being abandoned.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1061.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Identify, for each existing rigor practice, which agent-readable surface now carries it, and relocate it there. Three concrete relocations: (a) tacit conventions and architecture decisions move into the agent&#39;s context file (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, system prompt) so they are read every session, not learned once by a human; (b) hand-enforced invariants move into machine-enforced rules — types, assertions, schema validators, policy-as-code gates — so they bind every generated change, not only the reviewed ones; (c) periodic verification moves into continuous evaluation — eval-as-contract on every PR, agent-as-judge on trajectories, scorer-live-monitoring in production — so the bar is enforced on every change instead of every release. Pair with decision-log and provenance-ledger so the relocations are auditable.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1080.85" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Rigor practice once inside the agent loop --&amp;gt; Relocation map --&amp;gt; (tacit conventions --&amp;gt; context file | hand-enforced invariants --&amp;gt; types, validators, policy gates | periodic checks --&amp;gt; continuous evaluation) --&amp;gt; Wrapper catches failures on every change; decision log + provenance ledger record each relocation; stale-rule detector --&amp;gt; context file&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1186.85" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team&#39;s senior engineer is alarmed that nobody is hand-writing argument validation anymore — the agent just generates the function and merges. Instead of forbidding agent-authored code, the team relocates the rigor: a CLAUDE.md rule says &#39;public functions take validated inputs and the agent must add the type or assertion that enforces it&#39;, a policy-as-code gate rejects PRs that introduce unchecked public entry points, and an eval-as-contract case fails closed if the validation is silently dropped. The senior&#39;s discipline is still in the codebase; it just lives on three new surfaces instead of in one human&#39;s habit.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1319.85" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Discipline survives the shift to agentic generation instead of degrading into review folklore.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Context files turn one-time onboarding into per-session enforcement.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Machine-enforced invariants catch deviations the human reviewer would miss in a 2000-line diff.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Continuous evaluation surfaces regressions on the change that caused them, not on the release that shipped them.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Authoring and maintaining context files is real engineering work, and stale context files actively mislead the agent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Machine-enforced invariants are only as good as the rules; missing rules produce a false sense of safety.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Continuous evaluation has cost and calibration overhead; bad evals fail loud and block legitimate work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Relocating the wrong practice (e.g. relocating taste to a linter) produces ritual without rigor.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1349.85" width="755" height="377" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Any rigor practice the team claims to hold must be expressible on a surface the agent reads or is checked against — context file, machine-enforced rule, or continuous evaluation. Practices that live only in human habit are not counted as rigor in agentic mode.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1520.85" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Code-writing work is materially handed to agents and prior rigor practices were tied to human keystrokes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Senior engineers can point to specific disciplines (invariant checks, naming, architecture decisions) that used to bind behaviour and now do not.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent-readable surfaces (context files, machine-enforced rules, continuous evals) exist or can be introduced.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1740.85" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent&#39;s role is narrow enough that prior review-time rigor still binds every change.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The team will not invest in maintaining context files and evaluations, in which case the relocation produces stale rigor instead of relocated rigor.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Practices being relocated are taste, not invariants; taste does not survive translation to a machine-checked rule.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1645.85" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent Context File — CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md / system prompt that carries conventions and architecture decisions the agent reads every session.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Machine-Enforced Invariants — types, assertions, schema validators, and policy-as-code gates that bind every generated change, not only reviewed ones.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Continuous Evaluation — eval-as-contract, agent-as-judge on trajectories, scorer-live-monitoring in production, run on every change.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Relocation Map — explicit register of which prior rigor practice now lives on which surface; what got relocated, what got retired.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale-Rule Detector — flags context-file rules contradicted by current code so the relocation does not silently rot.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1922.85" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Observability — logs, traces, and metrics that surface the pattern in production&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eval harness — runs that quantify the pattern&#39;s frequency or severity over time&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1808.85" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stale context file — the context file still describes last quarter&#39;s architecture, and the agent follows the outdated convention in every session.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing rule mistaken for safety — an invariant was never written as a validator or gate, yet the team assumes the machine checks cover it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Taste moved to a linter — a judgement call is reduced to a lint rule, and changes pass the rule while the design still gets worse.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unmapped retirement — an old review practice is dropped without being placed on any surface, and nothing in the relocation map shows it is gone.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2180.85" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Context-file coverage — share of recurring agent-behaviour mistakes prevented by a rule in the context file rather than caught at review.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Machine-enforced-invariant share — fraction of historical bug classes that now fail closed via types, assertions, or policy-as-code instead of human review.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Continuous-evaluation cadence — share of PRs (not releases) gated by eval-as-contract or agent-as-judge.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Relocation completeness — count of prior rigor practices explicitly assigned to a new surface versus left implicit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale-context-file rate — share of context-file rules contradicted by the codebase or by current architectural intent.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1914.85" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.honeycomb.io/blog/production-is-where-the-rigor-goes&quot;&gt;Honeycomb (Chad Fowler)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Original &#39;Relocating Rigor&#39; framing — control does not disappear, it moves closer to reality; if generation gets easier, judgment must get stricter.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://martinfowler.com/fragments/2026-01-22.html&quot;&gt;martinfowler.com fragments&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Martin Fowler endorses Chad Fowler&#39;s framing: AI-enabled development demands rigor in evaluating software rather than abandoning discipline for speed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://bjorn.now/link/2026-01-28-relocating-rigor-by-chad-fowler/&quot;&gt;bjorn.now (Björn Andersson)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Applies the concept to working with Claude on legacy code: tests before changes, intent specified as failing tests first, ruthless trace-the-call-sites verification before refactors.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://bits-bytes-nn.github.io/insights/agentic-ai/2026/04/05/evolution-of-ai-agentic-patterns-en.html&quot;&gt;Bits, Bytes and Neural Networks (Jonas Kim)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Frames the relocation across three eras — prompt engineering, context engineering, harness engineering — with rigor migrating up at each step.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kode24.no/&quot;&gt;kode24.no&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Norwegian-language application of Fowler&#39;s term to agentic coding with three concrete relocations: CLAUDE.md context files, deterministic constraints, continuous verification.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2400.85" width="755" height="358" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Spec-Driven Loop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Spec-First Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Eval as Contract&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Policy-as-Code Gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agentic Context Engineering Playbook&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Decision Log&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Provenance Ledger&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-as-a-Judge&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Scorer Live Monitoring&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Errors Swept Under the Rug&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Perma-Beta&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Automating a Broken Process&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agentic Skill Atrophy&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2172.85" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.honeycomb.io/blog/production-is-where-the-rigor-goes&quot;&gt;Production Is Where the Rigor Goes (Relocating Rigor)&lt;/a&gt; — Chad Fowler&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://martinfowler.com/fragments/2026-01-22.html&quot;&gt;Fragments: January 22&lt;/a&gt; — Martin Fowler, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://bjorn.now/link/2026-01-28-relocating-rigor-by-chad-fowler/&quot;&gt;Relocating Rigor by Chad Fowler&lt;/a&gt; — Björn Andersson, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://bits-bytes-nn.github.io/insights/agentic-ai/2026/04/05/evolution-of-ai-agentic-patterns-en.html&quot;&gt;From Prompts to Harnesses — Four Years of AI Agentic Patterns&lt;/a&gt; — Jonas Kim, 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2772.85" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="risk-averse-reward-proxy" name="Risk-Averse Reward Proxy">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1946.6697556866047" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="1946.6697556866047" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Risk-Averse Reward Proxy&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Safety &amp;amp; Control &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; experimental &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Goodhart-Robust Optimisation, IRD-Based Conservatism&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="275.67" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Context: in or out of design dist?" mermaidId="n:Ctx" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Context: in or out of design dist?" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="66.87" width="365.33" x="65.0" y="219.4" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="OOD?" mermaidId="n:OOD" mermaidBaseStyle="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="OOD?" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rhombus;html=1;strokeWidth=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="92.88" width="92.88" x="492.25" y="205.78" as="geometry" />
