        <UserObject label="reflection" mermaidId="e:Tick-&gt;Cfg#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.37;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="reflection" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.37;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="215.35" y="1018.35" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Cfg-&gt;Sc#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.63;exitY=0;entryX=0.62;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.63;exitY=0;entryX=0.62;entryY=1;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="379.65" y="1018.35" />
                <mxPoint x="379.65" y="922.25" />
                <mxPoint x="379.65" y="841.65" />
                <mxPoint x="379.65" y="761.05" />
                <mxPoint x="379.65" y="680.45" />
                <mxPoint x="379.65" y="599.85" />
                <mxPoint x="379.65" y="519.25" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Score every candidate memory item with a weighted salience function so each tick attends to a small, relevant top-k subset rather than re-reading all memory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1199.75" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running agent&#39;s memory store grows past what can fit into a single call&#39;s context. The agent has accumulated thoughts, summaries, insights, and observations over hours or days, and on every tick only a small, currently relevant slice of that store should drive the next step.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1199.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Without an explicit notion of salience, the agent has only two bad strategies. Dumping all of memory into context blows up the token budget and gives the model no focus on what matters now. Taking only the most recent items provides no continuity and misses anything older that has become relevant again because of a surprise in the current context. Recency alone misses the items that matter; bulk loading buries them in noise. The agent needs a way to score every candidate memory by how salient it is to the current moment and to surface only the top-scoring ones into context.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1305.75" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Recency, novelty, goal-relevance, and prediction error all matter, and they trade off.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Re-reading all memory each tick is unaffordable at scale.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Pure recency loses long-tail relevance; pure relevance loses temporal grounding.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rumination loops reward the same items over and over without a fatigue term.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1324.75" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: score each candidate memory by a weighted sum of novelty, goal-relevance, recency, prediction error, and fatigue and pick the top-k each tick, so that attention is bounded, tunable, and resistant to rumination loops.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1487.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Score each candidate memory item &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;m&lt;/font&gt; with a weighted sum: &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;alpha &lt;i&gt; novelty(m) + beta &lt;/i&gt; goal_relevance(m) + gamma &lt;i&gt; recency(m) + delta &lt;/i&gt; prediction_error(m) - epsilon * fatigue(m)&lt;/font&gt;. Pick the top-k into the working set for the next tick. Persist the weights in a tunable config so a reflection pass can adjust them. The fatigue term penalises items that have already been attended to many times in the recent window, breaking rumination loops.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1468.75" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Candidate memory items --salience score (novelty + goal + recency + prediction error - fatigue)--&amp;gt; Top-k --&amp;gt; Working set --&amp;gt; Next tick -.reflection.-&amp;gt; Tunable weights --&amp;gt; Salience score&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1612.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running personal agent has months of memory; dumping it all into context is impossible and grabbing the most recent items misses the user&#39;s recurring goals. The team scores each candidate memory with a weighted sum of novelty, goal-relevance, recency, prediction-error, and a fatigue penalty. Each tick attends to top-k items only. Surprising long-tail facts rise above last-hour chatter when they actually matter, and token usage per tick stays flat as memory grows.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1631.75" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bounded attention cost per tick regardless of memory store size.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Salience scores are inspectable and tunable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fatigue term breaks repetitive attention loops without manual intervention.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Weight tuning is empirical and per-deployment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A bad scoring function can suppress genuinely relevant items.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Salience scoring is itself work; it has to stay cheap to run every tick.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1737.75" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent cannot read its full memory store at every tick; salience scoring is mandatory and the top-k cap is enforced by the retrieval layer, not left to the model.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1794.75" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The persistent memory store is too large to read in full at every tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Memory items have features (recency, importance, frequency, similarity) that can be combined into a salience score.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent needs predictable per-tick read cost.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2014.75" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The memory is small enough to fully load every tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; All memory items are equally relevant and ranking adds noise rather than signal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Strict determinism is required and salience scores would change with every new write.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1900.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Candidate memory store — every item that could be considered for the next tick&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Salience scorer — weighted sum over novelty, goal-relevance, recency, prediction error, and a fatigue penalty&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Top-k selector — keeps only the highest-scoring items and enforces the bound at the retrieval layer, feeding the next-tick working set&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fatigue tracker — counts recent attends per item so loops cannot reward the same memory forever&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tunable weight config — persisted alpha/beta/gamma/delta/epsilon values a reflection pass can update&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2158.75" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Embedding model — produces vectors used by goal-relevance and novelty terms&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vector index — Chroma/FAISS over candidate memories for fast top-k lookup&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Importance-rating LLM call — assigns the importance term at write time per the Generative-Agents recipe&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2025.75" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Suppressed relevance — a poorly weighted score keeps a relevant old item below the top-k cut on every tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rumination — the fatigue weight is too low, and the same items win attention tick after tick.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Costly scoring — the scorer runs heavy work over every candidate each tick and becomes the bottleneck it was meant to avoid.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reflection overcorrection — the tuning pass swings the weights too far after a few ticks and attention becomes erratic.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2378.75" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Top-k precision — fraction of selected items the agent actually used downstream&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Recall@k of golden memories — proportion of held-out important items that surface in the top-k for matching cues&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-tick scoring cost — milliseconds and tokens spent scoring candidates&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rumination-suppression effect — drop in repeat attention to the same item once the fatigue term is enabled&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Weight-tuning stability — variance in answer quality as alpha/beta/gamma/delta/epsilon shift within plausible ranges&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2169.75" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot (author&amp;#x27;s long-running personal agent; single private deployment)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Per-tick salience scoring directs attention toward what matters most rather than processing everything uniformly. Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2579.75" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Summaries&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Vector Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Five-Tier Memory Cascade&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Window Packing&lt;/b&gt; — Different stage of the pipeline: salience selects what to consider; packing decides how much fits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Preoccupation Tracking&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Mode-Adaptive Cadence&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Axis Promotion Scoring&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Corpus Vocabulary&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2389.75" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.03442&quot;&gt;Generative Agents: Interactive Simulacra of Human Behavior&lt;/a&gt; — Park, O&#39;Brien, Cai, Morris, Liang, Bernstein, 2023&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11256080/&quot;&gt;Computational modelling of visual attention&lt;/a&gt; — Laurent Itti, Christof Koch, 2001&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2723.75" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
