        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Periodic mining derives a self-vocabulary; downstream scoring uses it as an additional axis alongside generic similarity.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="397.89" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Mine a small bounded vocabulary from the agent&#39;s own writing and cache it as the conceptual axis for scoring new thoughts, so relevance reflects the agent&#39;s actual frame rather than a generic embedding space.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="472.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A long-running agent accumulates a corpus of its own output: thought traces, insights, journal entries, notes. Some downstream component wants to score new thoughts for relevance, novelty, or kinship with the agent&#39;s existing concerns. The default tool is a generic embedding space, which gives a sensible answer about semantic similarity but tells the agent nothing about its own preoccupations — &#39;is the agent still pulling at the things it has been pulling at?&#39; is a different question from &#39;is this semantically close to the previous paragraph?&#39;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="472.89" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Generic embeddings score against the world&#39;s distribution of meaning, not the agent&#39;s. A new thought that lands inside the agent&#39;s persistent web of concerns can come back with the same similarity score as a perfectly off-topic but topically-adjacent one, because the embedding space has no notion of what this particular agent has been writing about for months. The result is a salience signal that is plausible-on-paper and indifferent in practice: the agent cannot tell, from the score alone, whether a thought is on its own line of inquiry or just somewhere in the same neighbourhood.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="597.89" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent&#39;s own corpus is the only source that knows its frame.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vocabularies that grow unbounded become a different problem (everything matches).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The vocabulary must refresh as the agent&#39;s frame shifts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mining must be cheap or it cannot run on a schedule.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Storage must survive across sessions, like the corpus it derives from.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="654.89" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: periodically mine a small top-N concept vocabulary from the agent&#39;s own thoughts and insights — using a mix of frontmatter tags and content frequency — cache it to disk, and refresh on a schedule, so scoring new thoughts can use this learned axis alongside generic similarity.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="779.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Run a periodic mining pass over the agent&#39;s own corpus (e.g. last N weeks of thoughts plus the long-term insight store). Aggregate frontmatter tags and content frequency to extract the top-N concept tokens with weights. Persist this vocabulary as a small JSON cache. Downstream scoring components consume the cache as an additional axis: a thought is scored both on generic embedding similarity to recent context and on overlap with the cached self-vocabulary. Refresh on a cadence proportional to corpus volatility (e.g. weekly for a stable agent, after every dream-consolidation cycle for a more volatile one).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="817.89" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Own corpus (thoughts + insights) --periodic mining (tags + content frequency)--&amp;gt; Top-N vocabulary cache; New thought --&amp;gt; Salience scorer &amp;lt;-- vocabulary cache + generic embedding similarity --&amp;gt; Own-frame score&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="904.89" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent has been journalling for three months. Once a week, a mining job aggregates frontmatter tags and high-frequency content tokens across recent thoughts and the long-term insight store, picks the top thirty concepts with weights, and writes them to a small JSON cache. When the agent receives a new thought, the salience scorer combines generic embedding distance to recent context with overlap against the cached vocabulary. A thought that uses three of the top-thirty concepts scores higher than a thought with similar embedding distance but no overlap, because the cached vocabulary says &#39;this is on the line of inquiry&#39;.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1018.89" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Relevance scoring becomes sensitive to the agent&#39;s own frame.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vocabulary changes are visible and auditable — operators can see what the agent is currently &#39;about&#39;.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Small footprint (top-N tokens) is cheap to load and use.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frame lock-in: a stale vocabulary reinforces what the agent already knows at the expense of new directions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mining is opinionated; tag-vs-frequency weighting is a tuning knob.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; If the corpus is too small the vocabulary is noisy.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1048.89" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Scoring components cannot use only the generic embedding space for own-frame relevance; the agent&#39;s learned vocabulary must be available as a separate axis so generic similarity does not displace own-frame fit.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1219.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent has an own-writing corpus large enough to mine (weeks of thoughts).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Downstream scoring needs an own-frame axis beyond generic similarity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Refresh cadence is feasible on the deployment&#39;s compute budget.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1363.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent is short-lived and has no accumulating corpus.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Generic semantic similarity is sufficient for the salience use case.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Strong frame lock-in would harm exploration more than it helps relevance.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1344.89" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Own-writing corpus — the agent&#39;s accumulated thoughts, insights, and journal entries, possibly with frontmatter tags&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mining pass — periodic job that aggregates tag frequency and content tokens to produce a top-N concept list with weights&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vocabulary cache — small JSON file holding the current top-N concepts plus their weights&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Refresh scheduler — runs the mining pass on a cadence tied to corpus volatility (weekly, post-consolidation, etc.)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Own-frame scorer — downstream component that blends generic embedding similarity with overlap against the cached vocabulary&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1488.89" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; TF-IDF or BM25 implementation — provides the term-specificity backbone of the frequency aggregation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Optional topic modeller — BERTopic or similar when frontmatter tags are too sparse to anchor the vocabulary&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; JSON file or small KV store — persists the cached vocabulary across sessions&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1469.89" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Frame lock-in — a stale vocabulary keeps scoring familiar topics high, and new directions never reach attention.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Noisy vocabulary — the corpus is too small, so the top-N tokens are chance words rather than real concerns.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tag skew — frontmatter tags are weighted too high, and the vocabulary reflects tagging habits instead of content.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missed refresh — the cache is not rebuilt after a large shift in writing, and scores lag behind what the agent now cares about.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1727.89" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Own-frame lift over generic similarity — labelled-set quality gain when the cached vocabulary is added as an axis&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vocabulary churn — fraction of tokens that change between refreshes; high churn flags an unstable frame, low churn flags lock-in&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Coverage on recent thoughts — fraction of new entries that overlap with at least one cached concept&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mining cost per refresh — wall-clock and compute spent generating the vocabulary&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Operator-audit signal — sampled human judgement on whether the cached vocabulary captures what the agent is currently &#39;about&#39;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1632.89" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Author&#39;s long-running personal agent (single private deployment)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Single-source evidence: one private deployment by the catalog author; no independently documented use yet.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1947.89" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Vector Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cluster-Capped Insight Store&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Salience Attention Mechanism&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dream Consolidation Cycle&lt;/b&gt; — Consolidation cycles are a natural place to refresh the vocabulary.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Semantic Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1871.89" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.emerald.com/insight/content/doi/10.1108/eb026526/full/html&quot;&gt;A statistical interpretation of term specificity and its application in retrieval&lt;/a&gt; — Karen Spärck Jones, 1972&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.05794&quot;&gt;BERTopic: Neural topic modeling with a class-based TF-IDF procedure&lt;/a&gt; — Maarten Grootendorst, 2022&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2053.89" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
