        <UserObject label="single settlement + reconciliation" mermaidId="e:W-&gt;A#2" mermaidBaseStyle="dashed=1;fixDash=1;dashPattern=3 3;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" mermaidBaseValue="single settlement + reconciliation" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="dashed=1;fixDash=1;dashPattern=3 3;endArrow=block;endSize=9;verticalAlign=bottom;spacingBottom=2;edgeStyle=sequenceEdgeStyle;libavoidRouting=0;curved=0;rounded=0;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=none;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="421.5" y="911.4" />
              </Array>
              <mxPoint x="660.2" y="911.4" as="sourcePoint" />
              <mxPoint x="181.25" y="911.4" as="targetPoint" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;The session cap is the safety envelope: the agent streams micropayments freely under it and settles once on close.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1049.15" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Bound an agent&#39;s autonomous spending by having it open a payment session with a pre-approved cap, stream many micropayments inside that session, and settle once on close, instead of seeking approval for every transaction.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1124.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent transacts with paid services on a user&#39;s behalf — calling metered APIs, buying compute, paying other agents for sub-results. Each individual charge is tiny and frequent, so a human approval per transaction is impossible, but unbounded autonomous spend is unacceptable. Emerging agent-payment protocols — x402 (HTTP-402 stablecoin settlement), AP2 (Agent Payments Protocol), and ACP (Agentic Commerce Protocol) — give agents the rails to pay; the open question is how to cap the risk.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1124.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Per-transaction human approval does not scale to an agent making hundreds of micropayments a minute, but handing the agent an open-ended wallet exposes the user to runaway or adversarial spend. The system needs a unit of authorization larger than one transaction yet bounded enough that a compromised or looping agent cannot drain funds.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1249.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Micropayments are too frequent for per-transaction human approval.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An open-ended wallet exposes the user to runaway or malicious spend.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A cap that is too tight stalls legitimate work mid-session; too loose and it is no protection.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement and reconciliation want to happen once, not per micropayment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent, the wallet, and the paid service are separate trust domains that must agree on the cap.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1287.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: make the session the unit of authorization — pre-approve a spend cap when the session opens, let the agent stream micropayments freely under that cap, and settle and reconcile once when it closes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1393.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Introduce a session as the authorization boundary for spend. When the agent begins a paid workflow, it opens a session and the wallet (or a governance layer) pre-authorizes a maximum amount and possibly a time-to-live. Inside the session the agent streams micropayments to services without further approval, each debited against the remaining cap; when the cap is reached the session blocks or escalates. On completion the session closes and settles once, reconciling the streamed payments. The cap, TTL, and per-recipient limits are the safety envelope; the agent&#39;s freedom exists only inside it. This is the session model emerging in machine-payment protocols layered over x402, AP2, and ACP.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1450.15" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent opens session -&amp;gt; wallet pre-authorizes cap (+ TTL, per-recipient limits) -&amp;gt; agent streams micropayments under cap -&amp;gt; cap exhausted? block/escalate -&amp;gt; session close -&amp;gt; single settlement + reconciliation.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1518.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A shopping agent is told to assemble a parts list under a $200 budget. It opens a payment session pre-authorized to $200, then streams small payments to a dozen catalog and pricing APIs as it researches, each debited against the cap. When it has spent $187 it stops querying paid sources and reports back; the session closes and settles once, and even if the agent had looped, it could never have spent past the $200 it was granted.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1651.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Autonomous micropayment streams run without per-transaction human approval.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Worst-case loss is bounded by the session cap, not the wallet balance.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement and reconciliation happen once per session, not per payment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Caps, TTL, and per-recipient limits give graded control over autonomy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A cap set too high still permits significant loss before it trips.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mid-session cap exhaustion can strand a half-finished task.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Session state and pre-authorization add protocol complexity across trust domains.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A compromised agent can still spend up to the full cap before detection.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reconciliation disputes are harder to unwind after a single bulk settlement.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1662.15" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent must not initiate a payment that would take cumulative session spend over the pre-authorized cap, and must not transact outside an open, authorized session. When the cap is reached it must stop and escalate rather than seek funds elsewhere.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1814.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent makes frequent micropayments that cannot each be human-approved.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; You need a hard ceiling on autonomous spend per workflow.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement is cheaper or cleaner done once per session than per payment.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The payment rails support pre-authorization and held caps (x402, AP2, ACP).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1996.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Spend is rare enough that per-transaction approval is fine.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Each payment is large and warrants individual human sign-off.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No payment protocol in use supports session pre-authorization.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A single global budget already bounds the agent and per-session granularity adds no safety.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1939.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Session manager — opens and closes the authorization boundary and tracks remaining cap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Pre-authorization step — the wallet or governance layer that sets the cap, TTL, and per-recipient limits&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Micropayment streamer — issues the in-session payments debited against the cap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cap enforcer — blocks or escalates when cumulative spend reaches the limit&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement and reconciliation — the single end-of-session clearing of streamed payments&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2140.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Payment protocol — x402, AP2, or ACP rails that carry the pre-authorization and the micropayments&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent wallet — TEE/MPC or smart-contract-controlled wallet that holds and releases funds under the cap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ledger — records streamed payments for end-of-session reconciliation and audit&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2083.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Full-cap drain — a compromised or looping agent spends right up to the session cap before anyone notices.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stranded task — the cap runs out mid-session, payments stop, and the workflow is left half done with costs already paid.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hard dispute — one bulk settlement bundles hundreds of micropayments, and a single wrong charge is hard to find and reverse.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2322.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Cap-breach attempts — payments blocked for exceeding the session cap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Loss bound adherence — sampled sessions where spend stayed within the authorized cap&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stall rate — tasks stranded by mid-session cap exhaustion&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settlement reconciliation error rate — discrepancies found at end-of-session clearing&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2227.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/coinbase/x402&quot;&gt;x402 (Coinbase)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Open protocol for agent payments over HTTP 402 that the session/streaming models layer on to authorize and settle agent spend.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/google-agentic-commerce/AP2&quot;&gt;Agent Payments Protocol (AP2, Google)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Defines mandates and authorization scopes for agent-initiated payments, the substrate a session cap is expressed against.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://zenn.dev/komlock_lab/articles/agent-payments-stack-2026&quot;&gt;AIエージェント決済の6層構造 (Zenn)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Describes the session model: the agent opens a session, pre-approves a spending limit, streams micropayments within it, and settles at session close.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2504.15" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-Initiated Payment&lt;/b&gt; — Agent-initiated payment is the general capability; session-scoped authorization specialises it by making a capped session, not a single charge, the unit of approval.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Step Budget&lt;/b&gt; — Step-budget bounds compute steps; a session cap bounds money. Both are exhaustible envelopes around autonomy.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Circuit Breaker&lt;/b&gt; — A circuit-breaker halts on an error or anomaly signal; the session cap halts on cumulative spend. Together they bound both failure and cost.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Credential Vault&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Risk-Tiered Action Autonomy&lt;/b&gt; — Payment authorization is a high-materiality action that lands in the release tier.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Refund Threshold Drift&lt;/b&gt; — A session cap is the static spending control; this is the failure where the effective cap drifts above it over time through accommodation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Blanket-Authorization Accountability Rupture&lt;/b&gt; — Session-scoped authorization bounds a grant to a capped session; blanket authorization is the unbounded standing grant whose harm has no clear owner.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Verifiable Purchase Mandate&lt;/b&gt; — Session scoping bounds how much the agent may spend; the mandate proves the user authorised the spend in the first place — bound and proof are orthogonal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cumulative Disclosure Accounting&lt;/b&gt; — The same session-budget mechanism applied to money: a pre-authorised cap spent down by many small actions, escalating when exhausted.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2371.15" width="755" height="415" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/coinbase/x402&quot;&gt;x402: an open protocol for internet-native payments&lt;/a&gt; — Coinbase, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/google-agentic-commerce/AP2&quot;&gt;Agent Payments Protocol (AP2)&lt;/a&gt; — Google, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://zenn.dev/komlock_lab/articles/agent-payments-stack-2026&quot;&gt;エージェントが払う仕組み — AIエージェント決済の6層構造&lt;/a&gt; — komlock_lab, 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2724.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
