        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:edit-&gt;diff#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:diff-&gt;ok#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="yes" mermaidId="e:ok-&gt;promote#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.87;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="yes" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.87;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="226.2" y="1044.7" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="no" mermaidId="e:ok-&gt;discard#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.87;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="no" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.87;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="595.1" y="1044.7" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;The agent edits a checkpointed shadow; only accepted diffs are promoted to the real tree.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1187.1" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Mirror the workspace into an isolated, version-controlled shadow where the agent makes and reverts edits, surfacing diffs for review and promoting only accepted changes to the real tree.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1262.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An autonomous coding agent edits files in a developer&#39;s working tree. It needs to experiment — try an edit, run tests, back out, try another — and it gets things wrong. Editing the real tree in place means a bad run can corrupt uncommitted work, and there is no clean per-edit history to review or revert.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1262.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent that writes straight to the working tree gives the human no safe boundary: a wrong edit overwrites real work, a multi-step change is hard to review as a whole, and undoing one step without losing the others is fiddly. The agent needs room to make and unmake edits freely, while the human keeps a reviewable, revertible record and the real tree stays clean until changes are accepted.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1368.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent must experiment and recover from bad edits, but direct writes to the real tree risk corrupting the developer&#39;s uncommitted work.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-edit rollback and whole-change review need a version history, yet maintaining a parallel copy costs disk and bookkeeping.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The shadow must track the real tree closely enough that promoting accepted changes is clean, not a merge nightmare.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1406.1" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: keep the agent&#39;s edits in a version-controlled shadow of the workspace (a per-task checkpoint repo or an in-memory overlay), expose diffs for review and per-step rollback, and promote only accepted changes to the real tree.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1512.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Mirror the working tree into a shadow the agent edits instead of the real files — commonly a per-task hidden git repository that checkpoints every edit, or an in-memory overlay that tracks modifications without writing to disk. Each agent edit becomes a diff the human can inspect, and any step can be rolled back to a prior checkpoint without disturbing the others. When the change is accepted it is promoted to the real working tree; if rejected, the shadow is discarded and the real tree is untouched.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1588.1" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;real tree --mirror--&amp;gt; shadow (agent edits, checkpointed) --diffs--&amp;gt; review -&amp;gt; accept: promote to real tree | reject: discard shadow&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1637.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A coding agent refactors a module across eight files. It works in a hidden checkpoint repo that snapshots each edit, so when step six breaks the build the developer rolls back just that step instead of the whole run. Once the diff looks right the agent promotes the change to the real working tree; had it looked wrong, discarding the shadow would have left the original files exactly as they were.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1770.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A bad agent edit can never corrupt the developer&#39;s working tree; the real files change only on accept.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Every edit is a reviewable diff and any step can be rolled back independently.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent can experiment freely, which makes recovery from a wrong path cheap.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Maintaining a parallel shadow costs disk and synchronisation bookkeeping.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; If the shadow drifts from the real tree, promoting accepted changes turns into a merge problem.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An in-memory shadow can lose work if the process dies before promotion.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1762.1" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent does not write directly to the real working tree; all edits land in the shadow first and may only be promoted after review, so a rejected or broken edit never reaches the developer&#39;s files.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1914.1" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent edits a real workspace and a wrong edit must never corrupt the developer&#39;s files.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-edit diffs and independent rollback are needed for review and recovery.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The shadow can be kept close enough to the real tree that promotion stays clean.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2058.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The agent only proposes changes a human applies by hand, so no live edit boundary is needed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The workspace is throwaway and corrupting it carries no cost.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An undo-via-inverse-action approach already covers recovery without a parallel copy.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2020.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Real working tree — the developer&#39;s files, changed only on accept&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Shadow workspace — the version-controlled copy or overlay the agent edits&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Checkpointer — snapshots each agent edit so any step can be rolled back&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diff and review surface — presents agent edits for human inspection&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Promoter — applies accepted changes from the shadow back to the real tree&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2183.1" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Version control (git) — backs the per-edit checkpoints and rollback in the shadow&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diff viewer — renders agent edits for review before promotion&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Filesystem overlay — optionally tracks edits in memory without touching disk&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2145.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Shadow drift — the real tree changes underneath the shadow and promotion conflicts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lost promotion — accepted changes fail to apply cleanly back to the real tree.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Silent divergence — the agent reasons against the shadow while the human sees the stale real tree.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2346.1" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Real-tree corruption incidents — should be zero, since edits land in the shadow first&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rollback usage rate — how often a step is reverted, showing the safety net in use&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Promotion conflict rate — how often accepted changes fail to apply cleanly&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Review latency per change — time from agent edit to human accept or reject&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2270.1" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cline/cline&quot;&gt;Cline (shadow git checkpoints)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Keeps an isolated git repo per workspace and offers diff-based rollback of agent edits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Moatless Tools (in-memory shadow mode)&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Tracks file modifications in memory without writing to disk until accepted.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03515&quot;&gt;Inside the Scaffold (coding-agent taxonomy)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Catalogs shadow git checkpoints and in-memory shadow mode as execution-isolation and state-management techniques.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2471.1" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Compensating Action&lt;/b&gt; — Compensating Action undoes an effect by running an inverse action; a shadow workspace reverts by discarding a diff/checkpoint instead.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Durable Workflow Snapshot&lt;/b&gt; — Snapshots persist execution/workflow state for resume; a shadow workspace versions the files the agent mutates for review and rollback.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Synthetic Filesystem Overlay&lt;/b&gt; — An overlay presents a virtual filesystem surface; the shadow adds version history and diff-based rollback over the edits made through it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Subagent Isolation&lt;/b&gt; — Worktree isolation separates parallel subagents; a shadow workspace isolates the agent&#39;s edits from the real tree for safe review.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Forkable Agent Sandbox&lt;/b&gt; — A source-file mirror for edit-then-review covers the filesystem in a single branch; this extends the same discipline to running processes and desktop sessions across many branches.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2414.1" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03515&quot;&gt;Inside the Scaffold: A Source-Code Taxonomy of Coding Agent Architectures&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/cline/cline&quot;&gt;cline/cline&lt;/a&gt; — 2024&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.12806&quot;&gt;Fault-Tolerant Sandboxing for AI Coding Agents: A Transactional Approach to Safe Autonomous Execution&lt;/a&gt; — Boyang Yan, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.28138&quot;&gt;Crab: A Semantics-Aware Checkpoint/Restore Runtime for Agent Sandboxes&lt;/a&gt; — Tianyuan Wu, Chaokun Chang, Lunxi Cao, Wei Gao, Wei Wang, 2026&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.roocode.com/features/checkpoints&quot;&gt;Roo Code Checkpoints (shadow Git repository)&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2672.1" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="short-term-memory" name="Short-Term Thread Memory">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2127.1" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2127.1" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Short-Term Thread Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Memory &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; mature &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Conversation State, Per-Thread State, Working Memory&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="579.1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="n:root_start" mermaidBaseStyle="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="21.7" width="21.7" x="277.35" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Empty" mermaidId="n:Empty" mermaidBaseStyle="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Empty" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=10;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="62.0" width="94.55" x="241.7" y="254.2" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
