          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:CACHE-&gt;LK#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.06;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m22">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=1;entryY=0.06;" target="m14">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1295.92" y="664.49" />
                <mxPoint x="623.56" y="690.59" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:APP-&gt;SPEC#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.64;exitY=0;entryX=0.62;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m23">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m17" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.64;exitY=0;entryX=0.62;entryY=1;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="702.9" y="927.59" />
                <mxPoint x="702.9" y="873.3" />
                <mxPoint x="702.9" y="809.61" />
                <mxPoint x="702.9" y="744.88" />
                <mxPoint x="702.9" y="690.59" />
                <mxPoint x="1426.42" y="664.49" />
                <mxPoint x="1426.42" y="596.63" />
                <mxPoint x="1426.42" y="527.72" />
                <mxPoint x="1426.42" y="501.62" />
                <mxPoint x="1426.42" y="447.33" />
                <mxPoint x="1426.42" y="393.04" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Offline distillation and speculative pre-answering populate a cache that absorbs most test-time queries.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1042.16" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;During idle or downtime, run the model offline against the user&#39;s standing context to pre-compute dense summaries and likely future answers, so test-time latency and cost drop when the user actually asks.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1117.16" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is running an agent over persistent user context — a codebase, a set of documents, transcripts of prior sessions — that the user queries repeatedly. Many of the queries are predictable variants of previous ones, and the underlying corpus does not change between most of those queries. The provider infrastructure also has idle capacity between user sessions when nobody is actively waiting for an answer.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1117.16" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Conventional inference does all the work at test time, when the user is waiting. For every query the system parses the corpus, finds what matters, reasons about it, and produces an answer; the next query repays this work from scratch even if it is asking something very similar. Prompt caching helps only when the prefix matches exactly. The user therefore pays latency on every question even though many questions about a stable corpus could have been pre-processed during idle periods — yielding indices, summaries, or partial answers that would have made the eventual user-visible step nearly instantaneous.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1242.16" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Test-time latency is what the user feels; offline latency is invisible.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Most queries against a stable corpus are predictable variants — predict and pre-answer once.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Prefetching wastes compute on queries that never come, so prediction must be cheap and recoverable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Prompt caching only helps for matching prefixes; speculative pre-answering generates new content.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Pre-computed answers stale as the corpus changes — freshness vs cost trade-off.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1280.16" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: schedule idle-time inference passes that distill standing context into dense summaries and generate speculative answers to predicted future queries, so test-time work shrinks to retrieving or lightly adapting pre-computed material.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1443.16" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Run two kinds of offline passes against the user&#39;s standing context. (1) Distillation: compress the corpus into structured summaries — per-file, per-module, per-topic — that capture what queries would likely need. (2) Speculative pre-answering: predict likely next queries (from query history, recent context, structural signals) and generate answers ahead of time, stored against query embeddings. At test time, the agent first checks the speculative cache; on a hit it returns or lightly adapts the pre-answer; on a miss it falls back to live inference but adds the new query to the prediction set. Pre-computed material is invalidated when its source documents change. The Letta team and Lin et al. report substantial test-time cost and latency reductions on this pattern.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1462.16" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Idle scheduler -&amp;gt; Distillation pass (corpus -&amp;gt; summaries) -&amp;gt; Speculative-query generator -&amp;gt; Pre-answer pass (predicted Q -&amp;gt; A pairs, embedding-indexed) | Test-time: query -&amp;gt; embedding lookup -&amp;gt; pre-answer hit (cheap) or fallback to live inference (normal cost) -&amp;gt; append to prediction set.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1568.16" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A developer agent has indexed a 200K-file monorepo as the user&#39;s standing context. Overnight it runs a distillation pass that summarizes each top-level module and predicts likely next-day queries from the user&#39;s commit history and yesterday&#39;s questions. When the developer asks the next morning &#39;what changed in the billing module last week and which tests cover it&#39;, the agent retrieves a pre-answer generated at 03:00 that morning and adapts it with one extra inference call instead of re-walking the repo from scratch.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1682.16" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Test-time latency drops dramatically on hits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost shifts from peak (test-time) to trough (idle) capacity.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Distilled summaries also speed up cold queries by serving as compact retrieval targets.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Speculative coverage improves over time as the prediction model learns from misses.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Offline compute is real cost — wasted on predictions that never get asked.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale pre-answers can mislead if invalidation lags corpus changes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Privacy: pre-answering implies the system holds and reasons over user data during idle.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quality regression if the speculative pre-answer is lower-effort than live inference and the agent does not detect it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Storage and indexing overhead for the pre-answer cache.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1712.16" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent must not return a stale pre-computed answer when its source documents have changed since pre-computation; freshness checks must gate cache hits. Speculative pre-answers must be marked as such in the trace so downstream evaluation can distinguish them from live inference.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1864.16" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent operates over standing context that changes slowly relative to query volume.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider has idle capacity between sessions and peak-cost test-time inference.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User queries against the corpus are repetitive or predictable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency at test time matters more than offline compute cost.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2065.16" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Corpus changes faster than pre-computation can keep up.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Queries are highly novel and prediction yields no hits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Privacy regime forbids holding/processing user data outside live sessions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Idle compute is more expensive than the latency it saves.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1989.16" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Idle scheduler — kicks off offline passes when provider capacity is unused and no user is waiting&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Distillation pass — compresses the standing corpus into per-file, per-module, or per-topic structured summaries&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Speculative-query generator and pre-answer pass — predicts likely next queries from history and runs the model against them, storing Q/A pairs indexed by query embedding&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Pre-answer cache — embedding-indexed store consulted at test time before live inference&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Freshness invalidator — drops or marks-stale cache entries whose source documents have changed since pre-computation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2209.16" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Job scheduler — Airflow, cron, or a queue worker that runs the offline passes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Vector index — Pinecone/Weaviate/Chroma over query embeddings for the cache lookup&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Summarisation LLM — drives the distillation pass; usually a cheaper model than test-time inference&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Change-detection layer — git hooks, file mtime diff, or content-hashing to feed the freshness invalidator&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2133.16" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Stale pre-answer — a source file changes after the idle pass, and the cache returns an answer that is no longer true.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wasted idle spend — the predictor guesses questions nobody asks, and offline compute is spent for nothing.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Low-effort hit — a cheap speculative answer is returned in place of a better live answer, and quality drops unnoticed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unmarked origin — pre-answers are not tagged in the trace, so evaluation cannot tell them apart from live inference.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2429.16" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Speculative hit rate — fraction of user queries served from the pre-answer cache&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Test-time latency reduction — p50/p95 latency on hits vs cold queries&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Stale-answer rate — sampled cases where a cache hit was wrong because the source had changed&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Offline-to-test cost ratio — total offline spend per saved test-time dollar&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Prediction-coverage growth — improvement in hit rate as the predictor learns from misses over time&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2296.16" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.letta.com/blog/sleep-time-compute&quot;&gt;Letta&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Open-source agent platform with idle-time pre-computation against persistent user memory.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.13171&quot;&gt;Lin et al. arXiv:2504.13171&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Original sleep-time compute paper; demonstrates trade-off on standing-context benchmarks.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2649.16" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Episodic Summaries&lt;/b&gt; — Episodic summaries compact past conversation; sleep-time compute generates new speculative content.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Window Packing&lt;/b&gt; — Selection happens at prompt-time; sleep-time compute prepares the material being selected from.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Dream Consolidation Cycle&lt;/b&gt; — Both are between-session passes; dream-consolidation targets affective/embodied agents, sleep-time compute targets standing-context cost reduction.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Test-Time Compute Scaling&lt;/b&gt; — Inverts the trade-off: more offline compute so less test-time compute is needed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Prompt Caching&lt;/b&gt; — Prompt caching hits on matching prefixes; sleep-time compute generates new content that prompt caching cannot.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Cross-Session Memory&lt;/b&gt; — Standing user context is the substrate sleep-time compute operates on.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Adaptive Compute Allocation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Compaction&lt;/b&gt; — Compaction distils the live conversation at runtime; sleep-time compute distils standing context offline.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Adaptive Memory Decay&lt;/b&gt; — Sleep-time compute schedules when consolidation runs; adaptive decay decides what is forgotten.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Speculative Agentic Actions&lt;/b&gt; — Both precompute likely-future work, but sleep-time-compute runs offline during idle periods against the standing context, while speculation runs in-loop on the live trajectory and is discarded the moment the prediction misses.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2459.16" width="755" height="415" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.13171&quot;&gt;Sleep-time Compute: Beyond Inference Scaling at Test-time&lt;/a&gt; — Kevin Lin et al., 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.letta.com/blog/sleep-time-compute&quot;&gt;Sleep-time Compute&lt;/a&gt; — Letta, 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2793.16" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="socratic-questioning-agent" name="Socratic Questioning Agent">
