        <UserObject label="yes" mermaidId="e:Q-&gt;Synth#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="yes" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="user wants direct answer" mermaidId="e:Q-&gt;Direct#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.78;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="user wants direct answer" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.78;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1295.7" y="1156.3" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Drive the agent toward its goal by asking the user a sequence of strategic, open-ended questions that surface the user&#39;s own latent knowledge, goal, or context — rather than producing an answer directly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1498.9" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent operates in a domain where the user holds the ground truth or has to discover it for themselves: tutoring, requirements elicitation, coaching, self-knowledge, code review walkthroughs, therapy-adjacent tools. A direct answer would either be wrong (the agent does not know the user&#39;s situation) or actively unhelpful (the user needs to construct the understanding themselves).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1498.9" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Default agent shape — receive prompt, return answer — fits poorly when the answer must come from the user&#39;s own context or learning process. Princeton NLP&#39;s SocraticAI demonstration and Anthropic-style tutoring evaluations both find that a question-first agent produces materially better outcomes than a fact-first agent on these workloads. But the shape is not just &#39;ask a question&#39; (that is disambiguation) and not &#39;ask yourself&#39; (that is self-ask): it is a deliberately staged sequence of probing questions, calibrated to the user&#39;s responses, that ends in the user articulating the answer.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1623.9" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Direct answers are faster but wrong-shaped when the goal is user learning or user-context surfacing.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A bad question is worse than a bad answer — it can mislead or frustrate; the question sequence is itself a design surface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Users sometimes want answers, not questions; the agent must read when to switch modes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Question-driven dialogs are longer and more expensive in tokens than direct answers; the cost only pays off in workloads where understanding is the actual goal.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1642.9" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: design the agent&#39;s primary action as &#39;formulate the next strategic question&#39; rather than &#39;produce an answer&#39;, and track which question moved the user closer to their own articulation as the success signal.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1805.9" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Structure the agent loop around question selection: at each turn, choose a question that (a) targets the largest remaining uncertainty about the user&#39;s goal/context, (b) is answerable by the user with what they already know or can introspect, (c) advances toward a user-articulated conclusion. Maintain an explicit &#39;open questions&#39; store. Switch modes to direct-answer when the user signals they want one or when the user has articulated enough that synthesis is now low-risk. Pair with frozen-rubric reflection so the agent does not slide into rote question templates.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1843.9" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;User turn --&amp;gt; agent reads response --&amp;gt; update open-questions store --&amp;gt; user has articulated answer? --not yet--&amp;gt; select next strategic question (largest uncertainty, answerable by user) --&amp;gt; ask --&amp;gt; User | --yes--&amp;gt; synthesize and hand back | --user wants direct answer--&amp;gt; direct-answer mode&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1930.9" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A self-knowledge assistant takes the user through a weekly reflection. Instead of summarizing the user&#39;s notes, it opens with &#39;Which moment this week did you feel most yourself?&#39; Based on the user&#39;s answer it picks the next question: &#39;What was different about that moment from how you usually spend that time?&#39; The agent maintains an internal store of open tensions (&#39;user said X about work but Y about energy&#39;) and selects questions targeting the largest tension. After 4–6 turns the user articulates a pattern the assistant could not have produced cold. The session ends with the user, not the agent, writing the conclusion.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2025.9" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Output is grounded in the user&#39;s actual context, not the LLM&#39;s prior — fewer confabulated answers.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; User learning, self-knowledge, or requirements quality go up; the user owns the articulated conclusion.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent&#39;s failure modes become legible — bad questions are visible, bad answers can hide.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Slower and more expensive than direct-answer for users who just want an answer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misjudged question sequences frustrate or mislead users; the question is now a quality surface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hard to evaluate offline — the success criterion (user articulates the answer) requires the actual user in the loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2074.9" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Forbids the agent from producing direct answers when the goal is user understanding or context-surfacing. Restricts the LLM&#39;s freedom to assert, requiring it to interrogate instead.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2226.9" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tutoring, coaching, and pedagogical workloads where user understanding is the goal.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Requirements elicitation where the user holds context the agent cannot guess.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-knowledge / journaling assistants where the user is the source of truth.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Code review walkthroughs where the goal is the engineer&#39;s understanding, not just the patch.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2389.9" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Pure information-retrieval tasks where the user just wants an answer.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Time-pressured workflows where dialog rounds cost more than direct answers save.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Workloads where misjudged questions could mislead in safety-critical ways without an expert in the loop.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Settings where the success criterion cannot be measured (no follow-up signal from the user).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2332.9" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Question selector — picks next question targeting largest remaining tension&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Open-questions / tension store — what the agent does not yet know about the user&#39;s situation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mode switch — detects when the user wants a direct answer instead of more questions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Articulation detector — recognises when the user has reached the conclusion themselves&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Frozen-rubric reflection — keeps the agent from sliding into rote question templates&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2533.9" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM — for question generation and articulation detection&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tension store — explicit memory of what is still open&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Dialog history — turn-by-turn store the question selector reads&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Optional retrieval — to ground questions in domain knowledge (e.g., curriculum, prior sessions)&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2495.9" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Withheld answer — the user clearly wants a direct answer, but the agent keeps asking questions and the user gives up.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rote questions — the agent slides into the same question templates every turn, and the questions stop surfacing new context.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Misled user — a badly sequenced question steers the user toward a conclusion the agent assumed rather than one the user holds.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Premature synthesis — the agent switches to synthesis before the user has articulated enough, and its summary fills gaps with guesses.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2696.9" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; User-articulated-conclusion rate — share of sessions where the user, not the agent, states the conclusion&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Question quality — human-rated relevance and openness of agent questions (held-out sample)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mode-switch precision — agent correctly switches to direct-answer when the user signals they want one&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Session-length / cost vs direct-answer baseline — quantifies the tax the pattern imposes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Follow-up signal — user satisfaction, learning gain, or requirement completeness measured after the session&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2639.9" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://princeton-nlp.github.io/SocraticAI/&quot;&gt;Princeton NLP — SocraticAI demonstration of the method for self-discovery with LLMs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.05671&quot;&gt;MedTutor-R1 — clinical multi-agent tutoring simulation reporting +20% pedagogical-score improvement&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://marco-nissen.com/sparrot/&quot;&gt;Sparrot — long-running cognitive agent whose dialogue protocol leans on Socratic questioning for self-observation and human-agent bridging&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://qiita.com/syukan3/items/174e43235bde8a1a0694&quot;&gt;Reported in Japanese pattern surveys (Qiita syukan3 22-pattern comparison, listing &amp;#x27;Socratic/対話駆動 エージェント&amp;#x27;) and Russian habr practitioner write-ups (self-knowledge bot with LLM-as-periphery dialog architecture)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2916.9" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Disambiguation&lt;/b&gt; — disambiguation is one-shot clarification; Socratic is multi-turn structured questioning&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Ask&lt;/b&gt; — self-ask is agent-to-self; Socratic is agent-to-user&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Open-Question Tension Store&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Frozen Rubric Reflection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Human-in-the-Loop&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Passive Goal Creator&lt;/b&gt; — passive waits for the user to state the goal; Socratic actively elicits it&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tacit-Knowledge Elicitation Agent&lt;/b&gt; — The interview phase drives the expert with strategic open-ended questions to surface latent, unwritten know-how rather than asking them to summarise it directly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hint Ladder&lt;/b&gt; — Socratic questioning responds only in questions to surface the learner&#39;s own knowledge; the hint ladder releases help of rising specificity keyed to consecutive failures, and its rungs may be statements, not only questions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2859.9" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://princeton-nlp.github.io/SocraticAI/&quot;&gt;The Socratic Method for Self-Discovery in Large Language Models&lt;/a&gt; — 2024&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.05116&quot;&gt;Beyond Automation: Socratic AI, Epistemic Agency, and the Implications of the Emergence of Orchestrated Multi-Agent Learning Architectures&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.27410&quot;&gt;Closing the Expression Gap in LLM Instructions via Socratic Questioning&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0360131525002623&quot;&gt;Investigating the effects of an LLM-based Socratic conversational agent on students&amp;#x27; academic performance and reflective thinking in higher education&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://qiita.com/syukan3/items/174e43235bde8a1a0694&quot;&gt;多様な AI エージェント設計パターン22選を比較&lt;/a&gt; — 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://habr.com/ru/articles/1027210/&quot;&gt;Я строю AI-бот для самопознания. Вот спек, архитектура и почему LLM — это периферия, а не ядро&lt;/a&gt; — 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3155.9" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
