        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="routes" mermaidId="e:Pool-&gt;Dev#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.57;exitY=1;entryX=0.73;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="routes" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.57;exitY=1;entryX=0.73;entryY=0;" target="m2">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="505.2" y="334.8" />
                <mxPoint x="505.2" y="429.35" />
                <mxPoint x="505.2" y="525.45" />
                <mxPoint x="505.2" y="620.0" />
                <mxPoint x="505.2" y="716.1" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="routes" mermaidId="e:Pool-&gt;QA#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.83;exitY=1;entryX=0.92;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="routes" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.83;exitY=1;entryX=0.92;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="334.8" />
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="429.35" />
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="525.45" />
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="620.0" />
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="716.1" />
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="810.65" />
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="906.75" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Encode a human Standard Operating Procedure (roles, ordered phases, standardised hand-off artefacts) into a multi-agent pipeline so that agents communicate through structured documents rather than free-form chat.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1469.45" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is automating a complex, repeatable task — software development, document production, a regulatory submission — that already has a well-known human Standard Operating Procedure (SOP). The SOP names specific roles (product manager, architect, engineer, quality assurance) and specifies the deliverables that pass between them: a requirements document, then a design, then code, then a test report. The shape of the work is already understood; what is being automated is the execution.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1469.45" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;If the agents simply chat freely, they hallucinate context the SOP would have pinned down, drift off-task between roles, and produce no auditable trail of which agent did what. Without typed hand-off deliverables, agents redo each other&#39;s work or quietly skip steps, and ambiguity that the SOP would catch at a phase boundary propagates to the end. The team ends up with a multi-agent system that looks lively in the transcript but produces worse artefacts than a single human following the same procedure would.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1594.45" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The model is good at playing a role; it is bad at inventing the workflow that connects roles.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Free chat between agents is cheap to write but expensive to debug.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Defined artefacts (PRD, design doc, test plan) compress context across role hand-offs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rigid SOPs lose the model&#39;s ability to adapt; the SOP has to leave room for the role to think.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1632.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: encode the human SOP as named roles, ordered phases, and typed artefact contracts at every phase boundary, so that agents communicate through documents rather than drifting free-form chat.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1776.45" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Encode the SOP as: (a) a fixed set of named roles each with role-specific prompt and tool palette, (b) an ordered sequence of phases, (c) a typed artefact contract for each phase boundary (e.g. PRD → design doc → code → test plan → user manual). Agents communicate via the artefacts; a shared message pool plus a subscription filter routes only relevant context to each role.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1776.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Role_A -- artefact_1 --&amp;gt; Role_B -- artefact_2 --&amp;gt; Role_C ... ; shared message pool; per-role subscription filter.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1882.45" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A four-agent product-development chat keeps drifting because agents talk free-form and re-do each other&#39;s work. The team rewrites it as an SOP-encoded pipeline: PM writes a typed PRD artefact, Architect transforms PRD into an Architecture artefact, Engineer transforms Architecture into Code, QA transforms Code into Test Report. Each phase boundary is a typed contract, not a chat. Drift stops, the trail is auditable, and review focuses on the artefacts rather than the conversation.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1920.45" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Auditable trail of artefacts at every phase boundary.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Specialised role prompts beat one mega-prompt on long tasks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Standardised artefact schemas catch ambiguity at the hand-off, not at the end.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Designing the artefact contract is the real work; bad contracts propagate to every role.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Procedure rigidity makes the system brittle when the task does not match the SOP.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token cost scales with the number of phases.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2007.45" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Agents may not communicate outside the artefact contract; a role&#39;s output that does not conform to the next role&#39;s expected schema is rejected at the phase boundary.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2083.45" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; A complex repeatable task already has a documented human SOP with named roles.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hand-off artefacts between phases can be typed (PRD, design doc, code, test plan).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An auditable trail of artefacts is required.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2284.45" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The task is one-off and writing an SOP is more work than doing it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Free-form chat between agents is sufficient and cheaper.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phases cannot be cleanly separated and artefact contracts cannot be defined.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2189.45" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; SOP-encoded role — fixed agent persona (PM, Architect, Engineer, QA, tech-writer) with scoped prompt&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Typed artefact contract — schema for each phase boundary deliverable (PRD, design doc, code, test plan)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phase sequencer — ordered controller that gates phase transitions on artefact conformance&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Shared message pool — blackboard-style store of all artefacts and intermediate messages&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Subscription filter — routes only relevant artefacts to each role&#39;s inbox&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2409.45" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; MetaGPT or ChatDev framework — provides role definitions and SOP phase scaffolding&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Artefact-schema validator — enforces typed contracts at every phase boundary&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — invoked once per role-turn inside each phase&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Versioned artefact store — keeps every PRD, design, and test plan inspectable after the fact&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2314.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Bad artefact contract — the design-doc schema leaves out a field the developer needs, and every later role inherits the gap.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Task outside the SOP — a request does not fit the fixed phases, and the pipeline forces it through steps that make no sense for it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Over-strict filter — the subscription filter withholds context a role needed, and that role produces an artefact on partial information.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phase cost — every request pays for every phase, even when only one or two of them matter.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2591.45" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Artefact-conformance rate — share of role outputs that pass the next role&#39;s schema&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Phase rework rate — handoffs sent back upstream for failing the predicate&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; End-to-end success vs free-form-chat baseline — does the SOP actually improve outputs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; SOP-mismatch incidents — tasks where the encoded SOP did not fit the input task&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Token cost per phase — spend distribution across phases, used to find the heavy step&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2458.45" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/geekan/MetaGPT&quot;&gt;MetaGPT&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Five roles (Product Manager, Architect, Project Manager, Engineer, QA) producing standardised artefacts in an assembly-line pipeline.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/OpenBMB/ChatDev&quot;&gt;ChatDev&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — CEO/CTO/Programmer/Reviewer/Tester roles in a phased pipeline with artefact hand-offs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2792.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Role Assignment&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Supervisor&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Blackboard&lt;/b&gt; — Shared message pool plus subscription filter is a blackboard variant.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Spec-First Agent&lt;/b&gt; — The SOP is itself a spec for the multi-agent system.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hero Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Structured Output&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Chat Chain&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Control-Loop-Mapped Agent Chain&lt;/b&gt; — A standard operating procedure is a sequential hand-off of artefacts; a control chain is a set of loops acting at the same sample, arbitrated by structural priority rather than by order of work.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2621.45" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.00352&quot;&gt;MetaGPT: Meta Programming for A Multi-Agent Collaborative Framework&lt;/a&gt; — Hong et al., 2023&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.07924&quot;&gt;ChatDev: Communicative Agents for Software Development&lt;/a&gt; — Qian et al., 2023&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2936.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="sovereign-inference-stack" name="Sovereign Inference Stack">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2430.35" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2430.35" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sovereign Inference Stack&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Safety &amp;amp; Control &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: On-Premise Agent Stack, Data-Residency Agent Architecture, Sovereign AI&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="664.35" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Operator-controlled boundary" mermaidId="n:Boundary" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=light-dark(#ffffde,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#aaaa33,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Operator-controlled boundary" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=light-dark(#ffffde,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#aaaa33,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="584.35" width="669.6" x="65.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="On-prem inference" mermaidId="n:Inf" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="On-prem inference" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="303.8" x="364.15" y="224.75" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Tool gateway" mermaidId="n:Tools" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Tool gateway" id="m2">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="238.7" x="106.85" y="426.25" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
