        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Keep-&gt;FT#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.33;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.33;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="347.1" y="1621.3" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:FT-&gt;Base#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.78;exitY=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.87;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.78;exitY=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.87;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="1621.3" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="1540.7" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="1460.1" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="1379.5" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="1284.95" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="1188.85" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="1094.3" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="759.5" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="438.65" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="358.05" />
                <mxPoint x="793.5" y="277.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Bootstrap a model&#39;s reasoning by training it on its own correct chain-of-thought outputs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1788.75" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team wants to fine-tune a model to become a better reasoner on a class of problems where chain-of-thought prompting visibly helps. They have ground-truth final answers for a training set, and they have compute to generate many model outputs. What they do not have is a dataset of human-written rationales — the step-by-step solutions a person would normally write between problem statement and final answer.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1788.75" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Without supervised step-by-step explanations, supervised fine-tuning for reasoning is stuck: the model can be trained to produce final answers, but not to produce the rationales that lead to those answers. At the same time, just prompting the base model with chain-of-thought has plateaued and is as good as plain prompting can make it. The team needs a way to build a training set of rationales without humans writing them, and a training loop that does not require the unstable machinery of full reinforcement learning.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1880.75" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Filter quality determines what &#39;correct&#39; rationale gets reinforced.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wrong rationales that produce right answers can leak in.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compute cost of repeated generation + filtering.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1951.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: train the model on its own correct chain-of-thought outputs (rationalising failures with the known correct answer), so that rationales improve without any human-written labels.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2062.75" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Prompt the base model with CoT to generate rationale + answer pairs. Keep pairs where the answer matches ground truth. &lt;b&gt;Rationalization&lt;/b&gt;: when a generated rationale yields the wrong answer, prompt the model with the correct answer as a hint and ask for a rationale that justifies it; add the rationalized example to training. Fine-tune on the kept + rationalized pairs. Repeat: the fine-tuned model generates better rationales next round; iterate.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2076.75" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Base model --CoT prompt--&amp;gt; rationale + answer --&amp;gt; answer matches ground truth? --yes--&amp;gt; keep pair | --no--&amp;gt; rationalize with correct answer as hint --&amp;gt; justifying rationale --&amp;gt; keep --&amp;gt; fine-tune on kept + rationalized pairs --&amp;gt; improved model --&amp;gt; next round&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2168.75" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team has a small base model that knows facts but cannot reliably reason. They prompt it with CoT to generate (rationale, answer) pairs across a dataset with ground-truth answers. They keep pairs whose answer is right; for wrong answers they &#39;rationalize&#39; (give the model the right answer and ask for a rationale). They fine-tune on the kept set, then iterate. After two STaR rounds the model&#39;s reasoning capability climbs without any human-written rationales.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2239.75" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Self-improvement on reasoning without rationale labels.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Iterative gains compound.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Spurious-rationale leakage if filtering is too lax.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compute-heavy.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2312.75" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Training data is restricted to filter-passing rationales; ungrounded rationales are not reinforced.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2402.75" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning task where CoT helps but supervised rationale data is unavailable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ground-truth answers exist so generated rationales can be filtered.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fine-tuning the model on rationale + answer pairs is feasible.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2551.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; No ground-truth answers exist to filter rationales.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The base model is too weak to produce any correct CoT outputs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quick iteration matters more than the bootstrap-and-train cycle.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2494.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Base model — current checkpoint that generates (rationale, answer) pairs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; CoT sampler — prompts the model to produce a rationale alongside the final answer&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ground-truth filter — keeps pairs whose final answer matches the labelled target&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rationaliser — re-prompts the model with the correct answer as a hint to obtain a justifying rationale for failed items&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Supervised fine-tuner — trains the next checkpoint on kept and rationalised pairs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Round controller — drives successive STaR iterations and stops on plateau&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2676.75" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; LLM training stack — supervised fine-tuning runner with checkpoint rotation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Answer grader — exact-match or task-specific equivalence checker against ground truth&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Sampling cluster — inference infrastructure for repeated rationale generation&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2619.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Spurious rationale — a rationale reaches the right answer through flawed steps, passes the answer filter, and teaches the flawed reasoning.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Back-filled justification — rationalization with the correct answer as a hint produces reasoning that only works because the answer was given.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Plateau — later rounds add few new correct rationales, and the model stops improving while compute keeps running.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Easy-case bias — the kept set is dominated by problems the model already solves, so hard problems stay underrepresented.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2877.75" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Reasoning-task accuracy per round — held-out lift after each STaR iteration&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rationalised-share of training data — fraction of training pairs that came from the hint-then-rationalise path&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Spurious-rationale audit rate — share of kept pairs where the rationale does not actually justify the answer, manually sampled&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Kept-pair fraction per round — generation efficiency over iterations&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compute cost per accuracy point — total sampling and training cost per benchmark gain&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2744.75" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;STaR paper experiments&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Influences modern reasoning-distillation pipelines&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ezelikman/STaR&quot;&gt;STaR (ezelikman/STaR)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Official reference implementation of STaR: Bootstrapping Reasoning With Reasoning (NeurIPS 2022).&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3097.75" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Chain of Thought&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Self-Consistency&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;ReST-EM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2945.75" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.14465&quot;&gt;STaR: Bootstrapping Reasoning with Reasoning&lt;/a&gt; — Zelikman, Wu, Mu, Goodman, 2022&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3241.75" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
