        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A-&gt;G#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m8">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m1" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m2">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="role too broad" mermaidId="e:G-&gt;O#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.93;entryX=0.26;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="role too broad" id="m9">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0;exitY=0.93;entryX=0.26;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="136.3" y="798.25" />
                <mxPoint x="136.3" y="894.35" />
                <mxPoint x="136.3" y="974.95" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="role too narrow" mermaidId="e:G-&gt;B#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.93;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="role too narrow" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.93;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="571.85" y="798.25" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:B-&gt;O#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.73;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.73;entryY=0;" target="m3">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="571.85" y="974.95" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:O-&gt;H#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:H-&gt;X#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: authorize a goal-driven agent with static, login-time, role-based privileges, so its standing permissions persist between and beyond tasks, forcing a choice between over-granting broad access and blocking the agent mid-task.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1464.8" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An organisation already governs its people with role-based access control: users are placed in groups, groups map to roles, roles grant standing permissions, and access is decided once at login. When it deploys an agent it reaches for the same machinery — give the agent a role, put it in the right groups, grant the permissions that role implies. The agent, however, is goal-driven: it chains tools, retries, and discovers paths no one enumerated when the role was defined.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1464.8" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Role-based access control decides permissions once, from a static role, for a predictable actor. A goal-driven agent is none of those things. Its action set is dynamic and task-dependent, so the role either grants more standing privilege than any single task needs — broad, long-lived access that persists between and beyond tasks and becomes the blast radius when the agent is hijacked, prompt-injected, or simply wrong — or it grants too little and the agent is blocked mid-task, so someone widens the role to unblock it. Because each new task path wants a different permission combination, roles multiply until effective access can no longer be explained. The model cannot express what actually governs a safe agent action: this principal, this task, this moment, revocable when the task ends. Standing privilege is the default the model pushes toward, and it is exactly the wrong default for an actor that decides its own next step.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1589.8" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; RBAC decides access once, at login, from a static role; agents decide their next action continuously, at runtime.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A goal-driven agent&#39;s permission needs are task-dependent and not fully enumerable when the role is defined.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Granting the role enough privilege to never block the agent means granting standing access far broader than any single task needs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reusing the organisation&#39;s existing RBAC machinery is faster than building runtime, task-scoped authorization.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1627.8" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: authorize agents per action at runtime — bind each grant to a principal, a task, and a moment, make it least-privilege and short-lived, and revoke it when the task ends — instead of assigning a static role with standing privilege.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1847.8" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Replace standing, role-based grants with runtime, task-scoped authorization. Decide each consequential action against the current principal, task intent, and context rather than against a role assigned once at login; issue least-privilege, short-lived, revocable credentials per task so privilege never outlives the work that needed it; expand access only as the agent demonstrates it needs and can be trusted with more. Mitigation patterns: delegated-agent-authorization for scoped, short-lived, revocable per-action credentials, and progressive-tool-access for minimal access that expands only as competency is shown. Static RBAC is not wrong for human users whose access is decided at login; it is wrong as the authorization model for an actor that chooses its own next step, which is the mismatch this anti-pattern names.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1847.8" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: Static role at login -&amp;gt; standing permissions -&amp;gt; too broad (privilege beyond task) or too narrow (blocked, role widened) -&amp;gt; hijack or error acts with full role. Corrected: Agent action -&amp;gt; runtime check against principal, task, context -&amp;gt; short-lived, least-privilege task credential -&amp;gt; revoked when task ends.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1972.8" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team gives its new support agent a role in the existing identity provider: read the ticket store, call the refund API, query the customer database. It works until the agent, following a manipulated ticket, issues refunds it was never meant to — because the refund permission was standing, not task-scoped, and nobody was in the loop at the moment of action. To stop blocking the agent on edge cases, the team had already widened the role twice. They switch to runtime authorization: each consequential action is checked against the current task and principal, refund authority is granted as a short-lived token only for the ticket being handled, and it is revoked when the ticket closes — so privilege no longer outlives the work.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2086.8" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: reusing existing role-based access control is familiar, already deployed, and gets the agent running without new infrastructure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team explain why roles keep getting widened and push for task-scoped runtime authorization instead.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Standing privilege persists between and beyond tasks, so a hijacked, prompt-injected, or simply mistaken agent acts with the full breadth of its role.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Roles multiply as each new task path demands a different permission combination, until effective access can no longer be explained or audited.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Teams widen roles to unblock agents mid-task, ratcheting privilege upward and never back down.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2135.8" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;No useful constraint; the missing constraint is runtime, task-scoped authorization — every consequential agent action checked against principal, task, and context, granted least-privilege and short-lived, and revoked when the task ends.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2306.8" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; An agent is assigned a static role with standing permissions decided once, at deployment or login.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent&#39;s role is periodically widened to unblock it mid-task, and privilege never narrows again.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Effective agent access is assembled from proliferating roles or groups and can no longer be explained per action.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2469.8" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent actions are authorized at runtime against principal, task, and context, with least-privilege, short-lived grants.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent performs a single fixed, fully enumerable operation that a static scope captures exactly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credentials are task-scoped and revoked when the task ends, so no standing privilege accrues.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2431.8" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Static role — a fixed set of standing permissions decided once, at deployment or login&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Login-time decision point — authorization evaluated when the agent starts, not per action&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Standing privilege — access that persists between and beyond the task that needed it&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Role proliferation — new roles minted for each task-specific permission combination&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2632.8" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Runtime authorization engine — evaluates each agent action against principal, task intent, and context at the moment of action&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-lived credential broker — issues least-privilege, task-scoped, revocable grants instead of standing role permissions&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Standing-privilege auditor — flags agent permissions held continuously but rarely exercised, for narrowing or expiry&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2594.8" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Blast-radius amplification — a hijacked or mistaken agent acts with the full breadth of its standing role&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Privilege ratchet — roles are widened to unblock agents mid-task and never narrowed afterwards&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unexplainable access — effective permissions sprawl across roles until no one can say what the agent may do&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2776.8" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Standing-privilege ratio — permissions held continuously versus permissions actually exercised per task&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Credential lifetime versus task duration — how long agent grants live relative to the work they serve&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Roles per agent population — proliferation rate of task-specific roles and groups&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Runtime-authorized action share — fraction of consequential actions checked at the moment of action, not at login&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2776.8" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://labs.cloudsecurityalliance.org/research/csa-research-note-nist-ai-agent-standards-20260416-csa-style/&quot;&gt;Cloud Security Alliance — NIST AI agent standards &amp;amp; agentic identity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Reports that emerging agentic-AI controls move away from static role-to-permission mapping toward ephemeral, context-aware identities scoped to an agent&#39;s current task, because goal-driven agents chain tools and discover paths static RBAC never anticipated.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2026/04/27/ai-agents-access-control-model/&quot;&gt;Help Net Security — IAM built for humans versus agents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Argues that traditional IAM&#39;s static roles and long-lived credentials cannot govern agents whose behaviour is dynamic, contextual, and continuous, and that access must be evaluated at runtime, per action.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2939.8" width="755" height="225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Delegated Agent Authorization&lt;/b&gt; — The positive model: scoped, short-lived, revocable per-action credentials decided at runtime, in place of a static role&#39;s standing privilege.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Progressive Tool Access&lt;/b&gt; — The positive model: start minimal and expand access only as the agent proves competency, rather than granting a broad standing role up front.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Privilege Escalation&lt;/b&gt; — Standing role privilege is the breadth that escalation across agent-plus-tool-plus-service identities then exploits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Over-Broad Scope&lt;/b&gt; — Over-broad tool scope is the per-tool symptom; static-role authorization is the model-level cause that makes broad standing scope the default.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Identity Sprawl&lt;/b&gt; — Sibling non-human-identity failure: sprawl is the creation-versus-governance rate mismatch, this is the static-versus-dynamic authorization-model mismatch.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;conflicts-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Ephemeral Agent Identity&lt;/b&gt; — Pinning a dynamic agent to a fixed static role is the anti-pattern this replaces with an identity born and retired with each run.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2977.8" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.25819&quot;&gt;Identity Management for Agentic AI&lt;/a&gt; — arXiv:2510.25819&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://web.archive.org/web/20260610183423/https://www.scworld.com/resource/a-new-identity-class-why-ai-agents-require-runtime-control&quot;&gt;A New Identity Class: Why AI Agents Require Runtime Control&lt;/a&gt; — SC Media&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2026/04/27/ai-agents-access-control-model/&quot;&gt;Your IAM was built for humans, AI agents don&amp;#x27;t care&lt;/a&gt; — Help Net Security&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3178.8" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
