        <UserObject label="lazy hydration: list returns paths,&#xa;cat materialises content" mermaidId="e:RT-&gt;A#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.87;exitY=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.93;" mermaidBaseValue="lazy hydration: list returns paths,&#xa;cat materialises content" id="m21">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.87;exitY=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.93;" target="m0">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="892.7" y="468.1" />
                <mxPoint x="892.7" y="387.5" />
                <mxPoint x="892.7" y="292.95" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Heterogeneous sources are projected into one Unix-like tree behind five filesystem primitives; nodes hydrate only on cat.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="968.55" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Project heterogeneous enterprise data sources into a single Unix-like tree exposed through filesystem primitives so the agent reuses path semantics it already knows instead of learning a bespoke API per source.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1043.55" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building an enterprise agent that has to read across many heterogeneous internal systems: Notion, Slack, Google Drive, GitHub, Linear, Jira, email, plus internal databases. Each source has its own authentication, pagination, search dialect, and result shape, and cross-source tasks (a Slack thread plus the linked Notion doc plus the related pull request) are the norm rather than the exception.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1043.55" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Designing one agent-friendly tool API per source does not scale: every new connector adds a fresh vocabulary the model has to learn, and the tool count climbs past the point where the agent can choose well between them. Flattening everything into a vector store of chunks loses structure and makes cross-source joins impossible. Meanwhile the model has very strong priors for Unix-like filesystem navigation (list, find, cat, grep) from training data, but no native enterprise source matches those semantics — observations from production logs show agents inventing file-path syntax against APIs where no filesystem actually exists.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1168.55" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Each source has unique semantics, but a unified surface must hide them.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The agent&#39;s strongest navigation priors are filesystem operations, not REST.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-source joins (a Slack thread plus its linked Notion doc plus the related PR) require traversal, not separate tool calls.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Auth, rate limits, and pagination must remain per-source even when the surface is unified.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lazy enumeration matters: listing all of Slack as a directory cannot fetch every message eagerly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1206.55" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: build a virtual filesystem that maps each data source under a path prefix (/slack/, /notion/, /drive/) and expose exactly five primitives — list, find, cat, search, locate_in_tree — so the agent traverses cross-source data with semantics it already has.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1369.55" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Mount each connector under a deterministic path: /slack/&amp;lt;workspace&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;channel&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;date&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;message&amp;gt;.md, /notion/&amp;lt;workspace&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;page-path&amp;gt;.md, /github/&amp;lt;org&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;repo&amp;gt;/.... Expose five primitives: list (enumerate children, paginated), find (path-pattern matching), cat (fetch a node&#39;s content), search (full-text query, optionally scoped to a subtree), and locate_in_tree (resolve an opaque ID to its path). Each primitive translates into source-specific API calls on demand; nodes are virtual until cat. The agent navigates with shell-like idioms — list /slack/eng/, find /notion -name &#39;&lt;i&gt;onboarding&lt;/i&gt;&#39;, search &#39;incident 2026-05&#39; /slack/eng — and joins results by paths rather than per-source identifiers.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1388.55" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent | Five-primitive interface (list, find, cat, search, locate_in_tree) | Path-routing layer | Per-source adapters (Slack, Notion, Drive, GitHub...) with their own auth and rate-limit governors | Lazy hydration: nodes materialize on cat, not on list.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1494.55" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An on-call engineer asks the assistant to summarize last week&#39;s incident. The agent runs find /slack -name &#39;&lt;i&gt;incident&lt;/i&gt;&#39; -newer 2026-05-12, cats the matching channel transcripts, searches /notion for the linked postmortem template, and lists /github/infra/prs filtered by date. Three sources, one navigation idiom, no per-source SDK calls. The same agent on a new connector (Linear) needs only a new subtree under /linear/ — no new tools, no new prompts.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1589.55" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; One mental model across all sources; new connectors add a subtree, not a new vocabulary.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reuses the model&#39;s filesystem priors instead of training new tool affordances.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-source traversal becomes path concatenation rather than ID translation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Small primitive set keeps the tool surface tiny even as data grows.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lazy hydration bounds per-call cost.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Source semantics that do not map to trees (graph-heavy data, time-series streams) must be flattened or hidden.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Path stability becomes a contract — renames in upstream sources can break agent memory of paths.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Permission systems differ per source; a unified path namespace must still enforce per-source ACLs.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Full-text search quality depends on each adapter; uneven coverage frustrates the agent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Listing very large directories needs careful pagination defaults.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1638.55" width="755" height="358" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent must access enterprise data only through the five primitives — direct per-source API calls are forbidden once the overlay is mounted. It must treat paths as the canonical identifier and not invent paths that locate_in_tree has not validated.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1752.55" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Agent must read across many heterogeneous enterprise data sources.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-source joins are common and ID translation hurts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool count is climbing past what the model handles cleanly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Source data is mostly tree- or document-shaped.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2010.55" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Only one or two data sources exist — overlay is overkill.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Data is fundamentally graph-shaped (e.g. social network) and trees lose information.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-source APIs already share a clean uniform shape.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Real-time streaming dominates over snapshot reads.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1877.55" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Path-Routing Layer — maps a virtual path to the correct connector adapter&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Connector Adapters — per-source modules (Slack, Notion, Drive, GitHub) that materialise paths into source-specific calls&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Five-Primitive Interface — fixed action set: list, find, cat, search, locate_in_tree&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent — reuses Unix path semantics it already knows to navigate heterogeneous sources&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Search Index — backs the full-text search primitive, optionally scoped by subtree&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2154.55" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Full-text search backend (Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, or BM25 library) — answers the search primitive&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-source SDKs (Slack, Notion, Drive, GitHub) — back the connector adapters&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Path-resolver index — maps opaque source IDs back to their virtual paths for locate_in_tree&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2021.55" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Path breakage — an upstream source renames a channel or page, and paths the agent remembered now point at nothing.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; ACL flattening — the unified tree shows a file to an agent that the source system would deny, because the adapter does not enforce per-source permissions.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Invented path — the agent guesses a plausible path instead of resolving it with locate_in_tree, and acts on the wrong node or a missing one.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unbounded listing — a list call on a huge directory returns too many children, and the result floods the context.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2336.55" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-source task success — share of tasks completed that touch more than one connector&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Path-resolution accuracy — fraction of locate_in_tree calls returning the correct virtual path&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tokens per observation — cost of the five-primitive surface versus per-source tool APIs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Search-precision at k — relevance of search results scoped by subtree&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adapter error rate per connector — where the overlay leaks source-specific failures&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2146.55" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.dust.tt/building-deep-dive-infrastructure-for-ai-agents-that-actually-go-deep/&quot;&gt;Dust.tt production agents (Paris)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Five-primitive synthetic filesystem across Notion, Slack, GitHub, Drive and others. Internal logs documented agents inventing file-path syntax before the FS existed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2556.55" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Model Context Protocol&lt;/b&gt; — MCP exposes per-source tool surfaces; this overlay collapses them into one filesystem-shaped interface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-Computer Interface&lt;/b&gt; — Inverts ACI: instead of designing agent-friendly APIs per source, design one universal filesystem all sources project into.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Discovery&lt;/b&gt; — Discovery becomes ls/find against a tree rather than runtime tool enumeration.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Knowledge Graph Memory&lt;/b&gt; — Graph-of-triples vs tree-of-paths — different shapes for the same cross-source navigation problem.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Naive-RAG-First&lt;/b&gt; — Preserves source structure where vector RAG flattens it into chunks.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Filesystem as Context&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Shadow Workspace&lt;/b&gt; — An overlay presents a virtual filesystem surface; the shadow adds version history and diff-based rollback over the edits made through it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2309.55" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.dust.tt/building-deep-dive-infrastructure-for-ai-agents-that-actually-go-deep/&quot;&gt;Building Deep Dive: Infrastructure for AI Agents That Actually Go Deep&lt;/a&gt; — Dust, 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2700.55" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
