        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:EV-&gt;MK#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.25;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.25;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="319.2" y="1103.6" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="offload" mermaidId="e:EV-&gt;ST#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.96;entryX=0.3;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="offload" id="m13">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.96;entryX=0.3;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="629.2" y="1103.6" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="restore by id" mermaidId="e:ST-&gt;OBS#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.56;exitY=0;entryX=0.68;entryY=1;" mermaidBaseValue="restore by id" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=2 3;fixDash=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.56;exitY=0;entryX=0.68;entryY=1;" target="m1">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="781.1" y="1103.6" />
                <mxPoint x="781.1" y="1007.5" />
                <mxPoint x="781.1" y="912.95" />
                <mxPoint x="781.1" y="748.65" />
                <mxPoint x="781.1" y="599.85" />
                <mxPoint x="781.1" y="519.25" />
                <mxPoint x="781.1" y="438.65" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="arch-caption" value="&lt;i&gt;Consumed observations are swapped for compact markers; full payloads are offloaded and restored on demand.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=12;fontColor=#52606d;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="65" y="1275.45" width="1470" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Once a tool&#39;s raw output has been consumed, replace it in the live context window with a short marker of what was done, reclaiming tokens without losing that the call happened.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1350.45" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A tool-using agent calls search, file reads, API queries, or code execution, and each returns a bulky payload — a page of JSON, a file&#39;s full contents, a stack trace. The agent reads the payload, extracts what it needs, and acts. Turns later that raw payload is still sitting in the context window, consuming tokens and attention even though only its conclusion is still relevant.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1350.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Raw tool outputs are the largest and most disposable thing in an agent&#39;s context. Keeping every observation verbatim crowds the window, raises cost, and buries the signal the agent actually reasoned over; but deleting a tool turn entirely loses the record that the call was made and what it concluded, which the agent may need to avoid repeating work or to justify its actions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1456.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Raw observations dominate token usage but are mostly dead weight once consumed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Deleting an observation outright erases the trace that the call happened at all.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; What is &#39;consumed&#39; is not always obvious — a result may be needed again later.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Replacement markers must carry enough to prevent the agent re-issuing the same call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eviction policy competes with caching: one discards, the other retains for replay.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1494.45" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: after an observation has been acted on, replace its raw payload in the window with a compact &#39;called X, got Y conclusion&#39; marker, keeping the trace while dropping the bulk.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1600.45" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Treat tool observations as evictable. When a tool result has been consumed — its needed values extracted into the agent&#39;s reasoning or into external memory — replace the raw payload in the working context with a short marker that records the call, its target, and the one-line conclusion (&#39;read config.yaml: 3 services defined&#39;, &#39;searched docs: no rate-limit setting found&#39;). Keep the marker so the agent does not re-issue the call; offload the full payload to external storage if it might be needed verbatim again. Apply eviction lazily (oldest-consumed first) or eagerly (immediately after extraction) depending on how tight the window is. Manus and the Chinese context-engineering literature describe this as tool clearing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1657.45" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Tool call -&amp;gt; raw observation in window -&amp;gt; agent extracts needed values -&amp;gt; (consumed) -&amp;gt; evictor replaces payload with marker; full payload optionally offloaded to external store.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1706.45" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A research agent runs ten web fetches, each returning a full page of markdown. After pulling the one figure it needs from each, the runtime replaces every fetched page in the window with a line like &#39;fetched acme.com/pricing: enterprise tier is $499/mo&#39; and offloads the full pages to a blob store. The window stays lean across the next twenty reasoning steps, and when the agent later needs a page in full it restores it by call id instead of re-fetching.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1877.45" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Window pressure from bulky observations drops sharply.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost and latency per call fall because dead payloads stop being re-sent.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The trace of what was called and concluded survives in the marker.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Signal-to-noise in the window improves, helping the model attend to what matters.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evicting a result still needed forces a redundant re-call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A marker that loses a key value can mislead later reasoning.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Deciding when an observation is truly &#39;consumed&#39; is error-prone.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Without offload, an evicted payload needed verbatim later is gone.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Eviction logic adds bookkeeping to the agent loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1831.45" width="755" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent must not retain raw tool payloads in the live window after they have been consumed; a consumed observation has to be replaced with a marker that preserves the call and its conclusion. Eviction must not delete the record that a call happened, only its bulky body.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2040.45" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tool observations are large relative to the context window.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Most results are consumed once and not needed verbatim again.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Window pressure or per-call cost is a binding constraint.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; You can write a faithful one-line marker for each consumed result.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2165.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tool outputs are small and the window is not under pressure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Results are frequently revisited verbatim and re-calling is costly or non-deterministic.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Regulatory needs require the full observation to stay inline in the trace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; You cannot reliably tell when a result has been consumed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2165.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Observation buffer — holds raw tool payloads in the live window until they are consumed&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Consumption detector — decides when a result&#39;s needed values have been extracted&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Evictor — replaces a consumed payload with a compact call-and-conclusion marker&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; External payload store — optional offload so an evicted result can be restored verbatim if needed&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Marker record — the short note that keeps the call and its conclusion in context&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2309.45" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Token counter — quantifies how much window each observation costs to prioritise eviction&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Key-value or blob store — offloads full payloads keyed by call id for later restore&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent runtime — the loop that rewrites the message history to swap payloads for markers&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2309.45" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Premature eviction — a result is cleared before the agent has extracted every value it needs, and it has to re-issue the same call.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lossy marker — the one-line marker drops a key number, and later steps reason from an incomplete summary.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No offload — the payload is evicted without being saved, and a later step that needs it verbatim cannot get it back.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Erased record — eviction removes the whole tool turn instead of only its body, and the agent repeats work it already did.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2472.45" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Window reclaimed — tokens freed per evicted observation&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Redundant re-call rate — calls re-issued because a still-needed result was evicted&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Marker fidelity — sampled checks that markers preserved the conclusion accurately&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cost per resolved task — net effect of eviction on tokens spent end to end&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2434.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://manus.im/blog/Context-Engineering-for-AI-Agents-Lessons-from-Building-Manus&quot;&gt;Manus&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Context-engineering writeup describes compressing or dropping observations once their information has been used, keeping a restorable reference rather than the full payload.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://realtime-ai.chat/posts/context-engineering/&quot;&gt;上下文工程 (Chico&amp;#x27;s Tech Blog)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Names tool clearing: remove a tool result from the window after it is used and replace it with a brief summary statement.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2692.45" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Result Caching&lt;/b&gt; — Caching retains a result for replay across calls; eviction discards the consumed payload from the live window. The two trade off retention against window pressure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Compaction&lt;/b&gt; — Eviction removes a single consumed tool result; compaction folds a whole span of turns into a digest.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Context Window Packing&lt;/b&gt; — Packing decides what enters the window; eviction decides what leaves it once consumed.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Filesystem as Context&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Adaptive Memory Decay&lt;/b&gt; — Tool-result eviction trims the live context; adaptive decay governs the long-term store.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Foveated Perception Escalation&lt;/b&gt; — Eviction prunes consumed observations to reclaim context; foveation decides fidelity before and during perception, and lets an archived observation regain its pixels rather than only lose them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2578.45" width="755" height="282" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://manus.im/blog/Context-Engineering-for-AI-Agents-Lessons-from-Building-Manus&quot;&gt;Context Engineering for AI Agents: Lessons from Building Manus&lt;/a&gt; — Manus, 2025&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://realtime-ai.chat/posts/context-engineering/&quot;&gt;上下文工程：2026 年比 prompt engineering 更重要的事&lt;/a&gt; — Chico&#39;s Tech Blog, 2026&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2874.45" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="tool-result-reinforcement" name="Tool-Result Reinforcement">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2895.5" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2895.5" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:24px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tool-Result Reinforcement&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Planning &amp;amp; Control Flow &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; emerging &amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp; Also known as: Reinforcement (tool-return), Enriched Tool Return, Tool-Return Re-grounding&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="20" width="1540" height="58" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-panel" value="" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f8fc;strokeColor=#b6c6d8;strokeWidth=1;arcSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="95" width="1540" height="844.5" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="arch-heading" value="&lt;b&gt;ARCHITECTURE&lt;/b&gt; &amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;color:#52606d&quot;&gt;Editable diagram imported from the pattern source&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontSize=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="48" y="109" width="1504" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="Model issues tool call" mermaidId="n:C" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Model issues tool call" id="m0">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="328.6" x="677.25" y="155.0" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Dispatch -&gt; raw result" mermaidId="n:D" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Dispatch -&gt; raw result" id="m1">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="337.9" x="375.0" y="316.2" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Wrapper: append goal + status + failure/next-step hint, derived from live run" mermaidId="n:W" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Wrapper: append goal + status + failure/next-step hint, derived from live run" id="m2">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="956.35" x="65.0" y="477.4" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="Enriched return: raw result + reinforcement block" mermaidId="n:E" mermaidBaseStyle="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" mermaidBaseValue="Enriched return: raw result + reinforcement block" id="m3">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeWidth=1;fillColor=light-dark(#ECECFF,#1f2020);strokeColor=light-dark(#9370DB,#cccccc);fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontSize=16;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="83.7" width="649.45" x="218.45" y="638.6" as="geometry" />
