        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Fuse-&gt;Cat#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m10">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m3" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m4">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Cat-&gt;Planner#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m11">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m4" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m5">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="no" mermaidId="e:Thr-&gt;Keep#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.71;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" mermaidBaseValue="no" id="m12">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m2" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);html=1;fontSize=16;labelBackgroundColor=light-dark(#E8E8E88D,#2a2a2a8D);fontFamily=Trebuchet MS,Verdana,Arial,sans-serif;fontColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=1;exitY=0.71;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="810.16" y="308.55" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Mine tool-call telemetry for high-probability X-then-Y transitions and fuse those pairs into a single composite tool, shrinking the planner&#39;s step count.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="389.68" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An agent has been running long enough to accumulate substantial tool-call telemetry: which tool was called, then which tool followed, and how often. Each tool call is a model-decoding decision that can fail or cost tokens; the planner is also paying per-step latency.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="389.68" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Many tool sequences are nearly deterministic. After a search, the agent almost always fetches one of the top results; after a database lookup, it almost always formats and writes a row. These transitions are paid for over and over: each step is a model call, each decision an opportunity for the planner to mis-pick. The agent&#39;s intermediate decoding errors and per-step latency dominate the trajectory cost even though the team could see, from the telemetry alone, that the transition was effectively fixed.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="495.68" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Frequent X-then-Y pairs are visible from logs but require periodic mining to detect.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Fusing into a composite tool removes the per-step decoding decision and one step of latency.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Over-fusion hides flexibility — sometimes the agent does need to deviate from the common path.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composite tool surface must stay legible to the planner and to humans reviewing traces.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="514.68" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: mine telemetry for tool transitions above a fixed probability threshold and fuse them into named composite tools, shrinking the planner&#39;s step count along the dominant trajectory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="677.68" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Sweep tool-call telemetry for transitions P(Y|X) above a threshold (e.g. 0.8). Wrap qualifying X-then-Y pairs in a composite tool whose signature is X&#39;s input and Y&#39;s output. Add the composite to the catalog; leave X and Y available for edge cases. Re-run the sweep periodically as task mix shifts. Document why each composite exists so a later reviewer understands the fusion was telemetry-driven, not author intuition.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="658.68" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Tool-call telemetry --&amp;gt; Sweep P(Y|X) --(&amp;gt;= threshold)--&amp;gt; Compose X then Y into one tool --&amp;gt; Add to tool catalog --&amp;gt; Planner; --(&amp;lt; threshold)--&amp;gt; Keep X and Y separate&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="783.68" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A code-review agent&#39;s telemetry shows that after &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;read_file(path)&lt;/font&gt; it calls &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;parse_python(content)&lt;/font&gt; on 94% of trajectories. The team adds a composite &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;read_and_parse(path)&lt;/font&gt; tool; the planner now makes one call where it used to make two. End-to-end latency drops noticeably and a class of bug where the model occasionally called &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;parse_json&lt;/font&gt; instead of &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;parse_python&lt;/font&gt; disappears.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="821.68" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cuts one step (and one decoding decision) per fused pair.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Removes a recurring failure mode where the model picks the wrong follow-up.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Reusing telemetry instead of author intuition keeps the catalog grounded.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composite tools hide the X/Y boundary from anyone reading a trace.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Over-fusion entrenches the dominant path and slows divergence when task mix shifts.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Threshold choice is a judgment call; too low fuses noise, too high yields nothing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="908.68" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Tools must not be fused merely on author intuition; fusion is gated on observed transition probability above a documented threshold from real telemetry.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="965.68" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Sufficient tool-call telemetry exists to estimate transition probabilities.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-step latency or decoding-error rate is a measurable cost driver.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A clear majority transition (&amp;gt;0.8 conditional probability) recurs across many sessions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1185.68" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tool catalog churn is high; composites rot before they earn their keep.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The X/Y pair is logically separable but operationally diverse — fusion hides legitimate branching.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; No telemetry exists; intuition-only fusion is forbidden by this pattern.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1071.68" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Telemetry store — captures every tool call and its successor&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Transition mining job — computes P(Y|X) over the window and flags pairs above threshold&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composite tool generator — wraps the X-then-Y pair as a single tool exposing X&#39;s input and Y&#39;s output&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Catalog updater — registers the composite and keeps X, Y available for edge cases&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1310.68" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Tool-call log warehouse — durable store of every (tool, args, result) event&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Mining job runner — periodic batch computing transition probabilities&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool catalog registry — surface the agent loads each session&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1196.68" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Noise fused — the threshold is set too low, a pair that only sometimes follows is merged, and the composite does the wrong second step on the other cases.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Entrenched path — the task mix shifts but the sweep is not re-run, and the planner keeps reaching for a composite that no longer fits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Hidden boundary — a failure inside the composite shows up as one opaque call in the trace, and the reviewer cannot tell whether X or Y broke.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Intuition fusion — a pair is fused because it looked obvious to an author, with no telemetry behind it, and the composite is rarely the right choice.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1473.68" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Step reduction — average steps per task before vs after fusion.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Composite hit rate — fraction of composite calls that follow the dominant path (should stay high).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Divergence rate — fraction of tasks where the original X without Y still fires.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1321.68" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;Production agents with periodic tool-catalog pruning from logs&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://huyenchip.com/2025/01/07/agents.html&quot;&gt;AI Engineering (Huyen) — agent-design discussion of transition mining&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1693.68" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-Computer Interface&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent Skills&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Compound Error Degradation&lt;/b&gt; — Shrinking step count is one mitigation for multiplicative error.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Use&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;composes-with&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hierarchical Tool Selection&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1446.68" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://huyenchip.com/2025/01/07/agents.html&quot;&gt;Agents — Chip Huyen&lt;/a&gt; — Chip Huyen, 2025&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1818.68" width="755" height="78" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="tool-use" name="Tool Use">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="2710.5" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="2710.5" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
