        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Route inter-agent messages through named topics that agents subscribe to, instead of having senders address each other by id.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1057.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building a multi-agent system in which a message produced by one agent is potentially of interest to several others, and the set of interested agents may change over time. The sender does not know — and should not need to know — exactly which agents will care about its message, and new subscribers should be able to join the system without forcing changes to anyone who is already publishing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1057.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Direct agent-to-agent addressing, where a sender names each receiver explicitly, creates a dense web of dependencies in which every sender carries knowledge about every receiver it might want to reach. Adding a new participant then requires editing every sender that should be able to reach it, and removing one leaves dangling references everywhere. The team needs a routing mechanism where senders publish to named topics and interested agents subscribe to those topics, so that sender and receiver are decoupled and the wiring can change without touching either end.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1163.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Decoupling sender from receiver is the central benefit of pub/sub.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Topic semantics — wildcards, ordering guarantees, durability — change the failure modes substantially.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Broadcast traffic on a busy topic can overwhelm slow subscribers without back-pressure.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Debugging is harder when nobody owns the addressing decision.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1220.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: route inter-agent messages through named topics with explicit subscriptions, so that senders do not know who reads them and new subscribers can join without sender-side changes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1345.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a small set of typed Topics (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;telemetry.parsed&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;incident.opened&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;plan.proposed&lt;/font&gt;). Agents publish to topics; agents that care subscribe to topics. The runtime fans messages out to all subscribers of a topic, applies back-pressure on slow consumers, and provides delivery guarantees appropriate to the topic class. Pair with actor-model-agents to keep each subscriber&#39;s processing isolated, and with event-driven-agent when the topic carries external events. Topic schemas are first-class artefacts; subscribers depend on the schema, not on the publisher.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1383.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Publisher agent --publish(typed message)--&amp;gt; Named topic (versioned schema) --fan out with back-pressure--&amp;gt; Subscriber agents 1..N; new subscriber added without changing any sender&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1451.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;An incident-response platform has many agents. A monitor agent publishes to &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;telemetry.alert&lt;/font&gt;; a triage agent subscribes to it and may publish to &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;incident.opened&lt;/font&gt;; an audit agent subscribes to both topics; a paging agent subscribes only to &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;incident.opened&lt;/font&gt;. Adding a new compliance-export agent that needs every incident is a one-line subscription on &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;incident.opened&lt;/font&gt; — none of the existing publishers change. Topic schemas are versioned (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;incident.opened.v1&lt;/font&gt;) and subscribers declare which versions they accept.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1565.15" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Senders are decoupled from receivers; new subscribers join without sender changes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-cutting workflows (logging, audit, monitoring) attach as additional subscribers.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Scales to many participants where direct addressing would not.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diagnosing &#39;who is supposed to handle this topic?&#39; requires runtime subscription introspection.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Topic-schema drift can break subscribers silently.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Slow subscribers need explicit back-pressure rules or they degrade the topic for everyone.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1576.15" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Senders do not address receivers by id; cross-agent messaging must go through named topics with explicit subscriptions, and topic schemas are not allowed to mutate without versioning.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1747.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Sender should not know which agents care about a message.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Subscribers join and leave over time without sender-side changes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-cutting concerns (audit, observability) need to attach by adding a subscriber.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1853.15" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The interaction is strictly point-to-point and decoupling is overkill (use handoff or direct send).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Ordering and exactly-once semantics are required and the chosen bus does not provide them.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Schema discipline is impossible in the team — pub/sub without schema control is a hard place to debug.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1853.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Publisher agent — emits messages to a named topic without knowing the subscribers&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Subscriber agent — declares interest in one or more topics and reacts to published messages&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Named topic — typed channel (telemetry.alert, incident.opened) with a versioned schema&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Topic-schema registry — versioned envelope schemas subscribers depend on&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Back-pressure policy — per-subscriber rule that handles slow consumers without degrading the topic&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1978.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; AutoGen Core Topic and Subscription — provides the pub/sub primitives in-process&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; NATS or Kafka — durable message bus backing topics in production deployments&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Schema registry — stores versioned topic schemas and enforces compatibility&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Subscription-introspection tool — runtime listing of which agents subscribe to which topic&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1997.15" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Orphan topic — a message is published to a topic nobody subscribes to, and the event is silently dropped.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Schema drift — a publisher changes a topic&#39;s message shape without a new version, and subscribers break without an error at the sender.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Slow subscriber — one consumer falls behind without back-pressure rules, and delivery on the topic degrades for everyone.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unclear ownership — an incident lands on a topic, and finding out which agent should handle it requires digging through runtime subscriptions.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2141.15" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Subscriber-add velocity — engineer-hours to wire a new agent into existing topics&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Schema-drift incidents — subscribers broken silently by topic-version changes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Slow-subscriber back-pressure events — topic degradation traced to one lagging consumer&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Topic-fan-out distribution — number of subscribers per topic, used to find hot channels&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; End-to-end message latency — time from publish to last subscriber receipt&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2141.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/stable/user-guide/core-user-guide/core-concepts/topic-and-subscription.html&quot;&gt;AutoGen Core (Topic and Subscription)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — AutoGen Core exposes Topic and Subscription as core primitives, with documented example scenarios.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://nats.io/&quot;&gt;NATS / Kafka as agent buses&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Production multi-agent deployments often run topics on a message broker for durability and scale.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2361.15" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Actor-Model Agents&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Event-Driven Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Inter-Agent Communication&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Blackboard&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Pipes and Filters&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Complexity-Based Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;used-by&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Hierarchical Retrieval&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2304.15" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://microsoft.github.io/autogen/stable/user-guide/core-user-guide/core-concepts/topic-and-subscription.html&quot;&gt;AutoGen Core — Topic and Subscription&lt;/a&gt; — Microsoft&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2524.15" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
