        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:A4-&gt;Pn#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m20">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m6" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m10">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Expose text-to-speech, speech-to-text, and real-time speech-to-speech through a single interface so a voice agent can swap providers without rewriting the loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="642.56" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building a voice agent at a moment when the provider landscape is moving fast: OpenAI&#39;s realtime API, Google&#39;s voice models, ElevenLabs for text-to-speech (TTS), Deepgram for speech-to-text (STT), Azure, Amazon Web Services, and a growing set of on-device options. The agent needs some combination of three voice capabilities: TTS, which turns text into audio; STT, which turns audio into text; and real-time speech-to-speech (STS), which takes audio in and produces audio out without the round-trip through text. Capability, price, and quality shift between providers faster than the team can rewrite application code.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="642.56" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Each provider ships its own software development kit, with its own streaming chunk format, its own audio framing, its own lifecycle events for things like &quot;the user started talking&quot; or &quot;partial transcript ready&quot;, and its own way of exposing real-time speech-to-speech versus the older text-to-speech and speech-to-text shapes. Writing the agent loop directly against one of those kits binds the entire application to that vendor&#39;s release cadence and pricing, and forecloses a switch for cost, quality, latency, or feature reasons. The team needs one interface that spans all three modes and treats the provider as a configuration choice.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="748.56" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; TTS, STT, and STS have meaningfully different control-flow shapes (one-shot vs streaming vs bidirectional), but the application wants one mental model.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Realtime speech-to-speech needs bidirectional audio framing — half-duplex APIs cannot fully emulate it.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider feature parity is incomplete: not every provider offers all three modes or all voices.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency budgets in voice are tight (sub-300ms turn-taking); abstraction overhead must be small.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Voice-event vocabulary (turn-start, partial-transcript, barge-in, voice-activity) needs to be unified across providers.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="843.56" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: define one Voice interface that spans TTS, STT, and STS with capability flags, so that the agent loop addresses voice as one resource and the provider becomes a configuration choice rather than a code shape.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="949.56" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a Voice interface with three primary methods — &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;speak(text) -&amp;gt; AudioStream&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;listen(audio_stream) -&amp;gt; TranscriptStream&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;converse(audio_stream) -&amp;gt; AudioStream&lt;/font&gt; (the realtime STS path) — and a uniform event vocabulary (&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;turn_start&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;partial_transcript&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;final_transcript&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;barge_in&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;voice_activity_start/stop&lt;/font&gt;). Each provider implementation declares which modes and voices it supports via capability flags; the agent loop checks capability rather than provider name. Pair with streaming-typed-events (the underlying typed event transport), multilingual-voice-agent (language adaptation on top), and provider-string-routing (string-addressed provider selection). Treat realtime STS as a first-class mode, not a flavour of TTS+STT, because the bidirectional framing differs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1063.56" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Agent loop ↔ Voice interface { speak, listen, converse, capabilities } ↔ Provider adapter (OpenAI realtime, ElevenLabs, Deepgram, Azure, ...) ↔ provider API.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1074.56" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A consumer voice assistant team wants to ship realtime speech-to-speech on iOS, fall back to TTS+STT on platforms where realtime is unavailable, and run STT-only for transcription-mode users. They build their agent loop against a unified Voice interface with &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;speak&lt;/font&gt;, &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;listen&lt;/font&gt;, and &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;converse&lt;/font&gt; methods plus a capability flag for &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;realtime_sts&lt;/font&gt;. On iOS the loop picks the realtime provider; on Android it falls back to TTS+STT through the same interface; transcription-mode disables &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;speak&lt;/font&gt; entirely. When a cheaper TTS provider lands, the change is a configuration switch — the agent loop does not move.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1283.56" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider switch is configuration, not code.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multi-provider deployments (TTS from one provider, STT from another) become trivial.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability flags let the application degrade gracefully when a mode is unavailable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Event vocabulary stays uniform across providers, so UI components can be stable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lowest-common-denominator pressure on the abstraction — provider-specific voices and effects need capability flags.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Realtime STS bidirectional framing is hard to emulate when only TTS+STT are available; capability gaps must be explicit.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adding another mode (avatar, lip-sync) means evolving the interface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Voice-event vocabulary across providers drifts; the adapter layer has to keep up.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1199.56" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;The agent loop must call voice operations through the unified interface and must read provider capability via capability flags; the loop is not allowed to import provider-specific voice SDK classes.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1465.56" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Building voice agents that may switch providers for cost, quality, or latency reasons.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Multiple voice modes (TTS, STT, realtime STS) are in play in the same product.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The application UI consumes a uniform voice-event vocabulary independent of provider.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider capability gaps must be discoverable at runtime.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1552.56" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The application is locked to one provider&#39;s realtime offering and that lock is acceptable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency budgets are so tight that any abstraction layer is suspect — measure before rejecting.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Only one mode is needed and a thin per-provider client suffices.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1571.56" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Voice interface — unified contract exposing speak, listen, and converse plus capability flags&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability registry — declares per-provider support for TTS, STT, and realtime STS modes and voices&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider adapter — translates the unified interface into one vendor&#39;s SDK and audio framing&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Voice-event normaliser — maps each provider&#39;s events to the uniform vocabulary (turn_start, partial_transcript, final_transcript, barge_in, voice_activity_start/stop)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Audio I/O pipeline — microphone capture and speaker playback feeding the unified streams&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1696.56" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; TTS service — text-to-audio streaming engine bound through a &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;speak&lt;/font&gt; adapter&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; ASR service — audio-to-transcript streaming engine bound through a &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;listen&lt;/font&gt; adapter&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Realtime speech-to-speech API — bidirectional audio engine bound through a &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;converse&lt;/font&gt; adapter&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Voice-pipeline framework — host (e.g. LiveKit, Pipecat) that runs the adapters and audio plumbing&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1696.56" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Lowest-common-denominator voice — the interface exposes only what every provider supports, so provider-specific voices and effects become unreachable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Faked realtime — a provider that offers only text-to-speech and speech-to-text is wired in as if it supported speech-to-speech, and barge-in and turn timing break.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability flag lies — an adapter claims a mode it handles poorly, and the agent loop picks it and fails at runtime.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Adapter drift — a provider changes its event names or chunk format, the adapter is not updated, and events like barge_in stop arriving.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1897.56" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Voice-pipeline end-to-end latency — wall-clock from user speech end to agent audio start, per mode&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider-swap effort — code diff size required to change the active TTS, STT, or STS provider&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability-flag accuracy — agreement between declared capabilities and runtime behaviour&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Event-vocabulary parity across providers — share of voice events that map cleanly to the unified set&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Barge-in handling rate — fraction of mid-speech interruptions the pipeline detects and honours&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1840.56" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://mastra.ai/docs/voice/overview&quot;&gt;Mastra Voice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Mastra&#39;s Voice system documents a unified interface spanning TTS, STT, and real-time STS.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.livekit.io/agents/&quot;&gt;LiveKit Agents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Voice-AI framework with pluggable TTS/STT and realtime model providers behind a uniform agent interface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/pipecat-ai/pipecat&quot;&gt;Pipecat&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Open-source voice-AI pipeline with provider-agnostic TTS/STT/realtime stages.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2117.56" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Streaming Typed Events&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multilingual Voice Agent Stack&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Provider-String Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Translation Layer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2022.56" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://mastra.ai/docs/voice/overview&quot;&gt;Mastra — Voice overview&lt;/a&gt; — Mastra&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.livekit.io/agents/&quot;&gt;LiveKit Agents&lt;/a&gt; — LiveKit&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2299.56" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
