        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:R-&gt;P1b#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.09;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.09;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m6">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="685.0" y="1145.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:R-&gt;P2#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m15">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:R-&gt;P3#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.91;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m16">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.91;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m8">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points">
                <mxPoint x="1252.3" y="1145.45" />
              </Array>
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: couple application code directly to one model provider&#39;s SDK, request shape, and proprietary features so that switching providers requires rewriting application code rather than swapping an adapter.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1328.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building an LLM application or agent framework directly against a single provider&#39;s SDK — calling its specific request shape, depending on its proprietary streaming chunks, using its particular tool-call format. There is no abstraction layer between the application code and the vendor SDK, because the team has no immediate plan to support a second provider and the SDK exposes useful features that would be diluted by a lowest-common-denominator interface.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1328.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Every provider has its own request schema, its own streaming semantics, its own tool-call shape, and its own rate-limit headers. Application code that has been written directly against one provider cannot be redirected to another without invasive changes through the whole codebase, because the vendor&#39;s shape has leaked everywhere. Once that coupling exists, the team can no longer evaluate routing requests to a cheaper or stronger competitor for the same task, cannot fall back to another provider during an outage, and cannot move workloads for compliance reasons. Switching providers is a normal lifecycle event, not a hypothetical one, and vendor lock-in turns it into a rewrite.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1453.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Provider SDKs are richer than the lowest common denominator and expose useful proprietary features.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; An abstraction layer adds maintenance cost and may lag behind upstream features.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-provider quirks (streaming chunks, tool-call shapes, rate-limit headers) are non-trivial to unify.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Switching providers for quality, cost, or compliance reasons is a normal lifecycle event, not a hypothetical.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1491.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: code against a provider-agnostic interface (a unified language-model spec, a &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string router, or a thin adapter), so that swapping providers is a configuration change rather than a code rewrite.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1654.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Don&#39;t couple application code to one provider&#39;s surface. Use a provider-agnostic abstraction (Vercel AI SDK&#39;s language model spec, LiteLLM, Mastra&#39;s &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string, OpenAI-API-compatible adapters) and keep provider-specific extensions behind capability flags. Where a feature only exists on one provider, isolate it in a feature module rather than threading it through the agent loop. See provider-string-routing, provider-fallback, multi-model-routing.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1692.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Anti-pattern: Application code -&amp;gt; provider SDK called directly everywhere -&amp;gt; provider shape leaks through codebase -&amp;gt; switching means rewrite. Corrected: Application code -&amp;gt; provider-agnostic adapter (+ capability flags / feature modules) -&amp;gt; any provider.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1779.4" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A startup builds its agent product against one provider&#39;s SDK, threading provider-specific objects through the agent loop and reading provider-specific error fields in retry logic. Two years later, the provider doubles per-token price and tightens rate limits; the team wants to fall back to a competitor for cheap traffic and keep the incumbent for hard tasks. The migration takes three months because tool-call shapes, streaming chunk formats, and error semantics are all wired into application code. They rebuild against a provider-agnostic adapter and a &lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;provider/model&lt;/font&gt; string router; the next vendor evaluation is a config change.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1855.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Short-term: calling one provider&#39;s SDK directly is the quickest path and gives early access to its proprietary features.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Naming it lets a team keep provider switching a normal adapter change and review imports for leaks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider outage forces the whole application offline.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Quality/cost evaluation against rival providers becomes a fork-and-rewrite project.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compliance moves (regional providers, sovereign inference) require invasive rewrites.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Negotiating-leverage with the incumbent provider erodes over time.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1923.4" width="755" height="301" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Avoiding it imposes an isolation rule: application code must not import a provider&#39;s SDK surface directly; all model access goes through a provider-agnostic adapter, with proprietary features behind capability checks or feature modules.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2056.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Cite this entry when application code is coupled to one provider&#39;s SDK, request shape, or proprietary features.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; You are already here if a provider outage or price change would require rewriting application code rather than swapping an adapter.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Bind to a provider-agnostic abstraction from the first commit and isolate provider-specific features behind capability flags.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2238.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The application is expected to live longer than one provider contract cycle (twelve to twenty-four months).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Compliance, cost, or quality may push the team to a different provider in future.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The application reads provider headers, error shapes, or rate-limit semantics directly — those will diverge.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2181.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Application code — calls one provider&#39;s SDK directly throughout the codebase&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider-specific request and streaming shapes — leak into agent loops, retry logic, and tool-call handlers&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider error fields and rate-limit headers — read by name from one vendor&#39;s response shape&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Missing provider-agnostic adapter — would isolate vendor surface behind a unified language-model spec&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2420.4" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Single-provider SDK — sole inference surface, threaded through application code without abstraction&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Provider-string router or unified adapter — missing layer that would make swaps a config change&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2344.4" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Outage stall — the single provider goes down, and the whole application goes offline because no other provider can be swapped in.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Rewrite to compare — testing a cheaper or stronger rival model turns into a fork of the codebase, so the comparison never happens.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Blocked compliance move — a requirement to use a regional provider forces invasive changes across the agent loop.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Leaked shapes — provider-specific tool-call and streaming formats spread through business logic until every module depends on them.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2602.4" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Provider-coupled call-site count — number of code locations that import or reference one vendor&#39;s SDK by name&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Time-to-swap-provider estimate — engineering days needed to redirect traffic to an alternative vendor&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Outage blast radius — share of traffic that goes offline when the bound provider has an incident&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-provider eval coverage — fraction of evals runnable against an alternative model without code changes&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2469.4" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/foundations/providers-and-models&quot;&gt;Vercel AI SDK (named as a deliberate design rejection)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Vercel AI SDK explicitly frames its standardised language-model specification against vendor lock-in.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.litellm.ai/&quot;&gt;LiteLLM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — OpenAI-compatible proxy across 100+ providers, marketed as the lock-in avoidance layer.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2822.4" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Provider-String Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Provider Fallback&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Multi-Model Routing&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Sovereign Inference Stack&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;MCP Bidirectional Bridge&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Channel-Decoupled Agent Core&lt;/b&gt; — Same adapter discipline on a different boundary: vendor-lock-in is solved by a model-provider adapter, this by a delivery-channel adapter; applying both keeps the core independent of providers and channels.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2670.4" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/foundations/providers-and-models&quot;&gt;Vercel AI SDK — Providers and Models&lt;/a&gt; — Vercel&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2985.4" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
