        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Send-&gt;End1#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m21">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m7" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m9">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Hum-&gt;End2#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m22">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m8" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m10">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Express agentic logic as a visual graph of typed nodes connected on a canvas with Start and End nodes so non-coding stakeholders can read and edit the flow.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1556.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is building on a low-code or no-code platform — Dify, Coze, n8n, Flowise, Langflow, FastGPT, Bisheng — or in an IDE-embedded workflow editor, where the same product surface is used both by developers and by non-developers such as business users or operations teams. The workflow itself is the artefact those users will edit and review, not the code behind it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1556.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Procedural agentic code is dense and unfamiliar for non-coders, and review-heavy even for developers because the orchestration logic is buried inside source files. The graph topology — which nodes feed which, which branches gate which — is the part that most needs to be inspectable, but in a procedural codebase that topology has to be reconstructed by reading code. The platform needs a graph-shaped representation of the workflow as the primary artefact, with code only behind the individual nodes that need it.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1662.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Visual editing lowers the bar for non-developer contributors but raises the bar for version control and merge.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A typed-node vocabulary (LLM, retrieval, tool, conditional, iteration, code) lets the canvas validate connections statically.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The graph must round-trip with the runtime — what runs is what is drawn.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Conditional and iteration nodes need to compose without becoming visually unreadable.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Agent nodes inside the graph blur the line between deterministic workflow and agentic loop.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1700.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: model the workflow as a typed-node graph with explicit Start and End nodes, validate connections by node-type contract, and execute the graph as drawn, so that topology is the source of truth and the canvas is what runs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1844.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a small vocabulary of node types — Start, End, LLM, Retrieval, Tool, Conditional, Iteration (see iteration-node), Code, Agent — each with a typed input/output schema. Build the workflow on a drag-and-drop canvas connecting nodes by edges; the editor validates connections by type. Persist the graph as a serialisable artefact (JSON/YAML) that the runtime executes directly. Pair with iteration-node (the per-element subgraph construct), pluggable execution semantics for Agent nodes, and policy-as-code-gate for guarded edges. Treat the canvas as a UI projection of the artefact, not the source of truth alone — diffs and reviews work on the artefact.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1901.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Canvas (drag-and-drop UI) ↔ Graph artefact (JSON/YAML, version-controlled) ↔ Workflow runtime that executes the graph.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1969.25" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A customer-success team wants to build a triage workflow that classifies incoming messages, retrieves relevant docs, drafts a reply, and routes high-confidence drafts to send while low-confidence drafts go to human review. Their engineering team uses Dify: a Start node receives the message; a Question Classifier routes by category; a Knowledge Retrieval node fetches docs per category; an LLM node drafts the reply; a Conditional node splits on confidence; one branch ends in Send, the other in Human Review. The whole workflow is one canvas. When customer success wants to add a new category, they edit the canvas; the engineering team reviews the artefact diff in the PR.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2102.25" width="755" height="187" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Topology is inspectable at a glance.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Non-developers can read and propose edits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Typed-node contracts catch wiring errors before execution.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Iteration, conditional, and agent nodes compose without leaving the canvas.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The graph artefact is auditable and reviewable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Version-controlling visual diffs is harder than text diffs without good artefact-level diffing.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Large graphs become visually unreadable — modularisation (subflows) is mandatory at scale.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Lowest-common-denominator node vocabulary may not cover bespoke logic; Code escape-hatch nodes appear and bypass the canvas&#39;s safety.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-graph refactoring is harder than across-code refactoring.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2094.25" width="755" height="339" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;All workflow logic must be expressed through typed nodes connected on the canvas; the runtime is not allowed to execute paths that do not appear in the graph artefact.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2303.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Non-developer stakeholders must read, review, or edit the workflow.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Topology inspectability is a stronger requirement than code-level concision.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Iteration, conditional, and agent constructs need to compose visibly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The runtime can execute a serialised graph artefact directly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2447.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; The workflow is mostly bespoke logic that the typed-node vocabulary cannot express cleanly.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The team has no good story for diffing and reviewing the graph artefact.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Latency budgets are so tight that node-by-node execution overhead is the bottleneck.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; The product needs LLM-driven dynamic plans rather than predefined topology.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2409.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Typed-node vocabulary — Start, End, LLM, Retrieval, Tool, Conditional, Iteration, Code, Agent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Drag-and-drop canvas — UI editor for connecting nodes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Graph artefact — serialisable JSON or YAML representation of the workflow&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Type validator — checks node-to-node connection contracts statically&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Workflow runtime — executes the graph artefact directly&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2591.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Low-code platform — Dify, Coze, n8n, Flowise, Langflow, FastGPT, or Bisheng&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; LLM API — invoked inside LLM and Agent nodes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Tool catalogue — registered functions exposed to Tool nodes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Version-control system — tracks graph-artefact diffs for review&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2553.25" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Code-node escape — bespoke logic moves into Code nodes, and the canvas shows a simple flow while the real behaviour hides inside them.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Unreadable canvas — a large graph is kept on one canvas without subflows, and reviewers can no longer follow its paths.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Diff blindness — changes are reviewed on the canvas only, and a moved edge goes unnoticed without an artefact-level diff.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Graph-runtime mismatch — the runtime executes a path that is not in the stored artefact, and the canvas stops describing what runs.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2754.25" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Non-developer edit rate — share of changes contributed without code edits&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Type-validation catch rate — wiring errors caught before execution&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Artefact-diff review quality — reviewer ability to read the diff versus reconstructing intent&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Code escape-hatch share — fraction of nodes that bypass the typed vocabulary via Code nodes&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Subflow modularisation depth — at what graph size readability collapses without it&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2697.25" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/langgenius/dify&quot;&gt;Dify&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Dify&#39;s headline feature is a visual canvas for building and testing AI workflows.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coze.com/&quot;&gt;Coze&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Coze workflows expose a typed-node canvas with Start/End nodes and full agent/tool/conditional vocabulary.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.n8n.io/&quot;&gt;n8n&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — n8n&#39;s visual node canvas hosts AI Agent and Chain root nodes alongside conventional automation nodes.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://flowiseai.com/&quot;&gt;Flowise / Langflow&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — LangChain-family visual workflow builders with typed-node canvases.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/dataelement/bisheng&quot;&gt;FastGPT / Bisheng&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Chinese-ecosystem visual workflow platforms with the same canvas shape.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2974.25" width="755" height="244" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;uses&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Iteration Node&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Event-Driven Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Policy-as-Code Gate&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Agent-as-Tool Embedding&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;alternative-to&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Spec-First Agent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Iteration Node&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2860.25" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/langgenius/dify&quot;&gt;Dify&lt;/a&gt; — LangGenius&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.n8n.io/&quot;&gt;n8n — AI nodes&lt;/a&gt; — n8n&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="3232.25" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
