        <UserObject label="" mermaidId="e:Sand-&gt;Result#0" mermaidBaseStyle="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" mermaidBaseValue="" id="m14">
          <mxCell edge="1" parent="1" source="m5" style="curved=1;startArrow=none;endArrow=block;endSize=7;strokeColor=light-dark(#333333,#cccccc);exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" target="m7">
            <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
              <Array as="points" />
            </mxGeometry>
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="s0" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;INTENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Package each agent skill as a WebAssembly module with a capability manifest, and run it inside a Wasm runtime that enforces those capabilities, so untrusted skills cannot weaken the host&#39;s sandbox.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1550.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s1" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTEXT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team is operating an enterprise agent platform that must accept skills authored by external users or partners and execute them on shared infrastructure. The skills are written in different languages — Rust, Python compiled to a runnable form, TypeScript, Go — and the platform has to enforce per-skill limits on CPU, memory, network access, and filesystem access while still serving them at the rate of incoming agent requests.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1550.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s2" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PROBLEM&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Running third-party skills as plain in-process code gives them the host&#39;s full privileges, which is unacceptable when the author is not fully trusted. Language-specific sandboxes such as a Python sandbox have a long history of escape vulnerabilities and only cover one language at a time. Spinning up a full container per skill invocation is too slow at request rate and too heavy on infrastructure. The team needs a sandbox that is light enough to start per request, language-agnostic enough to cover the polyglot skill set, and strict enough that a hostile skill cannot weaken the host environment.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1656.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s3" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FORCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Skills authored by partners cannot be trusted with host privileges.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-request container start-up is too slow and too expensive.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Polyglot authoring is a real requirement; Python-only is restrictive.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability declarations have to be checkable, not advisory.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1713.05" width="755" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s4" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THEREFORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Therefore: ship each skill as a Wasm component with a capability manifest the runtime enforces per call, so that partner-authored or untrusted skills cannot widen the host&#39;s sandbox and a fresh isolate spins up faster than a container.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1838.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s5" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SOLUTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;Define a Wasm Component Model interface for skills: each skill compiles to a Wasm module and ships with a manifest declaring (filesystem paths, network hosts, env vars, syscalls) it needs. The host runtime instantiates a fresh sandbox per call with only those capabilities. Skills can be authored in any language compiling to Wasm. The host treats the manifest as the contract; missing-capability calls fail at the boundary.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="1857.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s6" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;STRUCTURE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;monospace&quot;&gt;Host runtime { capability gate } -&amp;gt; Wasm sandbox(skill_module, manifest) -&amp;gt; deterministic IO -&amp;gt; result.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1963.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s7" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EXAMPLE SCENARIO&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A team wants to let the community contribute third-party skills to their agent but plain-process tools share the host&#39;s privileges and per-skill containers are too heavy. They define a Wasm Component Model interface for skills: each compiles to a Wasm module shipped with a manifest declaring filesystem paths, network hosts, env vars, and syscalls it needs. The Wasm runtime enforces those capabilities. Untrusted skills can run safely alongside trusted ones because a misbehaving skill cannot weaken the host&#39;s sandbox.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2020.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s8" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONSEQUENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Benefits&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Polyglot skill ecosystem with one runtime.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Strong capability isolation; manifest is the audit surface.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wasm cold-start is fast enough to run per request.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Liabilities&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wasm ecosystem maturity per language varies (Rust strong, Python heavier).&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability manifest design is the real engineering problem.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Some workloads (GPU, large data) don&#39;t fit Wasm well.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2069.05" width="755" height="263" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s9" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;WHAT THIS PATTERN CONSTRAINS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;A skill may not exercise any capability not declared in its manifest; manifest drift is detected at load time.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2202.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s10" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Enterprise platforms must accept user- or partner-authored skills in multiple languages.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-skill capabilities (filesystem, network, env, syscalls) must be enforced.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-call container overhead is too heavy for request-rate execution.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2346.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s11" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;DO NOT USE WHEN&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; All skills are first-party and trusted.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wasm tooling for the target languages is not mature enough for the workload.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; A simpler sandbox already meets the threat model.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2308.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s12" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;COMPONENTS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Wasm Module — skill compiled to a WebAssembly Component Model artefact&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability Manifest — declares filesystem paths, network hosts, env vars, and syscalls the skill needs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Wasm Host Runtime — instantiates a fresh sandbox per call with only the declared capabilities&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Capability Gate — rejects calls requesting undeclared capabilities and surfaces a typed error&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Skill Toolchain — compiles Rust, Python, TypeScript, or Go sources to Wasm modules plus manifests&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2471.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s13" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;TOOLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; WebAssembly runtime (Wasmtime, Wasmer) — executes the modules under the declared capabilities&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; WASI Preview 2 (Component Model) — standardises the host-skill interface across languages&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-language Wasm toolchains (cargo, py2wasm, AssemblyScript, TinyGo) — produce the modules&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2433.05" width="755" height="111" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s14" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FAILURE MODES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Over-broad manifest — a skill declares more paths or hosts than it needs, the runtime grants them, and a hostile skill uses the extra access.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Manifest drift unnoticed — the skill&#39;s code starts needing a capability its manifest lacks, and calls fail at the boundary in production instead of at load.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Poor language fit — a skill written in a language with a heavy Wasm toolchain starts slowly, and per-call instantiation misses the request budget.&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Workload mismatch — a GPU or large-data skill is forced into Wasm and either fails or runs far too slowly.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2653.05" width="755" height="206" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s15" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;EVALUATION METRICS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; Capability-gate enforcement rate — share of undeclared-capability calls correctly rejected&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Per-call sandbox cold-start latency — cost of instantiating a fresh Wasm sandbox per call&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Escape incidents — confirmed or attempted breaches of the Wasm boundary (should be zero)&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Manifest accuracy — fraction of skills whose declared capabilities match observed needs&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; Cross-language skill share — count of skills authored in each source language as a portability signal&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2558.05" width="755" height="168" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s16" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;KNOWN USES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;b&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Aleph-Alpha/pharia-engine&quot;&gt;Aleph Alpha PhariaEngine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;i&gt;available&lt;/i&gt; — Cognitive Business Units (Skills) compile to Wasm and run inside the engine&#39;s sandboxed runtime.&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2873.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s17" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;RELATED PATTERNS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;specialises&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Sandbox Isolation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Skill Library&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Tool Discovery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Secrets Handling&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;i&gt;complements&lt;/i&gt; &lt;b&gt;Code Execution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="815" y="2740.05" width="755" height="149" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="s18" value="&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:15px&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;REFERENCES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-size:13px;line-height:1.35&quot;&gt;&amp;bull; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/Aleph-Alpha/pharia-engine&quot;&gt;Aleph-Alpha/pharia-engine — Serverless AI powered by WebAssembly&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#c5d0db;spacing=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="2979.05" width="755" height="92" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="workflow-success-business-invalid" name="Workflow-Success vs Business-Validity Gap">
